ed special envoy for manufacturing the same day (UPI)", "cluster": "finance", "clusterLabel": "Other finance (cabinet family/funders)", "entityKind": "person"}, {"@id": "node/harmeet-dhillon", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Person"], "name": "Harmeet Dhillon", "description": "Ex-Assistant AG, DOJ Civil Rights Division (2025–resigned Nov 5 2026); says Wiles asked her to stay past midterms", "cluster": "gov", "clusterLabel": "Government / White House", "entityKind": "person"}, {"@id": "node/john-eisenberg", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Person"], "name": "John Eisenberg", "description": "Ex-Assistant AG, DOJ National Security Division (2025–resigned Nov 6 2026); ex-NSC legal adviser (first term)", "cluster": "gov", "clusterLabel": "Government / White House", "entityKind": "person"}, {"@id": "node/jason-reding-qui-ones", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Person"], "name": "Jason Reding Quiñones", "description": "Ex-US Attorney SD Fla. (2025–left Nov 6 2026); oversaw 'grand conspiracy' probe of Trump rivals (no charges)", "cluster": "gov", "clusterLabel": "Government / White House", "entityKind": "person"}, {"@id": "node/arxis-inc-defense-supplier", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Organization"], "name": "Arxis Inc (defense supplier)", "description": "Defense/aerospace components maker (Nasdaq ARXS, Arcline-sponsored IPO Apr 2026; ~47% Defense & Space: F-35, DDG-51, Virginia-class, SPY-6); Affinity Partners held 689,411 shares Jun 30 2026", "cluster": "defense", "clusterLabel": "Defense & Intel", "entityKind": "organization"}, {"@id": "node/darrell-issa", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Person"], "name": "Darrell Issa", "description": "Rep. (R-CA), House Judiciary member; Nov 10 2026 moved to refer the Hegseth impeachment resolution to Judiciary (agreed 211-204)", "cluster": "gov", "clusterLabel": "Government / White House", "entityKind": "person"}, {"@id": "node/jim-jordan", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Person"], "name": "Jim Jordan", "description": "Rep. (R-OH); House Judiciary Chair (119th); elected House GOP Minority Leader for the 120th Congress Nov 10 2026", "cluster": "gov", "clusterLabel": "Government / White House", "entityKind": "person"}, {"@id": "node/abdullah-bin-zayed-uae-fm", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Person"], "name": "Abdullah bin Zayed (UAE FM)", "description": "UAE Foreign Minister; brother of President Mohamed bin Zayed; at the table for the Nov 10 2026 Abu Dhabi US-Russia-Ukraine talks (TASS)", "cluster": "gulf", "clusterLabel": "Gulf sovereign money", "entityKind": "person"}, {"@id": "node/joseph-weirsky", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Person"], "name": "Joseph Weirsky", "description": "Nominee, Director of the National Counterterrorism Center (ODNI) Nov 10 2026, vice Joseph Kent (resigned)", "cluster": "defense", "clusterLabel": "Defense & Intel", "entityKind": "person"}, {"@id": "node/jeff-kessler-commerce-under-secretary-bis", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Person"], "name": "Jeff Kessler (Commerce Under Secretary, BIS)", "description": "Under Secretary of Commerce for Industry and Security (BIS; reports to Lutnick); named in Nvidia GC's Aug 2025 email to Megaspeed agents (NYT); asked by House chairs Nov 12 and Guthrie Nov 18 2026 for briefings; HFAC Nov 19 release: BIS approved >879,000 AI chips for China (Dec 2025-May 2026 per Reuters); BIS final rule adding Megaspeed International and six affiliates to the Entity List filed Nov 23 2026 (signed by DAS Julia Khersonsky)", "cluster": "gov", "clusterLabel": "Government / White House", "entityKind": "person"}, {"@id": "node/foundation-future-industries", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Organization"], "name": "Foundation Future Industries", "description": "Humanoid-robot maker (Phantom MK1; co-founder/president Mike LeBlanc); >$70M US military contracts and test funds (LeBlanc SAID); Eric Trump equity holder + chief strategic adviser (Mar 2026); in talks with IDF (LeBlanc SAID, Nov 2026)", "cluster": "defense", "clusterLabel": "Defense & Intel", "entityKind": "organization"}, {"@id": "node/jensen-huang", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Person"], "name": "Jensen Huang", "description": "Nvidia President, CEO and director, reinstated Nov 22 2026 (8-K Item 5.02; unanimous vote after 'input from senior levels of the United States government'); resigned Nov 11; House HFAC/China Select/HPSCI closed transcribed interview Dec 1 (reaffirmed Nov 23) and Senate Banking public hearing Dec 3 (sole witness); Trump SAID Nov 24 a pardon is 'always an option' (NY Post); AG Blanche Nov 24 would not say he was investigated; independent-committee (Wachtell) investigation continues; VP Vance SAID Nov 25 he 'doesn't need a pardon at all' and is 'under no investigation' (no DOJ document); five Senate Democratic ranking members demand an accounting of the administration's role (Nov 24); Nov 26: Trump SAID Huang is 'absolutely fine' and calls his return a 'second term'; CBS (Nov 25, anon.): Rubio memo and May Air Force One briefing on Alice Huang intel, Clayton intel review, Musk contact", "cluster": "media", "clusterLabel": "Media owners & platforms", "entityKind": "person"}, {"@id": "node/colette-kress", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Person"], "name": "Colette Kress", "description": "Nvidia EVP and CFO (since 2013); interim CEO Nov 11-22 2026; continues as EVP and CFO after Huang's reinstatement (8-K Nov 23)", "cluster": "media", "clusterLabel": "Media owners & platforms", "entityKind": "person"}, {"@id": "node/tim-cook-apple", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Person"], "name": "Tim Cook (Apple)", "description": "Apple executive chair; named by Trump (Truth Social, Nov 12 2026) to replace Huang at Nvidia - SAID only; Apple on the $25M ballroom tier (WaPo docs)", "cluster": "media", "clusterLabel": "Media owners & platforms", "entityKind": "person"}, {"@id": "node/house-chairs-mast-moolenaar-crawford", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "pm:Group"], "name": "House chairs (Mast / Moolenaar / Crawford)", "description": "House Foreign Affairs (Mast), China Select (Moolenaar), Intelligence (Crawford) chairs; Nov 4 2026 letter to Huang; Huang/Teter interviews Dec 1-2; Mast published Nvidia/AMD China AI-chip license data Nov 19 2026 (ECRA authority: 3.4 million requested, >879,000 approved by BIS)", "cluster": "gov", "clusterLabel": "Government / White House", "entityKind": "group"}, {"@id": "node/vulcan-elements", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Organization"], "name": "Vulcan Elements", "description": "US rare-earth magnet maker; 1789 Capital investor (Aug 2025); $620M Pentagon OSC loan (Nov 2025)", "cluster": "defense", "clusterLabel": "Defense & Intel", "entityKind": "organization"}, {"@id": "node/drw-don-wilson", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Organization"], "name": "DRW (Don Wilson)", "description": "Chicago trading firm (Cumberland DRW crypto arm); SEC case dismissed Mar 2025; ~$100M into Trump Media PIPE May 2025", "cluster": "finance", "clusterLabel": "Other finance (cabinet family/funders)", "entityKind": "organization"}, {"@id": "node/crypto-com", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Organization"], "name": "Crypto.com", "description": "Crypto exchange; SEC probe closed Mar 2025 (company SAID); $50M TMTG stock (Aug 2025)", "cluster": "finance", "clusterLabel": "Other finance (cabinet family/funders)", "entityKind": "organization"}, {"@id": "node/alt5-sigma-ai-financial-corp", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Organization"], "name": "Alt5 Sigma (AI Financial Corp.)", "description": "Nasdaq WLFI-treasury company (renamed AIFC Apr 2026); chair Zach Witkoff; going-concern warning May 2026", "cluster": "finance", "clusterLabel": "Other finance (cabinet family/funders)", "entityKind": "organization"}, {"@id": "node/new-america-acquisition-i-corp", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Organization"], "name": "New America Acquisition I Corp.", "description": "SPAC ($300M S-1 Aug 2025); Eric Trump + Donald Trump Jr. sponsor interests and advisory board", "cluster": "trumpbiz", "clusterLabel": "Trump family business & crypto", "entityKind": "organization"}, {"@id": "node/occ-comptroller-of-the-currency", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:GovernmentOrganization"], "name": "OCC (Comptroller of the Currency)", "description": "US national-bank regulator (Treasury bureau); preliminary charter to World Liberty Trust Co. Aug 14 2026", "cluster": "gov", "clusterLabel": "Government / White House", "entityKind": "government"}, {"@id": "node/iren", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Organization"], "name": "IREN", "description": "Nasdaq AI-cloud / data-center operator (Australia); Nvidia partner (May 7 2026: right to invest up to $2.1B; $3.4B cloud contract); $3B convertible May 2026 (Cantor a bookrunner)", "cluster": "finance", "clusterLabel": "Other finance (cabinet family/funders)", "entityKind": "organization"}, {"@id": "node/sens-elizabeth-warren-chris-coons", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "pm:Group"], "name": "Sens. Elizabeth Warren & Chris Coons", "description": "US senators (D-MA Banking ranking member; D-DE); Nov 11 2026 records-preservation letter on Nvidia exports", "cluster": "gov", "clusterLabel": "Government / White House", "entityKind": "group"}, {"@id": "node/sean-duffy-transportation-secretary", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Person"], "name": "Sean Duffy (Transportation Secretary)", "description": "US Transportation Secretary; Peraton ATC Prime Integrator (Dec 2025); FENS direct award to AT&T, Verizon to supporting role (Aug 2026); $30.1B letter / $50B ask Nov 13; joint ground-stop briefing with Mullin; SAID Nov 14 possible L3Harris 'incompetence'", "cluster": "gov", "clusterLabel": "Government / White House", "entityKind": "person"}, {"@id": "node/peraton-veritas-capital", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Organization"], "name": "Peraton (Veritas Capital)", "description": "Federal IT/defense contractor owned by Veritas Capital; FAA ATC Prime Integrator (IDIQ $1.5B ceiling, Dec 2025)", "cluster": "defense", "clusterLabel": "Defense & Intel", "entityKind": "organization"}, {"@id": "node/cove-kaz-capital-kaz-resources", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Organization"], "name": "Cove Kaz Capital (Kaz Resources)", "description": "Cove Capital unit developing a Kazakh tungsten deposit (with Tau-Ken Samruk); EXIM $900M + DFC $700M letters of interest (2025); Trump sons' indirect <1% stake; planned US listing as Kaz Resources", "cluster": "trumpbiz", "clusterLabel": "Trump family business & crypto", "entityKind": "organization"}, {"@id": "node/sec-cftc-nominees-johnson-levine-anonick-rowland", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "pm:Group"], "name": "SEC + CFTC nominees (Johnson, Levine, Anonick, Rowland)", "description": "Nominated Nov 12 2026: Kristin N. Johnson + Steven Levine (SEC), Nathan Anonick + Matthew Rowland (CFTC); Senate action pending", "cluster": "gov", "clusterLabel": "Government / White House", "entityKind": "group"}, {"@id": "node/brad-gerstner-altimeter-gavin-baker-atreides", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "pm:Group"], "name": "Brad Gerstner (Altimeter) & Gavin Baker (Atreides)", "description": "Altimeter Capital CEO + Atreides Management founder; major Nvidia shareholders; open letter to Nvidia board Nov 13 2026 (keep Huang's return an option)", "cluster": "finance", "clusterLabel": "Other finance (cabinet family/funders)", "entityKind": "group"}, {"@id": "node/wachtell-lipton", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Organization"], "name": "Wachtell Lipton", "description": "Law firm; reported (CNBC Nov 16 2026) to lead Nvidia board's probe of Huang's conduct", "cluster": "finance", "clusterLabel": "Other finance (cabinet family/funders)", "entityKind": "organization"}, {"@id": "node/l3harris", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Organization"], "name": "L3Harris", "description": "Defense/aerospace contractor; FAA Telecommunications Infrastructure (FTI) incumbent since 2002 ('current network service provider'); FAA Nov 15 2026: deploying a new Juniper router at El Dorado AR when the Nov 13 data flood began; root cause under FAA + L3Harris investigation", "cluster": "defense", "clusterLabel": "Defense & Intel", "entityKind": "organization"}, {"@id": "node/at-t-faa-fens", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Organization"], "name": "AT&T (FAA FENS)", "description": "AT&T Enterprise Services; FAA FENS direct award Aug 11 2026 ($74.3M TO; multi-billion IDIQ expected; BNATCS waiver)", "cluster": "defense", "clusterLabel": "Defense & Intel", "entityKind": "organization"}, {"@id": "node/eric-ueland", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Person"], "name": "Eric Ueland", "description": "OMB deputy director for management (under Vought); nominated Comptroller General (GAO head, 15-yr term) Nov 16 2026; HSGAC hearing Nov 19", "cluster": "gov", "clusterLabel": "Government / White House", "entityKind": "person"}, {"@id": "node/heidrick-struggles", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Organization"], "name": "Heidrick & Struggles", "description": "Chicago-based executive search firm; retained by Nvidia's board to lead the permanent-CEO search (Jones SAID on the Nov 17 2026 call)", "cluster": "finance", "clusterLabel": "Other finance (cabinet family/funders)", "entityKind": "organization"}, {"@id": "node/sen-tim-scott-senate-banking-chair", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Person"], "name": "Sen. Tim Scott (Senate Banking chair)", "description": "Senate Banking Committee chair (R-SC) until Jan 2027; Nov 12 2026 letters ask Huang (Dec 3) and Lutnick (Dec 10) to testify; Lutnick agreed; Huang confirmed as sole witness for the Dec 3 public hearing 'Protecting America's AI Advantage: Oversight of U.S. Export Controls' (notice Nov 23)", "cluster": "gov", "clusterLabel": "Government / White House", "entityKind": "person"}, {"@id": "node/sec-securities-and-exchange-commission", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Organization"], "name": "SEC (Securities and Exchange Commission)", "description": "US securities regulator; probe of Nvidia reported (WSJ Nov 17 2026; Reuters Nov 20, two people briefed: accounting practices); SEC declined to comment; no SEC or Nvidia confirmation on record", "cluster": "gov", "clusterLabel": "Government / White House", "entityKind": "organization"}, {"@id": "node/verizon-faa-fens", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Organization"], "name": "Verizon (FAA FENS)", "description": "Verizon; FAA FENS competitive award 2023 ($2.4B); moved to supporting role (core network functions) when AT&T took the prime under the Aug 11 2026 direct award", "cluster": "defense", "clusterLabel": "Defense & Intel", "entityKind": "organization"}, {"@id": "node/juniper-routers-faa-fti", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Organization"], "name": "Juniper routers (FAA FTI)", "description": "Juniper Networks routers in the FAA FTI network; FAA Nov 15 2026: new one deployed by L3Harris at El Dorado AR at the origin of the Nov 13 data flood; function disabled on 60+ others, installs paused", "cluster": "defense", "clusterLabel": "Defense & Intel", "entityKind": "organization"}, {"@id": "node/markwayne-mullin-dhs-secretary", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Person"], "name": "Markwayne Mullin (DHS Secretary)", "description": "Homeland Security Secretary; Nov 13 2026 joint ground-stop briefing with Duffy (SAID President declared a national emergency; zero evidence of cyberattack); Nov 17 SAID 98% not a cyberattack", "cluster": "gov", "clusterLabel": "Government / White House", "entityKind": "person"}, {"@id": "node/gen-chris-laneve", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Person"], "name": "Gen. Chris LaNeve", "description": "Army vice chief / acting chief of staff since Apr 2026; ex-military aide to Hegseth; nominated Army chief of staff Nov 17 2026 (not confirmed)", "cluster": "defense", "clusterLabel": "Defense & Intel", "entityKind": "person"}, {"@id": "node/heidi-overton", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Person"], "name": "Heidi Overton", "description": "WH Domestic Policy Council deputy director; FDA commissioner nominee (Aug 2026); Axios Nov 17 2026 (senior official): nomination being dropped", "cluster": "gov", "clusterLabel": "Government / White House", "entityKind": "person"}, {"@id": "node/delcy-rodriguez-