anned by Denmark's Supreme Court (2021); people linked to it charged (Nov 2026) with attempted murder and assisting a foreign intelligence service", "cluster": "russia", "clusterLabel": "Russia ties (Kremlin, oligarch, Lukoil)", "entityKind": "organization"}, {"@id": "node/megaspeed-singapore-entity-list-nov-2026", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Organization"], "name": "Megaspeed (Singapore; Entity List Nov 2026)", "description": "Singapore-based data-center company (Megaspeed International Pte. Ltd. + Malaysian/Thai/Singapore affiliates MSFusion, PT Megaspeed International, Speedmatrix, Apex Enterprise Solutions, Swiftdata, Megaspeed (Thailand)); added to the BIS Entity List Nov 23 2026; DOJ/Commerce export-control probe (Nov 17 joint statement); former executive Alice Huang; same rule lists Alibaba's Singapore unit Apex Enterprise Solutions (Speedmatrix pledged equipment/IP to Apex, Jun 2024; Straits Times); Federal Register prints the rule Nov 25 (not yet in the FR API at 11:40 PM EST Nov 24)", "cluster": "media", "clusterLabel": "Media owners & platforms", "entityKind": "organization"}, {"@id": "node/pure-lithium-ceo-emilie-bodoin", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Organization"], "name": "Pure Lithium (CEO Emilie Bodoin)", "description": "Privately held lithium-metal battery startup (CEO Emilie Bodoin; large shareholder Robert Friedland); suing Panasonic (preliminary-injunction hearing Jan 2027); refused Commerce's 51% stake request (Reuters, Nov 20 2026)", "cluster": "finance", "clusterLabel": "Other finance (cabinet family/funders)", "entityKind": "organization"}, {"@id": "node/i-pulse-robert-friedland", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Organization"], "name": "I-Pulse (Robert Friedland)", "description": "Pulsed-power / silicon-carbide semiconductor company co-founded by billionaire Robert Friedland; $250M CHIPS R&D award and a minority Commerce equity stake (Jun 25 2026); Friedland is a large Pure Lithium shareholder", "cluster": "finance", "clusterLabel": "Other finance (cabinet family/funders)", "entityKind": "organization"}, {"@id": "node/katie-miller", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Person"], "name": "Katie Miller", "description": "Podcaster (The Katie Miller Podcast, ended Nov 2026); ex-White House / DOGE spokesperson; ex-SpaceX adviser (left Nov 2026, sold shares, per The Atlantic); wife of WH Chief of Staff Stephen Miller", "cluster": "musk", "clusterLabel": "Musk network", "entityKind": "person"}, {"@id": "node/house-oversight-democrats-rep-robert-garcia", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:GovernmentOrganization"], "name": "House Oversight Democrats (Rep. Robert Garcia)", "description": "Democrats on the House Oversight and Government Reform Committee; ranking member Robert Garcia (in line to chair from Jan 3 2027)", "cluster": "gov", "clusterLabel": "Government / White House", "entityKind": "government"}, {"@id": "node/general-motors-gm-defense", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Organization"], "name": "General Motors (GM Defense)", "description": "Automaker; GM Defense unit; reported Nov 24 2026 (WSJ, people familiar) in Pentagon talks to supply drone motors and parts, no deal; declined comment on the report", "cluster": "defense", "clusterLabel": "Defense & Intel", "entityKind": "organization"}, {"@id": "node/mark-rutte-nato-secretary-general", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Person"], "name": "Mark Rutte (NATO Secretary General)", "description": "NATO Secretary General; met Trump at Mar-a-Lago Wed Nov 25 2026 (closed press, dinner; joint statement on Russia-Ukraine, Iran, defense spending); told Fox Trump is 'testing Putin'; NATO's own page (Nov 26) also shows a meeting with chief of staff Miller", "cluster": "defense", "clusterLabel": "Defense & Intel", "entityKind": "person"}, {"@id": "node/alibaba-group-apex-enterprise-solutions-singapore", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Organization"], "name": "Alibaba Group (Apex Enterprise Solutions, Singapore)", "description": "Chinese tech group; Singapore unit Apex Enterprise Solutions added to the BIS Entity List with Megaspeed Nov 23 2026; held a security interest over Megaspeed-unit Speedmatrix equipment/IP (Jun 2024, Straits Times); Alibaba calls the listing 'erroneous'", "cluster": "media", "clusterLabel": "Media owners & platforms", "entityKind": "organization"}, {"@id": "node/jim-o-neill-m-d-n-c-judicial-nominee", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Person"], "name": "Jim O'Neill (M.D.N.C. judicial nominee)", "description": "Forsyth County NC District Attorney (2009 - Dec 31 2026; lost Nov 2026 re-election); Trump's nominee for US District Court, Middle District of NC (announced Nov 24 2026), backed by Sens. Tillis and Budd", "cluster": "gov", "clusterLabel": "Government / White House", "entityKind": "person"}, {"@id": "node/senate-democratic-ranking-members-cantwell-coons-warren-wyden-reed", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "pm:Group"], "name": "Senate Democratic ranking members (Cantwell / Coons / Warren / Wyden / Reed)", "description": "Senate committee ranking members (Dem): Maria Cantwell (Commerce), Elizabeth Warren (Banking), Ron Wyden (Finance), Jack Reed (Armed Services) + Chris Coons; joint statement Nov 24 2026 demanding an accounting of the administration's role in Huang's reinstatement; majority from Jan 3 2027", "cluster": "gov", "clusterLabel": "Government / White House", "entityKind": "group"}, {"@id": "node/jamieson-greer-us-trade-representative", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Person"], "name": "Jamieson Greer (US Trade Representative)", "description": "US Trade Representative (confirmed 2025); Nov 25 2026 Section 301 determinations against China and 13 other economies with proposed tariffs (comments to Jan 5 2027)", "cluster": "gov", "clusterLabel": "Government / White House", "entityKind": "person"}, {"@id": "node/s-p-global-ratings", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Organization"], "name": "S&P Global Ratings", "description": "Credit rating agency (S&P Global Inc.); Nov 25 2026 placed Nvidia's AA on CreditWatch negative over board oversight after the Huang departure and reinstatement", "cluster": "finance", "clusterLabel": "Other finance (cabinet family/funders)", "entityKind": "organization"}, {"@id": "node/sen-john-cornyn-r-tx-outgoing", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Person"], "name": "Sen. John Cornyn (R-TX, outgoing)", "description": "US Senator (R-TX) through Jan 3 2027 (lost Trump-backed primary); withheld blue slip on Trump's N.D. Tex. nominee T. Elliot Gaiser (Nov 2026); pushed Steve Fahey, whom the WH began vetting (Nov 21-23); Nov 25: Senate Judiciary received partial materials for his pick Fahey (Reuters: Trump moving to replace Gaiser)", "cluster": "gov", "clusterLabel": "Government / White House", "entityKind": "person"}, {"@id": "node/sen-chuck-grassley-r-ia-judiciary-chair", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Person"], "name": "Sen. Chuck Grassley (R-IA, Judiciary chair)", "description": "US Senator (R-IA); chairs Senate Judiciary; Nov 25 2026 received partial materials for potential nominees Fahey (N.D. Tex.) and O'Neill (M.D.N.C.) and said he will test whether a confirmation path exists before year end", "cluster": "gov", "clusterLabel": "Government / White House", "entityKind": "person"}, {"@id": "node/coreweave", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Organization"], "name": "CoreWeave", "description": "GPU cloud (Nasdaq: CRWV, junk-rated); Nov 25 2026: Bloomberg says bankers (Morgan Stanley, MUFG) prepare $4.5B Meta-contract GPU-secured loan sale; 5-yr CDS record (ICE via Bloomberg)", "cluster": "finance", "clusterLabel": "Other finance (cabinet family/funders)", "entityKind": "organization"}, {"@id": "node/sen-jeanne-shaheen-sfrc-ranking-member", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Person"], "name": "Sen. Jeanne Shaheen (SFRC ranking member)", "description": "US Senator (D-NH); Senate Foreign Relations ranking member; Nov 25 2026 letter with Rep. Meeks to Rubio and Acting USAID Administrator Woolf on PII in the 'USAID Files' release", "cluster": "gov", "clusterLabel": "Government / White House", "entityKind": "person"}, {"@id": "node/mike-benz-foundation-for-freedom-online", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Person"], "name": "Mike Benz (Foundation for Freedom Online)", "description": "Former State Dept deputy assistant secretary (Nov 2020-Jan 2021); Foundation for Freedom Online; OCCRP (Nov 26 2026): appears to have orchestrated the 'USAID Files' release, reportedly a special government employee since Dec 2025", "cluster": "media", "clusterLabel": "Media owners & platforms", "entityKind": "person"}, {"@id": "node/usaid-remnant-omb-jurisdiction", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:GovernmentOrganization"], "name": "USAID (remnant; OMB jurisdiction)", "description": "US foreign-aid agency wound down 2025; Acting Administrator Bill Woolf (since Oct 3 2026); site relaunched Nov 24-25 2026 as 'USAID Files' (248 files); State says OMB holds jurisdiction over remaining elements", "cluster": "gov", "clusterLabel": "Government / White House", "entityKind": "government"}, {"@id": "node/masoud-pezeshkian-iran-president", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Person"], "name": "Masoud Pezeshkian (Iran president)", "description": "President of Iran (2024-); Nov 2026 video of him in an unheated office urging conservation; publicly taunted by Treasury Secretary Bessent Nov 27 2026", "cluster": "iran", "clusterLabel": "Iran & Yemen leadership", "entityKind": "person"}, {"@id": "node/leidos", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Organization"], "name": "Leidos", "description": "Defense/IT contractor (NYSE: LDOS, Reston VA); Dec 2025 $455M-ceiling Air Force Cloud One task order; Cloud One breach reported Nov 27 2026 (Reuters, anon.)", "cluster": "defense", "clusterLabel": "Defense & Intel", "entityKind": "organization"}, {"@id": "node/us-air-force-dept-of-the-air-force", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:GovernmentOrganization"], "name": "US Air Force (Dept. of the Air Force)", "description": "Military department; runs the Cloud One enterprise cloud (Leidos prime since 2025); Nov 27 2026 declined comment on a reported breach", "cluster": "gov", "clusterLabel": "Government / White House", "entityKind": "government"}, {"@id": "node/kirsten-davies-national-cyber-director-nominee", "@type": ["pm:Actor", "schema:Person"], "name": "Kirsten Davies (National Cyber Director nominee)", "description": "Pentagon (Department of War) CIO; named acting National Cyber Director Nov 19 2026 (WH release Nov 20); acting role moved to DNI Jay Clayton Nov 23 because a nominee cannot also be acting (WH official via CNBC, CyberScoop); Davies now ONCD senior adviser and Trump's intended nominee; nomination not yet on the Senate record (Nov 24)", "cluster": "defense", "clusterLabel": "Defense & Intel", "entityKind": "person"}, {"@id": "tie/gaetz-married-ginger-luckey", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/matt-gaetz", "to": "node/palmer-luckey", "name": "brother-in-law 2021", "tieType": "marriage/family", "category": "family", "kind": "register", "date": "2021-08-21", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-08 (v1)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-08", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-08-V-powermap-gaetz-married-ginger-luckey", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "MARRIAGE: Matt Gaetz married Ginger Luckey, sister of Oculus/Anduril founder Palmer Luckey, on Catalina Island on 2021-08-21 (engaged Dec 2020 at Mar-a-Lago). Palmer attended. This makes Palmer Luckey Gaetz's brother-in-law.", "citation": ["https://apnews.com/article/matt-gaetz-ginger-luckey-married-b71f9465e7c85e80e879802964adac69", "https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/americas/matt-gaetz-marries-ginger-luckey-b1906942.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/gor-officiated-gaetz-wedding", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/sergio-gor", "to": "node/matt-gaetz", "name": "personal 2021", "tieType": "personal (officiant)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2021-08-21", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-08 (v1)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-08", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-08-V-powermap-gor-officiated-gaetz-wedding", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "PERSONAL: Sergio Gor (then ex-Rand Paul staffer, later Trump White House personnel chief) officiated the Gaetz-Luckey wedding on 2021-08-21.", "citation": ["https://apnews.com/article/matt-gaetz-ginger-luckey-married-b71f9465e7c85e80e879802964adac69", "https://www.vice.com/en/article/matt-gaetz-wife-ginger-luckey-wedding-sex-trafficking/"]}, {"@id": "tie/gor-ambassador-india", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/sergio-gor", "name": "appointment 2025-26", "tieType": "appointment", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-10 (confirmed); in post Jan 2026", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-08 (v1)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-13", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-13-V-powermap-v11-recheck-roles", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "APPOINTMENT: Sergio Gor confirmed (51-47, Oct 2025) as US Ambassador to India and Special Envoy for South and Central Asia; took up post in New Delhi Jan 2026; still serving per NYT June 2026.", "citation": ["https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/india/sergio-gor-confirmed-as-us-ambassador-to-india/articleshow/124376385.cms", "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/06/13/us/politics/sergio-gor-ambassador-transformation-trump-era.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/gaetz-promoted-anduril-pre-marriage", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/matt-gaetz", "to": "node/anduril", "name": "advocacy 2018-20", "tieType": "advocacy (pre-engagement)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2018-2020", "grade": "I", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-10-09", "statusNote": "Hearing half superseded by V edge gaetz-zuckerberg-luckey-hearing; Twitter-promotion half stays I.", "addedIn": "2026-10-08 (v1)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-08-I-powermap-gaetz-promoted-anduril-pre-marriage", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "ADVOCACY (I): USA Today Network (Apr 2021) reports Gaetz promoted Luckey's company Anduril on Twitter and raised Luckey's Facebook ouster at a congressional hearing before his engagement to Ginger Luckey. Exact hearing date not independently confirmed here; graded I.", "citation": ["https://www.heraldmailmedia.com/story/news/2021/04/02/embattled-congressman-matt-gaetz-is-engaged-to-sister-of-pro-trump-tech-mogul/43725017/"]}, {"@id": "tie/gaetz-oan-host", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/matt-gaetz", "to": "node/oan", "name": "employment 2025-now", "tieType": "employment (media)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-01 - present", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-08 (v1)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-08", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-08-V-powermap-gaetz-oan-host", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "EMPLOYMENT: After withdrawing as AG nominee (Nov 2024), Matt Gaetz hosts 'The Matt Gaetz Show' on One America News, premiered Jan 2025; still airing 2026.", "citation": ["https://www.oann.com/newsroom/matt-gaetz-joins-oan-primetime-lineup-show-premieres-january-2025/", "https://www.oann.com/shows/themattgaetzshow/"]}, {"@id": "tie/luckey-trump-fundraisers", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/palmer-luckey", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "funding 2020-24", "tieType": "funding (fundraiser host)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2020-10 ; 2024-06", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-08 (v1)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-08", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-08-V-powermap-luckey-trump-fundraisers", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "FUNDING: Palmer Luckey hosted a Trump fundraiser at his Southern California home in Oct 2020 (raised ~$10M per LA Times) and co-hosted a June 2024 Trump fundraiser in Newport Beach.", "citation": ["https://www.cnbc.com/2020/10/16/palmer-luckey-to-host-trump-fundraiser-in-southern-california.html", "https://www.latimes.com/socal/daily-pilot/news/story/2020-10-19/private-trump-fundraiser-in-newport-beach-raises-10-million-for-reelection-campaign", "https://www.ocregister.com/2024/06/08/trump-supporters-line-the-streets-in-newport-beach-in-anticipation-of-his-visit/"]}, {"@id": "tie/founders-fund-anduril", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/founders-fund", "to": "node/anduril", "name": "funding (lead, $1B) 2017-25", "tieType": "funding", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2017 - 2025-06", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-08 (v1)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-recheck-roles", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "FUNDING: Peter Thiel's Founders Fund has backed Anduril since its 2017 founding; co-led the $1.5B Series F (Aug 2024) and put $1B (its largest check ever) into the $2.5B Series G at $30.5B valuation (2025-06-05).", "citation": ["https://www.reuters.com/business/anduril-secures-305-billion-valuation-latest-fund-raise-2025-06-05/", "https://www.cnbc.com/2025/06/05/anduril-valuation-founders-fund.html", "https://news.crunchbase.com/venture/defense-tech-unicorn-anduril-doubles-valuation/"]}, {"@id": "tie/trae-stephens-ff-anduril", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/trae-stephens", "to": "node/anduril", "name": "employment/board 2017-now", "tieType": "employment/board", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2017 - present", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-08 (v1)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-08", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-08-V-powermap-trae-stephens-ff-anduril", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "EMPLOYMENT/BOARD: Trae Stephens is simultaneously Anduril co-founder/executive chairman and a partner at Founders Fund, the lead Anduril investor (reported 2025).", "citation": ["https://www.reuters.com/business/anduril-secures-305-billion-valuation-latest-fund-raise-2025-06-05/", "https://news.crunchbase.com/venture/defense-tech-unicorn-anduril-doubles-valuation/"]}, {"@id": "tie/anduril-army-20b-enterprise", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/us-army", "to": "node/anduril", "name": "$20B ceiling contract 2026", "tieType": "government contract", "category": "contract", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-03", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-08 (v1)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-08", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-08-V-powermap-anduril-army-20b-enterprise", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "CONTRACT: US Army awarded Anduril (founded by Palmer Luckey) a 10-year enterprise contract with a ceiling of up to $20B in March 2026 (ceiling, not obligated); first task order $87M counter-drone C2 on Lattice.", "citation": ["https://defensescoop.com/2026/03/14/anduril-20-billion-dollar-army-contract/", "https://breakingdefense.com/2026/03/army-awards-anduril-counter-drone-task-order-as-first-in-new-20b-contract-vehicle/"]}, {"@id": "tie/anduril-meta-sbmc", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/us-army", "to": "node/anduril", "name": "government contract 2025", "tieType": "government contract", "category": "contract", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-09", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-08 (v1)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-08", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-08-V-powermap-anduril-meta-sbmc", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "CONTRACT: Army awarded Anduril (teamed with Meta) ~$159M OTA for Soldier Borne Mission Command (ex-IVAS) prototypes, Sept 2025 - reuniting Luckey with Meta, the firm that pushed him out in 2017.", "citation": ["https://defensescoop.com/2025/09/08/army-sbmc-contract-awards-anduril-rivet-soldier-borne-mission-command/", "https://breakingdefense.com/2025/09/ivas-anduril-meta-rivet-virtual-reality-goggle-army-sbmc/"]}, {"@id": "tie/thiel-employed-vance-mithril", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/peter-thiel", "to": "node/jd-vance", "name": "employs (Mithril) 2016-17", "tieType": "employment", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "c.2016-2017", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-08 (v1)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-08", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-08-V-powermap-thiel-employed-vance-mithril", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "EMPLOYMENT: JD Vance worked as a principal at Thiel's Mithril Capital (CBS: Thiel hired him in 2017) before moving to Ohio.", "citation": ["https://www.cbsnews.com/news/jd-vance-trump-vp-peter-thiel-billionaire/", "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/2022/07/27/why-peter-thiel-spent-millions-boost-jd-vance-ohio-senate-race/7710393001/"]}, {"@id": "tie/thiel-narya", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/peter-thiel", "to": "node/jd-vance", "name": "backs Narya fund 2019-20", "tieType": "funding (business)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2019-2020", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-08 (v1)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-08", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-08-V-powermap-thiel-narya", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "FUNDING: Thiel was a backer of Vance's Narya Capital (founded 2019; $93M first fund Jan 2020, also backed by Eric Schmidt and Marc Andreessen).", "citation": ["https://www.axios.com/2020/01/09/jd-vance-venture-capital-fund-ohio-silicon-valley-peter-thiel", "https://techcrunch.com/2020/01/09/hillbilly-elegy-author-j-d-vance-has-raised-93-million-for-his-own-midwestern-venture-fund/"]}, {"@id": "tie/thiel-15m-protect-ohio-values", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/peter-thiel", "to": "node/jd-vance", "name": "funds $15M super PAC 2021-22", "tieType": "funding (super PAC)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2021-03-12 ; 2022-04", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-08 (v1)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-08", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-08-V-powermap-thiel-15m-protect-ohio-values", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "FUNDING: Thiel gave $15M to Protect Ohio Values super PAC backing Vance's 2022 Senate run ($10M 2021-03-12, $3.5M 2022-04-18, $1.5M 2022-04-25 per FEC/OpenSecrets) - then the largest sum ever to boost a single Senate candidate.", "citation": ["https://www.opensecrets.org/political-action-committees-pacs/protect-ohio-values-pac/C00770495/donors/2022", "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/03/jd-vance-win-ohio-primary-00029881"]}, {"@id": "tie/vance-tiebreak-hegseth", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jd-vance", "to": "node/pete-hegseth", "name": "VP tie-break confirms 2025", "tieType": "appointment (confirmation vote)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-01-24", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-08 (v1)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-08", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-08-V-powermap-vance-tiebreak-hegseth", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "APPOINTMENT: VP Vance cast the tie-breaking vote (51-50) confirming former Fox News weekend host Pete Hegseth as Secretary of Defense on 2025-01-24. Hegseth still in office Oct 2026.", "citation": ["https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1191/vote_119_1_00015.htm", "https://apnews.com/article/pete-hegseth-defense-secretary-trump-cabinet-confirmation-12491935023692bce0a04d149663e784"]}, {"@id": "tie/thiel-karp-palantir", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/peter-thiel", "to": "node/palantir", "name": "founder/board 2003-now", "tieType": "founder/board", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2003 - present", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-08 (v1)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-08", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-08-V-powermap-thiel-karp-palantir", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "FOUNDER/BOARD: Palantir co-founded 2003 by Peter Thiel (chairman), Alex Karp (CEO), Joe Lonsdale, Stephen Cohen, Nathan Gettings; early funding included CIA's In-Q-Tel.", "citation": ["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palantir_Technologies", "https://www.forbes.com/sites/andygreenberg/2013/08/14/agent-of-intelligence-how-a-deviant-philosopher-built-palantir-a-cia-funded-data-mining-juggernaut/"]}, {"@id": "tie/palantir-army-10b-ea", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/us-army", "to": "node/palantir", "name": "$10B ceiling EA 2025", "tieType": "government contract", "category": "contract", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-07-31", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-08 (v1)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-08", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-08-V-powermap-palantir-army-10b-ea", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "CONTRACT: Army consolidated 75 Palantir contracts into one 10-year Enterprise Agreement with ceiling up to $10B (announced 2025-07-31/Aug 2025; ceiling, not committed spend).", "citation": ["https://www.army.mil/article/287506/u_s_army_awards_enterprise_service_agreement_to_enhance_military_readiness_and_drive_operational_efficiency", "https://breakingdefense.com/2025/08/army-consolidates-dozens-of-palantir-software-contracts-into-one-deal-worth-up-to-10-billion/"]}, {"@id": "tie/palantir-maven-feinberg", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/stephen-feinberg", "to": "node/palantir", "name": "Maven = CJADC2 core 2025-26", "tieType": "government contract/program of record", "category": "contract", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-05 ; 2026-03/04", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-08 (v1)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-08", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-08-V-powermap-palantir-maven-feinberg", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "CONTRACT: Pentagon raised Palantir Maven Smart System ceiling by $795M to ~$1.3B (May 2025); in March 2026 Pentagon memo made Maven a core program of record, and Deputy SecDef Stephen Feinberg (ex-Cerberus) issued an April 2026 directive making Maven AI decision-making 'the cornerstone' of CJADC2.", "citation": ["https://defensescoop.com/2025/05/23/dod-palantir-maven-smart-system-contract-increase/", "https://www.reuters.com/technology/pentagon-adopt-palantir-ai-as-core-us-military-system-memo-says-2026-03-20/", "https://defensescoop.com/2026/04/03/palantir-maven-feinberg-directive/"]}, {"@id": "tie/feinberg-deputy-secdef", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/stephen-feinberg", "name": "appointment 2025", "tieType": "appointment", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-03-14", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-08 (v1)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-27", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-27-V-powermap-v21-recheck-roles", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "APPOINTMENT: Cerberus Capital co-founder Stephen Feinberg confirmed Deputy Secretary of D