dreessen and Lonsdale (Palantir co-founder) asked to help DOGE; formal role unconfirmed.", "citation": ["https://techcrunch.com/2024/11/27/marc-andreessen-joe-londsale-and-all-the-other-vcs-reportedly-in-the-running-for-new-trump-committees/"]}, {"@id": "tie/gaetz-zuckerberg-luckey-hearing", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/matt-gaetz", "to": "node/palmer-luckey", "name": "advocacy 2020", "tieType": "advocacy (congressional)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2020-07-29", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v1, second batch)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-gaetz-zuckerberg-luckey-hearing-jul2020", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "ADVOCACY: At the Jul 29 2020 House antitrust hearing Gaetz pressed Zuckerberg on Luckey's firing (5 months before the Gaetz-Luckey engagement).", "citation": ["https://www.bbc.com/news/live/world-us-canada-53582909"]}, {"@id": "tie/hegseth-meridian-musk", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/pete-hegseth", "to": "node/elon-musk", "name": "Meridian co-lead 2026-09", "tieType": "appointment (advisory: Project Meridian co-lead)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-09-30", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v3)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-19", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-hegseth-meridian-musk", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "APPOINTMENT (ADVISORY): Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth named Elon Musk a co-lead of 'Project Meridian', a 120-day Pentagon future-warfare study run under CTO Emil Michael (public report + classified annex due by Jan 28 2027). Axios: Musk's first official advisory role since the DOGE exit and feud. SpaceX holds large Pentagon contracts (Axios 'follow the money').", "citation": ["https://www.axios.com/2026/09/30/pentagon-hegseth-musk-gingrich-anduril", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/06/anduril-navy-submarine-shipyard-contract.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/hegseth-meridian-luckey", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/pete-hegseth", "to": "node/palmer-luckey", "name": "Meridian co-lead 2026-09", "tieType": "appointment (advisory: Project Meridian co-lead)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-09-30", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v3)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-hegseth-meridian-luckey", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "APPOINTMENT (ADVISORY): Hegseth named Anduril founder Palmer Luckey a Project Meridian co-lead on 2026-09-30 (with Musk and Newt Gingrich). Pentagon CTO Emil Michael to CNBC on the conflict question: 'There's really nothing to see here.'", "citation": ["https://www.axios.com/2026/09/30/pentagon-hegseth-musk-gingrich-anduril", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/06/anduril-navy-submarine-shipyard-contract.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/hegseth-meridian-gingrich", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/pete-hegseth", "to": "node/newt-gingrich", "name": "Meridian co-lead 2026-09", "tieType": "appointment (advisory: Project Meridian co-lead)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-09-30", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v3)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-hegseth-meridian-gingrich", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "APPOINTMENT (ADVISORY): Hegseth named former House Speaker Newt Gingrich a Project Meridian co-lead on 2026-09-30. Gingrich's wife Callista is Trump's ambassador to Switzerland (separate edge).", "citation": ["https://www.axios.com/2026/09/30/pentagon-hegseth-musk-gingrich-anduril"]}, {"@id": "tie/callista-gingrich-switzerland", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/callista-gingrich", "name": "Amb. Switzerland 2025", "tieType": "appointment + family", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-09-18 ; 2025-10-23 - present", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v3)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-callista-gingrich-switzerland", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "APPOINTMENT+FAMILY: Callista Gingrich (wife of Newt Gingrich) confirmed in the Sep 18 2025 en-bloc vote and presented credentials as US Ambassador to Switzerland on Oct 23 2025 (also accredited to Liechtenstein). Confirmation vote per register row (Axios).", "citation": ["https://ch.usembassy.gov/ambassador-callista-l-gingrich-presents-her-credentials-to-swiss-president-karin-keller-sutter/"]}, {"@id": "tie/anduril-navy-2-9b-shipyard", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/us-navy", "to": "node/anduril", "name": "$2.9B sub contract 2026-10", "tieType": "government contract", "category": "contract", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-06", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v3)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-anduril-navy-2-9b-shipyard", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "CONTRACT: Navy awarded Anduril an up-to-$2.9B contract for Virginia-class submarine components (2026-10-06); Anduril is putting $3.7B into an Arsenal shipyard at Sparrows Point, MD. Trump called Luckey a 'friend' that afternoon. Six days after Luckey was named a Meridian co-lead: SEQUENCE ONLY, no causal link shown.", "citation": ["https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/06/anduril-navy-submarine-shipyard-contract.html", "https://defensescoop.com/2026/10/06/white-house-anduril-announce-new-shipyard-baltimore-county/"]}, {"@id": "tie/dpb-andreessen", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/pete-hegseth", "to": "node/marc-andreessen", "name": "Defense Policy Bd 2026-06", "tieType": "appointment (Defense Policy Board)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-06-29", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v3)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-dpb-andreessen", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "APPOINTMENT (ADVISORY BOARD): Hegseth named Marc Andreessen to the revived Defense Policy Board (chair Robert Lighthizer) on 2026-06-29. a16z's portfolio includes Anduril, SpaceX, xAI, OpenAI, Shield AI and others with DoD contracts (InsideDefense).", "citation": ["https://insidedefense.com/insider/pentagon-names-new-defense-policy-board-nearly-year-after-renewal", "https://archive.ph/6UYLt"]}, {"@id": "tie/thiel-masters-dpb", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/peter-thiel", "to": "node/blake-masters", "name": "Thiel Capital COO -> DPB 2026", "tieType": "employment -> appointment (Defense Policy Board)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "to 2022 ; 2026-06-29", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v3)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-thiel-masters-dpb", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "EMPLOYMENT->APPOINTMENT: Blake Masters, former COO of Thiel Capital and Trump-endorsed 2022 Arizona Senate candidate, was named to the Defense Policy Board by Hegseth on 2026-06-29.", "citation": ["https://insidedefense.com/insider/pentagon-names-new-defense-policy-board-nearly-year-after-renewal", "https://archive.ph/6UYLt"]}, {"@id": "tie/thrive-anduril-series-h", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/josh-kushner-thrive-capital", "to": "node/anduril", "name": "co-leads $5B @ $61B 2026-05", "tieType": "funding (co-lead $5B Series H)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-05-13", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v3)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-thrive-anduril-series-h", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "FUNDING: Thrive Capital (founded and ~66% owned by Josh Kushner, Jared Kushner's brother) co-led Anduril's $5B Series H at a $61B valuation with Andreessen Horowitz (2026-05-13), doubling the $30.5B 2025 valuation.", "citation": ["https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/13/anduril-raises-5b-doubles-valuation-to-61b/", "https://www.forbes.com/profile/josh-kushner/"]}, {"@id": "tie/a16z-anduril-series-h", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/andreessen-horowitz", "to": "node/anduril", "name": "co-leads $5B @ $61B 2026-05", "tieType": "funding (co-lead $5B Series H)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-05-13", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v3)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-a16z-anduril-series-h", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "FUNDING: Andreessen Horowitz co-led Anduril's $5B Series H at $61B (2026-05-13) with Thrive; six weeks later Andreessen joined the Defense Policy Board.", "citation": ["https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/13/anduril-raises-5b-doubles-valuation-to-61b/"]}, {"@id": "tie/andreessen-meta-board", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/marc-andreessen", "to": "node/meta", "name": "Meta director 2008-now", "tieType": "board", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2008-06 - present", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v3)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-andreessen-meta-board", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "BOARD: Marc Andreessen has been a Meta director since June 2008 (also Coinbase and Samsara boards), per Meta's governance page.", "citation": ["https://investor.atmeta.com/leadership-and-governance/default.aspx", "https://a16z.com/author/marc-andreessen/"]}, {"@id": "tie/powell-mccormick-meta", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/meta", "to": "node/dina-powell-mccormick", "name": "ex-Dep. NSA -> President 2026", "tieType": "employment (ex-Trump Deputy NSA -> Meta President)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-01-12 - present", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v3)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-powell-mccormick-meta", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "EMPLOYMENT: Dina Powell McCormick, Trump's former Deputy National Security Advisor and ex-Goldman partner (previously a Meta director), became Meta President and Vice Chairman on 2026-01-12, tasked with 'strategic capital partnerships' for Meta's AI build-out.", "citation": ["https://about.fb.com/news/2026/01/dina-powell-mccormick-joins-meta-as-president-and-vice-chairman/", "https://investor.atmeta.com/leadership-and-governance/default.aspx"]}, {"@id": "tie/charles-josh-kushner-family", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/charles-kushner", "to": "node/josh-kushner-thrive-capital", "name": "son (Thrive founder)", "tieType": "family (son)", "category": "family", "kind": "register", "date": "1985 (birth) ; Forbes 2026-09", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v3)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-charles-josh-kushner-family", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "FAMILY: Josh Kushner, founder of Thrive Capital ($65B+ AUM; backer of OpenAI, Stripe, Instagram), is the son of Ambassador Charles Kushner and brother of Jared Kushner (Forbes, updated Sep 15 2026).", "citation": ["https://www.forbes.com/profile/josh-kushner/"]}, {"@id": "tie/christie-prosecuted-charles-kushner", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/chris-christie", "to": "node/charles-kushner", "name": "prosecutes; plea 2004", "tieType": "prosecution (guilty plea)", "category": "pardon/settlement", "kind": "register", "date": "2004-08-18 ; 2005-03-04", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v3)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-christie-prosecuted-charles-kushner", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "PROSECUTION: Then-US Attorney Chris Christie announced Charles Kushner's guilty plea (2004-08-18) to 16 false-tax-return counts, retaliating against a cooperating witness (hiring a prostitute to seduce and film his brother-in-law, tape mailed to his sister) and false FEC statements; sentenced to 24 months (2005-03-04). Pardoned by Trump 2020 (existing edge).", "citation": ["https://www.justice.gov/archive/tax/usaopress/2004/txdv04kush0818_r.htm", "https://www.justice.gov/archive/tax/usaopress/2005/txdv05kush0304_r.htm"]}, {"@id": "tie/lunate-affinity", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/lunate-tahnoon", "to": "node/jared-kushner", "name": "LP ($1.5B w/ QIA 2024)", "tieType": "funding (LP stake)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2024 ; 2026", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v3)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-lunate-affinity", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "FUNDING: Abu Dhabi's Lunate (a fund Sheikh Tahnoon bin Zayed helps oversee; his Aryam bought 49% of WLF) and QIA added $1.5B to Kushner's Affinity in 2024 (Reuters, per register row); NYT (Oct 2026): Lunate is among Affinity's largest stakeholders, making Tahnoon 'effectively a business partner' of Kushner.", "citation": ["https://www.smh.com.au/world/europe/us-russia-talks-on-ukraine-now-involve-an-oil-deal-tied-to-trump-allies-20261004-p612ot.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/khayyat-kushner-albania", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/al-khayyat-brothers-qatar", "to": "node/jared-kushner", "name": "Albania resort partners 2025-26", "tieType": "business deal (Albania resort partnership)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2025 - 2026", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v3)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-khayyat-kushner-albania", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "BUSINESS: Qatari brothers Moutaz and Ramez Al-Khayyat (attended Trump's 2025 inauguration) partner with Jared Kushner and Ivanka Trump to finance a multibillion-dollar luxury resort in southern Albania; Ramez met Ivanka in Albania in 2026 (NYT). They are a major equity holder in the Boehly-led Lukoil bid.", "citation": ["https://www.smh.com.au/world/europe/us-russia-talks-on-ukraine-now-involve-an-oil-deal-tied-to-trump-allies-20261004-p612ot.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/putin-kremlin-kushner-lukoil", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/vladimir-putin", "to": "node/jared-kushner", "name": "Kremlin mtg; Lukoil pitch 2026-09", "tieType": "meeting + deal negotiation (Lukoil)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-09-05 ; 2026-10", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v3)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-putin-kremlin-kushner-lukoil", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "MEETING/DEAL: Putin raised a sale of Lukoil's ~$20B foreign assets when he met Kushner and Witkoff at the Kremlin on 2026-09-05 (NYT, three people familiar). A senior administration official confirmed on record that Kushner and Witkoff helped negotiate the US government's financial terms ('substantial upfront payment and profits interest'). No indication either profits (NYT).", "citation": ["https://www.smh.com.au/world/europe/us-russia-talks-on-ukraine-now-involve-an-oil-deal-tied-to-trump-allies-20261004-p612ot.html", "https://thehill.com/homenews/administration/6127449-trump-russia-ukraine-oil-deal-lukoil/"]}, {"@id": "tie/putin-kremlin-witkoff-lukoil", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/vladimir-putin", "to": "node/steve-witkoff", "name": "Kremlin mtg; Lukoil pitch 2026-09", "tieType": "meeting + deal negotiation (Lukoil)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-09-05 ; 2026-10", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v3)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-putin-kremlin-witkoff-lukoil", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "MEETING/DEAL: Same 2026-09-05 Kremlin meeting: Putin raised the Lukoil asset sale with envoy Witkoff (and Kushner). Witkoff's spokesperson: 'no conflict of interest and no financial stake in this matter.'", "citation": ["https://www.smh.com.au/world/europe/us-russia-talks-on-ukraine-now-involve-an-oil-deal-tied-to-trump-allies-20261004-p612ot.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/boehly-lukoil-consortium", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/todd-boehly", "to": "node/lukoil-international-assets", "name": "leads bid (+DFC, Qatar, UAE) pending", "tieType": "business deal (pending; needs OFAC)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-09 - 2026-10", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-24", "statusNote": "No OFAC action Nov 24 (index latest 20261123); GL 131L to Dec 19; sale not authorized.", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v3)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-24", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-boehly-lukoil-consortium", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "BUSINESS DEAL (PENDING): A consortium led by Trump donor Todd Boehly (Eldridge; Dodgers co-owner), with the Qatari Al-Khayyat brothers, Abu Dhabi royal-linked investors and the US DFC (~15% stake, no upfront cash), is the leading bidder for Lukoil's foreign fields, refineries and gas stations; Carlyle's earlier deal lapsed in July without OFAC approval. Not signed as of 2026-10-09.", "citation": ["https://www.smh.com.au/world/europe/us-russia-talks-on-ukraine-now-involve-an-oil-deal-tied-to-trump-allies-20261004-p612ot.html", "https://nypost.com/2026/10/09/us-news/trump-backed-lukoil-bid-aims-to-deliver-billions-to-us-treasury/", "https://www.privateequitywire.co.uk/carlyles-lukoil-oversees-assets-deal-expires/"]}, {"@id": "tie/boehly-trump-donations", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/todd-boehly", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "$2M (MAGA Inc + inaugural)", "tieType": "funding (super PAC + inaugural)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2024-12/2025-01 ; 2025-12", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v3)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-boehly-trump-donations", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "FUNDING: Boehly gave $1M to MAGA Inc. (Dec 2025) and $1M via Eldridge Industries to Trump's inauguration; $2M total to Trump's political causes (NYT).", "citation": ["https://www.smh.com.au/world/europe/us-russia-talks-on-ukraine-now-involve-an-oil-deal-tied-to-trump-allies-20261004-p612ot.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-putin-call-diesel-gl135", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/vladimir-putin", "name": "call + diesel GL 135 2026-10-09", "tieType": "call + sanctions licence (GL 135)", "category": "pardon/settlement", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-09", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v3)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-21", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-trump-putin-call-diesel-gl135", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "CALL + SANCTIONS RELIEF: Trump and Putin spoke 2026-10-09 (Kremlin statement: Russia 'willing to supply oil and petroleum products to the US market'); Treasury's OFAC issued General License 135 the same afternoon, temporarily authorizing Russian-origin diesel sales and imports through Apr 2027. Tonnages (300k t now ... 4M t) are Trump SAID only.", "citation": ["http://en.kremlin.ru/events/president/news/80960", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/09/trump-putin-russian-diesel-us-global-markets.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/kremlev-donjr-wedding", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/umar-kremlev", "to": "node/donald-trump-jr", "name": "pays wedding party 2026-05", "tieType": "gift (wedding celebrations; repayment SAID)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-05-22/24 ; SAID 2026-10-06", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-10-06", "statusNote": "Repayment SAID by Trump and Kremlev; no proof of repayment published (hole).", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v3)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-06", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-kremlev-donjr-wedding", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "GIFT/FUNDING: Putin-linked oligarch Umar Kremlev (IBA head; Order of Friendship 2026) paid hundreds of thousands of dollars for Donald Trump Jr.'s Bahamas wedding celebrations (private island, fireworks) via an IBA-linked Dubai entity (ProPublica, records); the couple confirmed it as a 'wedding gift'. Repayment: Trump SAID 'he paid them back'; Kremlev SAID 2026-10-06 'Yes, he did'; no proof shown (AP). Guests included Jared Kushner and WLF/1789 executives.", "citation": ["https://www.propublica.org/article/donald-trump-jr-wedding-bankrolled-russian-oligarch-umar-kremlev-putin", "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/nation/russian-oligarch-says-trump-jr-has-paid-him-back-for-wedding-celebration"]}, {"@id": "tie/donjr-bettina-marriage", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump-jr", "to": "node/bettina-anderson", "name": "marriage 2026-05", "tieType": "marriage/family", "category": "family", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-05-22", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v3)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-donjr-bettina-marriage", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "MARRIAGE: Donald Trump Jr. married socialite Bettina Anderson in a family-only ceremony in the Bahamas on 2026-05-22, followed by two nights of celebrations hosted by Umar Kremlev.", "citation": ["https://www.propublica.org/article/donald-trump-jr-wedding-bankrolled-russian-oligarch-umar-kremlev-putin", "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/nation/russian-oligarch-says-trump-jr-has-paid-him-back-for-wedding-celebration"]}, {"@id": "tie/cuellar-pardon", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/henry-cuellar", "name": "pardon 2025-12", "tieType": "pardon", "category": "pardon/settlement", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-12-03", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v3)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-cuellar-pardon", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "PARDON: Trump fully pardoned Rep. Henry Cuellar (D-TX) and his wife Imelda in their federal bribery/conspiracy case (Azerbaijan-controlled energy company and a Mexican bank; trial had been set for Apr 2026) on 2025-12-03, after a Nov 12 letter from their daughters; Trump: 'Henry, I don't know you'.", "citation": ["https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/trump-pardons-cuellar-in-bribery-and-conspiracy-case", "https://www.justice.gov/pardon/media/1419976/dl?inline="]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-v-irs-weaponization-fund", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/us-doj-acting-ag-blanche", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "settles: $1.776B fund 2026-05 (enjoined)", "tieType": "settlement (own government; $1.776B fund; enjoined)", "category": "pardon/settlement", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-05-18 ; 2026-06-12", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "enjoined", "statusDate": "2026-06-12", "statusNote": "Fund enjoined by EDVA (Brinkema); DOJ says 'not moving forward'; no binding closure statement found.", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v3)", "lastChecked": "2026-06-12", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-trump-v-irs-weaponization-fund", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SETTLEMENT: In Trump v. IRS (plaintiffs Trump, Don Jr., Eric Trump, Trump Org; suit over the tax-return leak, $10B sought), acting AG Todd Blanche's DOJ settled on 2026-05-18 by creating a $1.776B 'Anti-Weaponization Fund' from the Judgment Fund (plaintiffs: apology, no money). Blanche later told Congress it was 'not moving forward'; Judge Brinkema kept it enjoined on 2026-06-12, citing Trump's own statements that he still wanted it.", "citation": ["https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/justice-department-announces-anti-weaponization-fund", "https://rollcall.com/2026/06/12/court-extends-block-on-anti-weaponization-fund/"]}, {"@id": "tie/kotick-skydance-board", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/bobby-kotick", "to": "node/david-ellison", "name": "director 2026-10", "tieType": "board", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-04 (appointed) ; 2026-10-06 (effective)", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v3)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-powermap-v3-kotick-skydance-board", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "BOARD: Skydance (Ellison; now owner of CBS News + CNN) appointed ex-Activision CEO Bobby Kotick a director on 2026-10-04, effective at the WBD closing (SEC 8-K); Laurene Powell Jobs also joined; Tony Blair named board adviser (company release).", "citation": ["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2041610/000110465926114113/tm2626659d9_8k.htm", "https://www.skydance.com/news/press/skydance-announces-board-adding-ynon-kreiz-laurene-powell-jobs-and-bobby-kotick-as-directors-and-tony-blair-as-advisor"]}, {"@id": "tie/dmitriev-witkoff-miami-2025-10", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/kirill-dmitriev", "to": "node/steve-witkoff", "name": "meets x4+ 2025-26 (28-pt plan)", "tieType": "documented meetings (repeat)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-02-18 ; 2025-10-25/27 ; 2026-03-11 ; 2026-09-24", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-dmitriev-witkoff-miami-2025-10", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "MEETINGS: Sanctioned RDIF chief and Putin envoy Kirill Dmitriev met Witkoff repeatedly: Riyadh economic track Feb 18 2025 (Lavrov statement), Miami Oct 25-27 2025 (Reuters: produced the 28-point Ukraine plan; US issued a special waiver for his entry), Florida Mar 11 2026 (Witkoff statement). OUTCOME: 28-point plan published by Axios Nov 2025.", "citation": ["https://www.reuters.com/world/europe/trump-officials-meeting-with-russian-miami-spurs-questions-about-latest-ukraine-2025-11-22/", "https://www.reuters.com/world/us-russian-teams-met-florida-discussed-variety-topics-witkoff-says-2026-03-12/", "https://www.mid.ru/en/maps/us/1998294/"]}, {"@id": "tie/dmitriev-kushner-miami-kremlin", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/kirill-dmitriev", "to": "node/jared-kushner", "name": "meets Miami/Kremlin 2025", "tieType": "documented meetings (repeat)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-10 ; 2025-12-02 ; 2025-12-20", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-dmitriev-kushner-miami-kremlin", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "MEETINGS: Kushner attended the Oct 2025 Miami meeting with Dmitriev (Reuters), sat with Dmitriev and Witkoff at the Dec 2 2025 Kremlin meeting with Putin (Reuters/Sputnik pool photo), and Dmitriev flew to Miami to meet Witkoff and Kushner again Dec 20 2025.", "citation": ["https://www.reuters.com/world/europe/trump-officials-meeting-with-russian-miami-spurs-questions-about-latest-ukraine-2025-11-22/", "https://www.reuters.com/world/europe/russias-dmitriev-heading-us-meet-witkoff-kushner-source-says-2025-12-19/"]}, {"@id": "tie/dmitriev-gerson-plan-2016", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/kirill-dmitriev", "to": "node/rick-gerson", "name": "drafts 'reconciliation' plan 2016", "tieType": "collaboration (US-Russia 'reconciliation' plan)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2016-11 - 2017-01", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-dmitriev-gerson-plan-2016", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "TRANSITION BACK-CHANNEL: Mueller Report Vol. I: in Dec 2016-Jan 2017 Dmitriev and hedge-fund manager Rick Gerson drafted a short US-Russia reconciliation plan Dmitriev implied was cleared by Putin.", "citation": ["https://epic.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/Mueller-Report-vol-1.pdf", "https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/20/us/politics/trump-putin-russia-mueller.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/gerson-kushner-plan-2017", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/rick-gerson", "to": "node/jared-kushner", "name": "friend; hands plan 2017", "tieType": "friendship; passed document", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2017-01 (pre-inauguration)", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-gerson-kushner-plan-2017", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "CONTACT: Mueller Report: Gerson, 'a friend of Jared Kushner', gave the Dmitriev reconciliation plan to Kushner before the inauguration; Kushner gave copies to Bannon and Tillerson.", "citation": ["https://epic.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/Mueller-Report-vol-1.pdf", "https://www.washingtonpost.com/graphics/2019/politics/read-the-mueller-report/"]}, {"@id": "tie/dmitriev-prince-seychelles-2017", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/kirill-dmitriev", "to": "node/erik-prince", "name": "Seychelles mtgs 2017", "tieType": "documented meeting", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2017-01 (Seychelles, twice)", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-dmitriev-prince-seychelles-2017", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "reference", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "MEETING: Mueller Report: Dmitriev met Trump-campaign supporter Erik Prince twice in the Seychelles in Jan 2017 (arranged via George Nader) to discuss US-Russia relations.", "citation": ["https://epic.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/Mueller-Report-vol-1.pdf"]}, {"@id": "tie/uae-nsa-introduced-dmitriev-gerson", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/tahnoon-bin-zayed", "to": "node/kirill-dmitriev", "name": "introduces to Gerson 2016 (I)", "tieType": "introduction (UAE NSA)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2016-11", "grade": "I", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-I-uae-nsa-introduced-dmitriev-gerson", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "reference", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "INTRODUCTION (I): Mueller Report says 'the UAE national security adviser introduced Dmitriev to Rick Gerson' in late Nov 2016. The report does not print the name; Tahnoon bin Zayed held that office then. Identity is inference from the office, hence I.", "citation": ["https://www.openmuellerreport.org/person/richard-gerson", "https://epic.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/Mueller-Report-vol-1.pdf"]}, {"@id": "tie/putin-dmitriev-envoy-ofac", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/vladimir-putin", "to": "node/kirill-dmitriev", "name": "envoy; OFAC SDN 2022", "tieType": "appointment (special envoy) ; OFAC-designated", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2022-02-28 (SDN) ; 2025 (envoy)", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-putin-dmitriev-envoy-ofac", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "APPOINTMENT: Dmitriev is Putin's special presidential envoy for investment and economic cooperation and RDIF CEO. OFAC designated RDIF and Dmitriev on Feb 28 2022 (EO 14024); his US entries need waivers.", "citation": ["https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/jy0612", "https://tass.com/politics/2034787"]}, {"@id": "tie/ushakov-witkoff-call-2025-10-14", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/yuri-ushakov", "to": "node/steve-witkoff", "name": "Oct 14 2025 call (recorded)", "tieType": "documented contact (call recording) + meetings", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-02-18 ; 2025-10-14", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-ushakov-witkoff-call-2025-10-14", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "CONTACT: Bloomberg reviewed a recording of an Oct 14 2025 Witkoff-Ushakov call in which Witkoff coached Putin's top foreign-policy aide on pitching Trump (praise the Gaza deal, a '20-point' plan; 'Donetsk and maybe a land swap'). They also met at Riyadh Feb 18 2025. OUTCOME: Trump-Putin call followed on Oct 16 2025; the 28-point plan later emerged.", "citation": ["https://apnews.com/article/trump-witkoff-putin-ukraine-bloomberg-3844a3721d92dd9ae9681547a0814d88", "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2025-11-25/witkoff-discusses-ukraine-plans-with-key-putin-aide-transcript", "https://www.state.gov/secretary-rubios-meeting-with-russian-foreign-minister-lavrov"]}, {"@id": "tie/putin-ushakov-aide", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/vladimir-putin", "to": "node/yuri-ushakov", "name": "aide (foreign policy)", "tieType": "employment (presidential aide)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2012 - present", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-putin-ushakov-aide", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "EMPLOYMENT: Ushakov is Aide to the President of Russia (foreign policy); he joined Lavrov at Riyadh and reads out the Trump-Putin calls (State Dept readout; Kremlin).", "citation": ["https://www.state.gov/secretary-rubios-meeting-with-russian-foreign-minister-lavrov", "http://kremlin.ru/events/president/news/80961"]}, {"@id": "tie/rubio-lavrov-riyadh-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/marco-rubio", "to": "node/sergey-lavrov", "name": "Riyadh 2025-02-18", "tieType": "documented meeting", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-02-18", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-rubio-lavrov-riyadh-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "MEETING: Rubio (with Waltz, Witkoff) met Lavrov (with Ushakov) at Diriyah Palace, Riyadh, Feb 18 2025, hosted by MBS. OUTCOME: agreed to restore missions, name high-level teams, explore economic cooperation incl. energy.", "citation": ["https://www.state.gov/secretary-rubios-meeting-with-russian-foreign-minister-lavrov", "https://mid.ru/en/foreign_policy/news/1998279/"]}, {"@id": "tie/putin-novak-deputy-pm", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/vladimir-putin", "to": "node/alexander-novak", "name": "Deputy PM 2024", "tieType": "appointment (Deputy PM, energy + economy)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2024-05-14", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-putin-novak-deputy-pm", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "APPOINTMENT: Putin's decree of May 14 2024 reappointed Novak Deputy Prime Minister (energy; expanded to economic policy/sanctions mitigation). Novak announced the Oct-Dec 2026 diesel export schedule (register).", "citation": ["http://en.kremlin.ru/events/president/news/74028", "https://www.reuters.com/world/europe/russian-deputy-pm-given-new-tasks-coordination-economy-2024-05-17/"]}, {"@id": "tie/bessent-treasury-ofac-smith", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/scott-bessent", "to": "node/bradley-t-smith", "name": "OFAC director", "tieType": "employment (OFAC director under Treasury)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2023-09 - present", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-bessent-treasury-ofac-smith", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "EMPLOYMENT: Bradley T. Smith, career official (OFAC chief counsel 2013, deputy 2018, director Sep 2023; acting TFI under secretary Aug 2024), still signs OFAC general licenses as Director under Bessent's Treasury (e.g. ICCSR GL 10, Sep 4 2025).", "citation": ["https://ofac.treasury.gov/media/934606/download?inline=", "https://www.reuters.com/markets/us/us-treasury-names-acting-senior-sanctions-official-2024-08-02/"]}, {"@id": "tie/umerov-witkoff-kushner-miami", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/rustem-umerov", "to": "node/steve-witkoff-jared-kushner", "name": "Miami talks 2025-26", "tieType": "documented meetings (repeat)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-12-05 ; 2026-10-09", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-umerov-witkoff-kushner-miami", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "MEETINGS: Ukraine's NSDC secretary Umerov met Witkoff in Miami (Dec 2025) and leads Kyiv's delegation (with Budanov, Arakhamia, Kyslytsya) meeting Witkoff and Kushner in Miami on Oct 9 2026.", "citation": ["https://www.reuters.com/world/europe/witkoff-ukraines-umerov-meeting-again-miami-friday-2025-12-05/", "https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/witkoff-kushner-to-meet-ukrainians-in-miami-on-friday-says-us-source"]}, {"@id": "tie/driscoll-vance-classmate-envoy", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jd-vance", "to": "node/dan-driscoll", "name": "Yale Law friend -> Ukraine envoy", "tieType": "friendship (Yale Law classmates) -> appointment", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-02 - 2026-08-31", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-driscoll-vance-classmate-envoy", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "PERSONAL->APPOINTMENT: Army Secretary Dan Driscoll, Vance's Yale Law classmate and close friend, was sent by Trump to Kyiv, Geneva and Abu Dhabi (talks with Russians) in Nov 2025. Resigned Aug 31 2026 (register).", "citation": ["https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/national-security/drone-guy-ukraine-peace-negotiator-dan-driscoll-rcna246086", "https://www.politico.com/news/2025/11/21/dan-driscoll-army-secretary-trump-administration-prominence-00663917"]}, {"@id": "tie/araghchi-witkoff-oman-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/abbas-araghchi", "to": "node/steve-witkoff", "name": "Oman/Rome talks 2025", "tieType": "documented meetings (repeat)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-04-12 ; 2025-04-19 ; 2025-04-26", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-araghchi-witkoff-oman-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "MEETINGS: Iranian FM Araghchi and Witkoff held Oman-mediated nuclear talks (Muscat Apr 12, brief face-to-face; Rome Apr 19; Muscat Apr 26 2025).", "citation": ["https://apnews.com/article/iran-us-nuclear-talks-oman-3aaca426accb6e450fef6395cc5de909"]}, {"@id": "tie/ghalibaf-vance-islamabad-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/mohammad-bagher-ghalibaf", "to": "node/jd-vance", "name": "Islamabad talks 2026-04", "tieType": "documented meeting (Islamabad talks)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-04", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-ghalibaf-vance-islamabad-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "MEETING: Vance led the US team (with Witkoff, Kushner) in ~21-hour Pakistan-mediated talks in Islamabad with Iran's Speaker Ghalibaf and FM Araghchi. OUTCOME: no agreement (Vance); later 'Islamabad MoU' status disputed (register).", "citation": ["https://abcnews.com/Politics/high-stakes-us-iran-peace-talks-led-vance/story?id=131924414", "https://mofa.gov.pk/press-releases/arrival-of-the-us-delegation-for-islamabad-talks"]}, {"@id": "tie/khamenei-mojtaba-son-ofac", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/ali-khamenei", "to": "node/mojtaba-khamenei", "name": "son; successor 2026", "tieType": "family (son) ; successor", "category": "family", "kind": "register", "date": "2019-11-04 (SDN) ; 2026-03-08 (elected)", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-khamenei-mojtaba-son-ofac", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "FAMILY: Mojtaba is Ali Khamenei's second son; OFAC designated him Nov 4 2019 for acting for the Supreme Leader with IRGC-QF/Basij. Elected Supreme Leader by the Assembly of Experts Mar 8 2026 (Reuters, register).", "citation": ["https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/sm824"]}, {"@id": "tie/abdulmalik-houthi-leader", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/abdul-malik-al-houthi", "to": "node/houthis-ansar-allah", "name": "leader (UN/OFAC 2015)", "tieType": "leadership ; UN/OFAC sanctions", "category": "pardon/settlement", "kind": "register", "date": "2015-04-14", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-abdulmalik-houthi-leader", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "LEADERSHIP: Abdul-Malik al-Houthi leads Ansar Allah; UN 2140 committee and OFAC (EO 13611) designated him Apr 14 2015; SDGT Jan 2021, revoked Feb 2021, Yemen listing remains.", "citation": ["https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/sanctions/2140/materials/summaries/individual/abdulmalik-al-houthi", "https://ofac.treasury.gov/recent-actions/20150414_33"]}, {"@id": "tie/tahnoon-trump-wh-2025-03", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/tahnoon-bin-zayed", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "WH mtg 2025-03-18", "tieType": "documented meeting (White House)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-03-18", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-tahnoon-trump-wh-2025-03", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "MEETING: Trump received UAE NSA Tahnoon bin Zayed (MGX chair) at the White House Mar 18 2025 (WH statement); dinner with senior officials. Ten months later WSJ reported his Aryam's 49% WLF stake (existing edge).", "citation": ["https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/statement-the-presidents-meeting-with-national-security-adviser-tahnoon-bin-zayed-al", "https://www.mediaoffice.abudhabi/en/government-affairs/tahnoon-bin-zayed-meets-donald-trump-discusses-strategic-partnership-prospects/"]}, {"@id": "tie/tahnoon-controls-aryam", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/tahnoon-bin-zayed", "to": "node/aryam-tahnoon", "name": "backs", "tieType": "control (backer)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-01", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-tahnoon-controls-aryam", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "CONTROL: WSJ: Aryam, the buyer of 49% of WLF, is backed by Sheikh Tahnoon bin Zayed, UAE national security adviser and brother of President MBZ.", "citation": ["https://www.theblock.co/news/deals/2026-02-01-uae-sheikh-secretly-acquired-49-of-trumps-world-liberty-financial-days-before-inauguration-wsj-387931"]}, {"@id": "tie/mbz-tahnoon-brothers", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/mohamed-bin-zayed", "to": "node/tahnoon-bin-zayed", "name": "brothers", "tieType": "family (brothers)", "category": "family", "kind": "register", "date": "-", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-mbz-tahnoon-brothers", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "FAMILY: Tahnoon is the brother of UAE President Mohamed bin Zayed (WSJ via The Block).", "citation": ["https://www.theblock.co/news/deals/2026-02-01-uae-sheikh-secretly-acquired-49-of-trumps-world-liberty-financial-days-before-inauguration-wsj-387931"]}, {"@id": "tie/mbz-trump-abu-dhabi-2025-05", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/mohamed-bin-zayed", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "state visit; $200B 2025-05", "tieType": "documented meeting (state visit) ; deals", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-05-15", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-mbz-trump-abu-dhabi-2025-05", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "MEETING: MBZ received Trump at Qasr Al Watan May 15 2025. OUTCOME: WH fact sheet: $200B new deals, $1.4T 10-year UAE investment pledge accelerated, AI campus partnership.", "citation": ["https://www.whitehouse.gov/fact-sheets/2025/05/fact-sheet-president-donald-j-trump-secures-200-billion-in-new-u-s-uae-deals-and-accelerates-previously-committed-1-4-trillion-uae-investment/", "https://www.mohamedbinzayed.ae/en/latest-news-listing/2025/05/UAE-President-receives-US-President-Trump-in-official-ceremony-at-Qasr-Al-Watan"]}, {"@id": "tie/althani-witkoff-kushner-gaza", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/mohammed-bin-abdulrahman-al-thani", "to": "node/steve-witkoff-jared-kushner", "name": "Gaza mediation 2025-10", "tieType": "mediation (repeat meetings)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-10", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-althani-witkoff-kushner-gaza", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "MEDIATION: Qatar's PM/FM Mohammed bin Abdulrahman Al Thani mediated the Oct 2025 Gaza ceasefire with Witkoff and Kushner. OUTCOME: Sharm el-Sheikh declaration Oct 13 2025, signed by Trump, Sisi, Emir Tamim, Erdogan.", "citation": ["https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/israel-hamas-ceasefire-deal-came-together-rcna236789", "https://www.cnn.com/2025/10/19/politics/how-qatar-became-trumps-key-ally-in-his-middle-east-peace-efforts"]}, {"@id": "tie/dermer-netanyahu", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/benjamin-netanyahu", "to": "node/ron-dermer", "name": "minister/envoy", "tieType": "appointment (minister ; special envoy)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2022-12 - 2025-11-11", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-dermer-netanyahu", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "APPOINTMENT: Netanyahu confidant Ron Dermer was Strategic Affairs Minister until he resigned Nov 11 2025 after the Gaza deal. He stays a Netanyahu envoy on Abraham Accords expansion.", "citation": ["https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/israeli-minister-strategic-affairs-ron-dermer-has-resigned-israeli-media-reports-2025-11-11/", "https://www.thenationalnews.com/news/mena/2025/11/12/ron-dermer-israeli-strategic-affairs-minister-and-netanyahu-confidant-resigns/"]}, {"@id": "tie/blanche-maxwell-proffer-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/todd-blanche", "to": "node/ghislaine-maxwell", "name": "DAG proffer 2025-07", "tieType": "documented meeting (DOJ proffer)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-07-24/25", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-27", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-blanche-maxwell-proffer-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "MEETING: Then-Deputy AG Todd Blanche, formerly Trump's personal criminal lawyer, interviewed Maxwell at FCI Tallahassee Jul 24-25 2025 (DOJ released the transcript). OUTCOME: she was moved soon after to minimum-security FPC Bryan, TX. DOJ says no benefit was promised (Whitehouse letter disputes the transfer).", "citation": ["https://www.justice.gov/storage/audio-files/Interview%20Transcript/Interview%20Transcript%20-%20Maxwell%202025.07.24%20(Redacted).pdf", "https://www.whitehouse.senate.gov/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/2025-08-07-Letter-to-BOP-Maxwell-Transfer.pdf"]}, {"@id": "tie/epstein-beck-fec-2014", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jeffrey-epstein", "to": "node/gwendolyn-beck", "name": "$12.6K via PACs 2014", "tieType": "funding (campaign, via PACs)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2014", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-epstein-beck-fec-2014", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "FUNDING: Epstein gave $12,600 to Gwendolyn Beck's 2014 independent VA-8 campaign and related PACs: $5,000 each to CIVIC and Eagles Party PAC, each followed by $2,600 to Beck's committee. FEC ADR found a de minimis limit violation (letter to Epstein lawyer Darren Indyke).", "citation": ["https://www.fec.gov/files/legal/adrs/780/15190301971.pdf", "https://www.arlnow.com/2015/01/08/why-did-the-infamous-jeffrey-epstein-give-generously-to-a-long-shot-local-congressional-campaign/"]}, {"@id": "tie/epstein-npa-kellen-groff", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jeffrey-epstein", "to": "node/sarah-kellen-lesley-groff", "name": "NPA co-conspirators 2007", "tieType": "employment ; named potential co-conspirators (NPA)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2007-09-24", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-epstein-npa-kellen-groff", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "NPA: The 2007 federal non-prosecution agreement names Sarah Kellen, Lesley Groff, Adriana Ross and Nadia Marcinkova as potential co-conspirators the US will not charge (DOJ OPR report 2020).", "citation": ["https://www.justice.gov/opr/page/file/1336471/dl", "https://reason.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/Non-Prosecution-Agreement-1433.pdf"]}, {"@id": "tie/epstein-brunel-mc2", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jeffrey-epstein", "to": "node/jean-luc-brunel", "name": "MC2 backer", "tieType": "business (MC2 co-founder/financing)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "~2005 - 2015 ; d. 2022-02-19", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-epstein-brunel-mc2", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "BUSINESS: French model agent Jean-Luc Brunel founded MC2 Model Management in the US with Epstein's backing ($1M credit line per reporting); found dead in La Sante prison Feb 19 2022 while charged with rape of minors.", "citation": ["https://www.reuters.com/world/europe/french-modelling-agent-who-founded-agency-with-epstein-dies-custody-2022-02-19/", "https://www.bbc.com/news/world-europe-60443518"]}, {"@id": "tie/epstein-staley-fca", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jes-staley", "to": "node/jeffrey-epstein", "name": "banker; FCA ban upheld 2025", "tieType": "banker-client relationship ; regulatory finding", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2000 - 2015 ; ban upheld 2025-06-26", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-epstein-staley-fca", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "BANKER/FINDING: UK Upper Tribunal (Jun 26 2025) upheld the FCA ban on ex-JPMorgan/Barclays CEO Jes Staley: he recklessly approved misleading statements about his Epstein relationship; fine cut to GBP 1.1M.", "citation": ["https://www.fca.org.uk/news/press-releases/upper-tribunal-upholds-jes-staley-ban", "https://www.reuters.com/sustainability/boards-policy-regulation/ex-barclays-ceo-staley-loses-appeal-against-uk-ban-over-epstein-ties-2025-06-26/"]}, {"@id": "tie/black-epstein-158m", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/leon-black", "to": "node/jeffrey-epstein", "name": "$158-170M 2012-17", "tieType": "funding ($158M-$170M fees)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2012 - 2017", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-black-epstein-158m", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "FUNDING: Apollo's Dechert review found Leon Black paid Epstein $158M (2012-17) for 'tax/estate advice'. Senate Finance (Wyden) puts it at ~$170M and says it funded Epstein's USVI operations.", "citation": ["https://www.finance.senate.gov/chairmans-news/wyden-unveils-ongoing-investigation-into-private-equity-billionaire-leon-blacks-tax-planning-and-financial-ties-with-jeffrey-epstein", "https://www.finance.senate.gov/ranking-members-news/wyden-releases-new-information-on-financing-of-jeffrey-epsteins-operations-by-billionaire-leon-black-seeks-documents-from-trump-administration"]}, {"@id": "tie/wexner-epstein-poa", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/les-wexner", "to": "node/jeffrey-epstein", "name": "power of attorney 1991-2007", "tieType": "power of attorney (1991-2007)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "1991 - 2007-09", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-wexner-epstein-poa", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "POWER OF ATTORNEY: Wexner gave Epstein power of attorney in 1991 and says he revoked it in Sep 2007 (House Oversight deposition statement, Feb 18 2026).", "citation": ["https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/billionaire-les-wexner-is-being-deposed-in-the-epstein-files-probe-heres-what-documents-show-about-their-relationship", "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/billionaire-les-wexner-tells-lawmakers-was-conned-jeffrey-epstein-noth-rcna259573"]}, {"@id": "tie/khanna-massie-efta", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/ro-khanna", "to": "node/thomas-massie", "name": "EFTA co-sponsors 2025", "tieType": "co-sponsors (Epstein Files Transparency Act)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-07 - 2025-11-19", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-khanna-massie-efta", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "LEGISLATION: H.R.4405, introduced by Khanna and co-led by Massie (discharge petition), passed the House 427-1 and was signed Nov 19 2025 (P.L. 119-38). It binds DOJ (Bondi/Blanche) to release Epstein files.", "citation": ["https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/4405/history", "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefings-statements/2025/11/congressional-bill-h-r-4405-signed-into-law/"]}, {"@id": "tie/adelson-preserve-america-100m", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/miriam-adelson", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "$100M+ super PAC 2024", "tieType": "funding ($100M+ super PAC)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2024-07 - 2024-10", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v4)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v4-V-adelson-preserve-america-100m", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "FUNDING: FEC Schedule A: Miriam Adelson gave ~$100M (plus ~$6M in Oct) to pro-Trump Preserve America PAC in 2024.", "citation": ["https://docquery.fec.gov/cgi-bin/forms/C00878801/1827526/sa/11AI", "https://www.opensecrets.org/political-action-committees-pacs/preserve-america-pac/C00878801/donors/2024"]}, {"@id": "tie/smith-signed-gl135", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/bradley-t-smith", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "signs GL 135 2 min before post", "tieType": "signature (OFAC GL 135) sequenced with Trump post", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-09 14:43:59 ET", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": true, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v5)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v5-V-smith-signed-gl135", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "SIGNATURE: OFAC Russia-related GL 135 (Russian-origin diesel sale/import, incl. into the US, to Apr 7 2027; no debits to CBR/NWF/MinFin accounts) is digitally signed by Director Bradley T. Smith at 14:43:59 -04:00 on Oct 9 2026. That is ~2 minutes before Trump's 2:46pm ET Truth Social diesel post. Who cleared it above Smith is not shown (hole stays open for clearance).", "citation": ["https://ofac.treasury.gov/media/937216/download?inline=", "https://ofac.treasury.gov/recent-actions/20261009_33"]}, {"@id": "tie/ellison-trump-stargate", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/larry-ellison", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "Stargate WH 2025-01-21", "tieType": "documented meeting (WH announcement) ; business", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-01-21", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v5)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v5-V-ellison-trump-stargate", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "WH EVENT: Trump announced Stargate in the Roosevelt Room on Jan 21 2025 with Oracle chairman Larry Ellison, Masayoshi Son and Sam Altman. Initial equity funders: SoftBank, OpenAI, Oracle and MGX (Tahnoon-chaired).", "citation": ["https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/remarks-artificial-intelligence-infrastructure-development-and-exchange-with-reporters", "https://openai.com/index/announcing-the-stargate-project/"]}, {"@id": "tie/stargate-oracle-mgx", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/larry-ellison", "to": "node/mgx-abu-dhabi-binance", "name": "Stargate co-funders", "tieType": "co-investors (Stargate equity)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-01-21", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v5)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v5-V-stargate-oracle-mgx", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "CO-INVESTMENT: OpenAI: the initial Stargate equity funders are SoftBank, OpenAI, Oracle (Ellison) and MGX (Abu Dhabi, chaired by Tahnoon).", "citation": ["https://openai.com/index/announcing-the-stargate-project/"]}, {"@id": "tie/sacks-trump-fundraiser-2024", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/david-sacks", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "hosts $12M fundraiser 2024-06", "tieType": "fundraiser host ($12M)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2024-06-06", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v5)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v5-V-sacks-trump-fundraiser-2024", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "FUNDRAISER: Sacks (with wife Jacqueline and Chamath Palihapitiya) hosted Trump at his Pacific Heights home on Jun 6 2024. It raised ~$12M (top tickets $500K/couple); Trump pitched himself as the 'crypto president'. Sacks later became the AI/crypto czar.", "citation": ["https://www.reuters.com/world/us/trump-liberal-san-francisco-high-dollar-tech-fundraiser-2024-06-06/", "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/trump-pitches-himself-crypto-president-san-francisco-tech-fundraiser-2024-06-07/"]}, {"@id": "tie/chamath-sacks-fundraiser", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/chamath-palihapitiya", "to": "node/david-sacks", "name": "co-host (All-In)", "tieType": "co-host (All-In; Trump fundraiser)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2024-06-06", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v5)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v5-V-chamath-sacks-fundraiser", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "CO-HOST: Palihapitiya co-hosted the Jun 6 2024 Trump fundraiser with Sacks; both co-host the All-In podcast.", "citation": ["https://www.reuters.com/world/us/two-tech-investors-host-trump-june-san-francisco-fundraiser-2024-05-22/"]}, {"@id": "tie/musk-america-pac-239m", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/elon-musk", "to": "node/america-pac", "name": "$238.5M 2024", "tieType": "funding (~$239M)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2024-06 - 2024-11-25", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v5)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v5-V-musk-america-pac-239m", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "FUNDING: FEC Schedule A: Musk's contributions to America PAC aggregate $238.5M by Nov 25 2024. The PAC reported $261.3M in total 2024 disbursements (final Form 3X).", "citation": ["https://docquery.fec.gov/cgi-bin/forms/C00879510/1858330/sa/ALL", "https://docquery.fec.gov/cgi-bin/forms/C00879510/1872971/"]}, {"@id": "tie/lonsdale-america-pac-1m", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/joe-lonsdale", "to": "node/america-pac", "name": "$1M 2024-06", "tieType": "funding ($1M)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2024-06-07", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v5)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v5-V-lonsdale-america-pac-1m", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "FUNDING: FEC Schedule A: Lonsdale Enterprises Inc. gave $1M to America PAC on Jun 7 2024 (an early backer of Musk's PAC).", "citation": ["https://docquery.fec.gov/cgi-bin/forms/C00879510/1801554/sa/ALL", "https://www.opensecrets.org/political-action-committees-pacs/america-pac-texas/C00879510/donors/2024"]}, {"@id": "tie/america-pac-trump", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/america-pac", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "~$155M pro-Trump IE", "tieType": "independent expenditures (pro-Trump)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2024", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v5)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v5-V-america-pac-trump", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "SPENDING: America PAC spent ~$155-157M directly supporting Trump / opposing Harris in 2024 (NBC/BI from FEC).", "citation": ["https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/elon-musk-spent-quarter-billion-dollars-electing-trump-financing-myste-rcna182922"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-warsh-fed-chair", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/kevin-warsh", "name": "Fed chair nom 2026-01", "tieType": "nomination (Fed chair)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-01-30", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "changed", "statusDate": "2026-05-13", "statusNote": "Nomination confirmed 54-45 (roll call 120); Warsh succeeded Powell as Fed chair; still in post Oct 2026.", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v5)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-16", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v5-V-trump-warsh-fed-chair", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "NOMINATION: Trump picked Kevin Warsh to succeed Powell as Fed chair on Jan 30 2026.", "citation": ["https://apnews.com/article/kevin-warsh-federal-reserve-chair-48dcd3a768960eabb4e52183fa897aa1", "https://jewishinsider.com/2026/01/kevin-warsh-federal-reserve-trump-ron-lauder/"]}, {"@id": "tie/lauder-warsh-family", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/ronald-lauder", "to": "node/kevin-warsh", "name": "father-in-law", "tieType": "family (father-in-law)", "category": "family", "kind": "register", "date": "-", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v5)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v5-V-lauder-warsh-family", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "FAMILY: Warsh is married to Jane Lauder, daughter of Ronald Lauder (AP).", "citation": ["https://apnews.com/article/kevin-warsh-federal-reserve-chair-48dcd3a768960eabb4e52183fa897aa1"]}, {"@id": "tie/lauder-trump-friend", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/ronald-lauder", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "Wharton friend; donor", "tieType": "friendship (Wharton) ; donor", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "1960s - present", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v5)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v5-V-lauder-trump-friend", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "PERSONAL: Ronald Lauder has known Trump since Wharton (Penn) and is a close friend, confidant and major GOP donor (Politico 2017; Fortune 2026).", "citation": ["https://www.politico.com/story/2017/09/20/federal-reserve-chair-warsh-kevin-242901", "https://fortune.com/2026/01/30/who-is-kevin-warsh-new-fed-chair-ronald-lauder-president-trump-greenland-college-friends/"]}, {"@id": "tie/bondi-ballard-qatar-fara", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/pam-bondi", "to": "node/qatar-embassy-via-ballard-partners", "name": "FARA agent 2019-20", "tieType": "foreign agent (FARA) ; employment", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2019-07 - 2020", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v5)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v5-V-bondi-ballard-qatar-fara", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "FARA: Ballard Partners (reg. 6415) added Pamela Bondi in Jul 2019 as Key Personnel on its Qatar Embassy contract (anti-trafficking; political activity checked). Fee to the firm was $115K/month Jul 2019-Jun 2020, then $50K/month to Dec 2020. Bondi says the fee went to the firm, not her.", "citation": ["https://efile.fara.gov/docs/6415-Short-Form-20190723-106.pdf", "https://efile.fara.gov/docs/6415-Exhibit-AB-20190723-16.pdf"]}, {"@id": "tie/doj-fbi-epstein-memo-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/pam-bondi", "to": "node/kash-patel-dan-bongino", "name": "Epstein memo 2025-07-07", "tieType": "joint DOJ-FBI memo (Epstein) ; internal clash", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-07-07", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v5)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v5-V-doj-fbi-epstein-memo-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "MEMO: The unsigned DOJ-FBI memo of Jul 7 2025 found no 'client list', no credible blackmail evidence and no basis to charge third parties, and ruled out further disclosure. It contradicted Bondi's earlier 'on my desk' remark. Patel and Bongino backed it, then Bongino clashed with Bondi (AP). OUTCOME: the backlash fed the EFTA (signed Nov 19 2025).", "citation": ["https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/25993306-doj-epstein-july-2025-memo/", "https://apnews.com/article/epstein-files-dan-bongino-bondi-trump-fbi-0f02f67b6c97fc50e4d93bc4dbf4c4d0"]}, {"@id": "tie/bondi-halligan-appointment", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/pam-bondi", "to": "node/lindsey-halligan", "name": "installs; ruled invalid 2025-11", "tieType": "appointment (interim US Attorney EDVA) -> ruled invalid", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-09 ; 2025-11-24", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v5)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v5-V-bondi-halligan-appointment", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "APPOINTMENT: Bondi installed ex-WH aide Lindsey Halligan as interim US Attorney (EDVA) days before Halligan alone obtained the Comey indictment (Sep 25 2025) and the Letitia James indictment. On Nov 24 2025 Judge Currie ruled the appointment invalid (28 USC 546) and dismissed both without prejudice; DOJ appealed.", "citation": ["https://levin-center.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/2025-11-24-Opinion-and-Order-Granting-Motion-to-Dismiss-Indictment.pdf", "https://www.congress.gov/crs_external_products/LSB/PDF/LSB11380/LSB11380.1.pdf"]}, {"@id": "tie/khalid-bin-salman-hegseth", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/khalid-bin-salman", "to": "node/pete-hegseth", "name": "Pentagon 2025-02-24", "tieType": "documented meeting (Pentagon)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-02-24", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v5)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v5-V-khalid-bin-salman-hegseth", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "MEETING: Saudi Defense Minister Khalid bin Salman (MBS's brother) met Hegseth at the Pentagon Feb 24 2025 (Iran and the Houthis on the agenda; DoD transcript).", "citation": ["https://www.defense.gov/News/Transcripts/Transcript/Article/4077391/secretary-of-defense-pete-hegseth-greets-saudi-minister-of-defense-his-royal-hi/", "https://www.reuters.com/world/saudi-defence-minister-us-defense-secretary-discuss-cooperation-washington-2025-02-25/"]}, {"@id": "tie/faisal-riyadh-host-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/faisal-bin-farhan", "to": "node/marco-rubio", "name": "Riyadh host 2025-02-18", "tieType": "documented meeting (host, Riyadh US-Russia talks)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-02-18", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v5)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v5-V-faisal-riyadh-host-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "MEETING: Saudi FM Faisal bin Farhan and NSA Mosaad Al-Aiban sat with Rubio, Waltz, Witkoff, Lavrov and Ushakov at Diriyah Palace on Feb 18 2025 (AP pool photo, US Embassy).", "citation": ["https://ru.usembassy.gov/secretary-rubios-meeting-with-russian-foreign-minister-lavrov/", "https://apnews.com/article/russia-ukraine-war-riyadh-talks-trump-putin-rubio-0c3beebfef5839e9d509ff58239a6bc5"]}, {"@id": "tie/budanov-zelensky-chief", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/volodymyr-zelensky", "to": "node/kyrylo-budanov", "name": "chief of staff 2026-01", "tieType": "appointment (Head of Presidential Office)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-01-02", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v5)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v5-V-budanov-zelensky-chief", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "APPOINTMENT: Zelensky named military-intelligence chief Kyrylo Budanov head of the Presidential Office on Jan 2 2026, replacing Yermak.", "citation": ["https://www.ukrinform.net/rubric-polytics/4076184-budanov-officially-appointed-head-of-presidential-office-ivashchenko-takes-over-gur.html", "https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2026/01/02/kyrylo-budanov-zelensky-top-aide-ukraine/"]}, {"@id": "tie/budanov-arakhamia-miami", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/kyrylo-budanov-davyd-arakhamia", "to": "node/steve-witkoff-jared-kushner", "name": "Miami talks 2026", "tieType": "documented meetings (Miami)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-01 ; 2026-10-09", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v5)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v5-V-budanov-arakhamia-miami", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "MEETINGS: Budanov and Arakhamia (with Umerov) led Ukraine's delegations to Miami in Jan 2026 and Oct 9 2026 to meet Witkoff and Kushner.", "citation": ["https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/witkoff-kushner-to-meet-ukrainians-in-miami-on-friday-says-us-source", "https://censor.net/en/news/4027452/arakhamia-umerov-and-budanov-will-hold-talks-in-miami"]}, {"@id": "tie/mojtaba-vahidi-irgc", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/mojtaba-khamenei", "to": "node/ahmad-vahidi", "name": "appoints IRGC chief", "tieType": "appointment (IRGC commander-in-chief)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-03-01 ; 2026-08-10", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v5)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v5-V-mojtaba-vahidi-irgc", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "APPOINTMENT: Ahmad Vahidi became IRGC commander-in-chief on Mar 1 2026 after Pakpour's death. Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei confirmed and promoted him to major general on Aug 10 2026.", "citation": ["https://www.iranintl.com/en/202603010960", "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/8/11/whats-behind-irans-new-military-appointments-and-what-do-they-indicate"]}, {"@id": "tie/vahidi-irgc", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/ahmad-vahidi", "to": "node/irgc", "name": "commands", "tieType": "command", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-03-01 - present", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v5)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v5-V-vahidi-irgc", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "COMMAND: Vahidi commands the IRGC (Mehr; Iran International).", "citation": ["https://en.mehrnews.com/news/242266/General-Vahidi-appointed-IRGC-s-new-commander"]}, {"@id": "tie/epstein-npa-marcinkova-ross", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jeffrey-epstein", "to": "node/nadia-marcinkova-adriana-ross", "name": "NPA co-conspirators 2007", "tieType": "employment ; named potential co-conspirators (NPA)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2007-09-24", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v5)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v5-V-epstein-npa-marcinkova-ross", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "NPA: The 2007 non-prosecution agreement also names Nadia Marcinkova and Adriana Ross (with Kellen and Groff) as potential co-conspirators the US will not charge.", "citation": ["https://reason.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/Non-Prosecution-Agreement-1433.pdf", "https://www.justice.gov/opr/page/file/1336471/dl"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-hassett-nec", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/kevin-hassett", "name": "NEC director", "tieType": "appointment (NEC director)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2024-11-26 ; 2025-01", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v5)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v5-V-trump-hassett-nec", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "APPOINTMENT: Trump named Kevin Hassett director of the National Economic Council (announced Nov 26 2024).", "citation": ["https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/statement-president-elect-donald-j-trump-announcing-the-appointment-dr-kevin-hassett", "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/trump-taps-hassett-lead-national-economic-council-source-says-2024-11-26/"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-miran-cea-fed", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/stephen-miran", "name": "CEA -> Fed 2025-09", "tieType": "appointment (CEA chair -> Fed governor)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-03 ; 2025-09-15", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v5)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v5-V-trump-miran-cea-fed", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "APPOINTMENT: Trump's CEA chair Stephen Miran was confirmed 48-47 to the Fed Board Sep 15 2025 while on unpaid leave from the CEA. That dual role drew independence objections.", "citation": ["https://www.cnbc.com/2025/09/15/trump-stephen-miran-federal-reserve-interest-rates.html", "https://www.congress.gov/nomination/119th-congress/19"]}, {"@id": "tie/witkoff-park-lane-qia", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/steve-witkoff", "to": "node/qatar-investment-authority", "name": "sells Park Lane $623M 2023", "tieType": "business deal (asset sale, $623M)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2023-08", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v5)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v5-V-witkoff-park-lane-qia", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "BUSINESS DEAL: Qatar's sovereign fund QIA bought Witkoff Group's Park Lane Hotel (Central Park South) for ~$623M in Aug 2023, before Witkoff became the Mideast envoy who works with Qatar's PM.", "citation": ["https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2023-08-28/manhattan-hotel-once-linked-to-1mdb-scandal-sells-to-qataris", "https://therealdeal.com/new-york/2023/08/28/qia-buys-park-lane-hotel-from-witkoff/"]}, {"@id": "tie/stover-approved-maxwell-transfer", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/rick-stover-bop", "to": "node/ghislaine-maxwell", "name": "approves camp transfer 2025-08", "tieType": "approval (BOP waiver/transfer to FPC Bryan)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-08-01 ; confirmed 2026-09", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v6)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v6-V-stover-approved-maxwell-transfer", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "APPROVAL: The BOP press office confirmed to The Marshall Project (Sep 2026) that Rick Stover, special assistant to the BOP director, was the 'approving official' for Maxwell's move to FPC Bryan about a week after the Blanche proffer. A former senior BOP official says Maxwell is the only sex offender given such a waiver since 2006. Bondi told the House she had nothing to do with it. Who, if anyone, directed Stover is open (hole).", "citation": ["https://www.themarshallproject.org/2026/09/18/blanche-changes-federal-prison-placements", "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/us-news/texas-federal-prison-camp-bryan-ghislaine-maxwell-was-moved-steps-secu-rcna223464"]}, {"@id": "tie/bondi-qatar-jet-memo", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/pam-bondi", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "747 memo 2025-05 (I)", "tieType": "legal memo (Qatar 747 gift; OLC-cleared, unreleased)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-05", "grade": "I", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v6)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-12", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v6-I-bondi-qatar-jet-memo", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "MEMO (I): Per a DOJ official (CNN) and NYT/ABC sources, AG Bondi, Qatar's 2019-20 registered agent, signed an OLC-cleared memo, sent to WH Counsel Warrington, finding it lawful for DoD to accept Qatar's 747-8 and later transfer it to Trump's library foundation. The memo itself is unreleased (FOIA suit, Jul 2025), hence I.", "citation": ["https://www.cnn.com/2025/05/14/politics/bondi-justice-department-trump-qatar-747", "https://americanoversight.org/doj-sued-for-withholding-legal-memo-on-trump-administrations-400-million-jet-gifted-by-qatar/"]}, {"@id": "tie/hegseth-accepts-qatar-747", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/pete-hegseth", "to": "node/qatar-embassy-via-ballard-partners", "name": "accepts 747 2025-05-21", "tieType": "acceptance of foreign-government gift (747-8)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-05-21", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v6)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v6-V-hegseth-accepts-qatar-747", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "GIFT: Pentagon statement May 21 2025: 'The Secretary of Defense has accepted a Boeing 747 from Qatar' for presidential use (FactCheck.org quoting Parnell). Edge drawn to the Qatar state node.", "citation": ["https://www.factcheck.org/2025/05/unwrapping-qatars-400-million-winged-gift-to-trump/"]}, {"@id": "tie/son-trump-100b-pledge", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/masayoshi-son", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "$100B pledge 2024-12", "tieType": "documented meeting ; investment pledge", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2024-12-16 ; 2025-01-21", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v6)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-12", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v6-V-son-trump-100b-pledge", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "MEETING/PLEDGE: Son announced at Mar-a-Lago with Trump (and Lutnick) a $100B US investment over four years (Dec 16 2024). He then chaired Stargate, announced at the WH Jan 21 2025.", "citation": ["https://www.reuters.com/business/finance/softbank-ceo-announce-100-bln-investment-us-during-visit-trump-cnbc-reports-2024-12-16/", "https://apnews.com/article/donald-trump-softbank-investment-us-8df47668f894b5d922839d98887bbb0e"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-powell-fed-tour", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/jerome-powell", "name": "Fed tour 2025-07-24", "tieType": "pressure campaign ; documented meeting (Fed tour)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-07-24", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v6)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v6-V-trump-powell-fed-tour", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "MEETING: Trump toured the Fed renovation with Powell on Jul 24 2025 and disputed the cost on camera ($3.1B vs Powell's correction). He had called it a possible 'fireable offense', then said firing was not 'necessary'. Powell's chair term ended May 2026; Warsh was nominated.", "citation": ["https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/remarks-during-tour-the-federal-reserve-system-headquarters-and-exchange-with-reporters", "https://apnews.com/article/trump-federal-reserve-jerome-powell-145b0189a8c7acaab9fcfb097dc376c9"]}, {"@id": "tie/nader-mbz-adviser", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/george-nader", "to": "node/mohamed-bin-zayed", "name": "adviser", "tieType": "employment (adviser)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2016 - 2017", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v6)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v6-V-nader-mbz-adviser", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "EMPLOYMENT: Mueller Report: George Nader was an adviser to UAE Crown Prince Mohamed bin Zayed.", "citation": ["https://www.openmuellerreport.org/person/george-nader", "https://www.justice.gov/d9/report.pdf"]}, {"@id": "tie/nader-arranged-prince-dmitriev", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/george-nader", "to": "node/erik-prince", "name": "arranges Seychelles 2017", "tieType": "arranged meeting (Seychelles)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2017-01", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v6)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v6-V-nader-arranged-prince-dmitriev", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "ARRANGEMENT: Mueller Report: Nader arranged the Jan 2017 Seychelles meetings between Prince and Dmitriev.", "citation": ["https://www.justice.gov/d9/report.pdf"]}, {"@id": "tie/prince-bannon-briefing", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/erik-prince", "to": "node/steve-bannon", "name": "briefing (disputed, I)", "tieType": "contact (disputed briefing)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2017-01", "grade": "I", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v6)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v6-I-prince-bannon-briefing", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "CONTACT (I): Mueller Report: Prince said he briefed Bannon after the Seychelles trip. Bannon denied it, and the Office could not reconcile the accounts, hence I.", "citation": ["https://www.justice.gov/d9/report.pdf"]}, {"@id": "tie/lauder-greenland-pitch", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/ronald-lauder", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "Greenland pitch 2018 (I)", "tieType": "advocacy (Greenland purchase idea)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2018 ; 2025-26", "grade": "I", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v6)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v6-I-lauder-greenland-pitch", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "ADVOCACY (I): Per NYT (Baker/Glasser book, 2022) and Guardian (Jan 2026), Lauder pitched Trump in 2018 on buying Greenland and offered to be a back channel to Denmark. Trump told Bolton a 'really, really experienced businessman' proposed it. The Guardian reports Lauder holds Greenland business interests. Book and anonymous sourcing, hence I.", "citation": ["https://www.nytimes.com/2022/09/14/us/politics/trump-greenland.html", "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/jan/15/ronald-lauder-billionaire-donor-donald-trump-ukraine-greenland"]}, {"@id": "tie/palantir-ice-immigrationos", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/palantir", "to": "node/ice", "name": "ImmigrationOS $29.8M 2025", "tieType": "contract ($29.8M ImmigrationOS)", "category": "contract", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-04", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v6)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v6-V-palantir-ice-immigrationos", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "CONTRACT: ICE paid Palantir ~$29.8M (modification to an existing contract) to build the 'ImmigrationOS' prototype by Sep 25 2025, for deportation targeting and self-deportation tracking (contract doc via Wired).", "citation": ["https://www.wired.com/story/ice-palantir-immigrationos/", "https://www.businessinsider.com/ice-palantir-new-technology-30-million-visa-overstays-self-deportation-2025-4"]}, {"@id": "tie/waltz-riyadh-lavrov", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/mike-waltz", "to": "node/sergey-lavrov", "name": "Riyadh 2025-02-18", "tieType": "documented meeting", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-02-18", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v6)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v6-V-waltz-riyadh-lavrov", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "MEETING: NSA Mike Waltz joined Rubio and Witkoff with Lavrov and Ushakov in Riyadh Feb 18 2025 (State Dept).", "citation": ["https://www.state.gov/secretary-rubios-meeting-with-russian-foreign-minister-lavrov"]}, {"@id": "tie/tamim-trump-sharm", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/tamim-bin-hamad-al-thani", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "co-sign Sharm 2025-10-13", "tieType": "co-signatories (Gaza declaration)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-10-13", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v6)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v6-V-tamim-trump-sharm", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SIGNING: Emir Tamim signed the Sharm el-Sheikh Gaza agreement with Trump, Sisi and Erdogan on Oct 13 2025 (Amiri Diwan).", "citation": ["https://www.diwan.gov.qa/en/Briefing-Room/News/International-Occasions/2025/October/13/HH-the-Amir-participates-in-signing-ceremony-of-agreement-to-end-the-war-in-Gaza", "https://www.thenationalnews.com/news/mena/2025/10/14/full-text-of-trump-peace-agreement-signed-by-leaders-of-us-egypt-qatar-and-turkey-in-sharm-el-sheikh/"]}, {"@id": "tie/tamim-althani-pm", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/tamim-bin-hamad-al-thani", "to": "node/mohammed-bin-abdulrahman-al-thani", "name": "appoints PM", "tieType": "appointment (PM & FM)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2023-03", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v6)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v6-V-tamim-althani-pm", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "APPOINTMENT: The Emir appointed Sheikh Mohammed bin Abdulrahman PM (and FM); he attended Sharm with the Emir (Diwan).", "citation": ["https://www.diwan.gov.qa/en/Briefing-Room/News/International-Occasions/2025/October/13/HH-the-Amir-participates-in-signing-ceremony-of-agreement-to-end-the-war-in-Gaza"]}, {"@id": "tie/bessent-sanctions-lukoil-rosneft", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/scott-bessent", "to": "node/lukoil-international-assets", "name": "designates 2025-10-22", "tieType": "sanctions designation (Lukoil + Rosneft, EO 14024)", "category": "pardon/settlement", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-10-22", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v7)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v7-V-bessent-sanctions-lukoil-rosneft", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DESIGNATION: Treasury/OFAC designated Rosneft and Lukoil on Oct 22 2025 (first Ukraine-related sanctions of Trump's 2nd term). Bessent: 'Now is the time to stop the slaying and for an immediate ceasefire.' GLs 126-128 covered wind-down and retail stations. This designation is why Lukoil must sell its foreign assets.", "citation": ["https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/sb0290", "https://ofac.treasury.gov/recent-actions/20251022"]}, {"@id": "tie/treasury-blocks-gunvor-lukoil", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/scott-bessent", "to": "node/gunvor", "name": "'Kremlin's puppet' no license 2025-11", "tieType": "license refusal (Lukoil bid)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-11-06", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v7)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v7-V-treasury-blocks-gunvor-lukoil", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "REFUSAL: Treasury's official X account: 'the Kremlin's puppet, Gunvor, will never get a license'. Gunvor withdrew its Lukoil international bid the same day (Reuters/AP).", "citation": ["https://www.reuters.com/business/energy/gunvor-says-withdraws-bid-buy-assets-russian-energy-firm-lukoil-2025-11-06/", "https://apnews.com/article/gunvor-lukoil-russia-ukraine-trump-kremlin-putin-4664b2a87135b8960dedf0ad463ee4f5"]}, {"@id": "tie/carlyle-lukoil-agreement", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/carlyle", "to": "node/lukoil-international-assets", "name": "sale agreement 2026-01 (contingent)", "tieType": "business deal (non-exclusive sale agreement, OFAC-contingent)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-01-29", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "ended", "statusDate": "2026-07-31", "statusNote": "LIG's 2025 annual report (dated Sep 30 2026, via Interfax) says the non-exclusive Carlyle agreement lapsed in late July 2026 without OFAC clearance; Bloomberg: Carlyle confirmed it stopped pursuing the deal. Recorded ended in v17.", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v7)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-21", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v7-V-carlyle-lukoil-agreement", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DEAL: Lukoil agreed Jan 29 2026 to sell Lukoil International GmbH (ex-Kazakhstan) to Carlyle, non-exclusive and contingent on OFAC authorization (Lukoil press release). OFAC GL 131 series (131I to Sep 19 2026; 131J to Oct 22 2026) authorizes only contingent contracts. Competing Boehly-led bid is pending.", "citation": ["https://www.lukoil.com/PressCenter/Pressreleases/Pressrelease/lukoil-agrees-with-carlyle-on-sale-of", "https://ofac.treasury.gov/media/936731/download"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-barrack-syria-envoy", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/tom-barrack", "name": "Syria envoy 2025-05", "tieType": "appointment (Special Envoy for Syria, + Amb. Turkey)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-05-23", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v7)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-23", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v7-V-trump-barrack-syria-envoy", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "APPOINTMENT: Barrack, Trump's longtime adviser and Ambassador to Turkey, took the Syria special envoy role May 23 2025 to carry out sanctions removal (Reuters; State Dept).", "citation": ["https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/us-ambassador-turkey-will-serve-special-envoy-syria-2025-05-23/", "https://www.state.gov/releases/office-of-the-spokesperson/2025/06/u-s-ambassador-to-turkiye-and-special-envoy-for-syria-thomas-barrack-and-acting-under-secretary-brad-smith-terrorism-and-financial-intelligence-treasury"]}, {"@id": "tie/barrack-sharaa-istanbul", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/tom-barrack", "to": "node/ahmed-al-sharaa", "name": "Istanbul 2025-05-24", "tieType": "documented meeting", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-05-24", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v7)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v7-V-barrack-sharaa-istanbul", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "MEETING: Barrack met Syrian President Ahmed al-Sharaa and FM al-Shaibani in Istanbul May 24 2025 on sanctions relief (GL 25, Caesar waiver), ISIS and relations with Israel (US Embassy statement).", "citation": ["https://tr.usembassy.gov/u-s-ambassador-to-turkiye-and-syria-envoy-thomas-barracks-statement-on-meeting-with-syrian-president-ahmed-al-sharaa-and-fm-asaad-al-shaibani/"]}, {"@id": "tie/barrack-smith-syria-sanctions", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/tom-barrack", "to": "node/bradley-t-smith", "name": "joint Syria briefing 2025-06", "tieType": "joint official action (Syria sanctions removal briefing)", "category": "pardon/settlement", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-06-30", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v7)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v7-V-barrack-smith-syria-sanctions", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "JOINT ACTION: Barrack and Brad Smith (then acting Treasury TFI under secretary) briefed jointly on the record Jun 30 2025 on removing Syria sanctions (State transcript).", "citation": ["https://www.state.gov/releases/office-of-the-spokesperson/2025/06/u-s-ambassador-to-turkiye-and-special-envoy-for-syria-thomas-barrack-and-acting-under-secretary-brad-smith-terrorism-and-financial-intelligence-treasury"]}, {"@id": "tie/altman-trump-wh", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/sam-altman", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "WH 2025-01 + 2025-09", "tieType": "documented meetings (WH Stargate; WH tech dinner)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-01-21 ; 2025-09-04", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v7)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v7-V-altman-trump-wh", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "MEETINGS: Altman stood with Trump at the Jan 21 2025 Stargate announcement and attended the Sep 4 2025 WH tech dinner ('Thank you for being such a pro-business, pro-innovation President'; WH release).", "citation": ["https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2025/09/president-trump-tech-leaders-unite-american-ai-dominance/", "https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/remarks-artificial-intelligence-infrastructure-development-and-exchange-with-reporters"]}, {"@id": "tie/openai-g42-stargate-uae", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/sam-altman", "to": "node/g42", "name": "Stargate UAE 2025-05", "tieType": "business deal (Stargate UAE, 1GW)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-05-22", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v7)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v7-V-openai-g42-stargate-uae", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DEAL: OpenAI with G42, Oracle, NVIDIA, Cisco and SoftBank launched Stargate UAE (1GW Abu Dhabi cluster, 200MW in 2026) on the UAE-US AI Campus announced with MBZ and Trump the week before; 'developed in close coordination with the U.S. government' (OpenAI; G42).", "citation": ["https://openai.com/index/introducing-stargate-uae/", "https://www.g42.ai/resources/news/global-tech-alliance-launches-stargate-uae"]}, {"@id": "tie/vought-powell-letter", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/russ-vought", "to": "node/jerome-powell", "name": "letter 2025-07-10", "tieType": "official letter (pressure campaign)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-07-10 ; 2025-07-17", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v7)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v7-V-vought-powell-letter", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "LETTER: OMB Director Vought wrote Powell Jul 10 2025 ('The President is extremely troubled...', 'ostentatious overhaul'; 7-day deadline). Powell replied Jul 17 (Fed FOIA PDF).", "citation": ["https://www.federalreserve.gov/foia/files/vought-letter-20250717.pdf", "https://www.cnbc.com/2025/07/17/powell-trump-vought-renovation.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/palantir-maven-1-3b", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/palantir", "to": "node/pete-hegseth", "name": "Maven ceiling ~$1.3B 2025-05", "tieType": "contract (Maven Smart System ceiling to ~$1.3B)", "category": "contract", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-05-21", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v7)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v7-V-palantir-maven-1-3b", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "CONTRACT: DoD raised Palantir's Maven Smart System ceiling from $480M to ~$1.3B (+$795M modification, through May 2029) per the May 21 2025 contract announcements, under Hegseth's department.", "citation": ["https://www.war.gov/News/Contracts/Contract/Article/4194643/contracts-for-may-21-2025/", "https://defensescoop.com/2025/05/23/dod-palantir-maven-smart-system-contract-increase/"]}, {"@id": "tie/smith-gl131-series-lukoil", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/bradley-t-smith", "to": "node/lukoil-international-assets", "name": "GL 131I/J 2026-08/09", "tieType": "licenses (GL 131I/131J: Lukoil sale talks)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-08-20 ; 2026-09-18", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v8)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-21", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v8-V-smith-gl131-series-lukoil", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "LICENSES: Director Smith digitally signed GL 131I (2026-08-20 08:38:56 ET, to Sep 19) and GL 131J (2026-09-18 08:32:01 ET, to Oct 22 2026). Both authorize only contingent contracts for the sale of Lukoil International GmbH. OFAC FAQ 1224: any sale license will require cutting ties with Lukoil, blocking proceeds in a US account and 'no windfall'/up-front value to Lukoil.", "citation": ["https://ofac.treasury.gov/media/936951/download?inline=", "https://ofac.treasury.gov/media/936731/download", "https://ofac.treasury.gov/faqs/1224"]}, {"@id": "tie/tahnoon-chairs-g42", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/tahnoon-bin-zayed", "to": "node/g42", "name": "chairman", "tieType": "board (chairman)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2024 - present", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v8)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v8-V-tahnoon-chairs-g42", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "BOARD: Tahnoon is Chairman of G42 (Microsoft release on its $1.5B G42 stake, Apr 16 2024; Microsoft's Brad Smith, not OFAC's, joined the G42 board). This links Stargate UAE (OpenAI/Oracle/G42) to Tahnoon.", "citation": ["https://news.microsoft.com/source/2024/04/16/microsoft-invests-1-5-billion-in-abu-dhabis-g42-to-accelerate-ai-development-and-global-expansion/", "https://apnews.com/article/microsoft-g42-ai-uae-abu-dhabi-jais-8a9e3f9840a10f151e2421efb195c9b6"]}, {"@id": "tie/tahnoon-chairs-ihc", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/tahnoon-bin-zayed", "to": "node/international-holding-company-ihc", "name": "chairman", "tieType": "board (chairman)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "- present", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v8)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v8-V-tahnoon-chairs-ihc", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "BOARD: Tahnoon is Chairman of IHC (ADX FY2025 results release, Feb 13 2026; ultimate parent Royal Group Holding per 2024 directors' report).", "citation": ["https://apigateway.adx.ae/adx/cdn/1.0/content/download/4700060", "https://apigateway.adx.ae/adx/cdn/1.0/content/download/4267777"]}, {"@id": "tie/ihc-boehly-lukoil-bid", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/international-holding-company-ihc", "to": "node/lukoil-international-assets", "name": "in Boehly bid (I)", "tieType": "consortium member (bid, pending)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-09 - 2026-10", "grade": "I", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v8)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v8-I-ihc-boehly-lukoil-bid", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "BID (I): NYT (via SMH) names IHC, 'overseen by' Tahnoon, with Boehly, the US DFC and the Al-Khayyats' Power International in the Lukoil bid. FT (via secondary outlets) reports DFC ~15% equity. No filing seen, hence I.", "citation": ["https://www.smh.com.au/world/europe/us-russia-talks-on-ukraine-now-involve-an-oil-deal-tied-to-trump-allies-20261004-p612ot.html", "https://www.oilandgasmiddleeast.com/news/boehly-led-consortium-backed-by-us-and-gulf-investors-bids-for-lukoils-international-assets"]}, {"@id": "tie/dfc-boehly-lukoil-bid", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/us-dfc", "to": "node/lukoil-international-assets", "name": "~15% co-invest (I)", "tieType": "co-investor (bid, ~15% equity reported)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-09", "grade": "I", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v8)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v8-I-dfc-boehly-lukoil-bid", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "CO-INVEST (I): The US International Development Finance Corp. is reported (FT via secondary outlets; NYT) as an equity co-investor (~15%) in the Boehly-led bid. A senior official told NYT that Witkoff and Kushner helped negotiate 'a substantial upfront payment and profits interest for the United States'. No DFC board record seen.", "citation": ["https://www.smh.com.au/world/europe/us-russia-talks-on-ukraine-now-involve-an-oil-deal-tied-to-trump-allies-20261004-p612ot.html", "https://www.oilandgasmiddleeast.com/news/boehly-led-consortium-backed-by-us-and-gulf-investors-bids-for-lukoils-international-assets"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-sharaa-riyadh-wh", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/ahmed-al-sharaa", "name": "Riyadh 2025-05; WH 2025-11", "tieType": "documented meetings (Riyadh; White House)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-05-14 ; 2025-11-10", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v8)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v8-V-trump-sharaa-riyadh-wh", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "MEETINGS: Trump met al-Sharaa in Riyadh on May 14 2025, right after announcing all Syria sanctions would be lifted, and hosted him at the White House on Nov 10 2025 (first Syrian president). OUTCOME: Syria joins the anti-ISIS coalition; Treasury sanctions action announced the same day.", "citation": ["https://apnews.com/article/trump-syria-saudi-arabia-sharaa-assad-sanctions-bb208f25cfedecd6446fd1626012c0fb", "https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/trump-meet-sharaa-white-house-capping-major-turnaround-syria-2025-11-10/"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-putin-alaska-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/vladimir-putin", "name": "Anchorage 2025-08-15", "tieType": "documented meeting (Anchorage summit)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-08-15", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v8)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v8-V-trump-putin-alaska-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SUMMIT: Trump and Putin met at JB Elmendorf-Richardson Aug 15 2025, three-on-three with Rubio and Witkoff / Lavrov and Ushakov (Kremlin). The wider delegations included Bessent, Lutnick, Hegseth and Ratcliffe; on the Russian side Belousov, Siluanov and Dmitriev. OUTCOME: no deal.", "citation": ["http://en.kremlin.ru/events/president/news/77791", "https://www.adn.com/politics/2025/08/15/all-eyes-are-on-anchorage-as-trump-putin-talks-begin/"]}, {"@id": "tie/rubio-lavrov-repeat", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/marco-rubio", "to": "node/sergey-lavrov", "name": "Jul + Aug 2025", "tieType": "documented meetings (repeat)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-02-18 ; 2025-07 ; 2025-08-15", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v8)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v8-V-rubio-lavrov-repeat", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "REPEAT CONTACT: After Riyadh, Rubio met Lavrov in early July 2025 (The Hill) and sat across from him in the Anchorage three-on-three Aug 15 2025 (Kremlin).", "citation": ["http://en.kremlin.ru/events/president/news/77791", "https://thehill.com/homenews/administration/5453844-peace-talks-ukraine-russia/"]}, {"@id": "tie/dmitriev-alaska-delegation", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/kirill-dmitriev", "to": "node/scott-bessent-howard-lutnick", "name": "Anchorage delegations (I)", "tieType": "same summit delegation (economic track)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-08-15", "grade": "I", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v8)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v8-I-dmitriev-alaska-delegation", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "PRESENCE (I): Dmitriev was in Putin's Anchorage delegation; Bessent and Lutnick were in Trump's (ADN; PBS citing Ushakov). A direct Dmitriev-Bessent/Lutnick meeting there is not documented, hence I.", "citation": ["https://www.adn.com/politics/2025/08/15/all-eyes-are-on-anchorage-as-trump-putin-talks-begin/", "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/live-updates-trump-to-meet-with-putin-in-alaska"]}, {"@id": "tie/lutnick-epstein-neighbours-lsj-lunch-2012", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/howard-lutnick", "to": "node/jeffrey-epstein", "name": "island lunch 2012", "tieType": "documented meeting (Little St. James lunch) ; neighbours (E 71st St)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2005 ; 2012-12-23", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v9)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v9-V-lutnick-epstein-neighbours-lsj-lunch-2012", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE: Lutnick lived next door to Epstein on E 71st St and, by his own sworn account to House Oversight (transcribed interview May 6 2026, transcript released May 2026), visited Little St. James on Dec 23 2012 for an hour-long lunch with his wife, four children, another family and staff; Epstein's assistant emailed the next day 'Nice seeing you' (NBC, from the files). SAID: Lutnick calls his three in-person contacts (2005 coffee, the 2012 lunch, a later scaffolding chat) 'meaningless and inconsequential' and says Epstein's staff arranged the visit. Register: vault-2012-12-19-lutnick-lsj-lunch-email.", "citation": ["https://oversight.house.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Lutnick-Transcript.pdf", "https://abcnews.com/Politics/lutnick-called-interactions-epstein-meaningless-inconsequential-transcript/story?id=132938658", "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/politics-news/howard-lutnick-congressional-showdown-epstein-files-island-visit-rcna343523"]}, {"@id": "tie/lutnick-epstein-adfin-2012", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/howard-lutnick", "to": "node/jeffrey-epstein", "name": "AdFin co-investors 2012", "tieType": "business deal (same AdFin Series A purchase agreement)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2012-12-28", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v9)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v9-V-lutnick-epstein-adfin-2012", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE: Epstein (for Southern Trust Company) and Lutnick (for CVAFH I LLC) signed the same AdFin Solutions Series A preferred-stock purchase agreement dated Dec 28 2012, five days after the island lunch; their stakes were set for later 2013 closings (CBS; EFTA00289560). Lutnick communicated with Epstein through Epstein's assistant as late as 2018 (NPR). Two acts, same month: the lunch and the deal are separate edges; no claim the lunch caused the deal.", "citation": ["https://www.cbsnews.com/news/howard-lutnick-jeffrey-epstein-in-business-together/", "https://tommycarstensen.com/epstein/data/documents/set9/00289/EFTA00289560.html", "https://www.npr.org/2026/05/06/nx-s1-5814081/howard-lutnick-epstein-files-house-oversight-committee"]}, {"@id": "tie/hoffman-epstein-baume-2015", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/reid-hoffman", "to": "node/jeffrey-epstein", "name": "hosted dinner 2015", "tieType": "documented meeting (hosted dinner, Baume, Palo Alto)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2015-08-02", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v9)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v9-V-hoffman-epstein-baume-2015", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE: Reid Hoffman's office (EA Saida Sapieva, LinkedIn & Greylock) organised the Aug 2 2015 bought-out dinner at Baume, Palo Alto, for MIT's Ed Boyden, and Epstein's office confirmed he 'most definitely would like to participate'; the attendee list includes Epstein, Hoffman, Thiel, Musk, Zuckerberg, Chan and Joi Ito (EFTA02073963, EFTA02074074). Epstein's assistant called it 'Reid Hoffman/Peter Thiel's dinner party'. Separately, WSJ (2023, per NBC) reported Hoffman visited Epstein's island and introduced Epstein to Thiel. Register: grokbot-2026-10-09-I-farnsjennifer-2108740350491955289-baume-rykov-aug2015.", "citation": ["https://tommycarstensen.com/epstein/data/documents/set10/02073/EFTA02073963.html", "https://www.epsteinscan.org/document/1221465", "https://www.nbcnews.com/tech/tech-news/jeffrey-epstein-files-reveal-deep-tech-ties-musk-gates-rcna257092"]}, {"@id": "tie/zuckerberg-epstein-baume-2015", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/mark-zuckerberg", "to": "node/jeffrey-epstein", "name": "met at dinner 2015", "tieType": "documented meeting (same dinner; contact-details request)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2015-08-02 ; 2015-08-05", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v9)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v9-V-zuckerberg-epstein-baume-2015", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE: Zuckerberg (with Priscilla Chan) is on the Baume attendee list with Epstein (Aug 2 2015), and on Aug 5 Epstein's assistant wrote to Zuckerberg's chief of staff Andrea Besmehn that 'Mark requested Jeffrey send his contact details to him' and passed them on; Besmehn replied 'Noted, with thanks' (EFTA02074070). SAID: Meta says Zuckerberg 'met Epstein in passing one time' and did not communicate with him again (2019 and 2026 statements, NBC). Only the contact swap is one-to-one; no later contact is documented.", "citation": ["https://www.justice.gov/epstein/files/DataSet%2010/EFTA02074070.pdf", "https://epsteinexposed.com/documents/efta-efta02074070", "https://www.nbcnews.com/tech/tech-news/jeffrey-epstein-files-reveal-deep-tech-ties-musk-gates-rcna257092"]}, {"@id": "tie/musk-epstein-baume-2015", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/elon-musk", "to": "node/jeffrey-epstein", "name": "same dinner 2015", "tieType": "same event (attendee list, Baume dinner)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2015-08-02", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v9)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v9-V-musk-epstein-baume-2015", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "reference", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE: Elon Musk is listed as an attendee of the Aug 2 2015 Baume dinner with Epstein in the reconfirmation email from Reid Hoffman's office (EFTA02074074) and the Jul 31 confirmation (EFTA02073963). Attendance only: no one-to-one Musk-Epstein exchange from this dinner is in these documents.", "citation": ["https://www.epsteinscan.org/document/1221465", "https://tommycarstensen.com/epstein/data/documents/set10/02073/EFTA02073963.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/rubio-icc-entity-sanctions-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/marco-rubio", "to": "node/international-criminal-court", "name": "sanctions ICC 2026", "tieType": "sanctions designation (ICC itself, E.O. 14203; SDN list)", "category": "pardon/settlement", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-09", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v9)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v9-V-rubio-icc-entity-sanctions-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE: State (Rubio) designated the International Criminal Court itself under E.O. 14203 on Oct 9 2026 (full blocking; OFAC wind-down GLs 13-16). SAID: Rubio, 'Either the ICC will end its threats, or we will end the ICC.' Sequence only: it came hours after ex-ICC judge Navi Pillay won the Nobel Peace Prize; State says the designation had been deferred for over a year. Register: grokbot-2026-10-09-V-statedept-icc-entity-sanctions-hours-after-pillay-nobel.", "citation": ["https://www.state.gov/releases/office-of-the-spokesman/2026/10/imposing-sanctions-on-the-international-criminal-court/", "https://apnews.com/article/us-icc-trump-rubio-4ea3555403e3c695d8f81dc473515d9b", "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/9/us-sanctions-international-criminal-court-itself-in-latest-escalation"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-zacharia-press-secretary", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/katie-zacharia", "name": "press sec. 2026", "tieType": "appointment (White House press secretary)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-09", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "ended", "statusDate": "2026-11-09", "statusNote": "Ended Oct 16 2026; post still vacant Nov 9. Trump SAID Nov 9 the Dana White idea was 'sort of kidding' and brought White to the Brady podium as a guest ('we thought we'd have a little fun') — not an appointment (Fox News Digital, NBC).", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v9)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v9-V-trump-zacharia-press-secretary", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE: Trump announced on Truth Social on Oct 9 2026 that Katie Zacharia will succeed Karoline Leavitt as White House press secretary; per CNN she was not under consideration a week earlier and Trump sought Leavitt's counsel first.", "citation": ["https://apnews.com/article/trump-white-house-press-secretary-katie-zacharia-aaabf8627035da9bc4cd44173f22e02e", "https://www.politico.com/news/2026/10/09/white-house-offers-katie-zacharia-white-house-press-secretary-job-01114597"]}, {"@id": "tie/tmtg-zacharia-employment", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/trump-media", "to": "node/katie-zacharia", "name": "TMTG comms 2026", "tieType": "employment (Senior Communications Advisor, Truth Social/TMTG)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-06 - 2026-10", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v9)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v9-V-tmtg-zacharia-employment", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE: Zacharia was Senior Communications Advisor to Truth Social / Trump Media & Technology Group from June 2026 (after a two-month DHS stint) until her Oct 9 2026 selection; Trump's own post cites the TMTG job. The President's family-held media company is the direct feeder into the White House podium.", "citation": ["https://www.politico.com/news/2026/10/09/white-house-offers-katie-zacharia-white-house-press-secretary-job-01114597", "https://krdo.com/politics/cnn-us-politics/2026/10/09/trump-selects-katie-zacharia-as-next-white-house-press-secretary/"]}, {"@id": "tie/milton-trump47-donation-pardon", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/trevor-milton", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "$920K then pardon", "tieType": "funding (Trump 47 Committee) ... pardon (sequence)", "category": "pardon/settlement", "kind": "register", "date": "2024-10-10 ; 2025-03-27", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": true, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v9)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v9-V-milton-trump47-donation-pardon", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE, sequence only: FEC shows Trevor Milton gave $920,000 to the Trump 47 Committee on Oct 10 2024 (wife Chelsey $10,000 Oct 17); Trump fully pardoned Milton's 2022 securities-fraud conviction on Mar 27 2025 (CNBC). CBS (Oct 9 2026) puts the couple's pro-Trump giving near $2M. Order of events only; no document ties the money to the pardon. Democrats wrote Oct 6 2026 asking who advocated for it.", "citation": ["https://docquery.fec.gov/cgi-bin/forms/C00042622/1851953/sa/12", "https://www.cnbc.com/2025/03/28/trump-pardons-nikola-trevor-milton-ceo-securities-fraud-electric-vehicle.html", "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/rfk-jr-lee-zeldin-democrats-congress-trump-pardons/"]}, {"@id": "tie/milton-maha-alliance-750k", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/trevor-milton", "to": "node/maha-alliance-pac", "name": "$750K MAHA PAC", "tieType": "funding ($750K)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "before 2025-03-27", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v9)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-16", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v9-V-milton-maha-alliance-750k", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE: Milton and his wife gave $750,000 to the Make America Healthy Again Alliance PAC, aligned with Kennedy's MAHA agenda, before the March 2025 pardon (CBS, citing FEC records).", "citation": ["https://www.cbsnews.com/news/rfk-jr-lee-zeldin-democrats-congress-trump-pardons/", "https://thehill.com/business/5221471-who-is-trevor-milton-nikola-pardon/"]}, {"@id": "tie/rfk-milton-pardon-advocacy", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/robert-f-kennedy-jr", "to": "node/trevor-milton", "name": "pardon advocacy? [I]", "tieType": "advocacy (reported, pardon)", "category": "pardon/settlement", "kind": "register", "date": "2025 (reported Jun 2026)", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-10-20", "statusNote": "Oct 20 answer deadline (Welch/Blumenthal/Min/Scanlon letter) passed with no public reply from Kennedy or HHS; a source close to Kennedy SAID (CBS) he privately says he will not advocate for any pardons. Still I/SAID.", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v9)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-20", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-powermap-v9-I-rfk-milton-pardon-advocacy", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID: Reuters reported in June 2026 that Kennedy advocated to Trump for Milton's pardon; Senate and House Democrats cited it in an Oct 6 2026 letter asking him to answer by Oct 20 (CBS). A source close to Kennedy says he privately says he won't advocate for any pardons. No primary record of the advocacy is public.", "citation": ["https://www.cbsnews.com/news/rfk-jr-lee-zeldin-democrats-congress-trump-pardons/", "https://scanlon.house.gov/news/documentsingle.aspx?DocumentID=2082"]}, {"@id": "tie/kimbal-musk-epstein-contact-2012-2015", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/kimbal-musk", "to": "node/jeffrey-epstein", "name": "Kimbal in files 2012+", "tieType": "documented association / files references (post-conviction contact)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2012-10-07 ; 2012-2015", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-12 (v10)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-12", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-12-powermap-v10-V-kimbal-musk-epstein-contact-2012-2015", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 4, "description": "DONE: DOJ Jan 2026 Epstein-files release references Kimbal Musk in 300+ documents (Boulder Reporting Lab). Documented post-conviction contact 2012-2015 includes lunch at Epstein's NYC home Oct 7 2012; Kimbal emailed thanks to Epstein and Boris Nikolic for 'connecting me with' a woman he dated ~6 months 2012-13 (Guardian, Bloomberg/Axios); Jan 24 2013 island invite declined (EFTA02565983). Association/files references only; no causation claim. Register: grokbot-2026-10-11-V-farnsjennifer-2109355050279809061-kimbal-musk-epstein-files.", "citation": ["https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/feb/10/jeffrey-epstein-tesla-kimbal-musk", "https://boulderreportinglab.org/2026/02/11/how-boulders-kimbal-musk-appears-in-the-newly-released-epstein-files/", "https://tommycarstensen.com/epstein/data/documents/set11/02565/EFTA02565983.html", "https://www.axios.com/local/boulder/2026/02/02/kimbal-musk-jeffrey-epstein-post-conviction-emails"]}, {"@id": "tie/epstein-summers-treasury-nov2016", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jeffrey-epstein", "to": "node/larry-summers", "name": "treasury picks email 2016", "tieType": "documented email (treasury-secretary suggestions, Trump transition)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2016-11-27", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-12 (v10)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-12", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-12-powermap-v10-V-epstein-summers-treasury-nov2016", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE: DOJ doc EFTA02669281 (Dataset 11) exists. SAID (email content): Nov 27 2016 Epstein asks Summers 'do you have any suggestions for treasury?' (19 days after the 2016 election); Summers replies with candidates including Romney, Tony James, Larry Fink, Fred Smith, Peter Thiel, Jeff Immelt, Jamie Dimon; Epstein rates them (e.g. 'Peter Thiel austistic, no global sense'). Distinct from epstein-summers-apr2016 (digital-currency thread). No claim Summers caused any later appointment. Register: grokbot-2026-10-11-V-hannibal-2109367247613366555-epstein-summers-treasury-picks-2016.", "citation": ["https://www.justice.gov/epstein/files/DataSet%2011/EFTA02669281.pdf", "https://tommycarstensen.com/epstein/data/documents/set11/02669/EFTA02669281.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/gino-yu-epstein-email-pipeline-2018", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/gino-yu", "to": "node/jeffrey-epstein", "name": "Yu pipeline email 2018", "tieType": "documented email / funding-pipeline contact", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2018-01-17", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-12 (v10)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-12", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-12-powermap-v10-V-gino-yu-epstein-email-pipeline-2018", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "reference", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE: Jan 17 2018 email from Gino Yu to Epstein (EFTA00906974 / EFTA00907010, DOJ Dataset 9) is real; Yu writes as Epstein's pipeline into consciousness research and references funds Epstein offered (remainder of $100K). Documented contact/funding-pipeline email only. The 'stage 3 / special abilities' allegation about a mentee in the same email is NOT treated as proven DONE. Register: grokbot-2026-10-11-I-nickhintonn-2018182480554275270-gino-yu-stage3-clean.", "citation": ["https://tommycarstensen.com/epstein/data/documents/set9/00906/EFTA00906974.html", "https://epsteinexposed.com/documents/efta-efta00907010", "https://www.epsteinscan.org/document/637313", "https://epsteinexposed.com/persons/gino-yu"]}, {"@id": "tie/parscale-clocktowerx-israel-fara-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/brad-parscale", "to": "node/state-of-israel", "name": "FARA 7649 Israel 2025", "tieType": "FARA registration (foreign principal; via Clock Tower X LLC / Havas)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-09-18", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-12 (v10)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-20", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-12-powermap-v10-V-parscale-clocktowerx-israel-fara-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE: DOJ FARA Registration Statement for Clock Tower X LLC, registration no. 7649, received Sep 18 2025: Bradley Parscale is sole managing member/owner; foreign principal listed as State of Israel (Jerusalem) with HAVAS Media Network (Frankfurt) also named; Exhibit/appendix describes strategic communications, planning and media services in support of Havas' engagement by the State of Israel for a US campaign. Trump 2020 campaign-manager history is context only (not a separate causation edge). Register: grokbot-2026-10-11-I-madam-crass-2108981642077643002-grok-clocktowerx-46m-clean.", "citation": ["https://efile.fara.gov/docs/7649-Registration-Statement-20250918-1.pdf", "https://responsiblestatecraft.org/israel-