senior-bessent-staffer-to-serve-as-adviser", "https://www.citybiz.co/article/869152/warsh-taps-bessent-aide-samantha-schwab-as-adviser/"]}, {"@id": "tie/lutnick-khashoggi-pierre-deal", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/howard-lutnick", "to": "node/motasem-khashoggi", "name": "Pierre $2B bid (dead 10-13)", "tieType": "business deal (found buyer, helped structure $2B Pierre bid; terminated)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2024-05 intro ; 2026-10-13 terminated", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "ended", "statusDate": "2026-10-13", "statusNote": "Co-op terminated the $2B Sabre Park Avenue (Khashoggi) purchase after the $100M deposit missed the Oct 13 5pm deadline (NYT Oct 14). Remains ended as of Oct 15 recheck.", "addedIn": "2026-10-14 (v12)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-15", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-14-powermap-v12-V-lutnick-khashoggi-pierre-deal", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE business deal: NYT (Oct 14 2026) says Commerce Secretary Lutnick, who owns the Pierre penthouse, found Saudi investor Motasem Khashoggi (introduced May 2024 via WhatsApp), met him in London with Dorchester Collection (Brunei-owned) president Christopher Cowdray, and helped craft his $2B bid via Sabre Park Avenue LLC. Records show Lutnick would have netted ~$60M on his unit and Newmark (run by two of his sons) a $30M adviser fee. Lutnick offered Khashoggi's son a BGC internship (taken, per Khashoggi) and turned on disappearing messages after his Dec 2024 nomination. The co-op terminated the deal after the $100M deposit missed the Oct 13 2026 5pm deadline. Lutnick declined comment. Register: grokbot-2026-10-14-V-shachtman-pierre-saudi-deal-dead.", "citation": ["https://dnyuz.com/2026/10/14/battle-over-the-pierre-ends-in-defeat-for-the-buyer-pushed-by-lutnick/"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-habba-attorney", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/alina-habba", "name": "former attorney", "tieType": "employment (personal attorney)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "pre-2025", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-14 (v12)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-20", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-14-powermap-v12-V-trump-habba-attorney", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE employment: Axios (Oct 14 2026) describes Alina Habba as former Trump attorney, who raised the Kennedy Center allegation with Trump in the Oval Office on Fri Oct 9 2026.", "citation": ["https://www.axios.com/2026/10/14/trump-kennedy-center-donation-maga-feud", "https://nypost.com/2026/10/14/us-news/alina-habba-accuses-ric-grenell-of-failing-to-deposit-millions-donated-by-her-husband-to-the-kennedy-center/"]}, {"@id": "tie/habba-mildon-marriage", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/alina-habba", "to": "node/turhan-mildon", "name": "married (2026-09)", "tieType": "marriage", "category": "family", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-09", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-14 (v12)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-20", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-14-powermap-v12-V-habba-mildon-marriage", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE marriage: Alina Habba married Turkish billionaire businessman Turhan Mildon in September 2026; they met at the Kennedy Center in 2025 (Axios; Daily Beast; Telegraph). WH Counsel Will Scharf attended the wedding (NYT via Fastrack).", "citation": ["https://www.axios.com/2026/10/14/trump-kennedy-center-donation-maga-feud", "https://www.thedailybeast.com/maga-blood-feud-exposed-in-kennedy-center-cash-scandal", "https://www.telegraph.co.uk/us/news/2026/10/14/white-house-kennedy-centre-missing-1m/"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-grenell-envoy-kennedy-center", "@type": "pm:Tie", 