 9 2026) that in spring 2025 Grenell persuaded Mildon to fold a multimillion-dollar Kennedy Center gift (first $17M, later $5.6M) into a $17.6M lump-sum payment for a business deal with a US company, and the gift was never deposited (Axios, four senior officials; NY Post; Telegraph). DONE side: Kennedy Center books show only a $270K Mildon pledge, which he paid Oct 13 2026; staff searched for a ~$6M gift late 2025 and found none; WH Counsel Scharf asked for documents and had none. Grenell: 'Absurd.' Daily Beast: the two are friends with Venezuela interests. Register: grokbot-2026-10-14-I-axios-habba-grenell-kennedy-center.", "citation": ["https://www.axios.com/2026/10/14/trump-kennedy-center-donation-maga-feud", "https://nypost.com/2026/10/14/us-news/alina-habba-accuses-ric-grenell-of-failing-to-deposit-millions-donated-by-her-husband-to-the-kennedy-center/", "https://www.telegraph.co.uk/us/news/2026/10/14/white-house-kennedy-centre-missing-1m/", "https://www.thedailybeast.com/maga-blood-feud-exposed-in-kennedy-center-cash-scandal"]}, {"@id": "tie/crew-v-kushner-envoy-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/crew", "to": "node/jared-kushner", "name": "sued: unconfirmed envoy (10-14)", "tieType": "lawsuit (Appointments Clause + Ethics Act; D.D.C. 26-cv-3580)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-14", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-10-16", "statusNote": "CREW v. Kushner 26-cv-3580 pending; Kushner's lawyer says no merit/standing, WH says volunteer role lawful; no hearing or ruling reported Oct 16.", "addedIn": "2026-10-14 (v12)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-16", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-14-powermap-v12-V-crew-v-kushner-envoy-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 4, "description": "DONE lawsuit: CREW filed suit Oct 14 2026 (Case No. 26-cv-3580) to block Jared Kushner from acting as a top US diplomat without Senate confirmation and to compel Ethics Act financial disclosures; the complaint says he works with Special Envoy Witkoff, has filed no second-term disclosure and has overlapping business interests (CREW release; complaint PDF; AP; NBC). Merits pending. Register: grokbot-2026-10-14-V-crew-sues-jared-kushner-unconfirmed-diplomat.", "citation": ["https://www.citizensforethics.org/legal-action/lawsuits/crew-sues-to-block-jared-kushner-from-acting-as-trump-envoy/", "https://assets.bwbx.io/documents/users/iqjWHBFdfxIU/rv7jGS_EmY1Y/v0", "https://apnews.com/article/jared-kushner-crew-lawsuit-trump-envoy-diplomat-aa28eeb278937ec29c0f35e72d13ba45", "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/trump-administration/watchdog-group-sues-trump-administration-jared-kushners-government-wor-rcna603563"]}, {"@id": "tie/adl-frontier-labs-said", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/adl-jonathan-greenblatt", "to": "node/frontier-ai-labs-openai-anthropic-google-meta", "name": "'working with' labs (SAID)", "tieType": "working relationship (SAID by Greenblatt)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-13 statement", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-14 (v12)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-14", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-14-powermap-v12-I-adl-frontier-labs-said", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "social", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "SAID: ADL CEO Jonathan Greenblatt, speaking in Israel (clip relayed Oct 13 2026), said 'We've been working with the Frontier Labs: OpenAI, Anthropic, Alphabet/Google (Gemini), Meta...' on antisemitism in AI outputs. The clip is truncated; what any lab changed is not documented. Kept as SAID, not a DONE tie. Register: grokbot-2026-10-14-V-greenblatt-adl-frontier-labs.", "citation": ["https://x.com/infolibnews/status/2110091224627441737"]}, {"@id": "tie/rabbis-smotrich-bengvir-joint-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/religious-zionist-rabbis-lior-eliyahu-et-al", "to": "node/bezalel-smotrich-itamar-ben-gvir", "name": "rabbis back ministers (Jul 2025)", "tieType": "endorsement / consultation meeting (joint statement)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-07-31", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-15 (v13)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-15", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-15-powermap-v13-V-rabbis-smotrich-bengvir-joint-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE meeting+endorsement: Religious Zionist rabbis met Ministers Itamar Ben Gvir and Bezalel Smotrich and issued a joint statement backing their unified front against a hostage deal leaving captives with Hamas and against humanitarian aid, demanding complete victory over Hamas (Ynet, Shilo Freid; Hebrew corroboration hm-news Jul 31 2025). Signatories include Dov Lior, Eitan Eisman, Elyakim Levanon, Shmuel Eliyahu, David Hai Hacohen, David Turgeman. Endorsement/consultation only — not causation of later policy.", "citation": ["https://www.ynetnews.com/article/ehlzwlwz6", "https://hm-news.co.il/572327/"]}, {"@id": "tie/smotrich-consults-rabbis-five", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/bezalel-smotrich", "to": "node/religious-zionist-rabbis-the-five-yehoshua-shapira", "name": "consults 'the Five' rabbis [SAID]", "tieType": "consultation (SAID by Smotrich)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-03 (NPR cites prior video)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-15 (v13)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-15", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-15-powermap-v13-V-smotrich-consults-rabbis-five", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "SAID consultation (Smotrich's own words on video, reported by NPR Mar 21 2025): 'I struggled with this decision and gathered my rabbis to consult with them. After all, I want to influence the war.' NPR says he regularly consults a group known as the Five, including Rabbi Yehoshua Shapira (Ramat Gan). Page opened 2026-10-15 (prior UNVERIFIED correction cleared). Consultation claim only — not that rabbis caused any named policy act.", "citation": ["https://www.npr.org/2025/03/21/nx-s1-5323006/the-rise-of-israels-finance-minister-bezalel-smotrich"]}, {"@id": "tie/shmuel-eliyahu-amichai-eliyahu-family", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/rabbi-shmuel-eliyahu", "to": "node/amichai-eliyahu", "name": "father (Safed rabbi) / son (Heritage Min.)", "tieType": "family (father/son) + cabinet appointment", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "ongoing; Amichai Heritage Minister from 2022; nuke remark 2023-11-05", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-15 (v13)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-15", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-15-powermap-v13-V-shmuel-eliyahu-amichai-eliyahu-family", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE family+office: Heritage Minister Amichai Eliyahu is the son of Rabbi Shmuel Eliyahu (Safed chief rabbi) and grandson of former Chief Rabbi Mordechai Eliyahu (Times of Israel Nov 5 2023). On Radio Kol Berama he SAID a nuclear bomb on Gaza was 'one way' (Netanyahu suspended him from cabinet meetings). Family/appointment tie only; the nuke remark is SAID, not a DONE policy order.", "citation": ["https://www.timesofisrael.com/far-right-minister-says-nuking-gaza-an-option-pm-suspends-him-from-cabinet-meetings/"]}, {"@id": "tie/rubio-huckabee-netanyahu-elad-pilgrimage", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/marco-rubio", "to": "node/benjamin-netanyahu-mike-huckabee-elad-city-of-david", "name": "Pilgrimage Road inauguration", "tieType": "joint inauguration (Pilgrimage Road / City of David)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-09-15", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-15 (v13)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-15", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-15-powermap-v13-V-rubio-huckabee-netanyahu-elad-pilgrimage", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE joint inauguration: Secretary of State Marco Rubio, PM Benjamin Netanyahu and Ambassador Mike Huckabee inaugurated the fully excavated Pilgrimage Road at the City of David (Elad-operated) in East Jerusalem on Sep 15/16 2025 (Jerusalem Post; BBC). Appearance/backing of the site only — not a claim that the visit caused later settlement policy.", "citation": ["https://www.jpost.com/israel-news/benjamin-netanyahu/article-867585", "https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cg42v2r10kyo"]}, {"@id": "tie/johnson-huckabee-ariel-visit-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/mike-johnson", "to": "node/mike-huckabee", "name": "Ariel settlement visit", "tieType": "joint visit (West Bank settlement Ariel)", "category": "pardon/settlement", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-08-04", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-15 (v13)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-15", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-15-powermap-v13-V-johnson-huckabee-ariel-visit-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE joint visit: Speaker Mike Johnson, with Ambassador Mike Huckabee (and Sarah Huckabee Sanders), visited the West Bank settlement of Ariel on Aug 4 2025 — highest-ranking US official ever to visit a settlement per ToI. Johnson SAID Judea and Samaria belong to the Jewish people by right. Visit/endorsement language only.", "citation": ["https://www.timesofisrael.com/us-speaker-johnson-makes-landmark-visit-to-west-bank-settlement-of-ariel/"]}, {"@id": "tie/johnson-netanyahu-shiloh-dinner-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/mike-johnson", "to": "node/benjamin-netanyahu", "name": "Shiloh dinner with Netanyahu", "tieType": "meeting / dinner (Shiloh settlement)", "category": "pardon/settlement", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-08-04", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-15 (v13)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-15", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-15-powermap-v13-V-johnson-netanyahu-shiloh-dinner-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE meeting: Same day as the Ariel visit, PM Netanyahu and Sara hosted Speaker Mike Johnson and Kelly Lary for a meal in the West Bank settlement of Shiloh, with Ambassador Mike Huckabee and several Republican members of Congress (Ynet; ToI/JNS corroboration). Meeting only — not a claim of a specific deal made at dinner.", "citation": ["https://www.ynetnews.com/article/0b6i9zy87", "https://www.jns.org/israel-news/netanyahu-johnson-meet-in-ancient-shiloh-along-with-congress-members"]}, {"@id": "tie/errol-musk-netanyahu-family-friend", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/errol-musk", "to": "node/benjamin-netanyahu", "name": "family friend [SAID by Errol]", "tieType": "claimed family friendship (SAID by Errol Musk)", "category": "family", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-02 (~interview); Elon-Netanyahu meeting 2023-09-18 is separate DONE", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-15 (v13)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-15", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-15-powermap-v13-I-errol-musk-netanyahu-family-friend", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID only (Errol Musk interview ~Feb 12 2025, seen via Reddit/Rumble re-uploads): Netanyahu is a 'family friend'; also that Netanyahu called Elon de facto president (the latter traces to the Sep 18 2023 Tesla livestream, NYT/JTA — separate DONE meeting). No primary interview transcript or documented family-to-family relationship found. Keep I/SAID; do not promote to DONE.", "citation": ["https://www.reddit.com/r/LateStageCapitalism/comments/1jxgl18/", "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/09/18/world/middleeast/netanyahu-musk-meeting.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/smotrich-bessent-treasury-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/bezalel-smotrich", "to": "node/scott-bessent", "name": "Bessent-Smotrich Treasury meet", "tieType": "official meeting (Treasury)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-03-05", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-15 (v13)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-15", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-15-powermap-v13-V-smotrich-bessent-treasury-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE official meeting: Treasury press release SB0043 — Secretary Bessent and Israeli Finance Minister Bezalel Smotrich met in Washington Mar 5 2025 and agreed to strengthen dialogue on economic policy, technology and financial regulation (home.treasury.gov; Bessent calendar 9:00-9:45am; NYT). US-access tie on the rabbi→minister→US chain. Meeting only — not causation of later OFAC/aid decisions.", "citation": ["https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/sb0043", "https://home.treasury.gov/system/files/136/SB-March-2025.pdf", "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/03/05/world/middleeast/smotrich-bessent-us-israel.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/bengvir-gop-congress-maralago-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/itamar-ben-gvir", "to": "node/house-gop-emmer-mast-jordan-tenney-lawler", "name": "Mar-a-Lago + Capitol Hill meetings", "tieType": "meeting (Mar-a-Lago dinner + Capitol Hill)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-04-22 ; 2025-04-28", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-15 (v13)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-15", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-15-powermap-v13-V-bengvir-gop-congress-maralago-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE meetings (Ben Gvir office via JTA/ToI): on first official US trip Apr 2025, Ben Gvir had dinner at Mar-a-Lago Apr 22 with House Majority Whip Tom Emmer (Trump absent) and on Apr 28 met Reps Brian Mast (HFAC chair), Jim Jordan, Claudia Tenney, Mike Lawler on Capitol Hill. No Trump administration officials met him. US-access tie; not a claim those meetings caused named US policy.", "citation": ["https://www.jta.org/2025/04/28/israel/ben-gvir-says-he-met-with-4-members-of-congress-rebuffed-protesters-at-us-capitol", "https://www.timesofisrael.com/ben-gvir-meets-4-gop-lawmakers-on-capitol-hill-expanding-inroads-in-us-politics/"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-bailey-ola-director", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/katie-bailey", "name": "OLA director (Oct 2026)", "tieType": "appointment (WH Office of Legislative Affairs director)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-10", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-15 (v13)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-15", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-15-powermap-v13-V-trump-bailey-ola-director", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE appointment: President Trump named Katie Bailey Director of the White House Office of Legislative Affairs on or about Oct 10-11 2026, replacing James Braid (CBS News Oct 10; Trump Truth Social confirmation reported by CBS/The Hill). She had been deputy director / special assistant. Appointment only.", "citation": ["https://www.cbsnews.com/news/katie-bailey-new-head-of-white-house-office-of-legislative-affairs-sources/", "https://thehill.com/homenews/administration/6141177-trump-names-katie-bailey-legislative-director/"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-sonderling-labor-secretary", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/keith-sonderling", "name": "Labor Secretary (confirmed Sep 30)", "tieType": "appointment / Senate confirmation (Secretary of Labor)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-09-30 confirmed; sworn 2026-10-02", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-15 (v13)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-15", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-15-powermap-v13-V-trump-sonderling-labor-secretary", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE confirmation: Senate confirmed Keith Sonderling as Secretary of Labor Sep 30 2026 by 47-41 (roll call 256, PN1129); sworn Oct 2 2026 (Senate.gov; DOL). Had been Acting Secretary since Apr 2026. Appointment only.", "citation": ["https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1192/vote_119_2_00256.htm", "https://www.dol.gov/agencies/osec/keith-sonderling"]}, {"@id": "tie/susie-wiles-katie-wiles-family", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/susie-wiles", "to": "node/katie-wiles", "name": "mother/daughter", "tieType": "family (mother / daughter)", "category": "family", "kind": "register", "date": "ongoing (reported 2026-10)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-16 (v14)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-16", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-16-powermap-v14-V-susie-wiles-katie-wiles-family", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE family tie: Katie Wiles is the daughter of White House chief of staff Susie Wiles (CBS Oct 8 2026; NYT Oct 15 2026). White House official: Susie Wiles does not discuss work matters with her daughters (SAID). Family tie only.", "citation": ["https://www.cbsnews.com/news/russia-trump-susie-wiles-milorad-dodik-bosnia-serbia/", "https://dnyuz.com/2026/10/15/more-trump-allies-aided-pro-russian-balkan-government/"]}, {"@id": "tie/katie-wiles-continental-strategy-partner", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/katie-wiles", "to": "node/continental-strategy-alex-garcia-et-al", "name": "partner", "tieType": "employment (partner)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "as of 2026-10 (firm website)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-16 (v14)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-16", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-16-powermap-v14-V-katie-wiles-continental-strategy-partner", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE employment: Katie Wiles is a partner at Continental Strategy per the firm's website (CBS); NYT says Continental counts several former Trump campaign/administration officials among its partners plus Katie Wiles. Firm SAID she does not lobby the US government for any client and has not spoken with any US official about Srpska.", "citation": ["https://www.cbsnews.com/news/russia-trump-susie-wiles-milorad-dodik-bosnia-serbia/", "https://dnyuz.com/2026/10/15/more-trump-allies-aided-pro-russian-balkan-government/"]}, {"@id": "tie/srpska-continental-strategy-fara-35k", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/republika-srpska-govt-dodik-snsd", "to": "node/continental-strategy-alex-garcia-et-al", "name": "$35K/mo FARA (2026-02-)", "tieType": "funding (FARA lobbying retainer, $35K/month)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-02 onward", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-16 (v14)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-16", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-16-powermap-v14-V-srpska-continental-strategy-fara-35k", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE money flow: per Justice Department FARA filings (NYT), Republika Srpska began paying Continental Strategy $35,000 a month in February 2026; CBS reviewed FARA filings showing Continental registered for Srpska in early 2026, with Alejandro (Alex) Garcia signing as consultant. Lobbying retainer only; no claim it bought a named US decision.", "citation": ["https://dnyuz.com/2026/10/15/more-trump-allies-aided-pro-russian-balkan-government/", "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/russia-trump-susie-wiles-milorad-dodik-bosnia-serbia/"]}, {"@id": "tie/susie-wiles-cvijanovic-wh-meeting-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/susie-wiles", "to": "node/zeljka-cvijanovic-srpska-snsd", "name": "WH meeting (Sep 2026)", "tieType": "meeting (White House; arranged by Continental's Alex Garcia)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-09", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-16 (v14)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-16", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-16-powermap-v14-V-susie-wiles-cvijanovic-wh-meeting-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE meeting: WH chief of staff Susie Wiles met Zeljka Cvijanovic, a close Dodik ally, at the White House in September 2026; a White House official told CBS the meeting was arranged by Continental partner Alex Garcia, not by Katie Wiles (SAID). The Srpska official posted photos ('building new and strengthening old friendships', NYT). Sequence with the Continental retainer; no causation claimed.", "citation": ["https://www.cbsnews.com/news/russia-trump-susie-wiles-milorad-dodik-bosnia-serbia/", "https://dnyuz.com/2026/10/15/more-trump-allies-aided-pro-russian-balkan-government/"]}, {"@id": "tie/srpska-blair-lacivita-paid-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/republika-srpska-govt-dodik-snsd", "to": "node/james-blair-chris-lacivita-maga-inc", "name": "paid via Boies Schiller (Oct 2026)", "tieType": "funding (paid election consulting via Boies Schiller Flexner; hundreds of thousands $ each)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10 (trip before Oct 4 vote; reported 2026-10-06)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-16 (v14)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-16", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-16-powermap-v14-V-srpska-blair-lacivita-paid-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE: Blair and LaCivita travelled to Republika Srpska before its Oct 4 2026 elections and were paid hundreds of thousands of dollars each through Boies Schiller Flexner, a law firm retained by the Srpska government (NYT Oct 6, via CNN; NYT Oct 15). Dodik's party won and he thanked Trump and Putin. SAID Trump (Truth Social Oct 7): they are outside consultants; 'if there's a conflict, I will terminate them, immediately!' — later 'They don't have a conflict'. No termination as of Oct 16.", "citation": ["https://www.cnn.com/2026/10/07/politics/trump-fire-james-blair-chris-lacivita", "https://dnyuz.com/2026/10/15/more-trump-allies-aided-pro-russian-balkan-government/"]}, {"@id": "tie/flynn-srpska-fara-lobbyist-oct2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/michael-flynn", "to": "node/republika-srpska-govt-dodik-snsd", "name": "FARA lobbyist (Oct 2025)", "tieType": "employment (paid FARA-registered lobbyist)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-10", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-16 (v14)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-16", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-16-powermap-v14-V-flynn-srpska-fara-lobbyist-oct2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE: FARA filings cited in a House Democratic report and reviewed by CBS show Michael Flynn worked as a paid lobbyist for Republika Srpska in October 2025 — the month OFAC lifted the Dodik sanctions (Oct 29 2025, OFAC recent action). The two facts are a sequence; no causal link is claimed by this edge.", "citation": ["https://www.cbsnews.com/news/russia-trump-susie-wiles-milorad-dodik-bosnia-serbia/", "https://ofac.treasury.gov/recent-actions/20251029"]}, {"@id": "tie/srpska-delisting-aafs-pipeline-sequence", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/republika-srpska-govt-dodik-snsd", "to": "node/aafs-infrastructure-energy-binnall-joseph-flynn", "name": "delisting ... pipeline lead (seq)", "tieType": "sequence: OFAC sanctions delisting (2025-10-29) ... AAFS named lead pipeline developer", "category": "pardon/settlement", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-10-29 delisting ; by ~2026-04 lead-developer law", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": true, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-16 (v14)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-16", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-16-powermap-v14-V-srpska-delisting-aafs-pipeline-sequence", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "Sequence only. A: OFAC removed Dodik and 47 others (family, allies, companies) from the SDN list Oct 29 2025 (OFAC recent action; RFE/RL). B: within six months Dodik's party dropped its opposition and Bosnia's parliament passed legislation naming AAFS (Binnall / Joseph Flynn) lead developer of the Bosnia-Croatia gas pipeline (CBS, citing a House Democratic report). House Democrats allege the delisting enriched Trump allies; White House says it prevented Balkan instability (SAID). Two documented facts in time order; this edge claims no cause.", "citation": ["https://ofac.treasury.gov/recent-actions/20251029", "https://www.rferl.org/a/us-pro-russian-bosnian-serb-dodik-sanctions-list/33576314.html", "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/russia-trump-susie-wiles-milorad-dodik-bosnia-serbia/"]}, {"@id": "tie/trumpjr-america-first-refining-stake", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump-jr", "to": "node/america-first-refining-txc-energy-john-calce", "name": "minority stake (2025-)", "tieType": "ownership (minority stake via TX Fuels LLC)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2025 (TX Fuels LLC registered 2025-06) ; reported 2026-06-09", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-16 (v14)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-16", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-16-powermap-v14-V-trumpjr-america-first-refining-stake", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE ownership: Donald Trump Jr. secretly acquired a stake in America First Refining via a Wyoming LLC (TX Fuels) registered at his Jupiter FL address (ProPublica Jun 9 2026, records + seven people); his spokesperson SAID he is 'simply a passive minority investor'. NYT Oct 15: AFR shares an address with TXC Energy, whose CEO Calce Katie Wiles escorted to Srpska. Trump personally announced Reliance's AFR investment on Truth Social (Mar 2026). Size of stake undisclosed.", "citation": ["https://www.propublica.org/article/trump-ambani-reliance-industries-america-first-refining-texas", "https://dnyuz.com/2026/10/15/more-trump-allies-aided-pro-russian-balkan-government/"]}, {"@id": "tie/afr-continental-strategy-lobbying-750k", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/america-first-refining-txc-energy-john-calce", "to": "node/continental-strategy-alex-garcia-et-al", "name": "$750K lobbying", "tieType": "funding (lobbying fees $750K; WH + Energy Dept)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-2026 (lobbying records; reported 2026-10-15)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-16 (v14)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-16", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-16-powermap-v14-V-afr-continental-strategy-lobbying-750k", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE money flow: America First Refining and a predecessor company have paid Continental Strategy $750,000 to lobby the White House and the Energy Department on the Brownsville refinery and 'energy and industrial development', per lobbying records (NYT Oct 15 2026). Alex Garcia, not Katie Wiles, is the listed lobbyist on the account. Closes a loop: Don Jr.'s portfolio company pays the firm where the chief of staff's daughter is a partner.", "citation": ["https://dnyuz.com/2026/10/15/more-trump-allies-aided-pro-russian-balkan-government/"]}, {"@id": "tie/cantor-america-first-refining-adviser", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/brandon-kyle-lutnick-cantor", "to": "node/america-first-refining-txc-energy-john-calce", "name": "AFR adviser (2026-03)", "tieType": "business (Cantor = AFR adviser on nine-figure Reliance raise)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-03", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-16 (v14)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-16", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-16-powermap-v14-V-cantor-america-first-refining-adviser", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "reference", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE: Cantor Fitzgerald — run by Commerce Secretary Lutnick's sons since he joined the cabinet — announced it is financial adviser to America First Refining, including on the Ambani/Reliance nine-figure investment (ProPublica Jun 9 2026, citing Cantor's announcement; Cantor declined comment). Same company Don Jr. holds a stake in.", "citation": ["https://www.propublica.org/article/trump-ambani-reliance-industries-america-first-refining-texas"]}, {"@id": "tie/katie-wiles-calce-srpska-trip-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/katie-wiles", "to": "node/america-first-refining-txc-energy-john-calce", "name": "Srpska trip w/ Calce [I]", "tieType": "contact (accompanied Calce to Srpska; comms client)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-08 (mid-Aug, two days)", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-16 (v14)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-16", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-16-powermap-v14-I-katie-wiles-calce-srpska-trip-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "BOTH, partly supported: Katie Wiles went to Republika Srpska for two days in mid-Aug 2026 (CBS verified photo with interior minister Zeljko Budimir; Continental SAID the trip was strategic-comms support for a US company she has served for over two years). NYT names that company as TXC Energy (John V. Calce), exploring a Croatia-Srpska gas pipeline with the Srpska government, on three unnamed people. Trip is DONE; the client identity rests on anonymous sourcing.", "citation": ["https://www.cbsnews.com/news/russia-trump-susie-wiles-milorad-dodik-bosnia-serbia/", "https://dnyuz.com/2026/10/15/more-trump-allies-aided-pro-russian-balkan-government/"]}, {"@id": "tie/andriesz-bgc-lutnick-whistleblower", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/simon-andriesz", "to": "node/howard-lutnick", "name": "ex-BGC whistleblower", "tieType": "employment (ex-senior employee, BGC Partners) + whistleblower reports", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "ex-BGC (dates not given) ; FCA/FBI reports 2018-2026 ; d. 2026-09-23", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-16 (v14)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-16", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-16-powermap-v14-V-andriesz-bgc-lutnick-whistleblower", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE: Andriesz was a former senior employee of BGC Partners, the firm Lutnick founded and ran; in 2026 he raised evidence of Epstein-Lutnick business links with the FCA, FBI and other watchdogs (BBC Oct 6 2026). SAID (his evidence): Lutnick in 2013 offered Andrew Mountbatten-Windsor a JV for a GBP1m loan; BGC says the JV did not go ahead. He died in Thailand Sep 23 2026; his family says he took his own life with no suggestion of foul play; FCA board member Lea Paterson is reviewing the FCA's handling. Employment + reporting tie; the death is a later fact in sequence, no causation claimed.", "citation": ["https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwm2686gl6kno"]}, {"@id": "tie/grenell-tx-at-consulting-2024", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/ric-grenell", "to": "node/tx-at-texas-defense-security-equipment-co", "name": "consulted 2024 (SAID)", "tieType": "employment (consultant 2024; SAID by Grenell)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2024 (consulting) ; 2025-05 alleged Mildon wire", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-16 (v14)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-16", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-16-powermap-v14-V-grenell-tx-at-consulting-2024", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "SAID by Grenell (NYT Oct 16 2026): he consulted for TX-AT in 2024 but had no connection to the company when Mildon says he made the transfer, and never solicited payments for it. Separately (I, SAID by Habba): Mildon wired $17.6M in May 2025 to TX-AT at Grenell's direction, $5.6M meant for the Kennedy Center; Mildon's lawyer sent WH Counsel Scharf a wire receipt and texts; NYT has not verified them; Grenell denies. Consulting tie held as Grenell's own SAID; the wire allegation stays I.", "citation": ["https://dnyuz.com/2026/10/16/behind-a-white-house-feud-that-is-bitter-even-by-trump-era-standards/"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-musk-national-medal-science-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/elon-musk", "name": "Nat'l Medal of Science (Oct 8)", "tieType": "honor (National Medal of Science, presented by the President)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-08", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-19 (v15)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-19", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-19-powermap-v15-V-trump-musk-national-medal-science-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE: White House release (Oct 8 2026): at the Science: A New Golden Age Summit, President Trump presented the National Medal of Science to Elon Musk, with Sergey Brin, Jensen Huang and Lisa Su; Michael Dell and Satya Nadella received the National Medal of Technology and Innovation. Context on the map: Musk is a current co-director of the Department of War's Project Meridian study and SpaceX is a major federal contractor. Honor and contracts sit side by side in time; no causation claimed.", "citation": ["https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/10/president-trump-presents-national-medals-of-science-and-national-medals-of-technology-and-innovation/"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-netanyahu-endorsement-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/benjamin-netanyahu", "name": "'Complete and Total Endorsement' (Oct 18)", "tieType": "political endorsement (Truth Social letter, Israel's Oct 27 2026 election)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-15 (Newsmax: not getting involved) ; 2026-10-18 (endorsement) ; 2026-10-19 (call video)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-19 (v15)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-28", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-19-powermap-v15-V-trump-netanyahu-endorsement-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 5, "description": "SAID by Trump (Truth Social letter 'To the Great People of Israel', Oct 18 2026): his 'Complete and Total Endorsement' of Netanyahu for re-election; 'If Israel has the wrong Leader, which would be anyone other than Bibi, America will have to do this work ourselves, and I am not inclined to do so'; Iran 'unless they change their ways, rapidly, we will soon finish the job' (conditional; no operation DONE). Sequence: Oct 15 Newsmax, Trump said he was not getting involved; Oct 18 endorsed; Oct 19 Netanyahu posted a 91-second video of the call ('we have a job to finish'). Oct 19 VP Vance SAID 'I'm not getting involved in Israeli elections' (Politico/Reuters), splitting from the President a day later.", "citation": ["https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/trump-gives-warrior-netanyahu-complete-and-total-endorsement-for-reelection/", "https://nypost.com/2026/10/18/us-news/trump-endorses-netanyahu-ahead-of-israels-elections/", "https://www.jpost.com/israel-election-2026/article-912080", "https://x.com/netanyahu/status/2112221725379514437", "https://www.politico.com/news/2026/10/19/jd-vance-declines-to-endorse-netanyahu-for-reelection-01127435"]}, {"@id": "tie/ellison-musk-twitter-equity-1b", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/larry-ellison", "to": "node/elon-musk", "name": "$1B Twitter equity (2022)", "tieType": "funding (equity commitment $1B, Twitter buyout; Lawrence J. Ellison Revocable Trust)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2022-05-05 (SC 13D/A) ; 2026-10-17 (TikTok suspends 'Musk' film ad account)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-19 (v15)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-19", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-19-powermap-v15-V-ellison-musk-twitter-equity-1b", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (SEC SC 13D/A filed by Elon Musk re Twitter, May 5 2022): 'Lawrence J. Ellison Revocable Trust $1,000,000,000', the largest listed co-investor equity commitment. Later, separate: on Oct 17 2026 TikTok, in which Oracle holds 15% of the US JV, suspended the paid advertising account for Alex Gibney's documentary 'Musk', in which Ellison appears (THR; the non-paid account stayed visible per THR). Both facts are DONE; any motive linking them is not shown. Whether each May 2022 commitment funded at the Oct 2022 close is a hole.", "citation": ["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1418091/000110465922056055/tm2214608-1_sc13da.htm", "https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/politics-news/musk-movie-tiktok-banned-theaters-showtimes-1236734308/", "https://www.theverge.com/tech/1013453/tiktok-bans-alex-gibneys-musk-documentary"]}, {"@id": "tie/binance-musk-twitter-equity-500m", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/binance-changpeng-zhao", "to": "node/elon-musk", "name": "$500M Twitter equity (2022)", "tieType": "funding (equity commitment $500M, Twitter buyout)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2022-05-05 (SC 13D/A) ; CZ pardon 2025-10-21", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-19 (v15)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-30", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-19-powermap-v15-V-binance-musk-twitter-equity-500m", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (SEC SC 13D/A, May 5 2022): Binance committed $500,000,000 of equity to Musk's Twitter buyout. Separately DONE: Trump pardoned Binance founder Changpeng Zhao on Oct 21 2025 (DOJ Pardon Attorney list), after the MGX/Binance USD1 deal with World Liberty Financial already on the map. Funding 2022 ... pardon 2025 is a sequence; no causation claimed.", "citation": ["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1418091/000110465922056055/tm2214608-1_sc13da.htm", "https://www.justice.gov/pardon/clemency-grants-president-donald-j-trump-2025-present"]}, {"@id": "tie/qatar-holding-musk-twitter-equity-375m", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/qatar-holding-qia", "to": "node/elon-musk", "name": "$375M Twitter equity (2022)", "tieType": "funding (equity commitment $375M, Twitter buyout)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2022-05-05 (SC 13D/A)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-19 (v15)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-19", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-19-powermap-v15-V-qatar-holding-musk-twitter-equity-375m", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE (SEC SC 13D/A, May 5 2022): Qatar Holding LLC, the Qatar Investment Authority's investment arm, committed $375,000,000 of equity to Musk's Twitter buyout. Qatari state money also appears on the map in the Skydance/CNN-CBS financing (PIF/QIA/L'IMAD). Whether the commitment funded at the Oct 2022 close is a hole.", "citation": ["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1418091/000110465922056055/tm2214608-1_sc13da.htm"]}, {"@id": "tie/witkoff-capital-musk-twitter-equity-100m", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/steve-witkoff", "to": "node/elon-musk", "name": "Witkoff Capital $100M (2022)", "tieType": "funding (Witkoff Capital equity commitment $100M, Twitter buyout)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2022-05-05 (SC 13D/A) ; envoy 2025-", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-19 (v15)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-19", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-19-powermap-v15-V-witkoff-capital-musk-twitter-equity-100m", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (SEC SC 13D/A, May 5 2022): Witkoff Capital committed $100,000,000 of equity to Musk's Twitter buyout; Slate's 2022 investor guide identifies Witkoff Capital as Steve Witkoff's firm. Witkoff later became Trump's special envoy (2025-). Same filing lists Ellison $1B, Binance $500M and Qatar Holding $375M. Whether the commitment funded at the Oct 2022 close is a hole.", "citation": ["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1418091/000110465922056055/tm2214608-1_sc13da.htm", "https://slate.com/technology/2022/05/elon-musks-twitter-investors-a-guide-to-whos-who.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/doe-williams-constitution-pipeline-dpa-42m", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/us-doe-sec-chris-wright", "to": "node/williams-cos-constitution-pipeline", "name": "DPA Title III up to $42M", "tieType": "government funding (Defense Production Act Title III, up to $42M)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-19", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-19 (v15)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-19", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-19-powermap-v15-V-doe-williams-constitution-pipeline-dpa-42m", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE: DOE announced (Oct 19 2026) up to $42M in DPA Title III funds for Williams' 125-mile Constitution Pipeline (Susquehanna Co. PA to Schoharie Co. NY), for pre-construction and permitting work, under Presidential Determination No. 2026-12 (gas pipelines essential to national defense), from $1B appropriated under the 'Working Families Tax Cut'. SAID: Wright says construction could start 'next spring', service by winter 2028. NOT DONE: no permits; FERC's earlier authorizations were vacated after the 2nd Circuit and the proceedings dismissed (FERC May 19 2026); NY DEC opposed. A defense-emergency label is SAID; the money is DONE.", "citation": ["https://www.energy.gov/articles/energy-department-advances-constitution-pipeline-project-42-million-defense-production-act", "https://www.energy.gov/hgeo/defense-production-act-title-iii-constitution-pipeline-project"]}, {"@id": "tie/puzder-spacex-eu-spectrum-threat", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/andrew-puzder-us-ambassador-to-eu", "to": "node/spacex", "name": "threatens EU over Starlink spectrum", "tieType": "official advocacy (SAID: 'devastating' retaliation if EU restricts 2 GHz spectrum for US firms incl. SpaceX/Starlink)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-18", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-19 (v15)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-19", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-19-powermap-v15-V-puzder-spacex-eu-spectrum-threat", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID by US Ambassador to the EU Andrew Puzder (FT, Oct 18 2026; AA): European firms could face 'devastating' US retaliation if Brussels reserves most of the 2 GHz direct-to-device band for European operators, cutting access for US firms including SpaceX/Starlink and Amazon. No retaliation DONE; the EU plan is not yet law. Same week: Rubio SAID (Oct 17) 'nobody ordered' the Starlink slowdown in Ukraine and Starshield is 'not at this moment available to Ukraine'. A US ambassador is acting as the voice of a contractor whose CEO co-directs a Pentagon study; no payment or instruction shown.", "citation": ["https://www.ft.com/content/d1e28d93-8574-4a46-946a-b261c401d6fa", "https://www.aa.com.tr/en/americas/us-warns-eu-of-devastating-retaliation-over-satellite-spectrum-plans/4092940"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-john-g-trump-uncle-tesla-1943", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/john-g-trump-1907-1985", "name": "uncle; 1943 Tesla papers assessor", "tieType": "family (paternal uncle)", "category": "family", "kind": "register", "date": "1907-1985 ; Tesla papers report 1943-01-30", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-19 (v15)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-19", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-19-powermap-v15-V-trump-john-g-trump-uncle-tesla-1943", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE: John G. Trump (1907-1985) was the President's paternal uncle (Physics Today; NYT obituary 1985). He was secretary of the NDRC Microwave Committee/Division 14 (radar) and NDRC liaison to the MIT Rad Lab. FBI Vault Tesla file Part 01: his two-page report of Jan 30 1943 to Walter Gorsuch (Office of Alien Property), signed 'Technical Aide, Division 14, NDRC', judged Tesla's papers of no significant value. That verdict is SAID by a sole assessor inside the wartime research establishment, written while the 1940-42 invention-secrecy law was in force; no independent check of the papers was found. National Medal of Science (1983 citation, presented posthumously by Reagan 1985).", "citation": ["https://physicstoday.aip.org/news/a-profile-of-john-trump-donalds-oft-mentioned-scientist-uncle", "https://vault.fbi.gov/nikola-tesla/Nikola%20Tesla%20Part%2001/view", "https://www.nsf.gov/honorary-awards/national-medal-science/recipients/john-g-trump"]}, {"@id": "tie/drc-finance-txat-17-6m-wire", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/drc-finance-ministry-kinshasa", "to": "node/tx-at-texas-defense-security-equipment-co", "name": "$17.6M wire (I, SAID)", "tieType": "funding (wire $17.6M, 2025-05-29; per an unnamed WH official's reading of the wire record)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-05-03 (alleged Grenell text) ; 2025-05-29 (wire) ; 2026-10-19 (Axios)", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-19 (v15)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-20", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-19-powermap-v15-I-drc-finance-txat-17-6m-wire", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "SAID (Axios, Oct 19 2026): an unnamed White House official says the May 29 2025 wire record shows the $17.6M sent to Texas Armament & Technology (Houston) came from Congo's 'Ministere des Finances', Kinshasa, not from Turhan Mildon's account ('We're trying to find out whose money this is'). SAID by Mildon via attorneys: he wired it at Grenell's direction, ~$5.6M meant for the Kennedy Center, which never got it. Axios reviewed a May 3 2025 text allegedly from Grenell: 'Once the money comes to the company here, I will arrange the donation to Kennedy Centre...'. Grenell SAID 'lies' and denies sending it. WH Counsel Will Scharf is reviewing (sources). Kennedy Center records show only a $270K Mildon pledge (Axios Oct 14). Graded I: the sender identity rests on one anonymous official; TX-AT, Congo and Mildon's lawyers did not confirm.", "citation": ["https://www.axios.com/2026/10/19/kennedy-center-text-trump-grenell-habba", "https://www.axios.com/2026/10/14/trump-kennedy-center-donation-maga-feud"]}, {"@id": "tie/alfozan-saudi-royal-contact", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/abdulrahman-alfozan-ex-openai-engineer", "to": "node/saudi-royal-unnamed-in-doj-memo", "name": "WhatsApp contact (prosecutors' SAID)", "tieType": "contact (frequent WhatsApp 2025-26; SAID by US prosecutors)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2025 - 2026-10-05 ; arrest 2026-10-09 ; memo 2026-10-18", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-19 (v15)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-20", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-19-powermap-v15-V-alfozan-saudi-royal-contact", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID by US prosecutors (N.D. Cal. detention memo, US v. Alfozan, 3:26-mj-71329, Dkt 12, Oct 18 2026): ex-OpenAI engineer Abdulrahman Alfozan was 'in frequent communication via WhatsApp with a member of the Saudi Royal Family' in 2025-26, as recently as Oct 5; that person pitched a Saudi AI initiative and wrote 'Saudi needs you more then the US!' (Alfozan: '100'). After his Oct 9 arrest his wife and son left on a one-way ticket 'booked and paid for by a Saudi military official'. DONE (CNBC Oct 19): held without bail. No espionage or foreign-agent charge filed; the royal is unnamed; Saudi government had not commented.", "citation": ["https://cdn.arstechnica.net/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/US-v-Alfozan-Memo-in-Support-of-Motion-for-Detention-10-18-26.pdf", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/19/openai-bugging-suspect-alfozan-saudi-royal-family.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/alfozan-openai-employment", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/abdulrahman-alfozan-ex-openai-engineer", "to": "node/frontier-ai-labs-openai-anthropic-google-meta", "name": "ex-OpenAI engineer", "tieType": "employment (ex-OpenAI engineer)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "to 2026-10 ; arrest 2026-10-09", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-19 (v15)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-19", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-19-powermap-v15-V-alfozan-openai-employment", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE: Alfozan is a former OpenAI engineer charged after a hidden recording device was found (arrest Oct 9 2026), per the DOJ detention memo and CNBC (Oct 19 2026). Employment tie only; it links the Saudi-royal contact above to the frontier-lab node.", "citation": ["https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/19/openai-bugging-suspect-alfozan-saudi-royal-family.html", "https://cdn.arstechnica.net/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/US-v-Alfozan-Memo-in-Support-of-Motion-for-Detention-10-18-26.pdf"]}, {"@id": "tie/shawn-ryan-anduril-investor", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/shawn-ryan-podcast-host", "to": "node/anduril", "name": "investor (self-disclosed)", "tieType": "ownership (minority investor since Oct 2025; self-disclosed)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-10 - present", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-19 (v15)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-19", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-19-powermap-v15-V-shawn-ryan-anduril-investor", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "social", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (self-disclosed, LinkedIn): Shawn Ryan lists himself as an investor in Anduril Industries since Oct 2025 and Shield AI since Nov 2025. SAID by Ryan (Oct 19 2026 episode note): 'my investments, I've intentionally made them public ... I invest in Shield AI and Anduril'. Founders Fund (Thiel) and a16z are separate Anduril investors already on the map; a shared cap table is not a joint investment with Thiel personally. Leah Files' account that she was told not to name names is one party's SAID (UNVERIFIED).", "citation": ["https://linkedin.com/in/shawn-ryan-84b97314a", "https://podcasts.apple.com/sr/podcast/my-unredacted-interview-with-the-leah-files/id1492492083?i=1000797160445"]}, {"@id": "tie/dow-oracle-enterprise-software-7b", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/us-dept-of-war-pentagon", "to": "node/larry-ellison", "name": "~$7B enterprise software (Jul 2026)", "tieType": "government contract (Enterprise Software Agreement, up to 10 yrs, ~$7B; all DoW + Coast Guard + Intelligence Community)", "category": "contract", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-07-23", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-19 (v15)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-19", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-19-powermap-v15-V-dow-oracle-enterprise-software-7b", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE (DoW CIO, Jul 23 2026): the Department of War awarded Oracle an Enterprise Software Agreement of up to 10 years, about $7B ($3.31B over the 5-year base, $6.99B with options), negotiated by the Navy, covering all of DoW plus the Coast Guard and the Intelligence Community. Oracle is chaired by Larry Ellison (alias on this map).", "citation": ["https://dowcio.war.gov/In-the-News/Article/4554232/dow-awards-a-nearly-7-billion-oracle-agreement-to-accelerate-the-arsenal-of-fre/"]}, {"@id": "tie/ellison-fidf-16-6m-2017", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/larry-ellison", "to": "node/friends-of-the-idf-fidf", "name": "$16.6M gift (2017)", "tieType": "funding (gift $16.6M; largest single gift in FIDF history)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2017-11-02", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-19 (v15)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-19", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-19-powermap-v15-V-ellison-fidf-16-6m-2017", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (Times of Israel; JTA, Nov 2017): at the FIDF Western gala in Beverly Hills on Nov 2 2017, Larry Ellison gave $16.6M, the largest single gift in FIDF history, earmarked for well-being facilities on an IDF training campus. Claims of 'close personal ties to Netanyahu' are not graded here (not re-sourced).", "citation": ["https://www.timesofisrael.com/record-53-8-million-raised-for-idf-soldiers-at-beverly-hills-gala/", "https://www.jta.org/2017/11/05/united-states/record-53-8-million-raised-for-idf-soldiers-at-beverly-hills-gala"]}, {"@id": "tie/exim-mesabi-770m-loan", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/us-export-import-bank-exim", "to": "node/mesabi-metallics", "name": "$770M direct loan (2026-09)", "tieType": "government financing (EXIM board-approved $770M direct loan for the Nashwauk MN iron-ore mine; separate EXIM indication of support noted in claim)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-09 (board approval, week before Sep 28)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-20 (v16)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-20", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-20-powermap-v16-V-exim-mesabi-770m-loan", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (EXIM release, Sep 28 2026): EXIM's board approved a $770M direct loan for Mesabi Metallics' Minnesota iron-ore mine the week before the Oval Office event; Mesabi's Jun 1 2026 release says it also holds an EXIM 'indication of support' of up to $10B. The only other EXIM package near that size is a $10B critical-minerals reserve (Star Tribune). Other lenders: Breakwall Capital/Vitol $520M, Macquarie $150M.", "citation": ["https://www.exim.gov/news/exim-chairman-jovanovic-oval-office-it-all-starts-mining-more-america", "https://www.mesabimetallics.com/mesabi-metallics-monetizes-portion-of-royalty-interest-for-265-million/", "https://www.startribune.com/trump-allies-stand-to-gain-from-minnesota-ore-company-with-iowa-steel-dreams/601898816"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-mesabi-oval-announcement-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/mesabi-metallics", "name": "Oval launch of Iowa mill (Sep 28 2026)", "tieType": "presidential promotion (Oval Office announcement of Mesabi's Iowa steel mill, Sep 28 2026; no money from Trump)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-09-28", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-20 (v16)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-20", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-20-powermap-v16-V-trump-mesabi-oval-announcement-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 4, "description": "DONE (White House, Sep 28 2026): Trump announced Mesabi Metallics' 15-billion-dollar Lee County, Iowa steel plant from the Oval Office, flanked by Lutnick, Wright, EXIM chair Jovanovic and the Ruia family. SAID (Lutnick): 'this deal's done'; WH officials said it did not depend on local incentives. DONE next: Iowa called a special session the next day and Gov. Reynolds signed HF 2801 on Oct 2 (MEGA credit up to 10%); the preliminary state package shown to lawmakers is about USD 1.36B (SAID, Des Moines Register via IPR); the IEDA board has not approved a final contract.", "citation": ["https://x.com/WhiteHouse/status/2104647442750951721", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/09/28/trump-steel-plant-iowa.html", "https://governor.iowa.gov/press-release/2026-10-02/gov-reynolds-signs-legislative-amendments-mega-program-paving-way-historic-15-billion-steel-mill", "https://www.iowapublicradio.org/political-news/2026-10-02/state-lawmakers-special-session-tax-breaks-steel-plant"]}, {"@id": "tie/jason-miller-mesabi-lobbyist", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jason-miller", "to": "node/mesabi-metallics", "name": "registered lobbyist (SHW Partners) -> EXIM/WH", "tieType": "lobbying (registered federal lobbyist via SHW Partners LLC; LDA reports list contacts at EXIM, the White House Office, Commerce, Energy, Treasury, Interior, USTR)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2025 - 2026", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-20 (v16)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-20", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-20-powermap-v16-V-jason-miller-mesabi-lobbyist", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (Senate/House LDA, SHW Partners LLC for client Mesabi Metallics Company LLC; Q3 2025 report filed Oct 20 2025): lobbyist Jason Miller; issues incl. Sections 232/301 trade actions; agencies contacted incl. EXIM Bank and the White House Office. Q4 2025 and Q2 2026 reports show $120,000 each. Star Tribune (Oct 17 2026): Miller lobbied for Mesabi shortly before rejoining the White House and two months before the Oval announcement. Lobbying, then WH job, then EXIM loan/Oval launch is a sequence; no cause claimed. Miller SAID he is 'proud' of bringing in the investment.", "citation": ["https://lobbyingsoftware.com/filing/758253", "https://lobbyingsoftware.com/filing/789871", "https://www.startribune.com/trump-allies-stand-to-gain-from-minnesota-ore-company-with-iowa-steel-dreams/601898816"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-jason-miller-wh-adviser-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/jason-miller", "name": "WH messaging adviser (Jul 2026)", "tieType": "appointment (senior White House messaging adviser, special government employee per reports)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-07 - present", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-20 (v16)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-20", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-20-powermap-v16-V-trump-jason-miller-wh-adviser-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (CNN Jul 1 2026; WaPo Jun 29): Jason Miller rejoined the White House in July 2026 in a senior messaging role for the midterms, described as a special government employee. He had been Mesabi Metallics' registered lobbyist (edge jason-miller-mesabi-lobbyist).", "citation": ["https://www.cnn.com/2026/07/01/politics/jason-miller-white-house-trump", "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2026/06/29/former-trump-adviser-jason-miller-eyed-join-white-house-midterms-shake-up/"]}, {"@id": "tie/tmcr-mesabi-royalty-265m", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/the-metals-royalty-company-tmcr", "to": "node/mesabi-metallics", "name": "$265M royalty purchase (2026)", "tieType": "financing / ownership (bought 50% of Mesabi's royalty interest for $265M, two $132.5M tranches; first closed Jun 1 2026)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-06-01", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-20 (v16)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-20", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-20-powermap-v16-V-tmcr-mesabi-royalty-265m", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (Mesabi Metallics release Jun 1 2026; TMCR closing release): TMCR agreed to buy 50% of Mesabi's royalty interest for $265M in two equal tranches; the first closed Jun 1 2026, and TMCR later closed an additional 1.0% royalty, taking its Mesabi interest to 2.0%. Star Tribune: TMCR has no revenue; its other major asset is a royalty on a seabed-mining company that owns 20% of TMCR.", "citation": ["https://www.mesabimetallics.com/mesabi-metallics-monetizes-portion-of-royalty-interest-for-265-million/", "https://www.nasdaq.com/press-release/metals-royalty-company-announces-closing-additional-10-mesabi-royalty-and-us-165", "https://www.startribune.com/trump-allies-stand-to-gain-from-minnesota-ore-company-with-iowa-steel-dreams/601898816"]}, {"@id": "tie/john-hess-tmcr-stake", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/john-hess", "to": "node/the-metals-royalty-company-tmcr", "name": "5% (+ son Michael 5.2%, co-chair)", "tieType": "ownership (John Hess 5% of TMCR common; son Michael Hess 5.2% and board co-chair, co-founder per an SEC filing)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-20 (v16)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-20", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-20-powermap-v16-V-john-hess-tmcr-stake", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE (SEC filings per Star Tribune, Oct 17 2026): John Hess owns 5% of TMCR's common stock and his son Michael Hess 5.2%; Michael is board co-chair and is listed as co-founder in one SEC filing. TMCR holds 2.0% of Mesabi's royalty. Star Tribune: Ivanka Trump and Jared Kushner reportedly attended Michael Hess's 2019 wedding (I, social). Trump SAID at a 2025 bill signing that John Hess is 'a friend of mine for a long time'. The Hess family did not respond.", "citation": ["https://www.startribune.com/trump-allies-stand-to-gain-from-minnesota-ore-company-with-iowa-steel-dreams/601898816"]}, {"@id": "tie/john-hess-maga-inc-1m", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/john-hess", "to": "node/maga-inc-pro-trump-super-pac", "name": "$1M (Dec 2025)", "tieType": "funding (donation $1M, Dec 12 2025; plus $1M from his wife per Star Tribune; $1M to Trump's 2017 inauguration)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-12-12", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-20 (v16)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-20", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-20-powermap-v16-V-john-hess-maga-inc-1m", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (FEC Schedule A, MAGA Inc. C00892471): 'HESS, JOHN BRIDGE' $1,000,000 on 2025-12-12. Star Tribune (citing FEC): Hess and his wife each gave $1M to MAGA Inc. in December, and he gave $1M to Trump's 2017 inauguration fund. Donation, then TMCR/Mesabi, then EXIM loan and Oval launch is a sequence; the Star Tribune found no evidence that Trump or his family directly benefit.", "citation": ["https://docquery.fec.gov/cgi-bin/fecimg/?202601029793901866", "https://api.open.fec.gov/v1/schedules/schedule_a/?committee_id=C00892471&contributor_name=hess&min_amount=500000", "https://www.startribune.com/trump-allies-stand-to-gain-from-minnesota-ore-company-with-iowa-steel-dreams/601898816"]}, {"@id": "tie/yorkville-tmcr-financing", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/yorkville-advisors", "to": "node/the-metals-royalty-company-tmcr", "name": "up to $100M equity line", "tieType": "financing (commitment to buy up to $100M of TMCR common; affiliate joined the stock financing for the Mesabi royalty deal)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-20 (v16)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-20", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-20-powermap-v16-V-yorkville-tmcr-financing", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (TMCR securities filings per Star Tribune Oct 17 2026; TMCR 6-K): Yorkville committed to buy up to $100M of TMCR common stock at a discount (the same structure it used with Trump Media), and a Yorkville affiliate joined a stock financing aimed at funding TMCR's Mesabi deal. Yorkville declined to comment.", "citation": ["https://www.startribune.com/trump-allies-stand-to-gain-from-minnesota-ore-company-with-iowa-steel-dreams/601898816", "https://www.stocktitan.net/sec-filings/TMCR/6-k-metals-royalty-co-inc-current-report-foreign-issuer-bb45858a4e18.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/yorkville-trump-media-450m", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/yorkville-advisors", "to": "node/trump-media", "name": "$450M stock buys + ETF sponsor", "tieType": "financing / services (bought ~$450M of TMTG shares under a standby equity agreement; affiliates sponsor Trump Media's ETFs; adviser on the TAE merger)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2024 - present", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-20 (v16)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-20", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-20-powermap-v16-V-yorkville-trump-media-450m", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (SEC filings via Fortune Feb 19 2025; Reuters Sep 10 2025; Star Tribune Oct 17 2026): Yorkville bought about $450M of Trump Media stock (more than half of TMTG's cash at the time), its affiliates manage and sponsor five Trump Media ETFs launched Dec 2025, and it advises on Trump Media's planned merger with TAE Technologies. Trump Media is held via the Trump trust run by Don Jr. (edge tmtg-trust-donjr). The same firm also finances TMCR, the Mesabi royalty buyer.", "citation": ["https://fortune.com/2025/02/19/more-than-half-of-trump-medias-cash-on-hand-came-from-selling-450-million-worth-of-shares-to-a-small-new-jersey-financial-firm/", "https://www.reuters.com/business/trump-media-technology-seeks-sec-approval-five-new-etfs-2025-09-10/", "https://www.startribune.com/trump-allies-stand-to-gain-from-minnesota-ore-company-with-iowa-steel-dreams/601898816"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-herrera-velutini-pardon-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/julio-herrera-velutini", "name": "pardon (Jan 2026)", "tieType": "pardon (full and unconditional, Jan 2026; co-defendants Wanda Vazquez Garced and Mark Rossini pardoned at the same time)", "category": "pardon/settlement", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-01-15", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-20 (v16)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-20", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-20-powermap-v16-V-trump-herrera-velutini-pardon-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (DOJ Office of the Pardon Attorney list): Julio M. Herrera Velutini (D. Puerto Rico; conspiracy, federal program bribery, honest services wire fraud as listed on the warrant) was pardoned, along with ex-Gov. Wanda Vazquez Garced and ex-FBI agent Mark Rossini, before their misdemeanor sentencings (NYT: Jan 15 2026, amended five days later). His lawyer Christopher Kise (ex-Trump legal team) and Ballard Partners (USD 600K Q4 2025 LDA, per CLC) worked the clemency push. WH SAID the review ran through WH Counsel and DOJ.", "citation": ["https://www.justice.gov/pardon/clemency-grants-president-donald-j-trump-2025-present", "https://dnyuz.com/2026/10/20/a-billionaire-wanted-a-trump-pardon-his-family-gave-alina-habba-a-50-million-deal/"]}, {"@id": "tie/herrera-velutini-isabela-herrera-family", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/julio-herrera-velutini", "to": "node/isabela-herrera-concord-partners-banvelca", "name": "father - daughter", "tieType": "family (father - daughter; she leads the family office Banvelca since Jul 2026)", "category": "family", "kind": "register", "date": "lifelong", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-20 (v16)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-20", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-20-powermap-v16-V-herrera-velutini-isabela-herrera-family", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE (NYT Oct 20 2026): Isabela Herrera, 27, an American citizen, is Julio Herrera Velutini's daughter; in July 2026 Banvelca, the family office since 1781, announced she was taking over its leadership.", "citation": ["https://dnyuz.com/2026/10/20/a-billionaire-wanted-a-trump-pardon-his-family-gave-alina-habba-a-50-million-deal/"]}, {"@id": "tie/isabela-herrera-concord-habba-50m", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/isabela-herrera-concord-partners-banvelca", "to": "node/alina-habba", "name": "GC contract >$50M / 4 yrs", "tieType": "employment (general counsel of Concord Partners; $10M/yr for 4 years + bonuses, >$50M guaranteed; began Jan 1 2026 while Habba was a DOJ special government employee and senior adviser to AG Bondi)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-10 (deal) / 2026-01-01 (start) - present", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-20 (v16)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-29", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-20-powermap-v16-V-isabela-herrera-concord-habba-50m", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (NYT Oct 20 2026, interviews + documents): the Herrera family hired Alina Habba as general counsel of Concord Partners, a company Isabela Herrera registered in Florida in late Oct 2025, at $10M a year for four years plus bonuses (more than $50M guaranteed). Habba finalized the deal days after registration and started Jan 1 2026 while still a senior adviser to AG Bondi (office at DOJ, Marshals detail). Weeks later Trump pardoned Herrera Velutini: SEQUENCE, no cause shown. SAID: Habba denies any role in the pardon and says DOJ approved the outside job; DOJ SAID she 'did not speak to anyone about a pardon'; a WH official SAID she had nothing to do with it. People familiar with the contract SAID they believed she was hired to help with the pardon push (unnamed).", "citation": ["https://dnyuz.com/2026/10/20/a-billionaire-wanted-a-trump-pardon-his-family-gave-alina-habba-a-50-million-deal/", "https://www.mediaite.com/crime/billionaire-scored-trump-pardon-after-50-million-deal-with-alina-habba/", "https://www.elnuevodia.com/corresponsalias/washington-dc/notas/herrera-velutini-consiguio-el-indulto-de-trump-despues-de-un-contrato-de-50-millones-a-una-funcionaria-de-justicia-federal/"]}, {"@id": "tie/isabela-herrera-maga-inc-3-5m", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/isabela-herrera-concord-partners-banvelca", "to": "node/maga-inc-pro-trump-super-pac", "name": "$3.5M (2024-25)", "tieType": "funding (donations $2.5M Dec 31 2024 + $1M Jul 22 2025; CLC FEC complaint alleges a straw-donor/foreign-national source)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2024-12-31 / 2025-07-22", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-20 (v16)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-20", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-20-powermap-v16-V-isabela-herrera-maga-inc-3-5m", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (FEC Schedule A, MAGA Inc. C00892471): HERRERA, ISABELA $2,500,000 on 2024-12-31 and $1,000,000 on 2025-07-22. Her prior federal giving was $20 (CLC). SAID (Campaign Legal Center FEC complaint, Feb 17 2026; interested watchdog): the money may have come from her father, a Venezuelan national, which would be a foreign-national/straw-donor violation; no FEC finding yet. WaPo (per Law Commentary): she pledged $2.5M to the White House ballroom on Sep 23 2025 and paid $835,000 on Oct 14 2025. Donations, then pardon (Jan 2026), is a sequence.", "citation": ["https://docquery.fec.gov/cgi-bin/fecimg/?202501319752674491", "https://docquery.fec.gov/cgi-bin/fecimg/?202601029793901866", "https://dnyuz.com/2026/10/20/a-billionaire-wanted-a-trump-pardon-his-family-gave-alina-habba-a-50-million-deal/", "https://www.lawcommentary.com/articles/trump-pardon-alina-habba-50-million-deal"]}, {"@id": "tie/grenell-fix-california-zacharia", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/ric-grenell", "to": "node/katie-zacharia", "name": "Fix California GC (2024-25)", "tieType": "employment (Zacharia listed as general counsel of Grenell's nonprofit Fix California, Jan 2024 - Mar 2025; IRS filings show $27,367 in fundraising commissions to her in 2024, no salary)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2024-01 - 2025-03", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-20 (v16)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-20", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-20-powermap-v16-V-grenell-fix-california-zacharia", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE/SAID: Zacharia's own LinkedIn listed her as full-time General Counsel of Fix California, the California nonprofit Grenell runs, Jan 2024 - Mar 2025 (she removed it by Oct 14 2026); the organization's IRS filings show no salary to her but $27,367 in fundraising commissions in 2024 (Campaign for Accountability State Bar complaint, an interested complainant). Telegraph (Oct 14 2026): Grenell runs a California nonprofit that until recently employed Zacharia. Grenell headed the Kennedy Center and now faces the WH Counsel review over the Mildon gift; Zacharia was named press secretary Oct 9 and was out Oct 16.", "citation": ["https://www.telegraph.co.uk/us/news/2026/10/14/white-house-kennedy-centre-missing-1m/", "https://san.com/wp-content/uploads/securepdfs/2026/10/cfa-ca-bar-katie-zacharia.pdf", "https://linkedin.com/in/katie-zacharia"]}, {"@id": "tie/uk-mod-saudi-defensive-air-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/uk-ministry-of-defence-sec-wes-streeting", "to": "node/kingdom-of-saudi-arabia", "name": "RAF Typhoons + tanking (announced Oct 20 2026)", "tieType": "military support (RAF Typhoon defensive counter-air over Saudi cities, A400M, advisers; extended air-to-air refuelling for Saudi operations incl. degrading Houthi targets)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-20", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-20 (v16)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-20", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-20-powermap-v16-V-uk-mod-saudi-defensive-air-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID (GOV.UK, MoD + Defence Secretary Wes Streeting, Oct 20 2026): 'The UK will fly defensive counter air missions to support the protection of Saudi cities... using RAF Typhoon fighter jets... will not conduct offensive strikes against the Houthis', plus an RAF A400M, advisers to Saudi staff officers, and an extension of air-to-air refuelling 'for Saudi defensive air operations including to degrade Houthi military targets in Yemen'. So UK tankers support Saudi strike sorties. First sortie DONE = not yet confirmed. AP: refuelling extended 90 days.", "citation": ["https://www.gov.uk/government/news/operational-update-20-october-uk-military-support-to-the-kingdom-of-saudi-arabia", "https://apnews.com/article/uk-air-patrols-saudi-houthis-3e56f4679565c985fd036302168a4f79"]}, {"@id": "tie/putin-witkoff-st-petersburg-hubbard-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/vladimir-putin", "to": "node/steve-witkoff", "name": "St Petersburg talks + Hubbard freed (Oct 21 2026)", "tieType": "documented meeting (Constantine Palace, St Petersburg; Kushner by phone; Ushakov + Dmitriev present) + detainee release (Stephen Hubbard)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-21", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-21 (v17)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-21", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-21-powermap-v17-V-putin-witkoff-st-petersburg-hubbard-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (Kremlin transcript, Oct 21 2026): Putin met US special envoy Steve Witkoff at the Constantine Palace, St Petersburg; on the Russian side Presidential Aide Yury Ushakov and RDIF CEO / special envoy Kirill Dmitriev attended; Jared Kushner joined by phone (Witkoff: 'Jared, who I think we will put on the phone shortly'; Al Jazeera: attended virtually). DONE: Russia released Stephen Hubbard (retired US teacher, held since 2022) the same day; Putin: 'He is currently at Pulkovo Airport.' SAID (Witkoff, on the record): 'You are a humanitarian also, sir. I salute that.' SAID (Kremlin/AJ): Putin agreed in principle to resume trilateral US-Russia-Ukraine technical talks (possibly Abu Dhabi); a Trump-Putin-Xi meeting at APEC was raised (Peskov: no agreements). Sequence only, no cause claimed: Trump's Oct 16 EO waived Graham Act Russia sanctions/duties ... Hubbard released Oct 21; Trump now cites Hubbard when defending the waiver (SAID); no document ties the two (hole).", "citation": ["http://en.kremlin.ru/events/president/news/81044", "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/21/what-happened-during-witkoff-and-kushners-latest-meeting-with-putin", "https://www.nbcnews.com/world/russia/russia-released-american-stephen-hubbard-trump-putin-ukraine-war-talks-rcna604730"]}, {"@id": "tie/dmitriev-us-treasury-channel-said-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/kirill-dmitriev", "to": "node/scott-bessent", "name": "Treasury 'working with' Dmitriev (Witkoff SAID)", "tieType": "working channel (SAID by Witkoff: 'Our Treasury Department is working with you now independently')", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-21", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-21 (v17)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-21", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-21-powermap-v17-V-dmitriev-us-treasury-channel-said-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "SAID (US envoy Witkoff to Putin, on the Kremlin's published transcript, Oct 21 2026), addressing Kirill Dmitriev (RDIF CEO, OFAC-designated, Putin's investment envoy): 'You have been outstanding, Kirill... Our Treasury Department is working with you now independently, and I think that is leading to a sense of what possibilities are between our two nations.' Witkoff also thanked Putin for lifting Russian diesel export controls (existing edge trump-putin-call-diesel-gl135). Bessent is the Treasury Secretary; Witkoff named the department, not Bessent personally. V at the office layer as SAID; what work, by whom, and under what OFAC license = DONE hole. Context: Dmitriev was in the Alaska delegation with Bessent/Lutnick (edge dmitriev-alaska-delegation).", "citation": ["http://en.kremlin.ru/events/president/news/81044"]}, {"@id": "tie/melania-trump-putin-humanitarian-channel", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/melania-trump", "to": "node/vladimir-putin", "name": "letter (2025) + 'humanitarian projects' (2026)", "tieType": "personal channel (Aug 2025 letter hand-delivered by Trump at Anchorage; 'humanitarian projects in the Russian Federation', SAID Oct 2026)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-08-15 ; 2026-10-21", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-21 (v17)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-21", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-21-powermap-v17-V-melania-trump-putin-humanitarian-channel", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (AP, Aug 2025): Melania Trump wrote a letter to Putin on protecting children, which Donald Trump hand-delivered at the Aug 15 2025 Anchorage summit. SAID (Kremlin transcript, Oct 21 2026): Putin asked Witkoff to pass 'my most sincere gratitude... to First Lady [Melania Trump] for her contribution to resolving humanitarian issues'; Witkoff: 'I know the First Lady is grateful for being able to work on behalf of some of her humanitarian projects in the Russian Federation.' What those projects are (children's reunifications or other) is not stated in the transcript (hole). Joins trump-putin-alaska-2025 and the Amazon/Melania documentary edge.", "citation": ["https://apnews.com/article/putin-melania-trump-ukraine-bb9b3baab659abc102ceba5d79fa54ff", "http://en.kremlin.ru/events/president/news/81044"]}, {"@id": "tie/rt-flynn-moscow-gala-45k-2015", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/rt-russian-state-tv", "to": "node/michael-flynn", "name": "$45K RT gala fee (2015)", "tieType": "funding (speaking fee $45,000 + expenses, RT 10th-anniversary gala, Moscow; seated at Putin's table)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2015-12-10", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-21 (v17)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-21", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-21-powermap-v17-V-rt-flynn-moscow-gala-45k-2015", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (documents released by House Oversight Democrats, Mar 2017; NBC, PBS): RT paid Flynn $45,000 plus expenses to speak at its Moscow 10th-anniversary gala in Dec 2015 (net $33,750 after his speakers' bureau's cut) and flew him and his son to Moscow; he sat at Putin's table. He also received $11,250 each from Volga-Dnepr (cargo airline) and Kaspersky Lab's US arm in 2015. Register: grokbot-2026-10-21-V-flynn-rt-gala-dec2015-putin-table-paid.", "citation": ["https://oversightdemocrats.house.gov/news/press-releases/cummings-releases-new-documents-confirming-that-flynn-received-funds-from", "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/nation/documents-detail-flynn-payments-russian-interests"]}, {"@id": "tie/flynn-kislyak-sanctions-calls-plea-2017", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/michael-flynn", "to": "node/sergey-kislyak-ex-russian-ambassador-to-us", "name": "sanctions calls; plea 2017", "tieType": "contact (Dec 2016 sanctions calls as incoming NSA) ; prosecution (guilty plea Dec 1 2017, lying to FBI about them)", "category": "pardon/settlement", "kind": "register", "date": "2016-12-29 ; 2017-12-01", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-21 (v17)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-21", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-21-powermap-v17-V-flynn-kislyak-sanctions-calls-plea-2017", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE (Special Counsel statement of the offense; Reuters): in Dec 2016, as incoming national security adviser, Flynn discussed US sanctions and a UN resolution with Russian ambassador Sergey Kislyak, directed in part by a 'very senior member' of the transition team. He pleaded guilty Dec 1 2017 to lying to the FBI about those calls. Later (same scrutiny): DOJ moved to dismiss in May 2020; Trump pardoned him Nov 25 2020 (edge trump-flynn-pardon-2020). Register: grokbot-2026-10-21-V-flynn-kislyak-sanctions-calls-guilty-plea.", "citation": ["https://www.reuters.com/article/world/flynn-pleads-guilty-to-lying-on-russia-cooperates-with-us-probe-idUSKBN1DV50S/", "https://www.reuters.com/article/us-usa-trump-russia-timeline/timeline-u-s-prosecutors-lay-out-flynns-dealings-with-russian-ambassador-idUSKBN1DV5Z3/"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-flynn-pardon-2020", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/michael-flynn", "name": "NSA 2017; pardon 2020", "tieType": "appointment (national security adviser, Jan-Feb 2017) ; pardon (full and unconditional, Nov 25 2020)", "category": "pardon/settlement", "kind": "register", "date": "2017-01-20 ; 2020-11-25", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-21 (v17)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-21", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-21-powermap-v17-V-trump-flynn-pardon-2020", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE: Trump named Flynn national security adviser (served Jan 20 - Feb 13 2017, resigned over the Kislyak calls). DONE (DOJ Office of the Pardon Attorney warrant, Nov 25 2020): full and unconditional pardon for false statements and any offense arising from the Special Counsel investigation; the pending US v. Flynn case was dismissed as moot. Since then Flynn became a paid FARA-registered lobbyist for Republika Srpska (Oct 2025; edge flynn-srpska-fara-lobbyist-oct2025).", "citation": ["https://www.justice.gov/pardon/pardons-granted-president-donald-j-trump-2017-2021", "https://trumpwhitehouse.archives.gov/briefings-statements/statement-press-secretary-regarding-executive-grant-clemency-general-michael-t-flynn/"]}, {"@id": "tie/charles-flynn-palantir-senior-adviser", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/charles-flynn-ret-gen-michael-flynn-s-brother", "to": "node/palantir", "name": "Palantir senior adviser; Michael Flynn's brother", "tieType": "employment (senior adviser, since retiring from the Army Nov 2024) ; family (brother of Michael Flynn)", "category": "family", "kind": "register", "date": "2024-11 - ; 2021-01-06", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-21 (v17)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-21", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-21-powermap-v17-V-charles-flynn-palantir-senior-adviser", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE/SAID: ASPI lists Gen. (ret.) Charles A. Flynn as 'Senior Advisor, Palantir; Commander General, US Army Pacific (2021-24)'; his LinkedIn lists Palantir 'Strategic Advisor' (self-reported). FAMILY: he is Michael Flynn's brother; the Army first falsely denied, then acknowledged, that he was in the room for part of the Jan 6 2021 call on the National Guard response (WaPo, CNN); he says his brother was no factor (SAID). Palantir holds Army contracts (edges palantir-army-10b-ea, palantir-maven-1-3b). A family tie plus a contractor seat is a tie, not proof of influence over any award.", "citation": ["https://www.aspi.org.au/bio/general-ret-charles-a-flynn/", "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/flynn-national-guard-call-riot/2021/01/20/7f4f41ba-5b4c-11eb-aaad-93988621dd28_story.html", "https://www.cnn.com/2021/01/21/politics/michael-flynn-brother-capitol-hill-riot"]}, {"@id": "tie/bush-sr-carlyle-senior-adviser-binladen-2001", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/george-h-w-bush", "to": "node/carlyle", "name": "Carlyle adviser; Sep 10 2001 conference", "tieType": "employment (Carlyle Asia senior adviser, investor) ; same conference as Shafiq bin Laden (Sep 10-11 2001); bin Laden family ~$2M in Carlyle Partners II, withdrawn Oct 2001", "category": "family", "kind": "register", "date": "1998 - 2003 ; 2001-09-10 ; 2001-10-26", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-21 (v17)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-21", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-21-powermap-v17-V-bush-sr-carlyle-senior-adviser-binladen-2001", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (Washington Post, Mar 16 2003; NYT Oct 26 2001): the Carlyle Group investor conference at the Ritz-Carlton, Washington, on Sep 11 2001 was attended by Shafiq bin Laden (Osama's half-brother); George H. W. Bush, a Carlyle senior adviser and fellow investor, 'had been with him at the conference the previous day' and left before the attacks (Briody). NYT: the bin Laden family liquidated its ~$2M stake in Carlyle Partners II in Oct 2001. Both attending a conference is not a documented one-on-one meeting. Bush was then the sitting president's father and an ex-CIA director. Joins the current Carlyle-Lukoil edge (Carlyle exited 2026). Register: grokbot-2026-10-21-V-grok-2112936305797599313-bush-carlyle-ritz-sep10-shafiq.", "citation": ["https://www.nytimes.com/2001/10/26/business/bin-laden-family-liquidates-holdings-with-carlyle-group.html", "https://www.ratical.org/ratville/CAH/CarlyleHead1.pdf", "https://www.economist.com/books-and-arts/2003/06/26/c-for-capitalism"]}, {"@id": "tie/schwarzman-maga-inc-5m-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/stephen-schwarzman-blackstone-ceo", "to": "node/maga-inc-pro-trump-super-pac", "name": "$5M (Sep 2026)", "tieType": "funding ($5M, Sep 2026)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-09", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-21 (v17)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-21", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-21-powermap-v17-V-schwarzman-maga-inc-5m-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (FEC filing Oct 20 2026, per Washington Post Oct 21): Blackstone CEO Stephen A. Schwarzman gave MAGA Inc. $5M in September 2026. Same filing: Diane Hendricks $5M (cycle total $30M), Stephen Wynn $8M. MAGA Inc. had ~$164M left after spending $277M, mostly via transfers ($200M to No Going Back PAC, $25M to Safety & Affordability PAC).", "citation": ["https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2026/10/21/trump-super-pac-maga-inc-pumps-277-million-into-midterms/", "https://docquery.fec.gov/pdf/296/202610209921424296/202610209921424296.pdf"]}, {"@id": "tie/geo-group-maga-inc-4-4m", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/geo-group-private-prisons-ice-detention", "to": "node/maga-inc-pro-trump-super-pac", "name": "$1M (total $4.4M)", "tieType": "funding ($1M Sep 2026 via a GEO division; cycle total $4.4M) ; federal contractor", "category": "contract", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-09", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-21 (v17)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-21", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-21-powermap-v17-V-geo-group-maga-inc-4-4m", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (FEC filing Oct 20 2026, per Washington Post Oct 21): MAGA Inc. received another $1M from a division of GEO Group, 'the private prison company that has major business with the federal government', bringing GEO's total to $4.4M. A federal contractor funding the President's super PAC is the tie; no quid pro quo is claimed. Whether the donating GEO unit is itself a federal contractor (52 USC 30119 bars contractor contributions) is not shown in the filing read here: legal status not graded (hole-style note).", "citation": ["https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2026/10/21/trump-super-pac-maga-inc-pumps-277-million-into-midterms/", "https://docquery.fec.gov/pdf/296/202610209921424296/202610209921424296.pdf"]}, {"@id": "tie/maga-inc-leavitt-buskirk-paid-advisers", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/maga-inc-pro-trump-super-pac", "to": "node/karoline-leavitt-chris-buskirk", "name": "paid advisers (Leavitt; Buskirk of 1789)", "tieType": "employment (paid advisers per FEC disbursements; Leavitt = ex-WH press secretary, left Aug 27 2026; Buskirk = 1789 Capital co-founder/CIO, Don Jr.'s firm)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-21 (v17)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-21", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-21-powermap-v17-V-maga-inc-leavitt-buskirk-paid-advisers", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (FEC filing Oct 20 2026, per Washington Post Oct 21): MAGA Inc.'s paid advisers include former WH press secretary Karoline Leavitt and investor Chris Buskirk (also fundraiser Meredith O'Rourke, pollster Tony Fabrizio, spokesman Alex Pfeiffer); MAGA Inc. also paid ~$50K for events at Trump properties. Buskirk is co-founder and CIO of 1789 Capital (firm page), where Donald Trump Jr. became a partner in Nov 2024 (Reuters). Revolving door: the President's ex-spokeswoman and his son's fund partner are both paid by his super PAC.", "citation": ["https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2026/10/21/trump-super-pac-maga-inc-pumps-277-million-into-midterms/", "https://1789capital.vc/christopher-buskirk", "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/trump-son-don-jr-joining-venture-capital-firm-1789-capital-sources-say-2024-11-12/"]}, {"@id": "tie/hegseth-aides-ncpc-arch-alternates-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/pete-hegseth", "to": "node/national-capital-planning-commission-chair-mark-paoletta", "name": "aides seated as alternates before arch vote", "tieType": "appointment (top aides Ricky Buria and Patrick Weaver added as Hegseth's alternate commissioners; Interior's Kevin Lilly + Aaron Calkins for Burgum; career alternates replaced) before the Nov 5 vote on Trump's 250-ft arch", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-21", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-21 (v17)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-21", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-21-powermap-v17-V-hegseth-aides-ncpc-arch-alternates-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE (Washington Post, Dan Diamond, Oct 21 2026, from a change to the commission's website): Hegseth's top aides Ricky Buria and Patrick Weaver were added as his alternate commissioners on the NCPC, and Interior's Kevin Lilly and Aaron Calkins as Burgum's, replacing career alternates (incl. NPS's Tammy Stidham) ahead of the Nov 5 2026 meeting on Trump's planned 250-foot triumphal arch at Memorial Circle near Arlington. SAID: chair Mark Paoletta (WH official) says he plans to approve it. Commission, Pentagon and Interior did not respond.", "citation": ["https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2026/10/21/trump-adds-four-political-appointees-federal-planning-body/"]}, {"@id": "tie/musk-starshield-ukraine-speed-cap-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/elon-musk", "to": "node/ukraine-armed-forces-starshield-terminals", "name": "Starshield speed cap (WSJ: Musk ordered)", "tieType": "service control (military Starshield speed cap ~160 km/h, from ~Oct 13 2026; WSJ: ordered by Musk) ; contact (Musk-Trump call after it became public, SAID)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-13 ; 2026-10-21", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "changed", "statusDate": "2026-10-24", "statusNote": "Ukraine MoD (Khmara) and Zelensky SAID Oct 24 speeds restored above 400 km/h after the ~160 km/h cap from ~Oct 13-14 (AP, Kyiv Independent). Musk SAID Oct 24 Ukraine's military 'violated Starlink terms of service' and Starshield 'is controlled by the US government'. Who ordered the cap is unproven; stays I.", "addedIn": "2026-10-21 (v17)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-26", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-21-powermap-v17-I-musk-starshield-ukraine-speed-cap-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "I overall. DONE (Ukraine MoD, CBS, Times): Ukraine's military Starshield link has been limited to ~160 km/h since ~Oct 13-14, still throttled Oct 21 (Zelensky's office SAID). WSJ (Oct 20, anonymous): Musk ordered the slowdown; one person says he spoke to senior officials incl. Trump before (UNVERIFIED); two people say Musk and Trump spoke by phone after it became public (SAID). SAID vs SAID on who decides: Musk (~Oct 14-15) 'Starshield systems are owned and controlled by the US government... decided by the US military and ultimately POTUS'; Rubio (Oct 21) 'governed by a private commercial contract'; Hegseth (Oct 20) 'terms of service... Starlink has the option'; NATO Amb. Whitaker 'They are a private company'. A, then B, then C: the company says the state decides; the state says the company decides; nobody has published the contract (forecast row: not by Nov 3). Grade I until a document or second named source shows who ordered it.", "citation": ["https://www.wsj.com/world/ukraine-starlink-elon-musk-trump-dbc49193", "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/elon-musk-ukraine-spacex-starshield-trump-administration/", "https://www.washingtonexaminer.com/policy/defense/4773319/hegseth-starshield-terms-of-service-ukraine-restrictions-stock-depletion/"]}, {"@id": "tie/spacex-tesla-merger-special-committees-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/spacex", "to": "node/tesla", "name": "merger committees formed (Oct 20 2026)", "tieType": "related-party deal (both boards formed special committees of independent directors to consider a merger; Musk recused)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-20", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-21 (v17)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-21", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-21-powermap-v17-V-spacex-tesla-merger-special-committees-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID (Musk on the SpaceX Q3 2026 earnings call, Oct 20; Reuters/NBC/Bloomberg): the SpaceX and Tesla boards formed special committees of independent directors to consider a merger; no terms, no guarantee, shareholder vote needed; Musk recused as conflicted. DONE history of Musk related-party consolidation: Tesla bought SolarCity (2016), xAI absorbed X (2025), SpaceX acquired xAI (Feb 2026). SpaceX Q3: revenue $14.6B; 9-month FCF about -$35B (register grokbot-2026-10-21-V-spacex-q3-2026-results-8k-figures). 'Bailout' framing is I, not graded here.", "citation": ["https://www.nbcnews.com/business/business-news/elon-musk-spacex-tesla-merger-rcna604685", "https://ca.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/spacex-quarterly-revenue-jumps-beats-estimates-as-ai-business-surges-4891702"]}, {"@id": "tie/musk-skydance-1b-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/elon-musk", "to": "node/david-ellison", "name": "~$1B into Skydance (Oct 2026)", "tieType": "funding (equity investment ~$1B in Skydance, the Paramount-WBD combine run by David Ellison)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10 (reported Oct 22 2026)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-22 (v18)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-22", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-22-powermap-v18-V-musk-skydance-1b-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID (Semafor exclusive, Rohan Goswami, Oct 22 2026, people familiar; CNBC confirms): Elon Musk invested roughly $1B in Skydance, which owns CBS News and CNN after the Oct 6 WBD close; board member Laurene Powell Jobs and other investors put in equity around the same time. Semafor: Larry Ellison has personally guaranteed more than $40B of the WBD equity financing. DONE history (same pair, other direction): the Lawrence J. Ellison Revocable Trust committed $1B to Musk's 2022 Twitter buyout (SC 13D/A; edge ellison-musk-twitter-equity-1b); Larry Ellison sat on Tesla's board. A, then B: Ellison $1B to Musk (2022), Musk ~$1B to Ellison's company (2026). Time order only, no exchange claimed. No filing or terms published; Musk and Paramount did not comment.", "citation": ["https://www.semafor.com/article/10/22/2026/elon-musk-makes-1-billion-investment-in-ellisons-skydance", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/22/elon-musk-skydance-investment.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-musk-starshield-call-restore-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/elon-musk", "name": "call to lift Starshield cap (WSJ, Oct 22)", "tieType": "contact (phone call asking Musk to ease the Ukraine Starshield cap, per WSJ citing US officials)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-22", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-22 (v18)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-26", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-22-powermap-v18-V-trump-musk-starshield-call-restore-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "SAID (WSJ citing US officials, via CNBC Oct 22 2026): Trump asked Musk to ease the restrictions Musk had imposed on Starshield in Ukraine; US and Ukrainian officials said it was 'working more normally Thursday, shortly after' the call. SAID (Trump, Oct 22): 'Whether I called or whether somebody else called, doesn't make any difference... The bottom line, he put it back.' SAID (Trump, Oct 21): 'I don't know who did it, but I was not involved.' DONE: Sen. Blumenthal opened an inquiry Oct 22 with letters to Musk and Hegseth. Grade V on the report and the quotes; who ordered the original cap stays I (edge musk-starshield-ukraine-speed-cap-2026).", "citation": ["https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/22/trump-musk-starlink-ukraine.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/greenberg-circle-v-trump-wlf-emoluments-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/j-benjamin-greenberg-circle-shareholder-derivative-plaintiff", "to": "node/world-liberty-financial", "name": "emoluments suit over UAE money (Oct 22 2026)", "tieType": "lawsuit (verified derivative complaint on Circle's behalf, D.D.C.; Foreign Emoluments Clause; defendants Trump and Witkoff in official capacity + WLF entities)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-22", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-22 (v18)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-22", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-22-powermap-v18-V-greenberg-circle-v-trump-wlf-emoluments-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (complaint filed, D.D.C., Oct 22 2026; published by CNBC; Bloomberg Law, Politico): Greenberg sued on Circle's behalf. Defendants: Donald J. Trump and Special Envoy Steven C. Witkoff (official capacity), World Liberty Financial LLC, WLF Holdco, Stablecoin Holdco, DT Marks DEFI, DT Marks SC. Counts target (a) the 49% WLF stake bought by an entity backed by UAE national security adviser Tahnoon bin Zayed (edge aryam-wlf-49pct) and (b) MGX's (Tahnoon-chaired) USD1 purchase used to settle its Binance investment. SAID (complaint): 'No president in American history has profited from his office so brazenly.' These are allegations, not findings. SAID: Circle did not initiate or authorize the suit; WLF spokesman: 'without merit'. Case number blank on the published copy.", "citation": ["https://fm.cnbc.com/applications/cnbc.com/resources/editorialfiles/2026/10/22/Emoluments_Lawsuit_102226.pdf", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/22/trump-world-liberty-crypto-lawsuit-uae.html", "https://www.politico.com/news/2026/10/22/donald-trump-lawsuit-crypto-world-liberty-financial-01131555"]}, {"@id": "tie/rfk-calley-means-adviser-resigned-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/robert-f-kennedy-jr", "to": "node/calley-means", "name": "senior adviser, resigned Oct 22 2026", "tieType": "employment (senior adviser to the HHS Secretary; resigned Oct 22 2026)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2025 ; 2026-10-22 (resigned)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "ended", "statusDate": "2026-10-22", "statusNote": "Means resigned Oct 22 2026 (Politico, AP); role ended, edge kept as historical DONE.", "addedIn": "2026-10-22 (v18)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-22", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-22-powermap-v18-V-rfk-calley-means-adviser-resigned-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (Politico, AP Oct 22 2026): Calley Means, senior adviser to HHS Secretary Robert F. Kennedy Jr. and a leading MAHA figure, resigned from the administration. SAID (per reports): frustration that MAHA food priorities stalled, including no federal ultra-processed food definition. Edge records the role and its end.", "citation": ["https://www.politico.com/news/2026/10/22/calley-means-top-maha-ally-resigns-from-trump-administration-01132073", "https://apnews.com/article/trump-maha-healthcare-rfk-jr-945acfc81edf8e837e969d42f01fb2a3"]}, {"@id": "tie/kushner-mivd-phone-uae-transfers-alleged", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jared-kushner", "to": "node/dutch-military-intelligence-mivd", "name": "phone seen by Dutch intel (alleged; denied)", "tieType": "alleged surveillance (MIVD reportedly saw Kushner's iPhone screen, early 2018) ; alleged UAE-linked transfers $700M+ (undocumented)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2018 (alleged) ; 2026-10-22 (published)", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-22 (v18)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-22", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-22-powermap-v18-I-kushner-mivd-phone-uae-transfers-alleged", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "I. DONE (published): Vanity Fair, Oct 22 2026, ran an excerpt of Matthew Cole's book 'Princes and Thieves' alleging the Dutch MIVD could see Jared Kushner's iPhone screen from early 2018 and saw UAE-linked accounts moving $700M+. SAID (denials): Kushner calls it 'outrageous fabrications'; his lawyer and ex-Ambassador David Friedman deny. The surveillance and the transfers are single-author allegations from unnamed sources; no document, no Dutch confirmation. Filed I so the claim is on the map with its denial, not as fact.", "citation": ["https://www.vanityfair.com/story/jared-kushner-hacked-phone-secret-negotiations", "https://www.mediaite.com/media/news/outrageous-fabrications-jared-kushner-rages-at-bombshell-report-in-vanity-fair/"]}, {"@id": "tie/aipac-udp-rogers-michigan-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/aipac-united-democracy-project", "to": "node/mike-rogers", "name": "up to $9M for Rogers (reported; FEC unchecked)", "tieType": "funding (super PAC spending up to $9M backing Republican Mike Rogers, Michigan Senate race)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-22 (v18)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-22", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-22-powermap-v18-I-aipac-udp-rogers-michigan-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "I. Reported (The Hill, Newsweek, Oct 22 2026): AIPAC's United Democracy Project sent up to $9M to back Republican Mike Rogers against Democrat Abdul El-Sayed in Michigan's Senate race. SAID: Sen. Bernie Sanders tied the spending to the Iran war and Gaza. SAID/DONE (WaPo Oct 22): AIPAC says it will stop endorsing and giving directly to candidates. Grade I until the FEC independent-expenditure filings are checked for the amount.", "citation": ["https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/6166208-sanders-aipac-michigan-clash", "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2026/10/22/pro-israel-lobby-aipac-no-longer-endorse-directly-give-candidates/"]}, {"@id": "tie/blanche-said-works-for-trump-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/todd-blanche", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "'I work for President Trump' (Oct 21 2026)", "tieType": "statement of allegiance (AG SAID 'I work for President Trump'; called DOJ independence a 'misperception') ; prior employment (Trump criminal defense lawyer)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-21", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-22 (v18)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-22", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-22-powermap-v18-V-blanche-said-works-for-trump-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID (Pod Force One with Miranda Devine, Oct 21 2026, transcript; Mediaite): Attorney General Todd Blanche called the idea that DOJ is independent of the White House a 'misperception' and said 'I don't. I work for President Trump.' DONE context: Blanche was Trump's criminal defense lawyer (2023-24), Deputy AG (2025), acting AG (Apr 2026), confirmed AG Aug 8 2026. Said, not done: no specific act attached to this edge.", "citation": ["https://podcastrex.com/shows/pod-force-one/democrats-gaslight-the-american-people-ag-todd-blanche/transcript", "https://www.mediaite.com/media/news/todd-blanche-wildly-claims-doj-independence-is-a-misperception-i-work-for-president-trump/"]}, {"@id": "tie/thiel-said-iran-war-should-not-have-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/peter-thiel", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "SAID Iran war 'should not have done it' (Oct 12 lecture)", "tieType": "public split (SAID in a closed-door lecture, audio obtained by Politico): Iran war 'we should not have done it' ; still SAID support for Trump", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-12 (lecture) ; 2026-10-21 (published)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-23 (v19)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-23", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-23-powermap-v19-V-thiel-said-iran-war-should-not-have-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID (audio of Thiel's third Nashville 'Antichrist' lecture, Oct 12 2026, obtained and published by Decoded by POLITICO, Calder McHugh, Oct 21-22 2026; Anadolu relays): 'I'm skeptical of [the Iran war], I think we should not have done it. There were a lot of mistakes that were made.' and 'Maybe we don't have the hard power. Maybe we're going to lose the soft power war.' Politico: in the same lecture Thiel stressed continued support for Trump and wanted to protect him. Said, not done: a private remark, no public statement, no change in funding or in the Palantir/Anduril ties on the map. Register forecast (Oct 23): he does not repeat it on the record before Nov 3.", "citation": ["https://www.politico.com/news/2026/10/21/peter-thiel-trump-iran-war-01131284", "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/decoded-by-politico/2026/10/22/thiels-big-break-with-trump-01131403", "https://www.aa.com.tr/en/americas/tech-investor-peter-thiel-says-us-should-not-have-launched-war-on-iran-report/4097137"]}, {"@id": "tie/uae-leads-boring-series-d-3b-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/uae-state-investors-boring-series-d-lead", "to": "node/the-boring-company", "name": "led $3B Series D ($23B val.), Sep 10 2026", "tieType": "funding (led $3B Series D at $23B valuation; 150+ km UAE tunnel deployment)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-09-10", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-23 (v19)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-26", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-23-powermap-v19-V-uae-leads-boring-series-d-3b-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (company statement via Reuters, Bloomberg, TechCrunch, Khaleej Times, Sep 10 2026): The Boring Company raised a $3B Series D at a $23B valuation, led by 'the United Arab Emirates and affiliated investment entities', to deploy 150+ km of tunnels across the UAE on top of the Dubai Loop (RTA implementation agreement Feb 2026). Other investors: Shamal Holding (Dubai; SAID its stake is private and separate from the RTA deal), Human Capital, Vy Capital, Valor, Sequoia, a16z, Temasek, Baron. Which UAE state vehicles and how much each put in are not public.", "citation": ["https://www.reuters.com/business/musks-tunnel-startup-boring-company-raises-3-billion-23-billion-valuation-2026-09-10/", "https://www.khaleejtimes.com/uae/elon-musks-the-boring-company-to-build-150km-of-tunnels-across-uae-raises-dh11-billion", "https://techcrunch.com/2026/09/10/the-boring-company-raises-3b-in-round-led-by-uae/"]}, {"@id": "tie/spacex-boring-561m-related-party-gain-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/spacex", "to": "node/the-boring-company", "name": "$561M paper gain on TBC stake (Q3 10-Q)", "tieType": "equity stake (related party; Musk controls TBC voting) ; $561M unrealized fair-value gain in Q3 2026", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-09 (mark) ; 2026-10-22 (10-Q)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-23 (v19)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-23", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-23-powermap-v19-V-spacex-boring-561m-related-party-gain-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (SpaceX Form 10-Q for Q3 2026, SEC EDGAR, Note 8 and income statement; CNBC Kolodny Oct 22 2026): after TBC's September 2026 financing (the UAE-led round), SpaceX marked its equity-method stake in The Boring Company to fair value and booked a $561M unrealized gain in other income (labelled related party). It was more than half of Q3 other income ($1,025M); Q3 net income $4,404M; nine-month net loss $413M. The filing says SpaceX is presumed to have significant influence over TBC 'given the Company's CEO has a controlling voting interest in TBC'. No cash moved; accounting fact, no wrongdoing alleged.", "citation": ["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1181412/000162828026066880/spcx-20260930.htm", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/22/spacex-records-561-million-investment-gain-from-stake-in-boring-co.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/lyons-skyhorse-rfk-4m-advances-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/tony-lyons-skyhorse-publishing", "to": "node/robert-f-kennedy-jr", "name": "$4M book advances (2 x $2M), disclosed Sep 2026", "tieType": "funding (two $2M book advances while HHS Secretary; earlier $451K consulting fees)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2024-08 (agreement) ; 2025-2026 (paid) ; 2026-09 (disclosed)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-23 (v19)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-26", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-23-powermap-v19-V-lyons-skyhorse-rfk-4m-advances-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (Kennedy's annual financial disclosure, signed by an HHS ethics official Sep 17 2026; NPR Sep 22/24, NYT, Guardian Sep 23 2026): Kennedy received two $2M book advances from Skyhorse Publishing, one for 'Unsettled Science'; Skyhorse also paid him $451,000 in consulting fees the year before he became HHS Secretary. Ground News/Guardian: Lyons reached the advance agreement in August 2024, the month Kennedy quit his campaign and endorsed Trump (time order only); Lyons is president of the MAHA Center. Kennedy's 2024 ethics pledge bars writing or promoting the books in office. SAID (HHS): Kennedy complies with all rules. Ethics experts SAID it raises salary-supplementation questions; no finding.", "citation": ["https://www.npr.org/2026/09/24/nx-s1-5979867/rfk-ethics-book-deals", "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/23/rfk-jr-maha-book-advances"]}, {"@id": "tie/debecker-rfk-gifts-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/gavin-de-becker", "to": "node/robert-f-kennedy-jr", "name": "~$270K gifts: flights + DC home (2025)", "tieType": "gifts (~$150K flights to Fiji and Greece + ~$126.5K Washington housing, 2025)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-07 ; 2025-11 ; 2026-09 (disclosed)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-23 (v19)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-23", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-23-powermap-v19-V-debecker-rfk-gifts-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (Kennedy's 2025 disclosure, amended Sep 2026; WSJ, NPR, Guardian): Gavin de Becker gave Kennedy about $45K round-trip airfare to Greece (Jul 2025), about $97K flights to Fiji where de Becker owns a compound (Nov 2025), and about $126.5K of use of a Washington vacation home; total over $250K. De Becker's own book is published by Skyhorse (Lyons). SAID (de Becker to NPR): 'Bobby is my closest friend... I have nothing whatsoever to do with HHS.' Gifts are disclosed; no finding of a violation.", "citation": ["https://www.npr.org/2026/09/24/nx-s1-5979867/rfk-ethics-book-deals", "https://www.wsj.com/politics/rfk-jr-got-free-flights-to-fiji-and-greece-from-a-top-donor-e4b8d525", "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/23/rfk-jr-maha-book-advances"]}, {"@id": "tie/germany-pays-ukraine-starshield-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/germany-federal-government", "to": "node/spacex", "name": "SAID 'we pay for it' (Ukraine Starshield, to Apr 2027)", "tieType": "contract payer (funds Ukraine's military Starshield/Starlink service, reported to Apr 2027)", "category": "contract", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10 (SAID) ; to 2027-04", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-23 (v19)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-23", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-23-powermap-v19-V-germany-pays-ukraine-starshield-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "other", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "SAID (German Foreign Minister Johann Wadephul on ZDF Maybrit Illner and to press, Oct 2026, via Kyiv Post 'We pay for it'): Germany funds the military Starlink/Starshield service for Ukraine and insists the speed limits be lifted. RBC-Ukraine (Kyiv sources): the Berlin-funded package runs to April 2027. Puck (Ioffe) adds other European payers; no contract or ministry document published. Connects to the Starshield speed-cap edges: the payer is a NATO government, the operator is SpaceX.", "citation": ["https://www.kyivpost.com/post/87287", "https://newsukraine.rbc.ua/news/germany-urges-us-to-lift-starlink-restrictions-1792142233.html", "https://www.zdfheute.de/video/maybrit-illner/maybrit-illner-clip-1-870.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/musk-slf-168m-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/elon-musk", "to": "node/senate-leadership-fund", "name": "$168M (SLF's top donor, Q3 2026)", "tieType": "funding (super PAC contributions, $168M total; $158M in Sep 2026 via SLF's affiliated Texas PAC for Ken Paxton)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-09 (two gifts $75M + $83M) ; 2026-10-15 (FEC Q3 filing)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-26 (v20)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-26", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-26-powermap-v20-V-musk-slf-168m-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (FEC Q3 filing Oct 15 2026; CNBC, Bloomberg, Public Citizen, WaPo): Musk gave the Senate Leadership Fund $158M in September 2026 (two contributions, $75M and $83M) through an affiliated Texas PAC created to back Ken Paxton's Senate race, bringing his total to SLF to $168M; SLF raised a record $272.9M in Q3, Musk about 58%. SLF moved most of the money to the Texas PAC (WaPo). CNBC Oct 12: his known 2025-26 federal political giving about $366M (Musk reps to NYT, confirmed by America PAC spokesperson). Money is filed; no claim here of what it bought.", "citation": ["https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/15/elon-musk-senate-leadership-fund-fundraising.html", "https://www.citizen.org/news/elon-musk-becomes-senate-leadership-funds-main-donor-in-quarter-three/", "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2026/10/21/musk-backed-pacs-have-spent-over-400-million-advertising/"]}, {"@id": "tie/anthropic-spacex-compute-120b-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/anthropic", "to": "node/spacex", "name": "up to $120.5B compute to 2029 (S-1)", "tieType": "contract (GPU compute purchase, up to $120.5B through 2029; ~$3.1B/month once capacity is delivered)", "category": "contract", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-05 (first deal, SpaceX S-1) ; 2026-10-26 (Anthropic S-1 public)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-26 (v20)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-26", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-26-powermap-v20-V-anthropic-spacex-compute-120b-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (Anthropic PBC Form S-1, public Oct 26 2026; Gizmodo, Yahoo Finance, The Verge): Anthropic may pay Elon Musk's SpaceX (which absorbed xAI) up to $120.5B through 2029 for Nvidia-GPU compute (Colossus 1 and II), about $3.1B a month once all capacity is delivered (expected Dec 2026); initial non-cancelable periods end Jan and Mar 2027, then either side can cancel on 90 days' notice, so $120.5B is a ceiling. SpaceX's own May 2026 S-1 had put it at $1.25B/month to May 2029. The same S-1 lists >=$114.5B to Google (to 2033), >=$110B to Amazon (to 2036), >=$44.9B to Microsoft. SpaceX Q3 10-Q: unnamed 'Customer B' = 34.5% of revenue; that it is Anthropic is inference, not filed.", "citation": ["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2130357/000162828026067168/anthropicpbc-sx1.htm", "https://gizmodo.com/anthropics-deal-with-elon-musks-spacexai-is-even-bigger-than-we-knew-ipo-filing-shows-2000830618", "https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/ai/articles/anthropic-discloses-120-5-billion-140613686.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-sons-american-ventures-powerus-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump-jr", "to": "node/powerus-corporation", "name": "Don Jr. + Eric: 9.9% via American Ventures", "tieType": "equity (Don Jr. + Eric Trump indirect 9.9% beneficial stake via American Ventures; reverse merger into Nasdaq-listed Aureus Greenway)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-03-09 (merger announced) ; 2026-10-01 (closed, PUSA) ; 2026-10-05 ($82M US order)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-26 (v20)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-26", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-26-powermap-v20-V-trump-sons-american-ventures-powerus-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (Reuters Mar 9 and Sep 30 2026, citing filings; Powerus 8-K/A Oct 16 2026): Powerus merged into Aureus Greenway Holdings, a golf operator indirectly backed by Donald Trump Jr. and Eric Trump through the fund American Ventures, which was expected to keep a 9.9% beneficial stake; the merger closed Oct 1 2026 (ticker PUSA). Company-disclosed government business: USAF Guardian-2 interceptor IDIQ ceiling up to $90M through mid-2028 (a maximum); $82M counter-UAS order announced Oct 5 2026 under an existing government contract (Defense Post). SAID (Powerus and the brothers' spokespeople to Reuters): passive investors, no operational role. Contracts and stake are time order only; no claim the stake won the orders.", "citation": ["https://www.reuters.com/technology/trump-brothers-backed-aureus-merge-with-drone-maker-powerus-2026-03-09/", "https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/americas/powerus-ukraine-drone-start-up-don-jr-eric-trump-b3059281.html", "https://ir.power.us/sec-filings/all-sec-filings/content/0001493152-26-047462/ex99-2.htm"]}, {"@id": "tie/kellogg-powerus-advisory-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/keith-kellogg", "to": "node/powerus-corporation", "name": "advisory board; SAID 'never hurts to have their name on something'", "tieType": "advisory board seat", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026 (as of Sep 30 2026 Reuters)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-26 (v20)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-26", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-26-powermap-v20-V-kellogg-powerus-advisory-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (Reuters Sep 30 2026 via The Independent): Keith Kellogg, Trump's former special envoy to Ukraine, sits on the advisory board of Powerus, the drone firm in which Don Jr. and Eric Trump hold an indirect 9.9% stake and which plans to bring Ukrainian battlefield drone technology to the Pentagon. SAID (Kellogg to Reuters) about the Trump brothers' involvement: 'It never hurts to have their name on something.' Former official to a contractor; no claim of lobbying.", "citation": ["https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/americas/powerus-ukraine-drone-start-up-don-jr-eric-trump-b3059281.html", "https://ca.finance.yahoo.com/news/drone-startup-tied-trump-sons-165303789.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/novatek-polar-lng-secret-funding-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/novatek", "to": "node/polar-lng-tech-wave-abu-dhabi", "name": "SAID secret funding (ex-CEO); Novatek SAID seeks minority stake", "tieType": "funding (alleged secret start-up funding, up to $15M discussed; Novatek SAID it seeks a minority stake)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-08 (Four Seasons Abu Dhabi meeting) ; 2026-09 (Riddle resigns) ; 2026-10-23 (NYT, FT)", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-26 (v20)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-26", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-26-powermap-v20-I-novatek-polar-lng-secret-funding-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 4, "description": "SAID (ex-CEO Joel Riddle to NYT, FT, WSJ, Oct 23-24 2026, with Baker Botts memos attached to his resignation and texts reviewed by NYT): Novatek secretly funded Polar LNG through its Abu Dhabi parent Tech Wave; Novatek's Solovyov and Mikhelson discussed up to $15M at a late-August Abu Dhabi meeting ('The first 5 million were supposed to arrive by today'). Baker Botts memo: Treasury's sanctions unit had flagged an investor that 'may be acting on Novatek's behalf'. SAID (Novatek to NYT): it is moving to acquire 'minority shareholder' status. SAID (Polar LNG): Riddle was 'terminated for cause'; NYT documents show he resigned six days before. Grade I: the funding is alleged with documents seen by reporters, not filed. Context in a separate edge: Putin discussed the plan with Witkoff and Kushner (anonymous sources). Gentry Beach (Don Jr.'s college friend) SAID in Feb 2026 he negotiated with Novatek; Novatek says he had no role in the stake talks.", "citation": ["https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/23/us/politics/in-us-gas-talks-with-kremlin-hidden-financing-for-alaska-project-emerges.html", "https://www.ft.com/content/e9cfbfbb-e65a-4303-aebb-20d59319ef1b", "https://www.wsj.com/business/energy-oil/u-s-energy-execs-say-they-quit-startup-over-undisclosed-russian-funding-b5eae266", "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-10-24/us-lng-project-developer-funded-by-russia-s-novatek-ft-says"]}, {"@id": "tie/putin-witkoff-kushner-alaska-lng-talks-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/vladimir-putin", "to": "node/steve-witkoff-jared-kushner", "name": "Alaska LNG / Novatek tech raised in talks (anon. sources)", "tieType": "negotiation topic (Novatek technology for Alaska LNG raised in peace-track talks)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2025 (Putin SAID 'discussing with our American partners') ; 2026-09 (discussed with envoys, per NYT sources)", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-26 (v20)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-26", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-26-powermap-v20-I-putin-witkoff-kushner-alaska-lng-talks-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID (people familiar with the negotiations, anonymous, to NYT Oct 23 2026): Putin discussed the Novatek-technology Alaska LNG plan in September 2026 with Trump envoys Witkoff and Kushner, one of several energy deals White House officials think could smooth relations with Moscow. SAID (a US official): it was only broadly mentioned, no granular talks; NYT: no indication the envoys knew of Polar LNG or its Novatek ties. Putin SAID publicly in 2025 'we are discussing with our American partners' Novatek tech in Alaska. FT: discussions of Novatek tech in exchange for Arctic LNG 2 sanctions relief, which Novatek denies. No deal, no quid pro quo shown. Runs alongside the Lukoil sale talks (GL 131K) on the same channel - time order only.", "citation": ["https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/23/us/politics/in-us-gas-talks-with-kremlin-hidden-financing-for-alaska-project-emerges.html", "https://dnyuz.com/2026/10/24/in-u-s-gas-talks-with-kremlin-hidden-financing-for-alaska-project-emerges/"]}, {"@id": "tie/nvidia-meta-3b-equity-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/nvidia", "to": "node/meta", "name": "$3B into Meta equity offering (announced)", "tieType": "investment (equity: $3B into Meta's offering; supplier buys stock of its customer)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-27", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-27 (v21)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-29", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-27-powermap-v21-V-nvidia-meta-3b-equity-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 4, "description": "INVESTMENT (announced, not closed): Nvidia press release Oct 27 2026: 'NVIDIA will invest $3 billion in Meta's equity offering', alongside Meta expanding Vera Rubin / Vera CPU deployment and a deeper Muse partnership. Meta priced $25B Class A common at $625 (forward sale agreements; common closes ~Oct 29; Meta gets no proceeds until forward settlement by Nov 19 2027) plus $12.5B mandatory convertible preferred; Reuters: total plan $97.5B incl. an ATM programme. Reuters: the commitments add to concerns about 'circular' capital as chip suppliers finance a top customer. INFERENCE (labeled): supplier equity in a buyer of its chips is vendor financing; why now is TK.", "citation": ["https://investor.nvidia.com/news/press-release-details/2026/NVIDIA-and-Meta-to-Expand-Collaboration-on-Muse-and-Muse-Family-of-Models-Amid-Robust-Growth/default.aspx", "https://investor.atmeta.com/investor-news/press-release-details/2026/Meta-Announces-Pricing-of-Offering-of-Depositary-Shares-Representing-Series-A-Mandatory-Convertible-Preferred-Stock-and-Offering-of-Class-A-Common-Stock-in-Connection-with-Forward-Sale-Agreements/default.aspx", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/27/nvidia-invest-meta.html", "https://www.investing.com/news/economy-news/meta-eyes-record-975-billion-equity-raise-to-fund-ai-expansion-4975360"]}, {"@id": "tie/amd-meta-1b-equity-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/amd", "to": "node/meta", "name": "$1B into Meta equity offering (announced)", "tieType": "investment (equity: $1B into Meta's offering; supplier buys stock of its customer)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-27", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-27 (v21)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-29", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-27-powermap-v21-V-amd-meta-1b-equity-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "INVESTMENT (announced, not closed): AMD IR release Oct 27 2026: 'AMD will invest $1 billion in Meta's equity offering', with its Helios racks running at Meta. Meta's Oct 26 launch release named Nvidia, AMD and Broadcom as interested in up to $5B of Class A shares; Broadcom has announced no amount. Same offering as the Nvidia edge. Register row grokbot-2026-10-27-V-pharmd_ks-...-v2 carries the timeline post. INFERENCE (labeled): vendor financing of a buyer; intent TK.", "citation": ["https://ir.amd.com/news-events/press-releases/detail/1302/amd-and-meta-advance-strategic-partnership-to-power-metas-superintelligence-infrastructure", "https://investor.atmeta.com/investor-news/press-release-details/2026/Meta-Announces-Launch-of-Offering-of-Depositary-Shares-Representing-Series-A-Mandatory-Convertible-Preferred-Stock-and-Offering-of-Class-A-Common-Stock-in-Connection-with-Forward-Sale-Agreements/default.aspx", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/27/nvidia-invest-meta.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/feinberg-kollitides-pentagon-roles-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/stephen-feinberg", "to": "node/george-kollitides", "name": "named co-chief of staff; heads BOND + Economic Defense Unit", "tieType": "appointment (co-chief of staff; head of BOND and the Economic Defense Unit; vice-chair OSC investment committee)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2025 ; 2026-02 (EDU director)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-27 (v21)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-27", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-27-powermap-v21-V-feinberg-kollitides-pentagon-roles-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "reference", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "APPOINTMENT: ProPublica (Oct 9 2026, records): Deputy SecDef Feinberg, a former private-equity colleague, brought George K. Kollitides II into the Pentagon and named him co-chief of staff and senior adviser, vice chairman of the Office of Strategic Capital's investment committee, and director of the Economic Defense Unit (Feb 2026) and Business Operators for National Defense (BOND). His employment status for those roles is unclear per ProPublica.", "citation": ["https://www.propublica.org/article/george-kollitides-pentagon-contracts-alvarez-marsal", "https://news.bgov.com/bloomberg-government-news/pentagon-investment-chief-exits-board-of-offshore-defense-funder"]}, {"@id": "tie/kollitides-alvarez-marsal-federal-contracts-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/george-kollitides", "to": "node/alvarez-marsal-a-m-capital-a-m-federal", "name": "~$350M DoD contracts to A&M Federal; listed A&M Capital adviser", "tieType": "contract (DoD ~$350M to A&M Federal incl. $281M no-bid OTA advising his BOND office) ; employment (listed 'Senior Advisor' to A&M Capital in an Apr 2026 SEC filing)", "category": "contract", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-12 ($67.6M) ; 2026-04 (SEC filing) ; 2026-06 ($281M OTA)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-27 (v21)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-27", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-27-powermap-v21-V-kollitides-alvarez-marsal-federal-contracts-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "reference", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "CONTRACT + EMPLOYMENT (records): ProPublica Oct 9 2026: DoD awarded Alvarez & Marsal Federal $67.6M (Dec 2025) and a $281M no-bid consulting OTA (Jun 2026) advising BOND, the office Kollitides heads; ~$350M is ~5x what A&M entities got from all US agencies in the prior two decades. An Apr 2026 SEC filing by D. Boral Acquisition I listed Kollitides as 'Senior Advisor' to A&M Capital. SAID (DoD official): he 'does not and has never had' investments or financial relations with A&M consulting and is recused on A&M Capital matters. Contracts after his arrival = sequence only; no finding he steered them.", "citation": ["https://www.propublica.org/article/george-kollitides-pentagon-contracts-alvarez-marsal"]}, {"@id": "tie/kollitides-d-boral-board-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/george-kollitides", "to": "node/d-boral-acquisition-i", "name": "board seat Feb-Sep 2026 (resigned)", "tieType": "board seat (Cayman SPAC whose affiliate finances defense firms; stock worth up to $1M) - resigned end Sep 2026", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-02 (joined, six days after EDU appointment) ; 2026-09-30 (resigned, SEC filing)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "ended", "statusDate": "2026-09-30", "statusNote": "Resigned from the D. Boral Acquisition I board at end of September 2026 per the company's SEC filing (Bloomberg Government Oct 2).", "addedIn": "2026-10-27 (v21)", "lastChecked": "2026-09-30", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-27-powermap-v21-V-kollitides-d-boral-board-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "reference", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "BOARD: Bloomberg Government (Oct 2 2026, SEC filing): Kollitides joined the board of D. Boral Acquisition I, a Cayman shell whose parent finances defense companies, and accepted stock worth up to $1M in February 2026, six days after being named director of the Pentagon's Economic Defense Unit; the company's SEC filing announced his resignation (end of September). Status: ended.", "citation": ["https://news.bgov.com/bloomberg-government-news/pentagon-investment-chief-exits-board-of-offshore-defense-funder", "https://www.propublica.org/article/george-kollitides-pentagon-contracts-alvarez-marsal"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-said-cruz-scotus-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/ted-cruz", "name": "SAID he'd name Cruz to Supreme Court (no vacancy, no nomination)", "tieType": "stated nomination intent (Supreme Court) - SAID only", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-27 (Lubbock rally)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-27 (v21)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-27", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-27-powermap-v21-V-trump-said-cruz-scotus-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "SAID (AP, Oct 27 2026, Lubbock rally): Trump said he would pick Sen. Ted Cruz as his next Supreme Court nominee: 'I'd get 100% of the vote, and he would be a Supreme Court justice.' He has floated it before; Cruz has repeatedly rejected the idea. No vacancy and no nomination filed. Campaign stop a week before the Nov 3 midterms (time order only).", "citation": ["https://apnews.com/live/trump-midterm-elections-news-updates-10-27-2026", "https://apnews.com/article/trump-iran-texas-talarico-paxton-venezuela-2f949ea7aa0f34757f8efab3f78b700d"]}, {"@id": "tie/vance-rezaei-letter-iran-talks-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jd-vance", "to": "node/mohsen-rezaei", "name": "letter proposing renewed Iran talks (Oct 2026)", "tieType": "contact (letter to Iran's Supreme National Security Council secretary proposing renewed talks, via Qatari mediators) - DONE per US officials; Trump SAID it was about medical supplies", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10 (sent ~week of Oct 19, delivered Sun Oct 25 per NYT; reported Oct 28)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-28 (v22)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-28", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-28-powermap-v22-V-vance-rezaei-letter-iran-talks-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 4, "description": "CONTACT (DONE per officials, three outlets): WSJ (Oct 28 2026, exclusive) reports VP Vance sent a letter to Mohsen Rezaei, secretary of Iran's Supreme National Security Council, to revive peace negotiations; one person said it was sent at Trump's direction. NYT (senior US official + Iranian official): letter sent last week via Qatari mediators, delivered Sunday, proposing immediate comprehensive talks incl. the nuclear program. Axios (US official): Vance suggested the letter; 'The President was enthusiastic'; talks 'require discussions on the nuclear issue'. SAID (Trump to reporters Oct 28): the letter was about helping Iran get medical supplies; no medical-supply channel documented. Whether Trump directed it is anonymous-sourced and contested by his own account. Letter one week before the Nov 3 midterms while strike options are prepared = time order only.", "citation": ["https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/vance-reaches-out-to-iranian-hard-liner-in-bid-to-restart-peace-talks-2c8a2ab8", "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/28/us/politics/vance-peace-talks-letter-iran.html", "https://www.axios.com/2026/10/28/vance-iran-nuclear-talks-letter", "https://www.ynetnews.com/article/1vep5ade5"]}, {"@id": "tie/putin-said-musk-satellite-contact-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/vladimir-putin", "to": "node/elon-musk", "name": "SAID Russia in 'close contact' with Musk on LEO satellites (Oct 28)", "tieType": "stated contact (low-Earth-orbit satellite coordination; 'brilliant person') - SAID only", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-28 (Russia-Africa summit exhibition, Moscow)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-28 (v22)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-28", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-28-powermap-v22-V-putin-said-musk-satellite-contact-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "SAID (Putin, Oct 28 2026, TASS / Interfax-Ukraine / The Insider): 'Elon Musk is a brilliant person - truly brilliant ... We are in close contact with our American partners, including Mr. Musk, because it is crucial in orbit not to interfere with one another'; Roscosmos and other companies involved 'despite any political issues'. V that he said it; the contact itself is not confirmed by Musk or SpaceX and no agreement is published. Context dated: Starshield speed cap on Ukraine's terminals ~Oct 14, lifted Oct 24 (Ukraine MoD); same day Musk reposted that Russia can destroy satellites and Starlink 'must remain a civilian operation'. Praise four days after restoration = time order only.", "citation": ["https://en.interfax.com.ua/news/general/1227612.html", "https://tass.com/politics/2209699", "https://theins.press/en/news/298878"]}, {"@id": "tie/hegseth-removes-sylvia-j5-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/pete-hegseth", "to": "node/brett-sylvia", "name": "J-5 director removed (Oct 2026; reason anon.)", "tieType": "removal (Joint Staff J-5 director, strategy/plans/policy) - departure confirmed; 'Hegseth lost confidence' per anonymous officials", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10 (week of Oct 26; reported Oct 28)", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "changed", "statusDate": "2026-10-29", "statusNote": "Superseded by V edge hegseth-fires-sylvia-leak-referral-2026: firing and Hegseth's decision now on record (Reuters officials; Parnell: AFOSI investigation, DOJ referral). The 'lost confidence' reason (Oct 28, anon.) is replaced by a leak accusation; nothing proven or charged.", "addedIn": "2026-10-28 (v22)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-29", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-28-powermap-v22-I-hegseth-removes-sylvia-j5-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "REMOVAL (I): The Atlantic (Oct 28 2026; relayed by AP/Newsmax via Yahoo) and The Hill (two US officials): Lt. Gen. Brett Sylvia, Joint Staff J-5 director, removed this week with no public explanation; Pentagon officials said Hegseth had lost confidence in him and he had a difficult working relationship with Under Secretary Elbridge Colby. ON RECORD: Joint Staff spokesperson thanked him for 32 years of service (confirms departure, not a firing or its reason). Graded I because Hegseth's role and the reason rest on anonymous officials. Predecessor Lt. Gen. Joseph McGee was also pushed out (Atlantic). Removal while CENTCOM Iran strike options are prepared = time order only.", "citation": ["https://www.yahoo.com/news/politics/articles/report-top-pentagon-planner-ousted-013929085.html", "https://thehill.com/policy/defense/6180055-hegseth-ousted-military-strategist-syllia/"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-galanis-commutation-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/jason-galanis", "name": "commuted sentence 2025-03 (Archer/Hunter Biden-linked fraud)", "tieType": "pardon/commutation (entire sentence to time served, no further fines or restitution)", "category": "pardon/settlement", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-03-28 (DOJ grant) ; 2026-10-26 (engagement to Savannah Chrisley announced)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-28 (v22)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-28", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-28-powermap-v22-V-trump-galanis-commutation-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "PARDON/COMMUTATION (DOJ primary): Executive Grant of Clemency signed Mar 28 2025 commutes Jason Galanis's entire sentence (US v. Galanis 1:15-cr-643 and S1 16 CR 371) to time served with no further fines, restitution or conditions; SDNY (Castel, Jun 11 2025) held it does not return ~$2.17M already forfeited. He was serving ~14 years; prosecutors called him the 'mastermind' of the tribal-bond fraud in which Devon Archer (Hunter Biden's ex-partner, also granted clemency by Trump) was convicted. Oct 26-27 2026: Savannah Chrisley (RNC 2024 speaker; parents pardoned by Trump May 2025) announced engagement to him and SAID she met him while working on her parents' pardons. SAID (White House official to TMZ, Oct 28): commutation was for remorse, no link to the Chrisley pardons. Sequence only; no finding the grants are connected.", "citation": ["https://www.justice.gov/pardon/media/1395021/dl?inline=", "https://www.independent.co.uk/life-style/savannah-chrisley-fiance-trump-pardon-jason-galanis-b3074446.html", "https://www.tmz.com/2026/10/28/savannah-chrisley-fiance-jason-galanis-pardon-explained/"]}, {"@id": "tie/sitrick-epstein-crisis-pr-2011", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/mike-sitrick", "to": "node/jeffrey-epstein", "name": "crisis PR emails 2011-03 (offered TMZ contact)", "tieType": "employment/advisory (crisis PR on Epstein's March 2011 statement; offered TMZ's Harvey Levin as a 'good friend') - document", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2011-03-09 (emails, DOJ Data Set 9)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-28 (v22)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-28", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-28-powermap-v22-V-sitrick-epstein-crisis-pr-2011", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "reference", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "ADVISORY (document, DOJ Epstein release, Data Set 9, EFTA00682303): Mar 9 2011 email chain: Epstein relays that 'zuckerman suggested shorter m punchier, no attack on press. plead guilty to solicitation ... no allegations of minors since 05'; Sitrick: 'Okay with leaking to British press - but think we need to get a statement out'; then 'Harvey Levin, who runs TMZ, is a good friend ... I might be able to get him to do something on the Duchess and her backpedaling.' DONE: Sitrick advised Epstein on press strategy and offered a media contact. NOT established: that Levin was contacted, that TMZ ran anything, payment terms, or any tie to TMZ's 2026 coverage. 'zuckerman' is not further identified in the email; not mapped.", "citation": ["https://epsteinexposed.com/documents/efta-efta00682303", "https://www.epsteinscan.org/pdf/1468642"]}, {"@id": "tie/thrive-holdings-adt-acquisition-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/josh-kushner-thrive-capital", "to": "node/adt", "name": "buys ADT $15.3B EV 2026-10 (Apollo-financed)", "tieType": "deal (definitive agreement: Thrive Holdings to acquire ADT, all cash, $15.3B EV; Apollo-financed)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-29 (announced; close expected Q1 2027)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-27", "statusNote": "PREM14A filed Nov 20 (opened Nov 27); go-shop to 11:59 PM NY Nov 28 2026 still running at this pass; no superior proposal on EDGAR through Nov 27; Excluded Party talks to Dec 8; close Q1 2027.", "addedIn": "2026-10-29 (v23)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-27", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-29-powermap-v23-V-thrive-holdings-adt-acquisition-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DEAL (company primary): ADT IR / GlobeNewswire Oct 29 2026: definitive agreement, ADT board unanimous, Thrive Holdings acquires ADT for $10.00/share cash (45.6% premium to the Oct 27 unaffected close of $6.87), ~$7.6B equity value, ~$15.3B enterprise value; financing commitments 'solely provided by funds managed by affiliates of Apollo Global Management'; 30-day go-shop to Nov 28 2026; close expected Q1 2027 subject to stockholder and US antitrust approval. Axios (Oct 29): Thrive Holdings is the permanent-capital vehicle formed by Josh Kushner's Thrive Capital last year; Apollo is ADT's former owner, which sold its remaining stake five months ago. Thrive partners named in the release: Kareem Zaki, Anuj Mehndiratta (Josh Kushner is not quoted). Announced, not closed.", "citation": ["https://investor.adt.com/News--Events/news/news-details/2026/ADT-to-be-Acquired-by-Thrive-Holdings-in-15-3-Billion-Transaction/default.aspx", "https://www.axios.com/pro/all-deals/2026/10/29/thrive-holdings-adt-15b-take-private"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-adt-oge-278t-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/adt", "name": "278-T: ADT shares sold 2026-07 ($15K-50K)", "tieType": "financial disclosure (OGE 278-T: ADT stock sold 2026-07-29, $15,001-$50,000) - sequence only with the Thrive deal", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-07-29 (sale) ; 2026-09-08 (278-T) ; 2026-10-29 (deal announced)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": true, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-29 (v23)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-29", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-29-powermap-v23-V-trump-adt-oge-278t-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DISCLOSURE (OGE primary): President Trump's OGE Form 278-T dated Sep 8 2026 (text layer read) lists line 509 'ADT INC DEL' sale 7/29/2026, $15,001-$50,000 (same date as a batch of other equity sales; accounts are managed, discretionary orders). The Oct 29 register row also read earlier 2026 ADT purchases via OCR of the Feb 26 2026 278-T; this pass did not re-find those lines in the PDF text layer (left as filed there, not re-asserted here). SEQUENCE ONLY: the account sold ADT about three months before Thrive Holdings (Josh Kushner's Thrive Capital vehicle; Josh is Jared Kushner's brother) agreed to buy ADT at a 45.6% premium. No evidence of foreknowledge; no claim the trades and the deal are connected; whether any ADT position remained on Oct 29 is unknown (ranges, not holdings).", "citation": ["https://extapps2.oge.gov/201/Presiden.nsf/PAS%2BIndex/E590116FC9631E9885258E7A002DE209/%24FILE/Donald-J-Trump-09.8.2026-278T.pdf", "https://extapps2.oge.gov/201/Presiden.nsf/PAS%2BIndex/BCF60D94B8F1E59285258DB000347F61/%24FILE/Donald%20J.%20Trump%202.26.2026%20278-T%20%282%29.pdf"]}, {"@id": "tie/hegseth-fires-sylvia-leak-referral-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/pete-hegseth", "to": "node/brett-sylvia", "name": "fired J-5 Sylvia 2026-10 (leak accusation, DOJ referral)", "tieType": "removal (firing of Joint Staff J-5 director; Pentagon on record: AFOSI investigation, DOJ referral for alleged leaking)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10 (week of Oct 26; on record Oct 29)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-29 (v23)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-29", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-29-powermap-v23-V-hegseth-fires-sylvia-leak-referral-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "FIRING (V, upgrades the v22 I edge hegseth-removes-sylvia-j5-2026): Reuters via Military Times (Oct 29 2026): 'Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth has fired U.S. Army Lt. Gen. Brett Sylvia ... over accusations that he leaked classified information', officials said. ON RECORD: chief Pentagon spokesperson Sean Parnell said the decision followed an extensive Air Force OSI investigation and 'This matter, along with others, have been referred to the Justice Department for potential further legal action'; the Joint Staff withdrew its earlier thank-you statement. SAID (anonymous senior Pentagon official): Sylvia failed three polygraphs; 'Secretary Hegseth took immediate action and fired Sylvia'. SAID (Trump, to reporters, misgendering him): 'She's got problems ... We're very much looking for leakers'. NOT established: any leak, charge or court finding; Sylvia could not be reached. Firing while Iran strike options are prepared = time order only.", "citation": ["https://www.militarytimes.com/news/2026/10/29/senior-us-general-fired-accused-of-leaking-classified-information/", "https://apnews.com/article/general-firing-hegseth-pentagon-leaks-346ce31afab5dfc2cacc5efac502bc6d"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-said-habba-library-cut-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/alina-habba", "name": "SAID (anon.): give library a cut of $50M deal 2026-10", "tieType": "SAID (per people briefed): Habba should give part of her >$50M Herrera-family contract to his future library; family should stop paying", "category": "contract", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10 (week of Oct 19; reported Oct 29)", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-29 (v23)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-30", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-29-powermap-v23-I-trump-said-habba-library-cut-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "SAID (I): The New York Times (Oct 29 2026, relayed and quoted by Mediaite): Trump 'erupted last week' on learning Alina Habba Mildon secured a >$50M four-year contract from the family of Julio Herrera Velutini (pardoned weeks after she started), and 'has told aides and allies that she should donate a portion of that money to his future presidential library or another Trump-related entity, according to multiple people briefed on the conversations'; he told at least one ally the family should not pay the rest of the contract. Graded I: anonymous people briefed; no on-record Trump statement; no donation, payment stop or library receipt documented (DONE = nothing). Habba SAID: her employment was vetted and disclosed to DOJ and had nothing to do with securing a pardon.", "citation": ["https://www.mediaite.com/politics/trump/trump-reportedly-erupted-after-learning-his-former-lawyer-scored-50-million-in-alleged-pardon-deal/"]}, {"@id": "tie/blanche-odag-classified-epstein-material-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/todd-blanche", "to": "node/jeffrey-epstein", "name": "ODAG got 'classified' Epstein items 2025-03 (vs SAID none withheld)", "tieType": "document custody (DOJ release shows Blanche's ODAG received 'classified material' among 16 Epstein items, Mar 25 2025) vs his SAID 'not withholding anything' on that basis", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-03-25 (delivery) ; 2026-10-28 (CBS analysis)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-29 (v23)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-29", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-29-powermap-v23-V-blanche-odag-classified-epstein-material-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DOCUMENT (DOJ Epstein release, read and quoted by CBS News Oct 28 2026): an FBI New York timeline in the files shows delivery on Mar 25 2025 of '16 Epstein items to ODAG' (Office of the Deputy Attorney General, then Blanche), items 2 and 6 described as 'Epstein Transparency Project - Classified Material' and 'CDs with classified materials (x2)'; a same-day email from the FBI National Security Classification Operations Unit chief attaches 'Epstein - Classified Document Memo.docx' and says three documents 'remain classified'. SAID (Blanche): 'no files are being withheld or redacted on that basis'; 'we're actually not withholding anything based upon [national defense information]'. NOT established: what was classified, whether any of it was withheld from the release, or why; CBS's Bates-gap analysis (tens of thousands of missing pages incl. 66 check images) may partly reflect de-duplication. DOJ did not respond to CBS.", "citation": ["https://www.cbsnews.com/news/epstein-files-classified-material-missing-documents-suggest/"]}, {"@id": "tie/alice-huang-nvidia-ci-concern-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/alice-huang-megaspeed", "to": "node/nvidia", "name": "CI concern: 'asset' close to Jensen Huang (anon.) 2026-10", "tieType": "counter-intelligence concern (US officials: Megaspeed executive a Chinese intelligence asset with a close relationship to CEO Jensen Huang; Trump briefed, no action) - anonymous", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2024-2026 (relationship) ; ~2025-10 (Trump briefed) ; 2026-10-29 (NYT)", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "changed", "statusDate": "2026-11-12", "statusNote": "Huang resigned Nov 11 (8-K Nov 12, no reason stated). Counter-intelligence claim still anonymous (NYT); no agency on record.", "addedIn": "2026-10-29 (v23)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-12", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-29-powermap-v23-I-alice-huang-nvidia-ci-concern-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID (I): The New York Times (Oct 29 2026; relayed by Tom's Hardware, fetched): US officials concluded Alice Huang (Huang Le), a Megaspeed executive, is a Chinese intelligence asset passing information to Beijing and that she has a close relationship with Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang (seen together around Computex 2024 and 2025); Trump was briefed about a year ago and took no action; Jensen Huang has not received a defensive briefing; officials do not believe he knows. Megaspeed (Nvidia cloud partner) is under a Commerce probe since late 2024 over possible chip diversion, handed to DOJ. ON RECORD: Nvidia: Jensen's interactions with Ms. Huang are 'not unusual or unexpected'; customers get 'ordinary business information' and 'zero information relevant to national security'; Chinese embassy: 'groundless smears'. Graded I: no US agency statement; anonymous officials. Why Trump did not act = TK (outlets relay reluctance to hurt Nvidia sales; that is reporting, not a statement).", "citation": ["https://www.tomshardware.com/tech-industry/policy/nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-may-have-been-the-target-of-a-spy-plot-through-chinese-intelligence-asset-report-claims-exec-from-firm-under-investigation-for-smuggling-banned-ai-chips-to-china-accused-of-being-a-spy-was-also-feeding-information-to-beijing", "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/29/us/politics/nvidia-china-jensen-huang-trump.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/lagarde-ecb-step-down-costa-2027", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/christine-lagarde", "to": "node/european-council-antonio-costa", "name": "steps down ECB 2027-02-07; Costa opens succession", "tieType": "appointment (resignation notified; successor to be appointed by the European Council under TFEU Art. 283)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-29 (notified) ; 2027-02-07 (effective)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-29 (v23)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-29", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-29-powermap-v23-V-lagarde-ecb-step-down-costa-2027", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "APPOINTMENT (primary): ECB press release Oct 29 2026: Lagarde informed the Governing Council and European Council President Antonio Costa that she will step down on 7 February 2027; successor 'will be appointed by the European Council following the nomination process outlined in Article 283 TFEU'. Council statement (Costa, same day) says the appointment process is initiated. Term was due to end Oct 2027 (CNBC). SAID (Lagarde, X video): 'I will step down as @ECB President on 7 February 2027.' Reason: not stated on record (Politico relays an anonymous official: to speak more freely). Successor not named; press-named candidates are not an official list. Allied-power appointment tie; no US link claimed.", "citation": ["https://www.ecb.europa.eu/press/pr/date/2026/html/ecb.pr261029~abbb6dc64b.en.html", "https://www.consilium.europa.eu/en/press/press-releases/2026/10/29/statement-by-president-antonio-costa-on-the-forthcoming-departure-of-christine-lagarde-from-the-european-central-bank/"]}, {"@id": "tie/corecivic-dhs-prairie-495m-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/corecivic-private-prisons-ice-detention", "to": "node/ice", "name": "sold Prairie prison to DHS $495.6M 2026-08 (offered MN $75M 2025-05)", "tieType": "contract / asset sale (DHS bought the idle 1,600-bed Prairie Correctional Facility from CoreCivic for ~$495.6M, Aug 4 2026; CoreCivic manages it for ICE to Aug 2031) vs CoreCivic's $75M offer to Minnesota (May 2025)", "category": "contract", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-05-07 ($75M offer to Minnesota DOC) ; 2026-08-04 (sale to DHS + ICE management contract) ; 2026-10-29 (KARE 11 records)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-11-09", "statusNote": "Prices unchanged Nov 9. CoreCivic Oct 31 company statement SAID the $495.6M came from government-hired independent appraisers using replacement-cost methodology and that $75M was a 2015 preliminary figure; appraisal document itself still not public. MN AG Ellison Oct 30 asked Congress to investigate. Hole prairie-price-basis stays open.", "addedIn": "2026-10-30 (v24)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-30-powermap-v24-V-corecivic-dhs-prairie-495m-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (primary, CoreCivic 8-K, event Aug 4 2026): CoreCivic sold its 1,600-bed Prairie Correctional Facility (Appleton, Minnesota; idle since 2010) to the United States 'by and through the Department of Homeland Security' for approximately $495.6 million, and the 1,033-bed Midwest Regional Reception Center (Leavenworth, KS) for ~$238.4 million, both closing on signing; CoreCivic 'recently entered into a management agreement with ICE' for Prairie, expiring August 2031. DONE (records obtained by KARE 11, Oct 29 2026): a May 7 2025 email from CoreCivic to Minnesota's Deputy Corrections Commissioner offered the same facility to the state for $75M 'inclusive of the upgrades'; Minnesota declined. The gap is about $420M. SAID: CoreCivic (written statement): independent appraisers used a cost-based methodology and 'the federal government ultimately determined the sale price'; Minnesota Corrections Commissioner Paul Schnell: 'unexplainable'; Rep. Betty McCollum calls for a congressional investigation, citing the owners as 'mega donors'; DHS Secretary Markwayne Mullin's office did not answer KARE 11. GAO (Sep 2026, per KARE 11) warned ICE facility purchases risk waste. NOT established: how DHS set the price, any appraisal record, or any link between CoreCivic's donations and the price (time order only; see corecivic-trump-inaugural-500k-2024).", "citation": ["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1070985/000119312526335068/d174637d8k.htm", "https://www.kare11.com/article/news/investigations/kare-11-investigates-private-prison-was-on-sale-for-75-million-ice-paid-495-million/89-4b28b6c7-8823-42b3-9f70-95a78f714e18"]}, {"@id": "tie/corecivic-trump-inaugural-500k-2024", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/corecivic-private-prisons-ice-detention", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "$500K inaugural (2024-12)", "tieType": "funding ($500K to the Trump-Vance Inaugural Committee, Dec 2024)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2024-12", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-30 (v24)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-30", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-30-powermap-v24-V-corecivic-trump-inaugural-500k-2024", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE: CoreCivic reported in a lobbying disclosure that it donated $500,000 to the Trump-Vance inaugural committee in December 2024 (ABC News, Jan 29 2025); KARE 11 (Oct 29 2026): 'Federal records show CoreCivic donated half a million dollars to the Trump-Vance inaugural committee' and its CEO made personal contributions to Trump-affiliated committees (amounts not given; not mapped). Both CoreCivic and GEO Group subsidiaries gave $250K each to the 2017 inaugural (ABC). Sequence only with the 2026 DHS purchases: no exchange is shown.", "citation": ["https://abcnews.com/US/private-prison-firm-corecivic-gave-500k-trumps-inauguration/story?id=118218707", "https://www.kare11.com/article/news/investigations/kare-11-investigates-private-prison-was-on-sale-for-75-million-ice-paid-495-million/89-4b28b6c7-8823-42b3-9f70-95a78f714e18"]}, {"@id": "tie/binance-spacex-spcx-stake-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/binance-changpeng-zhao", "to": "node/spacex", "name": "holds SpaceX shares >$1B (SAID by CZ / Yi He) 2026-10", "tieType": "equity stake (SAID by Binance's founders: 'SPCX shares' worth more than $1B, from the $500M 2022 Twitter co-investment) - no filing read", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2022-10 ($500M wired to Twitter deal) ; 2026-10-30 (CZ / Yi He posts)", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-11-09", "statusNote": "Still SAID only (CZ / Yi He Oct 30); no SpaceX or Binance holding filing found Nov 9. Binance Nov 8 withdrawal re-enable + Elliptic Nov 7/9 laundering notes are operational, not ownership. Hole binance-spcx-holding-record stays open.", "addedIn": "2026-10-30 (v24)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-30-powermap-v24-I-binance-spacex-spcx-stake-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "SAID (Binance founder Changpeng Zhao on X, Oct 30 2026, replying to Elon Musk's emoji after the ~$6.3B Binance hack; quoted by Decrypt and Reuters via CNA): 'Our SPCX shares (from our $500m investment in your Twitter takeover) are worth more than a billion'; later 'we have $1.x billion in SPCX alone'. SAID (co-founder/co-CEO Yi He, X): 'we do not yet need to sell the SpaceX shares you are bullish on'. DONE (chain, earlier rows): Binance committed $500M of equity to Musk's 2022 Twitter buyout (SEC 13D/A; binance-musk-twitter-equity-500m); SpaceX absorbed xAI (which held X) in Feb 2026. Graded I: the holding, its size and the conversion path are the holders' own statements; no SpaceX or Binance filing showing the position was read. Musk replied only with an emoji; no statement from SpaceX. Binance founder CZ was pardoned by Trump in Oct 2025 (separate edge).", "citation": ["https://decrypt.co/382236/elon-musk-cz-trade-blows-spacex-shares-binance-hack", "https://www.channelnewsasia.com/business/binance-does-not-need-sell-spacex-shares-cover-losses-co-founder-says-6506791", "https://x.com/cz_binance/status/2116097554882728341"]}, {"@id": "tie/kushner-iger-walter-lakers-12-5b-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/josh-kushner-thrive-capital", "to": "node/mark-walter-guggenheim-dodgers-lakers-owner", "name": "buying Lakers $12.5B (agreed 2026-08; terms set 2026-10-30, unsigned)", "tieType": "deal (pending: agreement to buy the Los Angeles Lakers from Mark Walter at a $12.5B valuation, with Bob Iger; needs signing and NBA Board of Governors approval)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-08-12 (announced) ; 2026-10-30 (remaining terms agreed, anon.)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-09", "statusNote": "Still unsigned Nov 9 (no purchase-agreement signing or NBA Board of Governors vote reported Nov 7-9; LA Times Oct 30 'agree on all terms' newest). Hole lakers-signing-nba-approval stays open.", "addedIn": "2026-10-30 (v24)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-30-powermap-v24-V-kushner-iger-walter-lakers-12-5b-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE/SAID on record (Axios, Aug 12 2026): Josh Kushner and Bob Iger announced an agreement to buy the Lakers at a $12.5B valuation (statement to Axios); Walter issued a statement; Kushner to be control owner (per a source); 'only an agreement, not a finalized deal', needs league approval; Kushner must sell his Miami Heat minority stake. SAID (anon., LA Times Oct 30 2026, 'several people with knowledge'): Walter and Kushner agreed the outstanding terms at Walter's Florida home; the agreement still needs to be signed, reviewed by the NBA and approved by the Board of Governors; Kushner assured Walter he has the funds. Context (LA Times citing Bloomberg, anon.): Walter's TWG Global is raising money to pay down loans on its insurers' books that drew DOJ scrutiny - not established here, not mapped. Josh Kushner is Jared Kushner's brother; his Thrive Holdings agreed Oct 29 to buy ADT (separate edge). Not closed.", "citation": ["https://www.axios.com/2026/08/12/josh-kushner-bob-iger-lakers", "https://www.latimes.com/sports/lakers/story/2026-10-30/mark-walter-jared-kushner-agree-on-all-lakers-sale-terms"]}, {"@id": "tie/kushner-iger-thrive-eternal-partners-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/josh-kushner-thrive-capital", "to": "node/bob-iger", "name": "partners: Thrive Eternal + Lakers bid 2026", "tieType": "business partners (Thrive Eternal sports-investment platform; co-buyers of the Lakers)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026 (Thrive Eternal) ; 2026-08-12 (joint Lakers agreement)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-30 (v24)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-30", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-30-powermap-v24-V-kushner-iger-thrive-eternal-partners-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE/SAID (Axios Aug 12 2026; joint statement by Kushner and Iger): Kushner and Iger 'work together on a sports-focused investment platform called Thrive Eternal' and jointly agreed to buy the Lakers; each would invest individually, Thrive Eternal capped at 20% by NBA rules (per a source). LA Times Oct 30 2026: 'Bob Iger ... is in partnership with Kushner on the deal.'", "citation": ["https://www.axios.com/2026/08/12/josh-kushner-bob-iger-lakers", "https://www.latimes.com/sports/lakers/story/2026-10-30/mark-walter-jared-kushner-agree-on-all-lakers-sale-terms"]}, {"@id": "tie/walter-boehly-dodgers-coowners", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/mark-walter-guggenheim-dodgers-lakers-owner", "to": "node/todd-boehly", "name": "Dodgers co-owners; sold Chelsea stake 2026-09", "tieType": "co-owners (Los Angeles Dodgers) ; jointly sold their small Chelsea FC stake (Sep 2026, FT via LA Times)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "ongoing (Dodgers) ; 2026-09 (Chelsea stake sale, reported)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-30 (v24)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-30", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-30-powermap-v24-V-walter-boehly-dodgers-coowners", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE (LA Times, Oct 30 2026): Walter, owner of the Dodgers, 'and Dodgers co-owner Todd Boehly sold their small stake in the English Premier League club Chelsea last month, The Financial Times reported'; Walter will not sell the Dodgers (Kasten, Aug; TWG statement, Sep). Boehly separately leads the pending bid for Lukoil's international assets (boehly-lukoil-consortium). This edge links the Lakers seller to the Lukoil bidder as co-owners only; no tie between the two deals is claimed.", "citation": ["https://www.latimes.com/sports/lakers/story/2026-10-30/mark-walter-jared-kushner-agree-on-all-lakers-sale-terms"]}, {"@id": "tie/blackstone-anthropic-north-star-anchor-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/stephen-schwarzman-blackstone-ceo", "to": "node/anthropic", "name": "Blackstone anchors $63B North Star chip debt ($9B junior) 2026-10", "tieType": "funding (Blackstone funds anchor investor in Anthropic's $63B 'Project North Star' chip financing; ~$9B of the $18B junior debt) - reported, people familiar", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10 (North Star closed earlier in the week of Oct 26) ; 2026-10-30 (FT: rating guidance)", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-30 (v24)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-30", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-30-powermap-v24-I-blackstone-anthropic-north-star-anchor-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID (FT, Oct 30 2026, people familiar; text read via Valor Economico's FT republication): Blackstone is the anchor investor in 'Project North Star', Anthropic's $63B chip financing (lease of 1.5 GW of Google chips; >$42B senior debt guaranteed by Broadcom, $18B junior debt backed by Anthropic's lease payments), and its funds invested $9B in the junior debt at a >10% yield (FT earlier); Blackstone told investors Anthropic is now more likely to get a BB-or-higher (sub-investment-grade) rating after its IPO, versus earlier investment-grade guidance, and is working with the banks to sell the debt on. KBRA rated the junior debt BB+ (positive outlook), Morningstar DBRS BB (per sources); Fitch/Moody's/S&P have no Anthropic rating. Anthropic, Blackstone, KBRA, DBRS and S&P declined to comment. Graded I: no filing or on-record statement of Blackstone's position. Schwarzman node stands for Blackstone (he is co-founder/CEO); no personal role claimed.", "citation": ["https://valor.globo.com/financas/noticia/2026/10/30/ft-anthropic-pode-no-ter-grau-de-investimento-aps-ipo-diz-blackstone-a-investidores.ghtml", "https://www.ft.com/stream/15c0cb45-8892-46cd-a086-1d2716ae7246"]}, {"@id": "tie/khalid-bin-salman-hegseth-call-2026-11-02", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/khalid-bin-salman", "to": "node/pete-hegseth", "name": "phone call 2026-11-02 (MoD primary)", "tieType": "documented contact (phone call: strategic defense partnership / regional de-escalation / Houthi attacks)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-02", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-02 (v25)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-02", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-02-powermap-v25-V-khalid-bin-salman-hegseth-call-2026-11-02", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE/SAID (Saudi MoD primary): @modgovksa 2117370430918897806 (Mon Nov 2 2026 ~4:37pm ET): Defense Minister Prince Khalid bin Salman held a phone call with US Secretary of War Pete Hegseth; they reviewed strategic defense cooperation and regional/global developments, foremost de-escalation / containing tensions and continued Houthi attacks on the Kingdom (Arabic full text via note_tweet; English relays: Iran International, Arab News, Al Arabiya). Graded V on the MoD primary for the call occurring and the topics named. No US War.gov/Defense.gov readout fetched here (pages returned 403); no claim about strikes on Iranian launchers or any causal link. Separate from the Feb 24 2025 Pentagon in-person meeting (khalid-bin-salman-hegseth).", "citation": ["https://x.com/modgovksa/status/2117370430918897806", "https://www.iranintl.com/en/202611024568", "https://english.alarabiya.net/News/saudi-arabia/2026/11/03/prince-khalid-pentagon-chief-discuss-houthi-terrorist-attacks-on-saudi-arabia"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-habba-concord-unacceptable-2026-10-31", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/alina-habba", "name": "on-record: Concord $50M 'not acceptable' 2026-10-31", "tieType": "public statement (on-record: Habba's >$50M Concord Partners contract 'not acceptable' / 'obnoxious and outrageous')", "category": "contract", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-31", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-02 (v25)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-02", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-02-powermap-v25-V-trump-habba-concord-unacceptable-2026-10-31", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID on record (Reuters, Oct 31 2026, Palm Beach / Mar-a-Lago): President Trump told reporters Habba Mildon's ~$50M Concord Partners contract was 'totally obnoxious and outrageous' and 'not acceptable at all'; he said he told her he did not want her paid and called the episode 'terrible'. Distinct from trump-said-habba-library-cut-2026 (I, anonymous: donate part to his library). This edge is the on-record presidential criticism of the Concord employment contract itself; no payment stop, donation or library receipt is DONE here. Habba previously SAID the job was vetted/disclosed to DOJ and denied any pardon role. Sequence with isabela-herrera-concord-habba-50m and trump-herrera-velutini-pardon-2026 is time order only.", "citation": ["https://www.yahoo.com/news/articles/trump-calls-50-million-contract-022149834.html", "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/1/trump-slams-ex-lawyers-50m-deal-with-pardoned-bankers-family"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-netanyahu-iran-call-2026-10-31", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/benjamin-netanyahu", "name": "Iran phone call 2026-10-31", "tieType": "documented contact (phone call about Iran war / negotiations)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-31", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-02 (v25)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-02", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-02-powermap-v25-V-trump-netanyahu-iran-call-2026-10-31", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE/SAID: Trump confirmed on Sunday Nov 1 2026 that he spoke with Netanyahu on Saturday Oct 31 about Iran, calling it a 'very good talk' (ABC News via Yahoo live updates). Axios (Nov 1, one Israeli + one US source, both anonymous): Netanyahu pressed for renewed US strikes after the Nov 3 midterms while Trump preferred to let negotiations continue; call described as 'tough'/'direct'; WH and PMO declined to comment on content. Graded V for the call itself (Trump on record); the post-midterms pressure content remains SAID by anonymous sources and is not mapped as DONE. Contact edge only — no causation for later strike decisions. Separate from trump-netanyahu-endorsement-2026.", "citation": ["https://www.yahoo.com/news/politics/articles/iran-live-updates-trump-says-081133822.html", "https://www.axios.com/2026/11/01/trump-netanyahu-iran-negotiations-war"]}, {"@id": "tie/geo-ice-big-spring-2329-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/geo-group-private-prisons-ice-detention", "to": "node/ice", "name": "Big Spring 2,329 beds ~$200M/yr 2026-11", "tieType": "contract (GEO support services at 2,329-bed Big Spring Complex under City of Big Spring 10-year ICE IGSA; ~$200M/yr expected year 1)", "category": "contract", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-02 (GEO announcement; city IGSA approved ~Oct 28; term through ~2036)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-02 (v25)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-02", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-02-powermap-v25-V-geo-ice-big-spring-2329-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (GEO Group primary, Business Wire / IR, Nov 2 2026): City of Big Spring, Texas entered a 10-year intergovernmental service agreement with ICE to activate a federal immigration processing center at the 2,329-bed Big Spring Complex (1,404-bed Flightline + 925-bed Cedar Hill); GEO will provide support services (exclusive ICE use, security, maintenance, food, medical, recreation, transportation); GEO expects ~$200M annual revenue in the first full year. Local reporting: Big Spring City Council approved the ICE agreement ~Oct 28. GEO is already a MAGA Inc. donor (geo-group-maga-inc-4-4m); donation -> contract is time order only — no exchange claimed. Companion to CoreCivic's Prairie DHS purchase (separate operator).", "citation": ["https://investors.geogroup.com/node/19236/pdf", "https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20261030077010/en/The-GEO-Group-Announces-Contract-for-Big-Spring-Complex-in-Texas-Totaling-2329-Beds", "https://www.firstalert7.com/2026/10/29/big-spring-city-council-votes-7-0-approve-ice-detention-agreement/"]}, {"@id": "tie/lionsgate-mhr-rachesky-13pct-chair", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/mark-rachesky-mhr-fund-management", "to": "node/lionsgate-studios", "name": "MHR 13.0% + chair", "tieType": "ownership (13.0%, 37,648,498 shares, 13D/A) + board chair", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-07-08 (13D/A event)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-03 (v26)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-03", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-03-powermap-v26-V-lionsgate-mhr-rachesky-13pct-chair", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "MHR Fund Management (Mark Rachesky) beneficially owns 37,648,498 Lionsgate Studios common shares, ~13.0% (Schedule 13D/A filed Jul 9 2026); Rachesky chairs the board (2026 proxy). MHR and Liberty 77 vote for each other's board nominees under the Jan 26 2026 standstill (cap 17.5%).", "citation": ["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1277742/000119312526299128/xslSCHEDULE_13D_X02/primary_doc.xml", "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2052959/000119312526321010/d105125ddef14a.htm"]}, {"@id": "tie/lionsgate-mnuchin-liberty77-13pct-director", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/steven-mnuchin", "to": "node/lionsgate-studios", "name": "Liberty 77 13.0% + board seat", "tieType": "ownership (Liberty 77 / Liberty Strategic Capital 13.0%, 37.55M shares) + director", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-01-26", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-03 (v26)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-03", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-03-powermap-v26-V-lionsgate-mnuchin-liberty77-13pct-director", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "Liberty 77 Capital L.P. (Steven T. Mnuchin reporting person) holds 37,548,125 Lionsgate shares, ~13.0% (13D/A Jan 27 2026); Lionsgate appointed Mnuchin as the Liberty-designated director Jan 26 2026 under a governance, standstill and voting agreement with Liberty and MHR (8-K).", "citation": ["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1905374/000095014226000238/xslSCHEDULE_13D_X01/primary_doc.xml", "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2052959/000119312526021731/d101361d8k.htm"]}, {"@id": "tie/pif-mnuchin-liberty-strategic-1b", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/saudi-pif", "to": "node/steven-mnuchin", "name": "PIF $1B into Mnuchin fund", "tieType": "funding (LP commitment ~$1B to Liberty Strategic Capital fund)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2021-2022 (NYT report Apr 2022)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-03 (v26)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-03", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-03-powermap-v26-V-pif-mnuchin-liberty-strategic-1b", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "other", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "PIF invested $1B in Mnuchin's Liberty Strategic Capital fund (NYT, relayed by Bisnow, Apr 2022). Whether PIF money sits in the Liberty 77 funds that hold Lionsgate shares is not documented (hole).", "citation": ["https://www.bisnow.com/news/national/capital-markets/jared-kushner-private-equity-fund-2b-saudi-wealth-crown-princer-mbs-112574"]}, {"@id": "tie/apollo-owns-legendary", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/apollo-global-management", "to": "node/legendary-entertainment", "name": "Apollo owns Legendary", "tieType": "ownership (control, with Legendary management, after 2024 Wanda stake buyout)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2024 ; 2026-10", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-03 (v26)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-03", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-03-powermap-v26-V-apollo-owns-legendary", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "Legendary is owned by Apollo Global Management and company management (Bloomberg Oct 20 2026; Variety: 2024 buyout of Wanda's stake left Legendary and Apollo in control).", "citation": ["https://news.bloomberglaw.com/mergers-and-acquisitions/legendary-revives-lionsgate-takeover-talks-submits-offer", "https://variety.com/2026/film/news/lionsgate-stock-legendary-entertainment-acquisition-offer-1236917824/"]}, {"@id": "tie/legendary-lionsgate-offer-2026-10", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/legendary-entertainment", "to": "node/lionsgate-studios", "name": "takeover offer Oct 2026", "tieType": "takeover offer (reported, price undisclosed; ~$3.5-3.6B EV incl. ~$1.9B debt per Variety/MPN)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-20", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-09", "statusNote": "Still SAID (Bloomberg Oct 20 unnamed offer); Lionsgate CEO Feltheimer Nov 5 earnings call: 'We are not going to respond to M&A speculation' (Deadline). No price, agreement or filing. Hole legendary-lionsgate-offer-terms stays open.", "addedIn": "2026-11-03 (v26)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-03-powermap-v26-V-legendary-lionsgate-offer-2026-10", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID (Bloomberg, Oct 20 2026, unnamed sources): Legendary revived talks and submitted a takeover offer for Lionsgate; Legendary, Lionsgate and Apollo declined comment. No price, no agreement, no Lionsgate filing as of Nov 3 2026.", "citation": ["https://news.bloomberglaw.com/mergers-and-acquisitions/legendary-revives-lionsgate-takeover-talks-submits-offer", "https://deadline.com/2026/10/liongate-stock-jumps-takeover-offer-legendary-1237168877/"]}, {"@id": "tie/apollo-skydance-wbd-debt", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/apollo-global-management", "to": "node/david-ellison", "name": "co-led WBD deal debt", "tieType": "financing (co-led debt financing of Skydance/Paramount acquisition of WBD, with Bank of America and Citigroup)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-06", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-03 (v26)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-03", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-03-powermap-v26-V-apollo-skydance-wbd-debt", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "Skydance press release Oct 6 2026: 'The debt financing for the transaction was led by Bank of America, Citigroup and Apollo.' Same Apollo owns Legendary, the Lionsgate bidder.", "citation": ["https://www.skydance.com/news/press/paramount-completes-acquisition-of-warner-bros-discovery-creating-a-new-global-entertainment-leader-skydance"]}, {"@id": "tie/pif-skydance-classb-equity", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/saudi-pif", "to": "node/david-ellison", "name": "PIF equity in Skydance", "tieType": "funding (Class B equity in $47B raise for WBD deal, priced $12/share)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-06", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-03 (v26)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-03", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-03-powermap-v26-V-pif-skydance-classb-equity", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "Skydance PR Oct 6 2026: $47B new Class B equity led by Ellison Family, RedBird, PIF, L'IMAD, QIA and LionTree; Ellisons + RedBird hold 100% of voting Class A.", "citation": ["https://www.skydance.com/news/press/paramount-completes-acquisition-of-warner-bros-discovery-creating-a-new-global-entertainment-leader-skydance"]}, {"@id": "tie/liberty-global-fries-lionsgate", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/michael-fries-liberty-global", "to": "node/lionsgate-studios", "name": "Liberty Global 2.5% + Fries director", "tieType": "ownership (Liberty Global 7.04M shares, ~2.5%, 13D May 2025) + director", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-05-06", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-03 (v26)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-03", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-03-powermap-v26-V-liberty-global-fries-lionsgate", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "Liberty Global Ltd. holds 7,035,969 Lionsgate shares (~2.5%, 13D May 8 2025) under a voting agreement with MHR; Liberty Global CEO Michael Fries sits on the Lionsgate board (2026 proxy).", "citation": ["https://13f.info/cusip/53626N102", "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2052959/000119312526321010/d105125ddef14a.htm"]}, {"@id": "tie/jpmorgan-lionsgate-revolver-agent", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jpmorgan-chase", "to": "node/lionsgate-studios", "name": "revolver agent $800M", "tieType": "lending (administrative agent, $800M senior secured revolver, matures May 6 2030; undrawn Jun 30 2026)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-05-06", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-03 (v26)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-03", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-03-powermap-v26-V-jpmorgan-lionsgate-revolver-agent", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "Lionsgate 10-Q (Jun 30 2026): $800M revolver with JPMorgan Chase Bank as administrative agent, undrawn; corporate debt $1.94B = $389.9M senior notes + $362M eOne IP facility + $1,156M LG IP facility + $30.7M 3 Arts facility. Change of control is an event of default.", "citation": ["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2052959/000205295926000067/R13.htm"]}, {"@id": "tie/feltheimer-lionsgate-ceo-televisa", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jon-feltheimer", "to": "node/lionsgate-studios", "name": "CEO; Televisa director", "tieType": "employment (CEO + director; also director of Grupo Televisa)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-05", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-03 (v26)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-03", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-03-powermap-v26-V-feltheimer-lionsgate-ceo-televisa", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "2026 proxy: Feltheimer is Lionsgate CEO and a director, and a director of Grupo Televisa; holds ~1.0% (3.09M shares per Longbridge/Form 4 Jul 2026).", "citation": ["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2052959/000119312526321010/d105125ddef14a.htm"]}, {"@id": "tie/colorforce-lionsgate-hunger-games", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/color-force-nina-jacobson-brad-simpson", "to": "node/lionsgate-studios", "name": "Hunger Games rights partner", "tieType": "business deal (Hunger Games film rights partner; Lionsgate acquired worldwide distribution rights 2009 with Color Force producing)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2009-03 ; 2026-11-20", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-03 (v26)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-03", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-03-powermap-v26-V-colorforce-lionsgate-hunger-games", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "Scholastic 2009: Lionsgate acquired worldwide distribution rights to Suzanne Collins's The Hunger Games, in partnership with Color Force (Nina Jacobson); Jacobson and Simpson produce Sunrise on the Reaping (Nov 20 2026). Color Force is owned by Jacobson and Simpson (LA Times 2018).", "citation": ["https://www.scholastic.com/newsroom/all-news/press-release/lionsgate--feasts-on-the-hunger-games.html", "https://www.latimes.com/business/hollywood/la-fi-ct-nina-jacobson-color-force-20181002-story.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/malik-fannie-mae-board-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/omeed-malik-1789-capital", "to": "node/fannie-mae", "name": "Fannie Mae board (resigned Oct 30 2026)", "tieType": "employment (board of directors; appointed Apr 14 2025 by FHFA; resigned effective Oct 30 2026)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-04-14 ; 2026-10-30", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "ended", "statusDate": "2026-10-30", "statusNote": "Fannie Mae 8-K filed Nov 3 2026 (event Oct 30): Malik resigned from the Board effective Oct 30 2026; appointment edge kept as historical DONE; role ended. No reason stated. Unchanged Nov 6.", "addedIn": "2026-11-03 (v26)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-04", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-03-powermap-v26-V-malik-fannie-mae-board-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE (SEC primary): Fannie Mae 8-K (Apr 15 2025, event Apr 14): Omeed Malik appointed to the Board of Directors effective Apr 14 2025 (FHFA conservator appointment). Fannie Mae 8-K (filed Nov 3 2026, event Oct 30 2026, accession 0000310522-26-000095): Malik notified Fannie Mae of his resignation from the Board effective Oct 30 2026; no reason stated. Malik is president of 1789 Capital, where Donald Trump Jr. became a partner in Nov 2024 (existing edge trump-jr-1789-polymarket-kalshi). Board seat is historical DONE; role ended Oct 30 2026.", "citation": ["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/310522/000031052225000220/fnm-20250414.htm", "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/310522/000031052226000095/fnm-20261030.htm"]}, {"@id": "tie/zelenskyy-witkoff-kushner-call-2026-11-04", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/volodymyr-zelensky", "to": "node/steve-witkoff-jared-kushner", "name": "90-min call Nov 4 2026", "tieType": "documented contact (90-minute phone call: trilateral Ukraine-US-Russia prep, Patriot interceptors, Drone Deal, postwar security guarantees)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-04", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-11-09", "statusNote": "Call stands; Zelenskyy Nov 9 4:13pm ET SAID Ukraine's negotiating team is already in the UAE with the first meeting tomorrow (Nov 10), European partners present. Trilateral not yet held; no deal claimed.", "addedIn": "2026-11-04 (v27)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-10", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-04-powermap-v27-V-zelenskyy-witkoff-kushner-call-2026-11-04", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (Ukraine primary): President Zelenskyy held a 90-minute phone call on Nov 4 2026 with US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner (president.gov.ua English readout; Zelenskyy also posted). Topics: team-level Ukraine-US-Russia trilateral in less than a week (Abu Dhabi Nov 10-11 per press), Patriot interceptors, Drone Deal bilateral track, ironclad postwar security guarantees; same day Brussels recovery meeting (US/EU/France/UK/Germany/NATO/World Bank/business). Call content is Zelenskyy's readout (BOTH); Witkoff/Kushner had not publicly commented at report time. No causation claimed beyond the documented contact.", "citation": ["https://www.president.gov.ua/en/news/volodimir-zelenskij-obgovoriv-zi-stivenom-vitkoffom-i-dzhare-107153", "https://x.com/ZelenskyyUa/status/2118067876695564358", "https://kyivindependent.com/security-guarantees-must-be-ironclad-zelensky-speaks-to-trumps-envoys-ahead-of-trilateral-peace-talks/"]}, {"@id": "tie/jeffries-kushner-private-meeting-2026-08", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/hakeem-jeffries", "to": "node/jared-kushner", "name": "private NYC meeting ~Aug 2026", "tieType": "documented meeting (private NYC meeting; housing/immigration/cost of living discussed; Kushner suggested Jeffries meet Susie Wiles)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-08 (NYT Aug 23; meeting in 'recent weeks' before that)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-04 (v27)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-04", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-04-powermap-v27-V-jeffries-kushner-private-meeting-2026-08", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "BOTH: NYT (Haberman/Karni, Aug 23 2026; five unnamed people) reported House Minority Leader Hakeem Jeffries met privately with Jared Kushner in New York in a space offered by a mutual friend; discussed housing, immigration and cost of living; Kushner suggested Jeffries meet WH CoS Susie Wiles. Jeffries later acknowledged (Forbes/Inquirer Aug 25 video) that Kushner asked for the meeting and he took it to discuss affordability, while pledging tough oversight ('no one is going to get a pass'). Meeting occurrence confirmed by Jeffries (DONE); detailed content remains NYT anonymous-source SAID. No deal or appointment claimed. Post-midterms Jeffries is in line for Speaker — role note only, not an edge.", "citation": ["https://www.nytimes.com/2026/08/23/us/politics/jeffries-kushner-private-meeting.html", "https://www.inquirer.com/politics/hakeem-jeffries-jared-kushner-meet-midterms-trump-20260823.html", "https://www.forbes.com/sites/siladityaray/2026/08/25/hakeem-jeffries-addresses-kushner-meeting-says-trump-cartel-wont-get-a-pass/"]}, {"@id": "tie/schimpf-jeffries-battleground-100k-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/brian-schimpf-anduril-ceo", "to": "node/hakeem-jeffries", "name": "$100K Battleground Fund Apr 2026", "tieType": "funding (donation $100,000 to Jeffries Battleground Protection Fund, Apr 9 2026)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-04-09", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-04 (v27)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-04", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-04-powermap-v27-V-schimpf-jeffries-battleground-100k-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (FEC-derived): Brian Schimpf, CEO of Anduril Industries, contributed $100,000 to Jeffries Battleground Protection Fund (C00916429) on April 9 2026 (PaidForPolitics FEC aggregator updated Nov 4 2026 with filings through Nov 2; Sludge Nov 4 FEC review). Structural funding tie only — no claim that the donation sets speaker policy. Anduril already on the map (Founders Fund / Thrive / Luckey / Meridian). Soft-join to Sludge's broader Jeffries donor piece; other named donors (Grimm, Allhassani, Armstrong) left as holes/thin unless separately filed.", "citation": ["https://paidforpolitics.com/c/C00916429", "https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00916429/", "https://readsludge.com/2026/11/04/the-money-behind-hakeem-jeffries/"]}, {"@id": "tie/blanche-clayton-doj-sitf-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/todd-blanche", "to": "node/jay-clayton", "name": "DOJ-SITF partners SI Force (Clayton) 2026-11", "tieType": "institutional partnership (DOJ Super Intelligence Task Force partners with presidential SI Force chaired by Clayton; co-led by Assoc AG Stanley Woodward Jr. + Assoc DAG Stephen Weiss)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-13 (AG memo establishing DOJ-SITF) ; 2026-11-05 (DOJ OPA announce)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-05 (v28)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-05", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-05-powermap-v28-V-blanche-clayton-doj-sitf-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (DOJ primary): DOJ OPA Nov 5 2026 announces Super Intelligence Task Force (DOJ-SITF), led by Associate Attorney General Stanley E. Woodward, Jr. and Associate Deputy Attorney General Stephen Weiss; AG Todd Blanche SAID the SI Task Force will facilitate partnership with SI Force Chair Jay Clayton and continue prosecuting unlawful SI use targeting taxpayers, critical infrastructure, or national security. AG memo (Oct 13 2026, linked from OPA) establishes DOJ-SITF, merges Bondi's Jan 9 2026 AI Task Force into it, and names Woodward + Weiss co-chairs / designees. Jay Clayton already on map as DNI + WH AI/SI Force chair (clayton-ai-czar). Structural institutional partnership edge only — no specific prosecution or company action claimed.", "citation": ["https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/department-justice-launches-super-intelligence-task-force", "https://www.justice.gov/opa/media/1470291/dl?inline=", "https://x.com/TheJusticeDept/status/2118387344944308552"]}, {"@id": "tie/rezaei-putin-mojtaba-message-2026-11-05", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/mohsen-rezaei", "to": "node/vladimir-putin", "name": "Moscow meeting; Mojtaba message 2026-11-05", "tieType": "documented contact (Moscow meeting; Rezaei delivered a message from Mojtaba Khamenei; contents undisclosed)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-05", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-05 (v28)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-05", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-05-powermap-v28-V-rezaei-putin-mojtaba-message-2026-11-05", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (Iranian + international wire primaries): Mohsen Rezaei (SNSC secretary; Leader's representative) met Vladimir Putin in Moscow on Nov 5 2026 and delivered a message from Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei (Mehr News English; Anadolu Agency; Arab News citing AP/Reuters). Message contents undisclosed (SAID layer only as to substance). Distinct from the Oct 2026 Vance→Rezaei letter edge (vance-rezaei-letter-iran-talks-2026). Contact + message-delivery edge only — no causation for later Iran/US actions claimed.", "citation": ["https://en.mehrnews.com/news/249188/Rezaei-delivers-Leader-s-message-to-Putin-in-Moscow", "https://www.aa.com.tr/en/world/iran-s-security-chief-delivers-supreme-leader-s-message-to-putin-during-moscow-visit/4113203", "https://www.arabnews.com/middle-east/irans-security-chief-meets-with-putin-3010034"]}, {"@id": "tie/melania-dmitriev-oleshky-wh-2026-11-05", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/melania-trump", "to": "node/kirill-dmitriev", "name": "WH Oleshky gathering 2026-11-05", "tieType": "documented meeting (White House Oleshky ceasefire gathering; Melania SAID Exclusive Intermediary under written Russia/Ukraine agreements; Dmitriev spoke / presented gift)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-05 (WH gathering) ; 2026-10-23 (ceasefire agreements signed, per Melania)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-05 (v28)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-05", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-05-powermap-v28-V-melania-dmitriev-oleshky-wh-2026-11-05", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (White House primary Nov 5 2026): First Lady Melania Trump gathered Russian and Ukrainian representatives at the White House after the Oleshky ceasefire; she invited Kirill Dmitriev (Putin special envoy) to the podium and acknowledged Yana Lantratova (Russia) and Ukrainian representatives including Dmytro Lubinets; Ukrainian side presented her Ukraine's Order of Princess Olga, First Class. SAID (Melania, same WH release): her role as Exclusive Intermediary was memorialized in written agreements drafted and signed by Russia and Ukraine (she dates the bilingual signing Friday Oct 23 2026); she directed representative Marc Beckman; nearly 800 evacuated. AP/TASS/atrupar: Dmitriev presented a child's drawing from Oleshky. Distinct from melania-trump-putin-humanitarian-channel (letter/children). Meeting occurrence is DONE; Exclusive-Intermediary framing rests on Melania's WH statement (agreement PDFs not checked this pass — hole melania-oleshky-agreements-text).", "citation": ["https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefings-statements/2026/11/first-lady-melania-trump-unites-russia-and-ukraine-at-the-white-house-following-historic-ceasefire/", "https://apnews.com/article/ukraine-melania-trump-oleshky-ceasefire-putin-envoy-3ae35835dbc87ab348478c62c6c25ee3", "https://x.com/atrupar/status/2118376676417487092"]}, {"@id": "tie/grimm-jeffries-victory-44300-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/matthew-grimm-anduril-coo", "to": "node/hakeem-jeffries", "name": "$44.3K Victory Fund Aug 2026", "tieType": "funding (donation $44,300 to Jeffries Victory Fund C00768200, Aug 16 2026)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-08-16", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-05 (v28)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-05", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-05-powermap-v28-V-grimm-jeffries-victory-44300-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (FEC primary via OpenFEC API): Matthew Grimm, Anduril Industries co-founder and COO, contributed $44,300 to Jeffries Victory Fund (C00768200) on August 16 2026 (occupation 'CO-FOUNDER AND COO'). Sludge Nov 4 and PaidForPolitics cycle review match. Structural funding tie parallel to CEO Brian Schimpf's $100K Battleground Fund gift (schimpf-jeffries-battleground-100k-2026) — no claim that the donation sets speaker policy. Anduril already on the map.", "citation": ["https://api.open.fec.gov/v1/schedules/schedule_a/?committee_id=C00768200&contributor_name=Grimm&two_year_transaction_period=2026", "https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00768200/", "https://readsludge.com/2026/11/04/the-money-behind-hakeem-jeffries/"]}, {"@id": "tie/allhassani-jeffries-victory-44300-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/mehdi-allhassani-palantir", "to": "node/hakeem-jeffries", "name": "$44.3K Victory Fund Feb 2025", "tieType": "funding (donation $44,300 to Jeffries Victory Fund C00768200, Feb 28 2025)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-02-28", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-05 (v28)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-05", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-05-powermap-v28-V-allhassani-jeffries-victory-44300-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (FEC primary via OpenFEC API): Mehdi Allhassani, Palantir Technologies manager (Los Altos Hills CA), contributed $44,300 to Jeffries Victory Fund (C00768200) on February 28 2025 (earmarked through ActBlue; image 202610159914565072). Sludge Nov 4 describes him as leading internal operations at Palantir. Structural funding tie into House Democratic leadership from the Palantir cluster (already on map via Thiel/Karp) — no policy causation claimed. Remaining Sludge-named donors (Armstrong $7k, Wall $50k) still need cleaner Jeffries-committee line items.", "citation": ["https://api.open.fec.gov/v1/schedules/schedule_a/?committee_id=C00768200&contributor_name=Allhassani&two_year_transaction_period=2026", "https://docquery.fec.gov/cgi-bin/fecimg/?202610159914565072", "https://readsludge.com/2026/11/04/the-money-behind-hakeem-jeffries/"]}, {"@id": "tie/woodward-weiss-doj-sitf-cochairs-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/stanley-woodward-assoc-ag", "to": "node/stephen-weiss-assoc-dag", "name": "co-chair DOJ-SITF 2026-11", "tieType": "appointment (co-chairs, DOJ Super Intelligence Task Force)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-10-13 (AG memo) ; 2026-11-05 (OPA announce)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-05 (v28)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-05", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-05-powermap-v28-V-woodward-weiss-doj-sitf-cochairs-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE (DOJ primary): AG memo Oct 13 2026 (linked from OPA Nov 5) and DOJ OPA Nov 5 2026 announce that Associate Attorney General Stanley E. Woodward, Jr. and Associate Deputy Attorney General Stephen Weiss co-chair / lead the Department of Justice Super Intelligence Task Force (DOJ-SITF). Companion to blanche-clayton-doj-sitf-2026 (institutional partnership with SI Force Chair Jay Clayton).", "citation": ["https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/department-justice-launches-super-intelligence-task-force", "https://www.justice.gov/opa/media/1470291/dl?inline="]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-miller-chief-of-staff-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/stephen-miller", "name": "WH CoS from Nov 9 2026", "tieType": "appointment (White House Chief of Staff; announced Nov 6 2026, starts Monday Nov 9 2026; succeeds Susie Wiles)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-06 (announce) ; 2026-11-09 (start)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-11-09", "statusNote": "Occupancy DONE: Miller began as WH Chief of Staff Mon Nov 9 2026 (WaPo 'Stephen Miller starts job as chief of staff'; Guardian 'took up his new role'; The Hill). Wiles resigned Nov 5 (WH officials via Zaobao/AFP; CBS) and moves to the Trump Political Operation (title unspecified).", "addedIn": "2026-11-06 (v29)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-06-powermap-v29-V-trump-miller-chief-of-staff-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "BOTH (WH primary): White House release Nov 6 2026 names Stephen Miller 33rd White House Chief of Staff, succeeding Susie Wiles. Trump (Truth Social / @WhiteHouse Fri Nov 6 ~2:04pm ET) SAID Miller (current Deputy Chief of Staff) becomes Chief of Staff starting Monday November 9 2026, with Wiles moving to the Trump Political Operation. Announcement DONE Nov 6; CoS occupancy starts Nov 9 (not yet held as of Nov 6 night). NBC/AP/WaPo match. Miller also held homeland security adviser title; remains Deputy CoS until the Nov 9 handoff.", "citation": ["https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/11/president-trump-names-stephen-miller-as-33rd-white-house-chief-of-staff/", "https://x.com/WhiteHouse/status/2118781463382331432", "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/trump-stephen-miller-susie-wiles-white-house-chief-of-staff-rcna607892"]}, {"@id": "tie/armstrong-jeffries-congress-7000-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/brian-armstrong-coinbase-ceo", "to": "node/hakeem-jeffries", "name": "$7K Jeffries for Congress Apr 2026", "tieType": "funding (donation $7,000 total = two $3,500 receipts to Jeffries for Congress C00503052, Apr 28 2026)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-04-28", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-06 (v29)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-06", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-06-powermap-v29-V-armstrong-jeffries-congress-7000-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 4, "description": "DONE (FEC primary via OpenFEC + docquery images): Brian Armstrong (employer COINBASE) contributed two $3,500 receipts totaling $7,000 to Jeffries for Congress (C00503052) on April 28 2026 (image_numbers 202606119870633024 and 202606119870633025). Matches Sludge Nov 4 '$7,000 to Jeffries' campaign' line. Structural funding only — no policy causation. Closes the Armstrong half of hole-2026-11-05-powermap-v28-jeffries-armstrong-wall-fec.", "citation": ["https://api.open.fec.gov/v1/schedules/schedule_a/?committee_id=C00503052&contributor_name=Armstrong&two_year_transaction_period=2026", "https://docquery.fec.gov/cgi-bin/fecimg/?202606119870633024", "https://docquery.fec.gov/cgi-bin/fecimg/?202606119870633025", "https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00503052/", "https://readsludge.com/2026/11/04/the-money-behind-hakeem-jeffries/"]}, {"@id": "tie/wall-jeffries-victory-50000-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/adrian-wall-digital-sovereignty", "to": "node/hakeem-jeffries", "name": "$50K Victory Fund May 2026", "tieType": "funding (donation $50,000 to Jeffries Victory Fund C00768200, May 28 2026)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-05-28", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-06 (v29)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-06", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-06-powermap-v29-V-wall-jeffries-victory-50000-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 4, "description": "DONE (FEC primary via OpenFEC + docquery image): Adrian Wall (employer DIGITAL SOVEREIGNTY ALLIANCE; occupation MANAGING DIRECTOR) contributed $50,000 to Jeffries Victory Fund (C00768200) on May 28 2026 (image_number 202607159875110608; sub_id 4072820261539084186). Matches Sludge Nov 4 Adrian Wall / Digital Sovereignty $50K line. Structural funding only — no policy causation. Closes the Wall half of hole-2026-11-05-powermap-v28-jeffries-armstrong-wall-fec.", "citation": ["https://api.open.fec.gov/v1/schedules/schedule_a/?committee_id=C00768200&contributor_name=Wall&two_year_transaction_period=2026", "https://docquery.fec.gov/cgi-bin/fecimg/?202607159875110608", "https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00768200/", "https://readsludge.com/2026/11/04/the-money-behind-hakeem-jeffries/"]}, {"@id": "tie/massie-hegseth-impeachment-articles-2026-11-09", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/thomas-massie", "to": "node/pete-hegseth", "name": "8 impeachment articles Nov 9 2026", "tieType": "oversight (privileged impeachment resolution, 8 articles, filed on House floor Nov 9 2026)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-09", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "ended", "statusDate": "2026-11-10", "statusNote": "H.Res. 1655 referred to Judiciary Nov 10 2026 on Issa's motion, 211-204 (Roll Call 317; Massie sole R nay; no vote on the articles). Resolution sits in committee; dies Jan 3 2027 unless acted on. Filing edge kept as DONE history.", "addedIn": "2026-11-09 (v30)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-10", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-09-powermap-v30-V-massie-hegseth-impeachment-articles-2026-11-09", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 4, "description": "DONE (House floor + Massie office primary): Rep. Thomas Massie (R-KY, lost May 19 2026 primary; serves to Jan 3 2027) read and filed as privileged a resolution impeaching Secretary of Defense/War Pete Hegseth on eight articles (three War Powers Resolution counts on the Iran war; civilian-protection laws; extrajudicial deaths in boat strikes (article wording: extrajudicial); retaliation against Sen. Mark Kelly; Maduro capture; Yemen). Privileged status forces Speaker Johnson to schedule action within two legislative days (vote or motion to table/refer by ~Wed Nov 11). Same eight articles as the September filing that lapsed when the House recessed. Trump SAID (Truth Social card, Nov 9 evening) 'Congress, stand up for Pete'; Hegseth SAID 'we will never back down'. Filing DONE; floor outcome open. Oversight act, not a finding of wrongdoing.", "citation": ["https://massie.house.gov/news/documentsingle.aspx?DocumentID=395863", "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/trump-administration/thomas-massie-pete-hegseth-impeachment-house-defense-rcna597989", "https://rollcall.com/2026/11/09/massie-moves-to-force-hegseth-impeachment-vote/", "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/09/nx-s1-6034483/thomas-massie-impeachment-pete-hegseth"]}, {"@id": "tie/bruesewitz-loomer-paid-posts-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/alex-bruesewitz-x-strategies", "to": "node/laura-loomer", "name": "paid her in 2025 (purpose disputed)", "tieType": "funding (payments to Loomer / King Breaker Media; purpose disputed — paid posts vs research doc)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2025 (payments since May 2025; WaPo Nov 7 2026)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-09 (v30)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-09-powermap-v30-V-bruesewitz-loomer-paid-posts-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "BOTH (WaPo Nov 7 2026, Harwell/Nover): Alex Bruesewitz, Trump 2024 campaign adviser (X Strategies), told the Washington Post on record he paid Laura Loomer for political posts throughout 2025; three others (anonymous) described similar arrangements, two saying they paid her directly. WaPo reviewed bank-transaction emails and a wire statement showing four payments totalling more than $60,000 to Loomer and King Breaker Media (Florida company in her name) since May 2025; documents do not state purpose. Loomer SAID she was paid for a one-page research document that she then distributed and denies charging $5,000 per tweet. Payment DONE (both sides agree money moved from Bruesewitz); 'paid posts' purpose is SAID vs SAID. Influence-for-hire tie inside Trump-world; no government act claimed.", "citation": ["https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2026/11/07/trump-ally-laura-loomer-paid-thousands-political-tweets-people-familiar-say/", "https://www.jpost.com/american-politics/article-914158", "https://www.mediaite.com/media/news/sources-tell-washpo-trump-ally-laura-loomer-charges-up-to-5000-per-paid-post/"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-althani-wh-iran-mediation-2026-11-09", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/mohammed-bin-abdulrahman-al-thani", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "Oval Office Iran talks Nov 9 2026", "tieType": "documented meeting (Oval Office ~45 min, Iran mediation; Vance met him first)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-09", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-09 (v30)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-09-powermap-v30-V-trump-althani-wh-iran-mediation-2026-11-09", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 4, "description": "BOTH: Qatar PM/FM Sheikh Mohammed bin Abdulrahman Al Thani met President Trump in the Oval Office ~noon Mon Nov 9 2026 for ~45 minutes, closed press, focused on US-Iran negotiations (Axios/Ravid source; Times of Israel WH official: just under an hour); he met VP JD Vance separately first (Vance speaks with him almost daily per Axios). Al Thani SAID on X: 'We discussed the situation in the region and ways to progress the US-Iran talks... Grateful for the positive discussions on reaching a deal.' Trump SAID afterward in the briefing room the war is 'militarily effectively over', blockade + Task Force Iron Gate stay, 'locked and loaded'. Meeting DONE; deal terms (Al Arabiya $6-9B / 3.67%) remain anonymous SAID; no signed agreement. Sequence only: meeting then Trump remarks.", "citation": ["https://apnews.com/article/iran-us-war-trump-qatar-c38770b168faf5e094e96c1e1e212cff", "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/9/trump-calls-iran-war-effectively-over-after-talks-with-qatar-pm", "https://www.iranintl.com/en/202611090440", "https://www.channelnewsasia.com/world/trump-says-qatar-saudi-prefer-peace-iran-conflict-6536646"]}, {"@id": "tie/clayton-ratcliffe-gang-of-eight-iran-2026-11-09", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jay-clayton", "to": "node/gang-of-eight-congress", "name": "classified Iran briefing Nov 9 2026", "tieType": "intelligence briefing (classified, Iran-focused; with CIA Director John Ratcliffe)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-09", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-09 (v30)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-09-powermap-v30-I-clayton-ratcliffe-gang-of-eight-iran-2026-11-09", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 4, "description": "BOTH / I: A classified briefing of the congressional Gang of Eight took place Mon Nov 9 2026; House Democratic leader Hakeem Jeffries SAID (Punchbowl relay; Iran International 20:53 GMT; Reuters/Investing) it focused primarily on Iran and also touched the Nvidia/Jensen Huang spy allegations. CNBC (Nov 9) cites an anonymous administration official that CIA Director John Ratcliffe and DNI Jay Clayton were scheduled to lead a classified briefing on Iran threats with top congressional leaders; post-event reports naming Ratcliffe + Clayton as briefers are aggregator relays (OSINT613, Tree News) — hence I. Previous Gang of Eight briefing Feb 24 2026 preceded Feb 28 strikes (sequence only, not a forecast). Contents undisclosed.", "citation": ["https://www.iranintl.com/en/202611098029", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/09/nvidia-jensen-huang-china-spy-trump-lobbying.html", "https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/house-democratic-leader-says-lawmakers-need-answers-on-nvidia-wants-china-chip-restrictions-5013456", "https://www.osint613.com/post/gang-of-eight-briefed-on-iran-plans-27463"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-macneil-ftc-withdrawal-2026-11-09", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/david-macneil-weathertech", "name": "FTC nomination withdrawn Nov 9 2026", "tieType": "appointment (nomination withdrawn; FTC Commissioner seat re-nominated to Christopher Mufarrige)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-01-13 (nominated) ; 2026-11-09 (withdrawn)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "ended", "statusDate": "2026-11-09", "statusNote": "Nomination withdrawn Nov 9 2026 (WH list); seat re-nominated to Christopher Mufarrige.", "addedIn": "2026-11-09 (v30)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-10", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-09-powermap-v30-V-trump-macneil-ftc-withdrawal-2026-11-09", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (WH primary): The White House 'Nominations and Withdrawals Sent to the Senate' Nov 9 2026 withdraws David MacNeil of Florida (WeatherTech founder/CEO; nominated Jan 13 2026 per Reuters) as Federal Trade Commissioner, and the same list nominates Christopher Mufarrige of Texas to an FTC seat (seven-year term from Sep 26 2026, vice Alvaro Bedoya). MLex reported the pivot from MacNeil to Mufarrige. Same Nov 9 list also nominates Gary Lawkowski as ODNI General Counsel, Michael LoSapio as CISA Director and Jeffrey Colyer as Ambassador to the UAE. No reason for the withdrawal stated in the primary.", "citation": ["https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2026/11/nominations-and-withdrawals-sent-to-the-senate-ba2b/", "https://www.reuters.com/world/weathertech-founder-tapped-federal-trade-commission-2026-01-13/", "https://www.mlex.com/mlex/articles/2546523/white-house-to-withdraw-macneil-s-us-ftc-nomination-pivot-to-mufarrige"]}, {"@id": "tie/dhillon-doj-civil-rights-resigns-2026-11-05", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/harmeet-dhillon", "to": "node/todd-blanche", "name": "resigned AAG Civil Rights Nov 5 2026", "tieType": "appointment (ended — resigned as Assistant AG, Civil Rights Division, Nov 5 2026)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-04 (confirmed) ; 2026-11-05 (resigned)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "ended", "statusDate": "2026-11-05", "statusNote": "Resigned Nov 5 2026 (WaPo).", "addedIn": "2026-11-09 (v30)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-05", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-09-powermap-v30-V-dhillon-doj-civil-rights-resigns-2026-11-05", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE: Harmeet Dhillon resigned as head of the DOJ Civil Rights Division Thu Nov 5 2026 (WaPo Stein/Roebuck), the first DOJ shake-up after the Democratic midterm wave. Dhillon told the Guardian she submitted her letter Oct 13 and WH CoS Susie Wiles asked her to stay until at least early November; CBS reported Trump sought to dismiss her after an October 60 Minutes appearance (SAID, anonymous). Pre-midterm she had sought voter rolls from ~30 states. Role ended; reason contested (her account vs CBS sources).", "citation": ["https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2026/11/05/harmeet-dhillon-resigns-head-justice-depts-civil-rights-division/", "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/06/doj-officials-resign", "https://www.politico.com/news/2026/11/06/justice-department-officials-resign-01154909"]}, {"@id": "tie/eisenberg-doj-nsd-resigns-2026-11-06", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/john-eisenberg", "to": "node/todd-blanche", "name": "resigned AAG NSD Nov 6 2026", "tieType": "appointment (ended — resigned as Assistant AG, National Security Division, Nov 6 2026)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2025 ; 2026-11-06 (resigned)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "ended", "statusDate": "2026-11-06", "statusNote": "Resigned Nov 6 2026 (CBS, Guardian).", "addedIn": "2026-11-09 (v30)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-06", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-09-powermap-v30-V-eisenberg-doj-nsd-resigns-2026-11-06", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE: John Eisenberg, head of DOJ's National Security Division (terrorism/espionage cases; ex-NSC top lawyer in Trump's first term), resigned Nov 6 2026 (CBS 'abruptly resigns'; Guardian). AG Todd Blanche SAID on X he 'served with distinction'. Role ended; no reason stated.", "citation": ["https://www.cbsnews.com/news/john-eisenberg-justice-department-resigns/", "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/06/doj-officials-resign"]}, {"@id": "tie/quinones-sdfl-grand-conspiracy-resigns-2026-11-06", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jason-reding-qui-ones", "to": "node/todd-blanche", "name": "left SDFL US Attorney Nov 6 2026", "tieType": "appointment (ended — resigned as US Attorney SD Fla., overseer of 'grand conspiracy' probe, Nov 6 2026)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2025 ; 2026-11-06 (resigned)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "ended", "statusDate": "2026-11-06", "statusNote": "Announced departure Nov 6 2026 (AP, Guardian); grand-conspiracy probe had filed no charges.", "addedIn": "2026-11-09 (v30)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-06", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-09-powermap-v30-V-quinones-sdfl-grand-conspiracy-resigns-2026-11-06", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE: Jason Reding Quiñones, US Attorney for the Southern District of Florida, announced Nov 6 2026 he is leaving DOJ (AP; Guardian). He oversaw the 'grand conspiracy' inquiry into whether former officials (targets incl. ex-CIA director John Brennan) violated Trump's rights in post-2020 investigations; the Guardian (Nov 6, read Nov 9) reports charges had not yet been filed. AG Blanche SAID thanks, citing the Raúl Castro indictment. Conservative commentator Julie Kelly SAID the case is 'essentially dead' (opinion). Role ended; DOJ did not state the probe's status in the Blanche statement quoted by the Guardian.", "citation": ["https://apnews.com/article/justice-department-resignations-grand-conspiracy-florida-jason-quinones-9a10b4ffcb620edb3c2298cec066062d", "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/06/doj-officials-resign"]}, {"@id": "tie/affinity-arxis-13f-stake-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jared-kushner", "to": "node/arxis-inc-defense-supplier", "name": "Affinity 13F/A: $31.8M Arxis stake (Jun 30 2026)", "tieType": "ownership (Affinity Partners 13F-HR/A: 689,411 Class A shares, $31.8M at Jun 30 2026)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-06-30 (position) ; 2026-11-05 (amended 13F filed)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-10 (v31)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-10", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-10-powermap-v31-V-affinity-arxis-13f-stake-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (SEC EDGAR): Affinity Partners GP LP (CIK 0002059583; Jared Kushner's investment firm) filed a Form 13F-HR/A (Amendment No. 1, NEW HOLDINGS) on Nov 5 2026 for the quarter ended Jun 30 2026, adding 689,411 Class A shares of Arxis Inc (Nasdaq: ARXS) valued at $31,809,424, reported with Affinity Partners Fund I Co-Invest GP LP; the original Aug 14 13F-HR listed only QXO. Per the Kushner Report's reading of Arxis's April 2026 prospectus, Defense and Space is about 47% of revenue (F-35, DDG-51, Virginia-class, SPY-6 components); Arcline-sponsored IPO at $28. Kushner is Trump's informal peace envoy. The filing shows the position only at Jun 30: when it was bought and whether it is still held are not shown. No causal link to any defense decision is claimed.", "citation": ["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2059583/000090514826004664/0000905148-26-004664-index.htm", "https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0002059583&type=13F", "https://the.kushner.report/event/2026-11-05-affinity-disclosed-a-stake-in-defense-supplier-arxis/"]}, {"@id": "tie/issa-refers-hegseth-impeachment-judiciary-2026-11-10", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/darrell-issa", "to": "node/pete-hegseth", "name": "moved to refer Hegseth impeachment; agreed 211-204 (Nov 10 2026)", "tieType": "congressional action (motion to refer H.Res. 1655 impeachment articles to Judiciary, agreed 211-204, Roll Call 317)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-10", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-11-10", "statusNote": "Referral agreed; resolution in Judiciary (Chair Jordan voted yea).", "addedIn": "2026-11-10 (v31)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-10", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-10-powermap-v31-V-issa-refers-hegseth-impeachment-judiciary-2026-11-10", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (House Clerk): Tue Nov 10 2026 Rep. Darrell Issa (R-CA) moved to refer H.Res. 1655 (Massie's articles impeaching Secretary Pete Hegseth) to the Judiciary Committee; agreed 211-204 (Roll Call 317, 6:02 PM ET). Republicans 210-1 (Massie the sole R nay), Democrats 0-203 (11 not voting), Independent Kiley yea; Judiciary Chair Jim Jordan voted yea. No vote on the articles themselves. Press called it 'torpedoed'/'blocked' (SAID framing). Referral leaves the resolution in committee; unfinished measures die Jan 3 2027.", "citation": ["https://clerk.house.gov/Votes/2026317", "https://clerk.house.gov/FloorSummary/ViewFloorActions?date=2026-11-10", "https://www.foxnews.com/politics/house-gop-leaders-block-massie-hegseth-impeachment-push", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/10/pete-hegseth-impeachment-massie-iran.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/jordan-house-gop-minority-leader-120th-2026-11-10", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jim-jordan", "to": "node/mike-johnson", "name": "elected GOP Minority Leader for 120th Congress (Nov 10 2026)", "tieType": "party leadership succession (House Republicans elected Jordan Minority Leader for the 120th Congress; Speaker Johnson SAID congratulations)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-10", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-10 (v31)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-10", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-10-powermap-v31-V-jordan-house-gop-minority-leader-120th-2026-11-10", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE: House Republicans elected Rep. Jim Jordan (R-OH; current Judiciary chair) Minority Leader, Tom Emmer Minority Whip and Lisa McClain Conference Chair for the 120th Congress (Speaker Mike Johnson's office release, Nov 10 2026). SAID: Johnson congratulated them and said he looks forward to 'working alongside this leadership team to earn back our majority'. Democrats take the House majority in January after the Nov 2026 midterms. Johnson's own post-January role not stated in the release (hole). Same day Jordan voted yea on referring the Hegseth impeachment to his committee (sequence only).", "citation": ["https://mikejohnson.house.gov/news/documentsingle.aspx?DocumentID=2953"]}, {"@id": "tie/abu-dhabi-trilateral-witkoff-kushner-2026-11-10", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/steve-witkoff-jared-kushner", "to": "node/abdullah-bin-zayed-uae-fm", "name": "Abu Dhabi trilateral, UAE-hosted (Nov 10-11 2026)", "tieType": "meeting (US-Russia-Ukraine trilateral talks, Abu Dhabi, Nov 10-11 2026; UAE host)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-10 ; 2026-11-11", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-11-12", "statusNote": "Held Nov 10-11; Kushner SAID (Nov 12) next round expanded with Europeans and the largest prisoner exchange is being prepared; no signed text, no date.", "addedIn": "2026-11-10 (v31)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-12", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-10-powermap-v31-V-abu-dhabi-trilateral-witkoff-kushner-2026-11-10", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE: the first day of Abu Dhabi meetings was held Nov 10 2026, first Ukraine with European and US partners, then a trilateral with the US and Russian delegations (Zelenskyy, official X, thanking the US for organizing and the UAE for the platform). TASS (Nov 11 Moscow dateline) lists Witkoff, Kushner, SACEUR Alexus Grynkewich and UAE FM Abdullah bin Zayed at the table at the start; Russian delegation led by presidential aide Vladimir Medinsky. SAID: Zelenskyy called it constructive (prisoners, security guarantees, de-escalation) and later said Russia claimed half of Donbas, which he disputes; Ryabkov SAID too early to assess. No agreement DONE.", "citation": ["https://x.com/ZelenskyyUa/status/2120172358426042607", "https://tass.com/politics/2215785", "https://x.com/ZelenskyyUa/status/2120276452876967979"]}, {"@id": "tie/dmitriev-thanks-kushner-witkoff-2026-11-10", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/kirill-dmitriev", "to": "node/steve-witkoff-jared-kushner", "name": "SAID thanks 'Jared and Steve' (Nov 10 2026)", "tieType": "public statement (Dmitriev X post thanking 'Jared and Steve' during Abu Dhabi talks)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-10", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-10 (v31)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-10", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-10-powermap-v31-V-dmitriev-thanks-kushner-witkoff-2026-11-10", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "SAID: RDIF CEO and Putin special representative Kirill Dmitriev posted on X, quoted by TASS: 'Thank you, Jared and Steve, for all of your hard work to advance President Trump's peace plan. Peacemakers will prevail. Warmongers and their ubiquitous bots will lose.' Posted while the Nov 10-11 Abu Dhabi trilateral was under way. Office SAID only; shows the open public channel, not any agreed term or payment.", "citation": ["https://tass.com/politics/2215785"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-macneil-manufacturing-envoy-2026-11-09", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/david-macneil-weathertech", "name": "named special envoy for manufacturing (Nov 9 2026)", "tieType": "appointment (named special envoy for manufacturing the same day his FTC nomination was withdrawn)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-09", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-10 (v31)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-10", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-10-powermap-v31-V-trump-macneil-manufacturing-envoy-2026-11-09", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (UPI, Nov 10): Trump named WeatherTech founder/CEO and Republican donor David MacNeil special envoy for manufacturing on Mon Nov 9 2026, the same day the White House withdrew his FTC nomination; his third pick for a federal role this term (ambassador-at-large nomination returned Jan 3 2026 unconfirmed; FTC nomination withdrawn). Duties and whether the envoy post needs Senate confirmation were not stated. Sequence: withdrawal then envoy naming, same day; no reason stated.", "citation": ["https://www.upi.com/Top_News/US/2026/11/10/Trump-names-David-McNeil-manufacturing-envoy/4461794299374/", "https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2026/11/nominations-and-withdrawals-sent-to-the-senate-b6a4/"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-weirsky-nctc-nomination-2026-11-10", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/joseph-weirsky", "name": "nominated NCTC Director vice Joe Kent (Nov 10 2026)", "tieType": "appointment (nominated Director, National Counterterrorism Center, vice Joseph Kent, resigned)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-10", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-10", "statusNote": "Nominated; Senate action pending.", "addedIn": "2026-11-10 (v31)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-11", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-10-powermap-v31-V-trump-weirsky-nctc-nomination-2026-11-10", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE (White House nominations list Nov 10 2026): Joseph Weirsky of Virginia nominated Director of the National Counterterrorism Center (ODNI), vice Joseph Kent, resigned. Same list: Daniel Zimmerman to a new Assistant Secretary of Defense post; Peter Feldman as CPSC chair; Matthew Millhollin ambassador to Oman; James Cody Hiland to the 8th Circuit (Lee Rudofsky withdrawn). Nomination only; Senate action pending.", "citation": ["https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2026/11/nominations-and-withdrawals-sent-to-the-senate-b6a4/"]}, {"@id": "tie/nvidia-teter-bis-megaspeed-contact-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/nvidia", "to": "node/jeff-kessler-commerce-under-secretary-bis", "name": "GC Teter emailed BIS agents citing Kessler's permission (Aug 2025; NYT, people familiar)", "tieType": "contact (Nvidia general counsel Tim Teter emailed BIS agents on the Megaspeed chip-diversion case, writing that Under Secretary Kessler had given permission to reach out; DOJ then asked Commerce to pause and Commerce complied)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-08", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-11 (v32)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-11", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-11-powermap-v32-I-nvidia-teter-bis-megaspeed-contact-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "other", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID (NYT, Ana Swanson and Devlin Barrett, Nov 9-10 2026, via The Next Web; Bloomberg via Yahoo Finance): in August 2025, during a BIS probe of Singapore-based Nvidia customer Megaspeed over suspected chip smuggling to China, Nvidia general counsel Tim Teter emailed the agents and wrote that Under Secretary Jeff Kessler had given Nvidia permission to reach out. Agents declined a meeting and forwarded the emails to Kessler, who (per a Commerce official) told them to handle the case by the book. The Justice Department then asked Commerce to pause; Commerce complied; DOJ runs a criminal inquiry (people familiar). Commerce SAID it handled the case by the book; Nvidia (Rizzo) SAID it consults officials to answer questions; Megaspeed denies smuggling. Kessler and DOJ did not comment. Contact and pause are reported by people familiar; no document is public. The pause came at DOJ's request, not shown to be caused by the email (sequence only).", "citation": ["https://thenextweb.com/news/megaspeed-probe-commerce-nvidia-lawyer-justice-department-nyt", "https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/ai/articles/nvidia-intervened-us-probe-megaspeed-212826572.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/bessent-lutnick-megaspeed-situation-room-2026-11-05", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/scott-bessent", "to": "node/howard-lutnick", "name": "pressed Lutnick on Megaspeed not entity-listed (Axios, sources; Commerce: 'This is false')", "tieType": "confrontation (Treasury Secretary pressed Commerce Secretary in a Situation Room meeting on why Megaspeed is not on the Entity List; Commerce denies it happened)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-05", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-11 (v32)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-11", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-11-powermap-v32-I-bessent-lutnick-megaspeed-situation-room-2026-11-05", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "SAID vs SAID (Axios scoop, Maria Curi and Marc Caputo, Nov 11 2026, sources familiar): at a White House Situation Room meeting on the Thursday after the midterms (Nov 5 2026) Bessent asked Lutnick why Nvidia customer Megaspeed was not on the Commerce Entity List; Lutnick replied he would 'look into it'. Sources say Under Secretary Kessler deferred ('That's a decision for the secretary') and Lutnick received a Rubio-drafted memo on Megaspeed in May. Commerce spokesperson Kristen Eichamer: 'This is false. Secretary Bessent and Secretary Lutnick had no such conversation.' DONE on record only: Commerce has added no company to the Entity List in more than a year (Axios review of the Federal Register). Meeting content rests on anonymous sources and is denied.", "citation": ["https://www.axios.com/2026/11/11/bessent-lutnick-megaspeed-nvidia-china-chips"]}, {"@id": "tie/nvidia-trump-ballroom-25m-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/nvidia", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "$25M ballroom commitment (Oct 2025; WaPo donor documents)", "tieType": "funding (committed $25M to the White House ballroom fund via the Trust for the National Mall, Oct 2025; asked for anonymity)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-10", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-11 (v32)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-11", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-11-powermap-v32-V-nvidia-trump-ballroom-25m-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (Washington Post, Oct 15 2026, internal ballroom fundraising spreadsheet and records; NPR interview with WaPo reporter Sarah Blaskey Oct 16; NY Post Oct 15): Nvidia committed $25M (the top tier, with Apple, the Adelsons and Charles Ergen) to Trump's White House ballroom, routed through the nonprofit Trust for the National Mall into a White House account the president controls; documents show Nvidia asked that the gift stay anonymous; Huang said in Oct 2025 it was giving 'in a small way' without an amount. Sequence only: the commitment came about three months after Nvidia's July 2025 China chip-sale arrangement with the administration and two months after its GC's Aug 2025 Megaspeed contact; WaPo says it has no evidence of a quid pro quo. Schumer SAID (Nov 10 Senate floor) Trump 'accepted a twenty-five-million-dollar donation'.", "citation": ["https://www.washingtonpost.com/investigations/2026/10/15/secret-documents-reveal-donors-behind-330-million-trumps-ballroom/", "https://www.npr.org/2026/10/16/nx-s1-6003821/investigation-details-who-donated-to-the-white-house-ballroom-project", "https://nypost.com/2026/10/15/business/apple-nvidia-each-gave-25m-to-white-house-ballroom-project-among-top-donors-report/"]}, {"@id": "tie/eric-trump-foundation-future-industries-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/eric-trump", "to": "node/foundation-future-industries", "name": "equity stake; chief strategic adviser since Mar 2026", "tieType": "equity + adviser (early investor holding an equity stake; named chief strategic adviser Mar 2026)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-03 ; FT Nov 11 2026", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-11 (v32)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-11", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-11-powermap-v32-V-eric-trump-foundation-future-industries-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (FT Nov 11 2026, read via The Telegraph and Valor Economico's FT republication; Wired/CNBC earlier): Eric Trump is an early investor in humanoid-robot maker Foundation Future Industries (founded 2024), holds an equity stake, and was named its chief strategic adviser in March 2026. Co-founder/president Mike LeBlanc SAID Foundation and a company it acquired received more than $70M from the US military in contracts and test/development funds, including a major Pentagon purchase contract awarded after Trump joined (Valor/FT). SAID (Trump spokesman): no involvement in management, operations, strategy or any government contract; never introduced Foundation to any agency. LeBlanc SAID Trump's role played no part in securing contracts. Sequence only between his joining and the Pentagon award; no causation shown.", "citation": ["https://www.telegraph.co.uk/us/news/2026/11/11/trump-humanoid-robots-hamas-tunnels/", "https://valor.globo.com/empresas/tecnologia/noticia/2026/11/11/ft-startup-de-robos-apoiada-por-eric-trump-negocia-com-israel.ghtml", "https://www.ft.com/content/8117b912-ebc7-46b2-90cd-a1ec32e12c5a"]}, {"@id": "tie/foundation-idf-phantom-talks-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/foundation-future-industries", "to": "node/state-of-israel", "name": "SAID talks with IDF on up to 1,000 Phantom robots (no contract)", "tieType": "contract talks (LeBlanc SAID direct talks with the IDF chief of staff to supply up to 1,000 Phantom MK1 robots for Gaza tunnels; MoD declined comment)", "category": "contract", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-09 ; FT Nov 11 2026", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-11", "statusNote": "Talks SAID by one party; no contract or order.", "addedIn": "2026-11-11 (v32)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-11", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-11-powermap-v32-I-foundation-idf-phantom-talks-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID (FT Nov 11 2026 via The Telegraph and Valor): Foundation co-founder Mike LeBlanc said 'We're in direct talks with the chief of staff of the Israel Defense Forces' about up to 1,000 Phantom MK1 robots (~$150K each) to patrol Hamas tunnels and possibly fight; he met senior IDF officials in September and toured tunnels with a robot. The IDF referred questions to the Defense Ministry, which declined comment. One interested party on record; no contract, order or deployment shown.", "citation": ["https://www.telegraph.co.uk/us/news/2026/11/11/trump-humanoid-robots-hamas-tunnels/", "https://valor.globo.com/empresas/tecnologia/noticia/2026/11/11/ft-startup-de-robos-apoiada-por-eric-trump-negocia-com-israel.ghtml"]}, {"@id": "tie/putin-witkoff-kushner-moscow-2026-11-12", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/vladimir-putin", "to": "node/steve-witkoff-jared-kushner", "name": "Moscow meeting scheduled Nov 12 morning (Ushakov SAID)", "tieType": "meeting (scheduled: Putin to receive the envoys in Moscow the morning of Nov 12 2026 after the Abu Dhabi trilateral)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-12 (scheduled; announced Nov 11)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-11-12", "statusNote": "HELD Nov 12 in the Kremlin (Russian MFA video; TASS). Putin remarks and Ushakov readout are SAID; no US-side readout beyond Kushner's Nov 12 statement.", "addedIn": "2026-11-11 (v32)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-12", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-11-powermap-v32-V-putin-witkoff-kushner-moscow-2026-11-12", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "SAID (TASS 2216487, Nov 11 2026, Kremlin aide Yuri Ushakov on record): Putin will meet US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner on the morning of Nov 12; protocol 'as usual'. Kushner had SAID they would travel to Moscow Nov 12 to discuss issues raised at the Abu Dhabi trilateral, then go to Dublin to meet Zelenskyy. Scheduled, not shown held at filing.", "citation": ["https://tass.com/politics/2216487"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-empowers-vance-iran-talks-2026-11-11", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/jd-vance", "name": "open to Vance leading Iran talks (WSJ, officials; Rezaei denies talks)", "tieType": "delegation (WSJ, officials: Trump signaled he is open to Vance leading renewed Iran negotiations and gave him authority; direct Vance-Rezaei meeting under discussion, no date)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-11", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-11", "statusNote": "No meeting date; Rezaei denies talks.", "addedIn": "2026-11-11 (v32)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-11", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-11-powermap-v32-I-trump-empowers-vance-iran-talks-2026-11-11", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID (WSJ Nov 11 2026 via Anadolu, citing US and Middle Eastern officials): Trump signaled to aides and foreign counterparts that he is open to Vance leading renewed negotiations with Tehran and gave him authority to pursue them; a face-to-face Vance meeting with SNSC secretary Mohsen Rezaei is at an early stage with no date; Vance wrote Rezaei in October requesting a meeting. A White House official rejected claims that Trump had second thoughts about the June framework. SAID vs SAID: Rezaei told Al Mayadeen (Nov 10) claims of continuing negotiations or a Qatar meeting are 'a pure lie'. No talks DONE.", "citation": ["https://www.aa.com.tr/en/us-israel-iran-war/us-jd-vance-weighs-direct-talks-with-iranian-security-official-to-end-war-report/4121438", "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/11/iran-denies-talks-with-us-says-hormuz-will-stay-shut-until-demands-are-met"]}, {"@id": "tie/huang-resigns-nvidia-2026-11-11", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jensen-huang", "to": "node/nvidia", "name": "resigned CEO + director Nov 11 (8-K: no reason)", "tieType": "employment ended (resigned as President, CEO and director; board accepted Nov 11 2026, effective immediately; no reason stated)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-11 (8-K accepted Nov 12 8:52 AM EST)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "changed", "statusDate": "2026-11-23", "statusNote": "Ended by reinstatement: 8-K Item 5.02 (accession 0001045810-26-000090, opened) says the board reinstated Huang as President, CEO and director on Nov 22, effective immediately. The Nov 11 resignation stays a historical fact; the office is restored.", "addedIn": "2026-11-12 (v33)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-23", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-12-powermap-v33-V-huang-resigns-nvidia-2026-11-11", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE (NVIDIA 8-K Item 5.02, accession 0001045810-26-000082, fetched): on Nov 11 2026 the Board accepted Jen-Hsun Huang's resignation as President, CEO and Board member, effective immediately. Neither the 8-K nor EX-99.1 states a reason (hole). Any link to Megaspeed/BIS, the ballroom commitment or China chip matters is not shown and is not inferred.", "citation": ["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1045810/000104581026000082/nvda-20261111.htm", "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1045810/000104581026000082/0001045810-26-000082-index.htm"]}, {"@id": "tie/nvidia-kress-interim-ceo-jones-chair-2026-11-11", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/nvidia", "to": "node/colette-kress", "name": "interim CEO (keeps CFO); Jones Chair", "tieType": "appointment (interim CEO, keeps CFO role; Harvey C. Jones named board Chair; CEO search internal and external)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-11", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-12 (v33)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-12", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-12-powermap-v33-V-nvidia-kress-interim-ceo-jones-chair-2026-11-11", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (NVIDIA 8-K, fetched): the Board appointed EVP and CFO Colette M. Kress (59; CFO since 2013) interim CEO while it searches for a new CEO; she keeps the CFO role and signed the 8-K as Interim CEO. Harvey C. Jones (73; director since 1993; Managing Partner, Square Wave Ventures) appointed Chair. SAID (EX-99.1): operations, commitments and roadmap 'continue without interruption'.", "citation": ["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1045810/000104581026000082/nvda-20261111.htm", "https://investor.nvidia.com/news/press-release-details/2026/NVIDIA-Announces-CEO-Transition/default.aspx"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-said-cook-for-nvidia-ceo-2026-11-12", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/tim-cook-apple", "name": "SAID Cook should replace Huang at Nvidia", "tieType": "public endorsement (Truth Social: 'only one man to take his place - TIM COOK of Apple'; no Nvidia filing names Cook)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-12", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "changed", "statusDate": "2026-11-23", "statusNote": "Not followed: Trump posted Nov 12 that Tim Cook was 'the only man to take his place'; Nov 23 he celebrated Huang's return. Cook was never named in an Nvidia filing.", "addedIn": "2026-11-12 (v33)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-23", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-12-powermap-v33-V-trump-said-cook-for-nvidia-ceo-2026-11-12", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "SAID (Trump on Truth Social Nov 12 2026, reported by Politico 11:27 AM EST and screenshotted by @RapidResponse47): Huang 'has done a fantastic job' and 'there is only one man to take his place - TIM COOK of Apple. A Legend replaces a Legend!' Cook is Apple's executive chair; Apple did not comment. Nothing DONE: no Nvidia filing or board statement names Cook. Context (join, not cause): WaPo documents (Oct 15 2026) put both Nvidia and Apple at the $25M top tier of the ballroom fund.", "citation": ["https://www.politico.com/news/2026/11/12/trump-apple-tim-cook-nvidia-01162128", "https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2120909107385569646", "https://www.washingtonpost.com/investigations/2026/10/15/secret-documents-reveal-donors-behind-330-million-trumps-ballroom/"]}, {"@id": "tie/house-chairs-huang-briefing-2026-11", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/house-chairs-mast-moolenaar-crawford", "to": "node/jensen-huang", "name": "closed-door briefing requested; Huang agreed (Mast SAID)", "tieType": "oversight request (Nov 4 letter requesting a joint closed-door briefing Nov 18; Mast SAID Huang agreed to brief by Thanksgiving)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-04 ; 2026-11-12", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-27", "statusNote": "Dec 1 interview still set (CNBC Nov 24: Huang confirmed); Nvidia's Dec 1 GTC DC live session (newsroom, opened Nov 27) lists Buck, Boitano, Briski, Lebaredian, not Huang.", "addedIn": "2026-11-12 (v33)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-27", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-12-powermap-v33-V-house-chairs-huang-briefing-2026-11", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (letter PDF): House Foreign Affairs, China Select and Intelligence chairs Brian Mast, John Moolenaar and Rick Crawford wrote Huang Nov 4 2026 requesting a joint closed-door briefing on Nov 18 (room 2172 Rayburn). SAID (TechCrunch, NBC Nov 12): Mast says Huang agreed to testify behind closed doors by Thanksgiving, expected recorded and transcribed; Moolenaar would back a subpoena and named 'chip diversion'. No briefing held yet.", "citation": ["https://foreignaffairs.house.gov/sites/evo-subsites/republicans-foreignaffairs.house.gov/files/evo-media-document/11.4.26nvidialetter.pdf", "https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/12/jensen-huang-agrees-to-testify-before-congress/", "https://www.nbcnews.com/tech/tech-news/jensen-huang-agrees-brief-congress-interactions-alleged-spy-lawmaker-s-rcna608990"]}, {"@id": "tie/witkoff-kushner-zelensky-dublin-2026-11-12", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/steve-witkoff-jared-kushner", "to": "node/volodymyr-zelensky", "name": "Dublin meeting Nov 12 (after Putin); prisoner exchange SAID", "tieType": "meeting (Dublin, Ireland, after the Moscow meeting with Putin the same day)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-12", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-11-12", "statusNote": "Held Nov 12 (official photos). Outcomes SAID; no exchange date.", "addedIn": "2026-11-12 (v33)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-12", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-12-powermap-v33-V-witkoff-kushner-zelensky-dublin-2026-11-12", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "social", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE (official photos, @ZelenskyyUa 5:52 PM ET Nov 12 2026): Zelenskyy met US envoys Witkoff and Kushner in Ireland following the week's negotiations. SAID (Zelenskyy; Kushner 7:35 PM ET statement): working toward the largest prisoner exchange of the war; next round expanded with Europeans; nothing final until a comprehensive agreement; significant differences remain. No exchange date or terms.", "citation": ["https://x.com/ZelenskyyUa/status/2121013268110033316", "https://x.com/jaredkushner/status/2121039333100486752"]}, {"@id": "tie/1789-vulcan-elements-round-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/1789-capital-polymarket-kalshi", "to": "node/vulcan-elements", "name": "joined $65M round (Aug 2025)", "tieType": "investment (1789 Capital joined Vulcan's $65M round, Aug 2025)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-08", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-12 (v33)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-12", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-12-powermap-v33-V-1789-vulcan-elements-round-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (ProPublica, May 2026; Reuters): 1789 Capital, where Donald Trump Jr. is a partner, joined rare-earth magnet maker Vulcan Elements' $65M funding round in Aug 2025. SAID: 1789 says it had no role in Vulcan's later federal loan; Trump Jr.'s spokesman says he did not speak to Navarro about Vulcan.", "citation": ["https://www.propublica.org/article/donald-trump-jr-vulcan-deal-white-house", "https://www.reuters.com/investigations/trump-linked-venture-fund-1789-capital-tops-1-billion-assets-2025-09-08/"]}, {"@id": "tie/pentagon-osc-vulcan-620m-loan-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/us-dept-of-war-pentagon", "to": "node/vulcan-elements", "name": "$620M OSC loan (Nov 2025; seq. after 1789 round)", "tieType": "loan (Office of Strategic Capital, $620M, its largest; ~3 months after 1789 invested - sequence only)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-11", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": true, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-12 (v33)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-12", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-12-powermap-v33-V-pentagon-osc-vulcan-620m-loan-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (ProPublica; Huffman/Garcia release): the Pentagon's Office of Strategic Capital announced a $620M loan to Vulcan Elements in Nov 2025, its largest ever, about three months after 1789 Capital invested. Sequence only: no document shows the investment caused the loan. SAID (ProPublica, Pentagon records and unnamed officials): White House adviser Peter Navarro initiated the request ('the only deal initiated by a top aide to the president'). SAID denials: Pentagon (no preferential treatment), 1789, Trump Jr.'s spokesman. Reps. Huffman and Garcia demanded documents.", "citation": ["https://www.propublica.org/article/donald-trump-jr-vulcan-deal-white-house", "https://huffman.house.gov/media-center/press-releases/huffman-garcia-demand-documents-from-vulcan-elements-after-white-house-pushed-through-620-million-loan-to-company-tied-to-donald-trump-jr"]}, {"@id": "tie/drw-trump-media-100m-pipe-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/drw-don-wilson", "to": "node/trump-media", "name": "~$100M PIPE (May 2025; seq. after SEC dismissal)", "tieType": "investment (~$100M in Trump Media's bitcoin-treasury PIPE, May 2025; ~2 months after SEC dismissed its Cumberland DRW case - sequence only)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-03 ; 2025-05-27", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": true, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-12 (v33)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-12", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-12-powermap-v33-V-drw-trump-media-100m-pipe-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE: SEC dismissed its case against Cumberland DRW with prejudice in Mar 2025 (SEC litigation release LR-26276); DRW Investments then put about $100M into Trump Media's ~$2.3-2.5B bitcoin-treasury financing announced late May 2025. Sequence only; no source shows a link. SAID, DRW: no connection, no quid pro quo.", "citation": ["https://www.sec.gov/enforcement-litigation/litigation-releases/lr-26276", "https://cryptoslate.com/sec-greenlights-trump-medias-2-3b-bitcoin-treasury-deal/"]}, {"@id": "tie/cryptocom-trump-media-50m-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/crypto-com", "to": "node/trump-media", "name": "$50M TMTG stock in treasury deal (Aug 2025)", "tieType": "investment + deal ($50M of TMTG stock in the Aug 2025 treasury deal; SEC had closed its Crypto.com probe Mar 2025 - sequence only)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-03-27 ; 2025-08-26", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": true, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-12 (v33)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-12", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-12-powermap-v33-V-cryptocom-trump-media-50m-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (Reuters): in the Aug 2025 Trump Media / Crypto.com treasury deal, Crypto.com agreed to buy $50M of TMTG stock. SAID (Crypto.com): the SEC closed its investigation of Crypto.com with no action Mar 27 2025. Sequence only. The CRO-treasury SPAC was later terminated (register row tmtg-trust-bitcoin-treasury).", "citation": ["https://www.reuters.com/legal/government/trump-media-cryptocom-launch-new-crypto-treasury-firm-via-spac-deal-2025-08-26/", "https://crypto.com/en/company-news/sec-closes-crypto-com-investigation-with-no-action"]}, {"@id": "tie/alt5-wlf-1-5b-deal-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/alt5-sigma-ai-financial-corp", "to": "node/world-liberty-financial", "name": "$1.5B WLFI deal; Zach Witkoff chair (~$500M to Trump family)", "tieType": "deal ($1.5B WLFI treasury deal, Aug 11 2025; Zach Witkoff became Alt5 chair; Trump family entitled to 75% of token-sale proceeds, ~$500M)", "category": "family", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-08-11", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-12 (v33)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-12", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-12-powermap-v33-V-alt5-wlf-1-5b-deal-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (CNBC Jun 9 2026; CoinDesk): Alt5 Sigma announced Aug 11 2025 a $1.5B deal with World Liberty Financial ($750M in shares/warrants to WLF for WLFI plus a $750M stock sale whose proceeds bought WLFI), receiving ~7.3B WLFI; Zach Witkoff (son of envoy Steve Witkoff) became Alt5 chair. Per WLF disclosures the Trump family is entitled to 75% of token-sale proceeds, ~$500M from this deal (CNBC). Alt5 renamed AI Financial Corp. (Apr 2026), going-concern warning (May 2026), stock down ~93%. SAID, White House: no conflicts.", "citation": ["https://www.cnbc.com/2026/06/09/trump-world-liberty-financial-crypto-alt5-sigma.html", "https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/19/world-liberty-financial-wlfi-treasury-company-ai-financial-warns-in-sec-filing-that-it-may-not-survive-the-year"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-sons-new-america-acquisition-spac-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/eric-trump", "to": "node/new-america-acquisition-i-corp", "name": "SPAC sponsor stake + adviser (with Don Jr.)", "tieType": "business (SPAC sponsor interests + advisory board, with Donald Trump Jr.; S-1 Aug 4 2025, $300M IPO)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-08-04", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-12 (v33)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-12", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-12-powermap-v33-V-trump-sons-new-america-acquisition-spac-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (SEC S-1, CIK 2074878, Aug 4 2025): New America Acquisition I Corp. filed for a $300M SPAC IPO; Eric Trump (3M founder shares) and Donald Trump Jr. (2M) hold indirect interests through the sponsor and sit on its advisory board. The first S-1 said the target would be well positioned to benefit from 'government contracts or preferential procurement programs'; a same-day amendment removed the line after AP asked (AP).", "citation": ["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2074878/000149315225011551/forms-1.htm", "https://apnews.com/article/trump-eric-don-jr-spac-manufacture-shell-company-86760765e1dc12a923d357d1cf448fcc"]}, {"@id": "tie/occ-world-liberty-trust-charter-2026-08-14", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/occ-comptroller-of-the-currency", "to": "node/world-liberty-financial", "name": "preliminary trust-bank charter (Aug 14 2026)", "tieType": "regulatory approval (preliminary conditional national trust charter, World Liberty Trust Company N.A., Aug 14 2026)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-08-14", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-12 (v33)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-12", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-12-powermap-v33-V-occ-world-liberty-trust-charter-2026-08-14", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (OCC decision cd1385, Aug 14 2026): preliminary conditional approval for World Liberty Trust Company, N.A. (charter 344521); must meet pre-opening conditions. SAID, OCC: charter decisions are delegated to career staff. SAID, WLF: no special treatment.", "citation": ["https://www.occ.gov/topics/charters-and-licensing/interpretations-and-decisions/2026/cd1385.pdf", "https://www.foxbusiness.com/politics/trump-linked-world-liberty-crypto-venture-gets-preliminary-approval-from-currency-comptroller"]}, {"@id": "tie/cantor-nvidia-13f-holdings-2024-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/brandon-kyle-lutnick-cantor", "to": "node/nvidia", "name": "13F Nvidia stake $479M (YE24) -> $310M (Q1 26); hosted Huang (SAID)", "tieType": "holdings (13F-reported Nvidia common equity, Dec 2024-Jun 2026; count down 49% Sep 2025-Mar 2026) + investor-meeting host (late Sep 2026, CNBC) - timing vs Megaspeed pressure is sequence only", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2024-12-31 ; 2026-06-30", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": true, "status": "changed", "statusDate": "2026-11-16", "statusNote": "Q3 13F filed Nov 16 2026: 1,000,332 Nvidia common sh / $228.5M at Sep 30, down from 1,810,531 at Jun 30 (~-45%); puts 1.3M sh. Cantor SAID (Nov 13) lines are client-swap hedges. Sequence only.", "addedIn": "2026-11-13 (v34)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-16", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-13-powermap-v34-V-cantor-nvidia-13f-holdings-2024-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (SEC 13F-HR, Cantor Fitzgerald L.P., CIK 1024896; information tables opened Nov 13): Nvidia common equity 3,568,118 sh / $479.2M at Dec 31 2024; 3,492,970 sh / $651.7M at Sep 30 2025 (13F-HR/A); 3,000,419 sh at Dec 31 2025; 1,778,504 sh / $310.2M at Mar 31 2026; 1,810,531 sh / $362.3M at Jun 30 2026; most booked to otherManager 4, CF Secured LLC; Nvidia puts reported every period. SAID (CNBC, Luke Fountain, Nov 13 2026; CNBC = NBCUniversal/Comcast): Cantor hosted Huang and Nvidia executives for investor meetings in New York in late Sep 2026 (Cantor research report reviewed by CNBC); Brandon Lutnick told Fox Business Nov 11 Nvidia has 'an amazing leadership team'. SAID, Cantor spokesperson: 13F positions are client-swap hedges, proprietary Nvidia positions 'immaterial'. SEQUENCE ONLY: the 49% drop overlaps the months when, per Axios (anonymous), Lutnick resisted pressure to list Megaspeed; CNBC states there is no evidence the decline was tied to any warning. Next 13F due Nov 16 2026.", "citation": ["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1024896/000092963826000651/informationtable.xml", "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1024896/000092963826001888/informationtable.xml", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/13/howard-lutnick-nvidia-jensen-huang-china-cantor-fitzgerald.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/cantor-iren-3b-convertible-bookrunner-2026-05-14", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/brandon-kyle-lutnick-cantor", "to": "node/iren", "name": "bookrunner on $3B convertible (May 14 2026); $115M IREN stake", "tieType": "deal (bookrunner, IREN $3.0B 1.00% convertible notes due 2033, closed May 14 2026) + holding ($115M IREN shares, Jun 30 2026 13F) - timing vs China trip / H200 clearances is sequence only", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-05-14", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": true, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-13 (v34)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-13", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-13-powermap-v34-V-cantor-iren-3b-convertible-bookrunner-2026-05-14", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (IREN EX-99.1 on SEC EDGAR, May 14 2026): Cantor Fitzgerald & Co. was one of seven bookrunners (with J.P. Morgan, Goldman Sachs, Citi, Jefferies, MUFG, Wells Fargo) on IREN's $3.0B convertible notes offering, closed May 14 2026. DONE (Nvidia/IREN release May 7 2026): IREN granted Nvidia a five-year right to buy up to 30M shares at $70 (up to $2.1B) in a strategic partnership; CNBC adds a $3.4B five-year Nvidia cloud contract. DONE (13F, Jun 30 2026): Cantor reported 2,514,830 IREN shares ($115.0M). SEQUENCE ONLY (CNBC): pricing came May 12, the day Trump left for China (NYT, anonymous: Rubio warned him about Huang that day), and the close fell on May 14, the day Commerce cleared ~10 Chinese buyers for H200 chips. CNBC: unclear when IREN hired Cantor or what it earned; Cantor declined to answer.", "citation": ["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1878848/000114036126021285/ef20073507_ex99-1.htm", "https://investor.nvidia.com/news/press-release-details/2026/NVIDIA-and-IREN-Announce-Strategic-Partnership-to-Accelerate-Deployment-of-up-to-5-Gigawatts-of-AI-Infrastructure/default.aspx", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/13/howard-lutnick-nvidia-jensen-huang-china-cantor-fitzgerald.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/bessent-said-megaspeed-listing-favored-2026-11-13", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/scott-bessent", "to": "node/howard-lutnick", "name": "SAID: 4 agencies favored listing Megaspeed 'for months'; 'ask them' (Commerce)", "tieType": "public statement (on camera: Treasury, Defense, State, USTR 'were in favor of putting Megaspeed on the entity list for months'; points to Commerce)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-13", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "changed", "statusDate": "2026-11-23", "statusNote": "SAID followed by DONE: BIS listed Megaspeed and six affiliates Nov 23 (final rule filed 4:15 pm).", "addedIn": "2026-11-13 (v34)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-23", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-13-powermap-v34-V-bessent-said-megaspeed-listing-favored-2026-11-13", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "SAID (named official, on camera; CNBC Squawk Box Nov 13 2026, quoted in CNBC's Luke Fountain article; CNBC = NBCUniversal/Comcast): Treasury Secretary Bessent said the departments of Treasury, Defense and State and USTR 'were in favor of putting Megaspeed on the entity list for months,' and that Commerce is responsible for the Entity List: 'You will have to ask them about their internal processes.' This is the first on-record version of the split the Nov 11 Axios account (anonymous; Commerce: 'This is false') described. Megaspeed is not on the Entity List as of build. The Squawk Box transcript/video itself was not opened.", "citation": ["https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/13/howard-lutnick-nvidia-jensen-huang-china-cantor-fitzgerald.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/warren-coons-nvidia-records-preservation-2026-11-11", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/sens-elizabeth-warren-chris-coons", "to": "node/howard-lutnick", "name": "preserve-all-records letter (also Rubio, Miller); reply due Nov 17", "tieType": "official letter (records-preservation demand to Lutnick, Rubio and WH Chief of Staff Miller on Nvidia chip exports and the Huang intelligence matter; confirm by Nov 17)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-11", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-16", "statusNote": "Written confirmation requested by Nov 17 2026 (tomorrow at build); no response on record.", "addedIn": "2026-11-13 (v34)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-16", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-13-powermap-v34-V-warren-coons-nvidia-records-preservation-2026-11-11", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (letter PDF, Nov 11 2026, opened): Sens. Warren and Coons asked Commerce Secretary Lutnick, Secretary of State Rubio and White House Chief of Staff Stephen Miller to preserve all records on Nvidia advanced-AI-chip exports to China or diverting entities and on the reported Chinese intelligence operation targeting Huang, confirm preservation directives in writing by Nov 17, and brief Congress. The letter cites NYT reporting (anonymous) that officials at the White House, State and Commerce knew of the concerns. Democrats take both chambers in January. Response not on record at build.", "citation": ["https://static.foxbusiness.com/foxbusiness.com/content/uploads/2026/11/warren-coons-letter-nvidia-china-spy-allegations.pdf", "https://www.politico.com/live-updates/2026/11/11/congress/nvidia-documents-coons-warren-01161917"]}, {"@id": "tie/house-chairs-kessler-teter-appearance-request-2026-11-12", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/house-chairs-mast-moolenaar-crawford", "to": "node/jeff-kessler-commerce-under-secretary-bis", "name": "letters asking Kessler, Teter, Huang to appear (Nov 12)", "tieType": "official letters (second request: Huang, Nvidia GC Tim Teter and BIS Under Secretary Kessler asked to appear; Dec 1 closed-door interview for Huang; subpoena warned)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-12", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "changed", "statusDate": "2026-11-17", "statusNote": "Teter agreed to a Dec 2 transcribed interview; no date for Kessler in the Nov 17 release.", "addedIn": "2026-11-13 (v34)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-19", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-13-powermap-v34-V-house-chairs-kessler-teter-appearance-request-2026-11-12", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (House Foreign Affairs Committee release, Nov 12 2026, opened): Chairmen Mast, Moolenaar and Crawford sent letters to former Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang, Nvidia General Counsel Tim Teter and Under Secretary of Commerce Jeffrey Kessler requesting their appearance. SAID (CBS News Nov 12): the Huang letter asks for a closed-door interview Dec 1 and says HFAC will subpoena if he does not accept by Friday evening (Nov 13); Senate Banking Chair Tim Scott asked Huang to testify in early December and Lutnick to a public hearing next month. Kessler is the BIS official named in Nvidia GC Teter's Aug 2025 email to the Megaspeed agents (NYT, anonymous; v32 edge). Acceptance not on record at build.", "citation": ["https://foreignaffairs.house.gov/news/press-releases/chairmen-mast-moolenaar-and-crawford-send-second-request-to-jensen-huang-and-nvidia-to-brief-congress-on-the-chinese-intelligence-asset", "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/jensen-huang-nvidia-congress-testify/"]}, {"@id": "tie/dot-faa-peraton-atc-prime-integrator-2025-12-04", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/sean-duffy-transportation-secretary", "to": "node/peraton-veritas-capital", "name": "ATC Prime Integrator contract ($1.5B ceiling, Dec 2025)", "tieType": "contract (Prime Integrator, Brand New Air Traffic Control System; IDIQ 693KA726D00003, 10 yr, $1.5B ceiling; announced Dec 4 2025)", "category": "contract", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-12-04", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-13 (v34)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-13", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-13-powermap-v34-V-dot-faa-peraton-atc-prime-integrator-2025-12-04", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (FAA release Dec 4 2025, opened): Transportation Secretary Duffy and FAA Administrator Bedford named Peraton Prime Integrator for the Brand New Air Traffic Control System, first priority moving remaining copper telecom to fiber and a new digital command center; Duffy SAID Peraton shares 'President Trump's drive'. DONE (contract record, HigherGov/FPDS): IDIQ 693KA726D00003, awarded Dec 2025, 10 years, cost-plus-award-fee, $1.5B ceiling, 2 bids. Peraton is owned by Veritas Capital. SAID (Reuters Feb 10 2026, read via search text; page returned 401): Bedford told House members Trump negotiated a $200M discount off the proposed price. Context: Duffy and Vought renewed the $30.1B ATC request Nov 13 (separate edge), hours before the 3:54 PM EST nationwide ground stop; no document ties Peraton or the request to the stop.", "citation": ["https://www.faa.gov/newsroom/trumps-transportation-secretary-duffy-faa-administrator-bedford-announce-prime-integrator", "https://www.highergov.com/idv/693KA726D00003/", "https://www.reuters.com/business/aerospace-defense/faa-says-air-traffic-control-overhaul-management-contract-worth-15-billion-2026-02-11/"]}, {"@id": "tie/duffy-vought-30-1b-atc-letter-2026-11-13", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/sean-duffy-transportation-secretary", "to": "node/russ-vought", "name": "joint $30.1B ATC request to Congress (Nov 13, ~1 PM)", "tieType": "official letter (joint, to Congress: approve $30.1B for ATC modernization and airports before year end)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-13", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-11-16", "statusNote": "Letter (~1 PM Nov 13) asked $30.1B; same-evening briefing Duffy SAID 'the president has asked for $30 billion. I want $50 billion' (Roll Call Factba.se). Nov 14 he named L3Harris among possible causes. Sequence only vs the stop.", "addedIn": "2026-11-13 (v34)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-16", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-13-powermap-v34-V-duffy-vought-30-1b-atc-letter-2026-11-13", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE/SAID (AvWeb Nov 13 2026 1:13 PM EST, opened; Reuters): Duffy and OMB Director Vought wrote lawmakers urging approval of $30.1B ($10.1B ATC technology incl. $7.2B common automation platform and $2B cloud/telecom; $2B towers; $18B airports), renewing the September request (Schmitt's Modern Skies Act), on top of $12.5B enacted Jul 2025; letter quotes 'a resilient telecommunications backbone'. GAO (Sep 2026) found no life-cycle cost estimate or integrated master schedule. SEQUENCE ONLY: the AvWeb report precedes the FAA nationwide ground stop (3:54 PM EST) by ~2h40m; no document ties the letter to the stop and no office has named the stop's cause.", "citation": ["https://avweb.com/aviation-news/white-house-renews-30b-atc-modernization/", "https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/white-house-urges-congress-to-provide-301-billion-for-aviation-reform-5024655"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-sons-cove-kaz-tungsten-stake-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/eric-trump", "to": "node/cove-kaz-capital-kaz-resources", "name": "indirect <1% stake (with Don Jr.); American Ventures $32M", "tieType": "business (indirect stake <1% with Donald Trump Jr. in Kazakh tungsten venture via Skyline Builders merger; American Ventures $32M commitment Nov 2 2026)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-04 ; 2026-11-02", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-13 (v34)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-13", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-13-powermap-v34-V-trump-sons-cove-kaz-tungsten-stake-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE/SAID: Eric Trump and Donald Trump Jr. hold an indirect stake of under 1% in Cove Kaz Capital (Kaz Resources), developer of a Kazakh tungsten deposit with state miner Tau-Ken Samruk (WSJ/FT via Bloomberg Nov 9 2026 and Reuters Nov 11, opened; Sen. Warren's Jul 7 2026 Banking letter, opened, citing FT Apr 30 2026 on the sons' stake via a Trump-linked firm merging with Cove Kaz). Cove Kaz SAID Nov 2 it got a $32M commitment from American Ventures LLC (a Trump-family-linked fund) at a $1.97B implied valuation and plans a US listing. Bloomberg: Lutnick facilitated talks with Kazakh officials before the deal was announced at the Nov 2025 White House Central Asia summit. SAID, sons' spokesperson: no involvement in day-to-day management or the listing decision; Cove Kaz: Trumps played no role in the deal.", "citation": ["https://www.mining.com/web/us-exim-dfc-sour-on-tungsten-mine-deal-backed-by-trump-sons/", "https://www.miningweekly.com/article/us-lenders-do-not-plan-to-approve-kazakh-mine-deal-backed-by-trumps-sons-us-official-says-2026-11-11", "https://www.banking.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/letter_re_kazakhstan_mining.pdf"]}, {"@id": "tie/exim-dfc-cove-kaz-letters-of-interest-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/us-export-import-bank-exim", "to": "node/cove-kaz-capital-kaz-resources", "name": "LOIs $900M (EXIM) + $700M (DFC); not proceeding (Nov 2026)", "tieType": "financing letters of interest (EXIM ~$900M, DFC ~$700M; Nov 2025) -> lenders not proceeding (Nov 9-11 2026)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-11 ; 2026-11-11", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "changed", "statusDate": "2026-11-11", "statusNote": "DFC official SAID not actively pursuing (stage one of four); EXIM not proceeding per a source (anonymous); EXIM LOI expired Aug 2026, renewal filed.", "addedIn": "2026-11-13 (v34)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-11", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-13-powermap-v34-V-exim-dfc-cove-kaz-letters-of-interest-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "other", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE: EXIM (~$900M) and DFC (up to $700M) issued non-binding letters of interest for Cove Kaz's tungsten project, announced at the Nov 2025 White House Central Asia summit (Reuters; Bloomberg FOIA documents include the EXIM letter). EXIM's letter expired Aug 2026; Cove Kaz filed for renewal (Bloomberg). SAID (Reuters Nov 11, opened): a DFC official confirmed lending would not proceed; the project 'has not advanced beyond stage one' of DFC's four-part review; a source familiar said EXIM would not proceed (anonymous); EXIM declined comment. SAID, Cove Kaz chair Pini Althaus: 'no indication of any change of heart'. EXIM vice-chair nominee Slade SAID Oct 1: 'there is no loan'.", "citation": ["https://www.miningweekly.com/article/us-lenders-do-not-plan-to-approve-kazakh-mine-deal-backed-by-trumps-sons-us-official-says-2026-11-11", "https://www.mining.com/web/us-exim-dfc-sour-on-tungsten-mine-deal-backed-by-trump-sons/"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-sec-cftc-nominations-2026-11-12", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/sec-cftc-nominees-johnson-levine-anonick-rowland", "name": "nominated 2 SEC + 2 CFTC commissioners (Nov 12)", "tieType": "nominations (SEC: Kristin N. Johnson [D], Steven Levine [R]; CFTC: Nathan Anonick [R], Matthew Rowland [D]; sent to Senate Nov 12 2026)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-12", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-12", "statusNote": "Sent to the Senate Nov 12 2026 (lame duck); no committee action at build.", "addedIn": "2026-11-13 (v34)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-12", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-13-powermap-v34-V-trump-sec-cftc-nominations-2026-11-12", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (White House 'Nominations Sent to the Senate', Nov 12 2026, opened): Anonick to CFTC (term to Jun 19 2031, vice Behnam); Johnson to SEC (to Jun 5 2029, vice Crenshaw); Levine to SEC (to Jun 5 2030, vice Peirce); Rowland to CFTC (remainder to Apr 13 2028, vice Mersinger). Bloomberg Law/CoinDesk: Levine a senior White House CEA official; Johnson an ex-CFTC commissioner; Anonick Senate Agriculture majority senior counsel; Rowland a CFTC attorney detailed to Agriculture. CFTC Chair Selig SAID 'strong bipartisan picks'. Context: the CFTC is allowing Kalshi perpetuals since May (NYT via UPI) and faces CME/Cboe suits. Lame-duck Senate; not confirmed at build.", "citation": ["https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2026/11/nominations-sent-to-the-senate-16a6/", "https://www.upi.com/Top_News/US/2026/11/13/trump-nominates-cftc-sec/1591794595229/"]}, {"@id": "tie/bessent-said-nvidia-outside-ceo-2026-11-15", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/scott-bessent", "to": "node/nvidia", "name": "SAID: board should hire outside CEO; answers in 10 days (Nov 15)", "tieType": "public demand on a company board (Treasury Secretary on Fox News 'Sunday Morning Futures', Nov 15 2026)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-15", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "changed", "statusDate": "2026-11-23", "statusNote": "Not followed: Huang reinstated Nov 22; Bessent's outside-CEO line was SAID only.", "addedIn": "2026-11-16 (v35)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-23", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-16-powermap-v35-V-bessent-said-nvidia-outside-ceo-2026-11-15", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID (Fox Business, Max Bacall, Nov 15 2026 2:25 PM EST, opened; Fox Corp): Bessent called for Nvidia's board to hire its next CEO from outside the company: 'They need a dramatic shake-up'; 'We will see if Nvidia intentionally ignored the warning signs of these shell companies, many of them in Singapore'; demanded answers 'in the next 10 days from the board and from the outside counsel'. CNBC (Nov 15/16, opened; NBCUniversal/Comcast) quotes: 'were they pressing these seemingly illicit sales to goose their revenues and their earnings?'. No Treasury action or document accompanies the statement; Treasury has no stated authority over Nvidia's board. The day after, Trump SAID he 'would not mind' Huang returning (separate edge): two named officials, opposite positions.", "citation": ["https://www.foxbusiness.com/business-leaders/bessent-calls-nvidia-leadership-shake-up-amid-china-chip-scandal-urges-outside-ceo", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/16/nvidia-jensen-huang-return-tech.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-said-open-to-huang-return-2026-11-16", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/jensen-huang", "name": "SAID: 'would not mind' Huang back; security 'not put at risk' (Nov 16)", "tieType": "public statement on a CEO seat (to reporters before departing for Asia, Nov 16 2026)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-16", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "changed", "statusDate": "2026-11-23", "statusNote": "SAID followed by DONE at the company: board reinstated Huang Nov 22 (8-K). The President's role stays SAID (see v40 tie).", "addedIn": "2026-11-16 (v35)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-23", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-16-powermap-v35-V-trump-said-open-to-huang-return-2026-11-16", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "SAID (CNBC, Nov 16 2026, two stories opened; NBCUniversal/Comcast): Trump told reporters before leaving for the Asia summits that he 'would not mind' if Huang returned and that Huang had learned a 'big lesson'; asked about national security: 'It was not put at risk, and our country is now stronger than ever before.' Same day CNBC, citing one person familiar (anonymous): the board is not considering bringing Huang back and is focused on the investigation. Contrast: Bessent SAID Nov 15 the board should go outside the company; Trump SAID Nov 12 Tim Cook should take the seat. Three on-record presidential/cabinet positions in five days; no filing or board action follows any of them.", "citation": ["https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/16/nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang.html", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/16/nvidia-jensen-huang-return-tech.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/musk-backs-stand-with-jensen-petition-2026-11-13", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/elon-musk", "to": "node/jensen-huang", "name": "SAID: 'I'm signing it too' (reinstatement petition, Nov 13)", "tieType": "public backing (signed the 'Stand with Jensen' reinstatement petition; X post Nov 13 2026)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-13", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-16 (v35)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-16", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-16-powermap-v35-V-musk-backs-stand-with-jensen-petition-2026-11-13", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID (CNBC, Jenny Lee / Sawdah Bhaimiya, updated Nov 16 2026 12:34 PM EST, opened): Musk posted Friday on X 'A petition is underway to reinstate Jensen and I'm signing it too.' The petition (standwithjensen.com, 'Not affiliated with NVIDIA') had nearly 180,000 signatures; CNBC also names Garry Tan (YC), Tim Sweeney (Epic), Tobias Lutke (Shopify), Travis Kalanick as signers; affiliations on the site are self-reported. SAID (FT via CNBC, anonymous ally): a 'war room' of Silicon Valley executives will seek White House backing, with Huang's support. Huang's representative declined to comment (CNBC). Musk's X post itself not opened this pass.", "citation": ["https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/16/nvidia-jensen-huang-return-tech.html", "https://standwithjensen.com/"]}, {"@id": "tie/altimeter-atreides-nvidia-board-letter-2026-11-13", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/brad-gerstner-altimeter-gavin-baker-atreides", "to": "node/nvidia", "name": "shareholder letter: keep Huang's return an option (Nov 13)", "tieType": "major-shareholder open letter to the board (Fri Nov 13 2026): keep all options incl. Huang's return", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-13", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-16 (v35)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-16", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-16-powermap-v35-V-altimeter-atreides-nvidia-board-letter-2026-11-13", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE (CNBC, Nov 16 2026, opened): Altimeter Capital CEO Brad Gerstner and Atreides Management's Gavin Baker urged Nvidia's board in an open letter Friday Nov 13 to consider all leadership options, including Huang's return, and a measured process. SAID (CNBC Nov 16): Gerstner told CNBC Huang had not discussed a comeback with him. Letter text not opened this pass; holdings sizes not checked against 13Fs.", "citation": ["https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/16/nvidia-jensen-huang-return-tech.html", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/16/nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/nvidia-board-wachtell-probe-2026-11", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/nvidia", "to": "node/wachtell-lipton", "name": "board probe counsel (CNBC; no Nvidia statement)", "tieType": "board-retained counsel (investigation into Huang's conduct and national-security / trade-secret exposure)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-16 (v35)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-17", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-16-powermap-v35-I-nvidia-board-wachtell-probe-2026-11", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "Reported (CNBC, Seema Mody / Kif Leswing, Nov 16 2026, opened): Nvidia has hired Wachtell Lipton to lead a probe into Huang's conduct and whether it compromised national security or company secrets; one person familiar (anonymous) says the board is focused on that investigation and is not in discussions to bring Huang back. No Nvidia filing or statement names the firm (inference grade). Bessent's 10-day demand (Nov 15) is addressed to 'the board and ... the outside counsel'.", "citation": ["https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/16/nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/kushner-witkoff-ushakov-call-2026-11-16", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jared-kushner", "to": "node/yuri-ushakov", "name": "call w/ Ushakov + Europe NSAs (Nov 16)", "tieType": "envoy call (Kushner + Witkoff with the Kremlin aide; then call with Ukraine, EU, NATO and five NSAs), Nov 16 2026", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-16", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-16 (v35)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-16", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-16-powermap-v35-V-kushner-witkoff-ushakov-call-2026-11-16", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "social", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "SAID (Jared Kushner on X, Nov 16 2026 1:31 PM EST, opened; amplified by WH deputy press secretary Anna Kelly): 'This morning, @SEPeaceMissions [Witkoff] and I spoke with Yuri Ushakov to discuss the progress we have made and the next steps'; then a call with Ukraine and the NSAs of Germany, France, the UK, Poland and Italy plus EU and NATO; aim to 'facilitate direct engagement between Europe and Russia'; agenda for 'the next multilateral meeting' (no date or venue). No Kremlin readout opened this pass. Kushner holds no Senate-confirmed post (CREW suit on his envoy status already mapped).", "citation": ["https://x.com/jaredkushner/status/2122397087115698445", "https://x.com/AnnaKelly47/status/2122435306133594312"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-xi-putin-shenzhen-trilateral-scheduled-2026-11-19", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/vladimir-putin", "name": "trilateral w/ Xi scheduled Nov 19 (not held)", "tieType": "scheduled trilateral with Xi Jinping (Kylin Villa, Shenzhen, APEC sidelines, Nov 19 2026 2:30 PM local) - UPCOMING, not held", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-19 (scheduled)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "changed", "statusDate": "2026-11-19", "statusNote": "Held Nov 19 2026; 'U.S.-Russia-China Heads of State Declaration toward Peace' adopted (WH, Kremlin). Scheduled -> held; see v38 tie.", "addedIn": "2026-11-16 (v35)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-19", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-16-powermap-v35-V-trump-xi-putin-shenzhen-trilateral-scheduled-2026-11-19", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "SAID (TASS, Nov 16 2026, opened, citing the newly released US presidential schedule): a Trump-Xi-Putin trilateral is listed at Kylin Villa, Shenzhen, starting 2:30 PM local (6:30 AM GMT) Nov 19; White House gave no further details. TASS: Peskov SAID Nov 14 it was agreed; China's MFA confirmed Nov 16. White House SAID Trump departs for Asia (register gz row). Scheduled only: no meeting has taken place at build; the WH schedule page itself not opened (TASS relay).", "citation": ["https://tass.com/world/2218449"]}, {"@id": "tie/l3harris-faa-fti-copper-fiber-conversion-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/sean-duffy-transportation-secretary", "to": "node/l3harris", "name": "FTI incumbent; Duffy SAID maybe contractor 'incompetence' (Nov 14)", "tieType": "FAA contractor (FAA Telecommunications Infrastructure incumbent since 2002; copper-to-fiber conversion) named by Duffy after the Nov 13 ground stop", "category": "contract", "kind": "register", "date": "2002 ; 2026-11-14", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-16 (v35)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-16", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-16-powermap-v35-V-l3harris-faa-fti-copper-fiber-conversion-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (Washington Technology, Mar 28 2023, opened): L3Harris has two decades of incumbency on the FAA Telecommunications Infrastructure (FTI) contract the heritage Harris Corp. won in 2002. SAID (The Verge, Nov 14 2026, opened): Duffy said the root cause of the Nov 13 ground stop could be faulty hardware, a misconfigured router, or 'incompetence' on the part of contractor L3Harris; a new router 'flooding' other routers, 'over 1,000 connection attempts every 4 to 5 seconds'. SAID (L3Harris statement via The Verge): it has completed more than 70% of the copper-to-fiber conversion with telco partners and is supporting the FAA investigation (names no fault). Root cause not established at build; FBI custody of the router rests on CNN reporting (register row, I).", "citation": ["https://www.theverge.com/transportation/1033898/faa-ground-stop-sean-duffy-faa-copper-wire", "https://www.washingtontechnology.com/companies/2023/03/faa-selects-verizon-24b-telecommunications-contract/384517/"]}, {"@id": "tie/faa-att-fens-direct-award-2026-08-11", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/sean-duffy-transportation-secretary", "to": "node/at-t-faa-fens", "name": "FENS direct award, $74.3M TO; multi-billion expected (Aug 2026)", "tieType": "FAA direct (non-competitive) award: FENS undefinitized IDIQ 693KA8-26-D-00016 + $74.3M task order, under BNATCS waiver authority (Aug 11 2026)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-08-11", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-16 (v35)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-16", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-16-powermap-v35-V-faa-att-fens-direct-award-2026-08-11", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (SAM.gov award notice, published Aug 12 2026, opened): FAA made a direct award of an undefinitized single-award IDIQ (693KA8-26-D-00016) to AT&T Enterprise Services for FAA Enterprise Network Services, using the AMS waiver authority granted for the Brand New Air Traffic Control System; initial task order 693KA8-26-F-00278 $74.3M; FAA 'anticipates a multi-billion dollar IDIQ' over up to 15 years. Justification: Dec 2028 BNATCS deadline; the current FTI network 'can no longer adequately support NAS operations'; a competition would take 22+ months; AT&T 'the only Tier-1 provider currently willing and able'. Context DONE: FENS was first awarded competitively to Verizon in Mar 2023 ($2.4B, SAM/Washington Technology); what became of that award is a hole. SEQUENCE ONLY vs the Nov 13 ground stop; no document ties the award to the outage. Award signed under the FAA (DOT, Duffy); no Duffy signature on the notice.", "citation": ["https://sam.gov/workspace/contract/opp/89275702a17c4bc4a1906fd596fe8828/view", "https://www.washingtontechnology.com/companies/2023/03/faa-selects-verizon-24b-telecommunications-contract/384517/"]}, {"@id": "tie/vought-ueland-omb-to-gao-nomination-2026-11-16", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/russ-vought", "to": "node/eric-ueland", "name": "his OMB deputy nominated to head GAO (Nov 16)", "tieType": "OMB deputy (employment) -> nominated Comptroller General / head of GAO, 15-year term (sent to Senate Nov 16 2026)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2025 ; 2026-11-16", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-16", "statusNote": "Sent to the Senate Nov 16; HSGAC hearing Nov 19 (Paul). Lame-duck confirmation; not confirmed at build.", "addedIn": "2026-11-16 (v35)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-16", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-16-powermap-v35-V-vought-ueland-omb-to-gao-nomination-2026-11-16", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (White House 'Nominations Sent to the Senate', Nov 16 2026, opened): Eric Matthew Ueland to be Comptroller General for fifteen years, vice Dodaro. DONE (Roll Call, Paul Krawzak, Nov 16 2026, opened): Ueland is OMB deputy director for management (confirmed 52-45 in 2025) under Vought; GAO has repeatedly found the administration's impoundments illegal (e.g. the $810M pocket rescission, Sep 2026); HSGAC chair Rand Paul set a Nov 19 hearing; the statutory bipartisan commission did not convene (Peters SAID); the six GOP commission members recommended Ueland, DeBusk and Foster (sources). SAID: Vought on X, GAO 'has become hyper partisan'; Murray: 'a Russ Vought acolyte'. Lame-duck Senate; Democrats take control in January (Roll Call/Politico).", "citation": ["https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2026/11/nominations-sent-to-the-senate-a864/", "https://rollcall.com/2026/11/16/white-house-budget-aide-ueland-slated-to-head-gao/"]}, {"@id": "tie/nvidia-board-heidrick-ceo-search-2026-11-17", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/nvidia", "to": "node/heidrick-struggles", "name": "board retains Heidrick for CEO search; 'does not intend to reinstate' Huang (Nov 17)", "tieType": "board-retained executive search firm for the permanent CEO (named by Chair Harvey Jones on the Q3 FY27 call, Nov 17 2026)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-17", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "changed", "statusDate": "2026-11-23", "statusNote": "Search overtaken: Huang reinstated as CEO Nov 22 (8-K); no filing says the Heidrick search continues.", "addedIn": "2026-11-17 (v36)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-23", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-17-powermap-v36-V-nvidia-board-heidrick-ceo-search-2026-11-17", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID (NBC News live blog, updated Nov 17 2026 6:29 PM EST, opened): Nvidia board Chair Harvey Jones said on the Q3 FY27 call the board has retained Heidrick & Struggles to lead the search for a permanent chief executive and will consider internal and external candidates; Heidrick did not immediately comment; the hiring was earlier reported by the WSJ. Jones: the board 'does not intend to reinstate' Jensen Huang; he took no questions on the circumstances of the resignation or the ongoing investigation. Same day the board announced a new 'National Security and Export Control Oversight Committee' (Jones statement, NBC). The earnings release lists 'the ongoing investigation by an independent committee of our board' as a risk factor (NBC). Huang SAID on X the same morning he would be honored to return (register row). No successor named; no 8-K names the firm.", "citation": ["https://www.nbcnews.com/business/business-news/live-blog/nvidia-stock-earnings-report-jensen-huang-rcna609804", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/17/nvidia-nvda-earnings-report-q3-2027.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/commerce-doj-megaspeed-joint-statement-2026-11-17", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/howard-lutnick", "to": "node/todd-blanche", "name": "joint statement: Commerce opened Megaspeed probe 2024, DOJ leads criminal case (Nov 17)", "tieType": "joint Commerce-DOJ public statement on the Megaspeed investigation (DOJ OPA, Nov 17 2026), crediting 'Secretary Howard Lutnick' and 'Attorney General Todd Blanche'", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-17", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-11-17", "statusNote": "Statement out (DOJ page dated Nov 17; CNBC: released Monday evening US time). No charges; DOJ leads the criminal case.", "addedIn": "2026-11-17 (v36)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-17", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-17-powermap-v36-V-commerce-doj-megaspeed-joint-statement-2026-11-17", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID/DONE (DOJ Office of Public Affairs, Tue Nov 17 2026, opened): Commerce and DOJ say Commerce opened an export-control investigation of Megaspeed in 2024; in May 2025 Commerce asked Nvidia for records of direct or indirect sales to Megaspeed; in June 2025 Nvidia put Megaspeed on its 'no sell' list; BIS agents with Singaporean officers did an on-site end-use check in June 2025 and interviewed CEO Alice Huang; DOJ then took the lead in the criminal investigation. The statement says it addresses 'inaccurate information circulating in public reporting' without saying which, credits 'the Department of Commerce under Secretary Howard Lutnick' and DOJ 'under Attorney General Todd Blanche', and charges no one. Timing: DOJ page dated Tue Nov 17; CNBC (published 1:36 AM EST Nov 17, opened) says it came out Monday evening US time and that Lutnick reposted it ('very proud of the work of the Bureau of Industry and Security'); CNBC also quotes CFR's Chris McGuire ('The facts here just don't add up') and Singapore's MHA (Alice Huang not investigated for espionage; barred from re-entry Feb 2026). It lands while Lutnick faces a Dec 10 Senate Banking hearing and Bessent's on-record account (Nov 13) that four agencies favored listing Megaspeed 'for months'. Sequence only; the statement does not mention any Entity List decision.", "citation": ["https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/joint-statement-department-commerce-and-department-justice-megaspeed-investigation", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/17/megaspeed-investigation-nvidia-jensen-huang.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/tim-scott-lutnick-senate-banking-dec10-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/sen-tim-scott-senate-banking-chair", "to": "node/howard-lutnick", "name": "Scott asks Lutnick (Dec 10) + Huang (Dec 3); Lutnick agrees (Nov 12)", "tieType": "committee request + voluntary appearance agreed: Senate Banking public hearing on Nvidia and Commerce's export-control role, Dec 10 2026 (letters Nov 12)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-12 ; 2026-12-10 (scheduled)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-24", "statusNote": "Huang confirmed as sole public witness Dec 3 (committee notice via TechCrunch/CNBC/Reuters); Lutnick Dec 10 still scheduled.", "addedIn": "2026-11-17 (v36)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-24", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-17-powermap-v36-V-tim-scott-lutnick-senate-banking-dec10-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE (NBC News, Kyla Guilfoil, Nov 12 2026 9:45 PM EST, opened): Senate Banking chair Tim Scott sent letters Nov 12 asking Huang and Lutnick to appear voluntarily Dec 3 and Dec 10; to Lutnick, a public hearing on 'recent public reports about Nvidia and the Department of Commerce's role'. SAID: Lutnick spokesperson Kristen Eichamer, 'Secretary Lutnick has proactively agreed to appear voluntarily'. White House SAID 'complete confidence' in Lutnick. Huang (Sep 2025, NBC): 'Howard is the person I talk to most in the administration'. NBC live blog (Nov 17) still lists Lutnick for Dec 10. Scheduled, not held; Huang's Dec 3 answer not on record. Scott chairs only until January (Warren takes the gavel).", "citation": ["https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/commerce-secretary-howard-lutnick-testify-pressure-nvidia-scandal-rcna609093", "https://www.nbcnews.com/business/business-news/live-blog/nvidia-stock-earnings-report-jensen-huang-rcna609804"]}, {"@id": "tie/sec-nvidia-disclosure-probe-2026-11", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/sec-securities-and-exchange-commission", "to": "node/nvidia", "name": "SEC civil probe of disclosures (WSJ, anon.; unconfirmed)", "tieType": "reported civil investigation into whether Nvidia misled investors in its disclosures (WSJ, people familiar, Nov 17 2026)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-17 (reported)", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-27", "statusNote": "No SEC or Nvidia statement; EDGAR (opened Nov 27): no Nvidia 8-K after Nov 23; 10-Q due by Dec 4.", "addedIn": "2026-11-17 (v36)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-27", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-17-powermap-v36-I-sec-nvidia-disclosure-probe-2026-11", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "Reported (Investing.com relaying The Wall Street Journal, Nov 17 2026 4:05 PM, opened; CNBC video same day): the SEC is conducting a civil investigation into whether Nvidia misled investors through its disclosures, citing people familiar; focus not established. Investing.com/WSJ: Nvidia dropped its Singapore sales breakdown last year; Commerce investigated Megaspeed since late 2024; DOJ leads probes involving Alice Huang. Neither the SEC nor Nvidia confirmed it in the coverage opened. An investigation is not a charge.", "citation": ["https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/nvidia-faces-sec-investigation-as-crisis-deepens-following-huang-resignation-5033965", "https://www.cnbc.com/video/2026/11/17/sec-is-probing-nvidia-amid-jensen-huang-departure-according-to-the-wall-street-journal.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/nvidia-anthropic-10b-class-n-placement-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/nvidia", "to": "node/anthropic", "name": "~$10B Class N placement at IPO price (S-1/A, Nov 10)", "tieType": "agreed concurrent private placement: ~$10.0B of Anthropic Class N common at the IPO price (S-1/A No. 2, Nov 10 2026), contingent on the IPO", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-10", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "changed", "statusDate": "2026-11-20", "statusNote": "Closed Nov 20 2026 (Anthropic release): 313,253,007 Class N shares, ~$26.0B aggregate, Nvidia among seven buyers; agreed -> closed.", "addedIn": "2026-11-17 (v36)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-20", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-17-powermap-v36-V-nvidia-anthropic-10b-class-n-placement-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE (Anthropic, PBC Form S-1/A Amendment No. 2, accession 0001628280-26-072484, filed Nov 10 2026, opened via EDGAR): Google, NVIDIA, AMD, Broadcom, Micron, Microsoft and TSMC agreed, severally, to buy an aggregate $26.0B of Class N common in a private placement at the IPO price, contingent on and closing right after the offering; at the $74.00 midpoint NVIDIA would buy 135,135,135 shares for about $10.0B (same as Google). Register row: unchanged in Amendment No. 3 (Nov 17). Not a new Nvidia announcement; Kress did not announce it on the Nov 17 call. Contingent on the IPO pricing; not closed at build. Nvidia sells the chips its customers' compute runs on; the S-1 shows Anthropic compute commitments to SpaceX, Google, Amazon and Microsoft (map edges).", "citation": ["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2130357/000162828026072484/anthropicpbc-sx1ax2.htm", "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2130357/000162828026072484/0001628280-26-072484-index.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/faa-verizon-fens-supporting-role-2026-08", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/sean-duffy-transportation-secretary", "to": "node/verizon-faa-fens", "name": "2023 FENS winner moved to supporting role under AT&T (Aug 2026)", "tieType": "FAA FENS: Verizon (competitive 2023 awardee) moved to a supporting role, AT&T lead/prime under the Aug 11 2026 direct award", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2023-03 ; 2026-08-11", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-17 (v36)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-17", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-17-powermap-v36-V-faa-verizon-fens-supporting-role-2026-08", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "other", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE (Washington Technology, Ross Wilkers, Aug 13 2026, opened): with the Aug 11 2026 FENS award AT&T 'is taking over as the lead project manager and prime contractor with Verizon moving to a supporting role'; Verizon 'will still be tasked with providing core network functions'. SAID: Verizon referred questions to the FAA; FAA emailed statement: AT&T begins program management, network design and 'transition planning from legacy network services'; FAA says a new competition would take 22+ months and make the Dec 2028 BNATCS deadline 'impossible to meet'. The FAA first chose Verizon in spring 2023. No termination or protest reported; the contract modification itself was not opened. Sequence only vs the Nov 13 ground stop (FAA Q&A names the L3Harris-run FTI network, not FENS).", "citation": ["https://www.washingtontechnology.com/contracts/2026/08/faa-brings-t-network-modernization-program/415412/", "https://www.washingtontechnology.com/companies/2023/03/faa-selects-verizon-24b-telecommunications-contract/384517/"]}, {"@id": "tie/l3harris-juniper-routers-faa-fti-2026-11-15", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/l3harris", "to": "node/juniper-routers-faa-fti", "name": "FAA: L3Harris-deployed Juniper router at El Dorado AR; 60+ disabled (Nov 15)", "tieType": "FAA-named equipment in the Nov 13 ground stop: new Juniper router deployed by L3Harris at the El Dorado, AR radio site; function disabled on 60+ Juniper routers, installs paused", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-13 ; 2026-11-15", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-17 (v36)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-19", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-17-powermap-v36-V-l3harris-juniper-routers-faa-fti-2026-11-15-r2", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID/DONE (FAA newsroom, 'Nationwide Ground Stop: Questions and Answers', Sun Nov 15 2026, opened): legacy equipment became unstable when data flooded the FTI network at 1,000 connection attempts every 4 to 5 seconds; the initial investigation points to a radar site in Amarillo, TX and a radio site in El Dorado, AR, where L3Harris, 'the FAA's current network service provider', had been deploying a new router; L3Harris blocked both locations and the network stabilized. DONE (FAA): it disabled the functionality of 'the originating Juniper routers', disabled the same function on 'more than 60 other Juniper routers' and paused installing them; broadcasting disabled on all new routers. SAID: 'no indication' of a cyberattack; 'not' caused by modernization; FAA and L3Harris 'continue to investigate the root cause'. On the FAA Q&A page (re-opened Tue Nov 17 2026 about 11:40 PM EST) the root cause is still under investigation by FAA and L3Harris; that page names the router maker but states no fault by it.", "citation": ["https://www.faa.gov/newsroom/nationwide-ground-stop-questions-and-answers", "https://www.channelnewsasia.com/business/us-official-says-recent-tech-woes-not-tied-cyberattacks-6559696"]}, {"@id": "tie/mullin-duffy-ground-stop-briefing-not-cyber-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/markwayne-mullin-dhs-secretary", "to": "node/sean-duffy-transportation-secretary", "name": "joint ground-stop briefing; Mullin SAID '98%' not cyber (Nov 17)", "tieType": "joint White House ground-stop briefing (Nov 13 2026) + DHS Secretary's on-record 'not a cyberattack' line (Nov 13, Nov 17)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-13 ; 2026-11-17", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-17 (v36)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-17", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-17-powermap-v36-V-mullin-duffy-ground-stop-briefing-not-cyber-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID (DHS release 'ICYMI: Secretary Mullin and Secretary Duffy Address Nationwide FAA Ground Stop', Nov 13 2026, opened): Mullin with Duffy at the White House: 'We have seen zero evidence that this is a cyberattack'; 'The President has declared this a national emergency, and now we have to have Congress act and fund it'; DHS assets 'from DOW, to CISA' with 'NSA working with us'. SAID (Reuters via CNA, Nov 17 2026, opened): Mullin told CNBC the week's outages (United, FAA, Microsoft, JPMorgan Chase) are aging systems, 'nothing to do with cyberattacks', '98 per cent certainty this isn't a cyberattack', and 'we're going to see more of this'. No national-emergency proclamation text opened this pass (hole). Both secretaries used the stop to press Congress for ATC money (Duffy's $30.1B letter / $50B ask, map edge). Sequence only.", "citation": ["https://www.dhs.gov/news/2026/11/13/icymi-secretary-mullin-and-secretary-duffy-address-nationwide-faa-ground-stop-all", "https://www.channelnewsasia.com/business/us-official-says-recent-tech-woes-not-tied-cyberattacks-6559696"]}, {"@id": "tie/hegseth-laneve-army-chief-nomination-2026-11-17", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/pete-hegseth", "to": "node/gen-chris-laneve", "name": "ex-aide nominated Army chief after Hegseth fired George (Nov 17)", "tieType": "former military aide to Hegseth -> acting Army chief of staff (after Hegseth fired Gen. Randy George, Apr 2026) -> nominated Army chief of staff by Trump (Nov 17 2026)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-04 ; 2026-11-17", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-23", "statusNote": "In SASC; no hearing or vote date; Wicker needs one or two GOP holdouts.", "addedIn": "2026-11-17 (v36)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-23", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-17-powermap-v36-V-hegseth-laneve-army-chief-nomination-2026-11-17", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE (ABC News, Steven Beynon, Nov 17 2026 4:56 PM, opened; Washington Post headline same day, body not loaded): Trump formally nominated Gen. Chris LaNeve to be Army chief of staff. LaNeve had been acting chief since Hegseth fired Gen. Randy George in April 'without explanation'; LaNeve previously served as one of Hegseth's top military aides and rose from a South Korea command to vice chief in under two years. Army Secretary Dan Driscoll resigned in August amid tension with Hegseth (a US official, ABC). SAID: LaNeve, 'deeply honored by the President's trust'. Lame-duck Senate; not confirmed at build. The firing and the nomination are time order; no document states a reason for George's removal.", "citation": ["https://abcnews.com/Politics/trump-nominates-laneve-top-army-officer/story?id=138219615"]}, {"@id": "tie/overton-fda-nomination-dropped-2026-11-17", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/robert-f-kennedy-jr", "to": "node/heidi-overton", "name": "FDA pick dropped (Axios, senior official; no withdrawal on record)", "tieType": "FDA commissioner nomination (Aug 2026) reported dropped by the White House for lack of Senate support (Axios scoop, senior administration official, Nov 17 2026)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-08 ; 2026-11-17 (reported)", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "changed", "statusDate": "2026-11-18", "statusNote": "Reuters/CNBC (three people): withdrawn; WH weighing Sen. Roger Marshall (two people); Senate withdrawal message not checked.", "addedIn": "2026-11-17 (v36)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-18", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-17-powermap-v36-I-overton-fda-nomination-dropped-2026-11-17", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "Reported (Axios, Alex Isenstadt, Nov 17 2026, opened): the White House is dropping Heidi Overton's nomination to lead the FDA; a senior administration official (unnamed) SAID she 'lacks the support on the Hill' and 'We need to go in a new direction at FDA, and everybody fully supports Secretary Kennedy's vision'. Overton, deputy director of the White House Domestic Policy Council, was nominated in August; HELP chair Bill Cassidy had 'strong concerns' over her role in changing childhood vaccine recommendations ('almost disqualifying'); MAHA critics saw her siding with health and agriculture interests. The HELP vote was set for Nov 18. FDA led by acting Commissioner Kyle Diamantas since Makary resigned in May. No formal withdrawal message opened.", "citation": ["https://www.axios.com/2026/11/17/heidi-overton-fda-nomination-dropped"]}, {"@id": "tie/treasury-nsc-written-bis-remote-access-rule-2026-11-16", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/scott-bessent", "to": "node/howard-lutnick", "name": "Commerce rule 'written by' Treasury + NSC (BIS, Nov 16)", "tieType": "Commerce/BIS interim final rule on remote access to advanced chips, 'written by and at the direction of the Department of Treasury and the National Security Council' (BIS release, Nov 16 2026)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-16", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-17 (v36)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-17", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-17-powermap-v36-V-treasury-nsc-written-bis-remote-access-rule-2026-11-16", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (BIS press release, Nov 16 2026, opened): Commerce's Bureau of Industry and Security released an interim final rule on remote access to advanced 'super intelligence' chips and servers, 'written by and at the direction of the Department of Treasury and the National Security Council'. DONE (Federal Register public-inspection text, Docket 261116-0005, RIN 0694-AK50, opened): licence needed for exports to data centers supplying more than 12 million aggregate TPP to companies headquartered in D:5 countries or Macau; new licence requirement for advanced chips to Indonesia, Malaysia, Singapore, Thailand and Brazil (US-parented buyers exempt with reporting); formally rescinds the AI Diffusion Rule. Context: Bessent SAID Nov 13 Treasury, DoD, State and USTR favored listing Megaspeed 'for months' and pointed at Commerce (map edge); CNBC (Nov 17) says the rule closes the rental route and puts Nvidia revenue at risk. The release names Treasury, not Bessent personally. Sequence only vs the Megaspeed dispute.", "citation": ["https://www.bis.gov/press-release/bis-issues-rule-addressing-remote-access-american-super-intelligence-technology", "https://www.federalregister.gov/public-inspection/raw_text/202/623/529.txt", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/17/nvidia-nvda-earnings-report-q3-2027.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/hegseth-rodriguez-venezuela-defense-pact-2026-11-18", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/pete-hegseth", "to": "node/delcy-rodriguez-venezuela-acting-president", "name": "signs defense pact w/ acting pres. Rodriguez in Caracas (Nov 18)", "tieType": "US-Venezuela military cooperation agreement signed in Caracas during an unannounced Hegseth visit (Nov 18 2026); cooperation severed by Venezuela in 2005", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-18", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-11-18", "statusNote": "Signed per Hegseth/Rodriguez remarks (AP, Anadolu, DW); no Department of War release or text opened.", "addedIn": "2026-11-18 (v37)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-19", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-18-powermap-v37-V-hegseth-rodriguez-venezuela-defense-pact-2026-11-18", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 4, "description": "DONE as reported (Anadolu Agency, Maryam Ashalem de Andres, Nov 18 2026, opened; AP, CARACAS; EFE; DW): Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth, on an unannounced visit to Caracas, and Venezuela's interim/acting President Delcy Rodriguez signed an agreement restoring military cooperation: joint training, intelligence sharing, defense equipment and capabilities. Cooperation had been curtailed in 2004-2005 under Chavez (military exchange suspended April 2005, Anadolu). SAID Hegseth: 'Venezuela has gone from our most aggressive regional threat to a compliant security partner'; 'We could not have accomplished so much in less than a year without her leadership'; he credited the January 2026 operation that captured Maduro. SAID Rodriguez: an 'extraordinarily important' step; she confirmed they discussed the bilateral oil agreement involving PDVSA. DW reports the Pentagon did not release information on the trip or confirm it; agreement text not checked this pass (hole filed). Next stops reported: Honduras (Asfura), Colombia (C-130 delivery).", "citation": ["https://www.aa.com.tr/en/politics/-us-venezuela-sign-defense-pact-to-expand-military-intelligence-cooperation/4129756", "https://apnews.com/article/hegseth-venezuela-maduro-trump-e02dd6173e575c644a37dd417d84296d", "https://www.dw.com/en/us-pentagon-chief-hegseth-signs-military-deal-in-venezuela/a-79985607", "https://efe.com/english/latest-news/2026-11-18/venezuela-us-resume-military-cooperation-severed-in-2005/"]}, {"@id": "tie/house-dems-cantor-nvidia-records-letter-2026-11-17", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/house-democrats-meeks-raskin-kamlager-dove", "to": "node/brandon-kyle-lutnick-cantor", "name": "Dem ranking members demand Cantor's Nvidia trade records (Nov 17-18)", "tieType": "records demand to Cantor Fitzgerald chair Brandon Lutnick on Nvidia trades since Jan 2024, China/SE Asia business and Commerce contacts (letter Nov 17, released Nov 18 2026)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-17 ; 2026-11-18 (released)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-18", "statusNote": "Letter sent; preservation confirmation asked by Nov 30 (CNBC) / Dec 1 (release); Cantor SAID 'baseless'. Minority request, no subpoena.", "addedIn": "2026-11-18 (v37)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-18", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-18-powermap-v37-V-house-dems-cantor-nvidia-records-letter-2026-11-17", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (House Foreign Affairs Democrats release, Nov 18 2026, opened; CNBC, Kevin Breuninger, Nov 18, opened: letter 'sent Tuesday'): Ranking Members Gregory Meeks (HFAC), Jamie Raskin (Judiciary) and Sydney Kamlager-Dove wrote to Cantor Fitzgerald Chairman Brandon Lutnick demanding records of every Nvidia trade since January 2024, Cantor's business in China and Southeast Asia, internal/client communications on export controls and chip smuggling, communications with Commerce about Nvidia, Megaspeed and Asian data-center projects, and records on President Trump's reported Nvidia investments; preservation to be confirmed in writing (release: by Dec 1; CNBC: by Nov 30). SAID (letter): 'Did the Secretary of Commerce seriously and perhaps irreversibly compromise U.S. national security interests to make money for his adult children and Cantor Fitzgerald?' (a question, not a finding). SAID (Cantor statement to CNBC): the letter is 'inaccurate', allegations 'baseless'; 'Cantor holds no material proprietary position in Nvidia'; holdings 'arise primarily from equity swaps executed for clients' and the decline reflects 'the unwinding of those hedges'. CNBC: 'There is no known evidence that Lutnick's sons had advance or insider knowledge'. Minority members; no subpoena power until January.", "citation": ["https://democrats-foreignaffairs.house.gov/2026/11/ranking-members-meeks-raskin-and-kamlager-dove-probe-whether-lutnicks-family-finances-shaped-his-response-to-the-nvidia-spy-scandal/", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/18/nvidia-lutnick-china-ai-megaspeed-cantor-fitzgerald.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/guthrie-briefing-requests-kress-lutnick-kessler-2026-11-18", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/rep-brett-guthrie-energy-commerce-chair", "to": "node/howard-lutnick", "name": "E&C chair asks Kress, Lutnick, Kessler for briefings by Dec 2", "tieType": "House Energy & Commerce chair's letters requesting briefings from Nvidia interim CEO Kress and from Lutnick + Under Secretary Kessler by Dec 2 2026 (Nov 18 2026)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-18", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-18", "statusNote": "Briefings requested by Dec 2 2026; no reply on record.", "addedIn": "2026-11-18 (v37)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-18", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-18-powermap-v37-V-guthrie-briefing-requests-kress-lutnick-kessler-2026-11-18", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (House Energy and Commerce Committee release, Nov 18 2026, opened): Chairman Brett Guthrie (R-KY) sent letters to Nvidia interim CEO Colette Kress and to Commerce Secretary Lutnick and Under Secretary Kessler requesting briefings no later than December 2 2026 'following recent reporting on Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang and his relationship with alleged Chinese intelligence asset and Megaspeed executive Alice Huang'; the Commerce letter asks about 'the application of export controls relating to semiconductor chips'. Also (CNBC Nov 18, opened): HFAC Chairman Brian Mast sent a letter Nov 17 to Kessler on possible chip smuggling by Megaspeed and affiliate Speedmatrix. A request, not a subpoena; no reply on record. Republican-led panel, same week as the Democrats' Cantor letter.", "citation": ["https://energycommerce.house.gov/posts/chairman-guthrie-requests-briefings-from-nvidia-and-department-of-commerce-over-megaspeed-and-national-security-concerns", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/18/nvidia-lutnick-china-ai-megaspeed-cantor-fitzgerald.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/clayton-rubio-no-cyberattack-outages-2026-11-18", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jay-clayton", "to": "node/marco-rubio", "name": "DNI + NSA: outages 'not a cyberattack' (WH, Nov 18)", "tieType": "joint White House line that the Nov 2026 outages (Microsoft, FAA, banks) were separate patching/upgrade incidents, not a cyberattack (WH release, Nov 18 2026)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-18", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-18 (v37)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-18", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-18-powermap-v37-V-clayton-rubio-no-cyberattack-outages-2026-11-18", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "SAID (White House release, Nov 18 2026, opened, '\"No Indication of a Cyberattack\": DNI Clayton and Secretary Rubio on Recent Tech Outages'; the release calls Rubio 'National Security Adviser' and 'Secretary'): DNI Jay Clayton: 'This is not a cyberattack, and this is not a coordinated effort by a nation state'; the cause is institutions patching identified vulnerabilities, 'a good news story'. Rubio: 'the Microsoft incident has nothing to do with what we saw with the FAA. The FAA has nothing to do with what we saw with the banks'; 'We are not under systemic attack'. Same day (register row, prepared House Homeland Security testimony): DHS Secretary Mullin SAID Iranian government cyber actors 'have targeted U.S. critical infrastructure networks since the conflict with Iran began'; that testimony does not mention the outages. Both are statements; the map records them side by side, not as a contradiction. Root cause of the FAA event still under investigation (FAA, CNBC).", "citation": ["https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/11/no-indication-of-a-cyberattack-dni-clayton-and-secretary-rubio-on-recent-tech-outages/"]}, {"@id": "tie/bezos-said-nvidia-no-outsider-ceo-2026-11-17", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jeff-bezos", "to": "node/nvidia", "name": "SAID: 'would not hire an outsider' for Nvidia (Nov 17)", "tieType": "public advice on the Nvidia CEO search (Semafor Silicon Valley & The World, Nov 17 2026)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-17", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-18 (v37)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-18", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-18-powermap-v37-V-bezos-said-nvidia-no-outsider-ceo-2026-11-17", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID (Reuters via GMA News, Nov 18 2026, opened; Semafor Flagship, Nov 18, opened): Amazon Executive Chair Jeff Bezos, at Semafor's Silicon Valley conference Nov 17: 'If you don't bring Jensen back, I would not hire an outsider. Nvidia is too complicated'; Semafor: an outside pick would have a 'vanishingly small chance of success'. Context: Bessent SAID Nov 15 Nvidia should hire an outside CEO (map edge); the board retained Heidrick & Struggles for internal and external candidates. Bezos holds no Nvidia role; this is advice, not a tie of money or office.", "citation": ["https://www.gmanetwork.com/news/money/companies/1009885/nvidia-chair-says-the-board-will-not-rehire-huang-as-ceo/story/", "https://www.semafor.com/article/11/18/2026/nvidias-board-divided-over-calls-for-huangs-return"]}, {"@id": "tie/nvidia-board-divided-huang-return-2026-11-18", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/nvidia", "to": "node/jensen-huang", "name": "board split on return; Arm/Marvell chiefs in running (Semafor, anon.)", "tieType": "board reportedly divided on Huang's return; heads of Arm and Marvell reportedly in the running (Semafor, unnamed, Nov 18 2026)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-18", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "changed", "statusDate": "2026-11-23", "statusNote": "The Nov 23 release says the board voted unanimously to reinstate; the earlier 'divided' report is overtaken as to the vote.", "addedIn": "2026-11-18 (v37)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-23", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-18-powermap-v37-I-nvidia-board-divided-huang-return-2026-11-18", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "Reported (Semafor, Prashant Rao, Nov 18 2026 6:23 AM EST, opened; unnamed sources): some members of Nvidia's board favor a return of Jensen Huang although the chair declared the company would look elsewhere; the heads of Arm and Marvell are 'in the running'. On the record the other way: Chair Harvey Jones SAID Nov 17 the board 'unanimously accepted his resignation and does not intend to reinstate Jensen' and interim CEO Kress SAID to CNBC 'The board has determined that they will not reinstate Jensen' (CNBC Nov 18, opened). Reuters: Kalshi odds Arm's Rene Haas 25%, Ian Buck 17%, Huang 9% (a market price, not a fact). No board member named; no candidate confirmed.", "citation": ["https://www.semafor.com/article/11/18/2026/nvidias-board-divided-over-calls-for-huangs-return", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/18/nvidia-kress-jensen-huang-return.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/xi-greets-trump-shenzhen-tarmac-2026-11-18", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/xi-jinping", "name": "Xi greets Trump at the plane, Shenzhen (Nov 18)", "tieType": "Xi personally greets Trump at the plane in Shenzhen ahead of APEC (Nov 18 2026), reciprocating Trump's Joint Base Andrews greeting in Sept 2026", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-09 ; 2026-11-18", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-18 (v37)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-18", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-18-powermap-v37-V-xi-greets-trump-shenzhen-tarmac-2026-11-18", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (NBC News, Jennifer Jett and Erin Tan, Nov 18 2026, opened; White House X post, register row): Xi Jinping personally greeted President Trump outside Air Force One in Shenzhen; NBC: believed to be the first time Xi has been on hand to greet any foreign leader arriving in China; Xinhua (via NBC) framed it as returning Trump's and Melania Trump's welcome at Joint Base Andrews in September. Putin, arriving earlier, was met by Cai Qi. NBC: a senior US official said the Nov 19 trilateral was unlikely to produce any agreement ('an entry point'). Protocol, not a deal.", "citation": ["https://www.nbcnews.com/world/asia/xi-jinping-greets-trump-arrives-china-tarmac-putin-talks-shenzhen-apec-rcna609962", "https://x.com/WhiteHouse/status/2123029314765484131"]}, {"@id": "tie/putin-xi-shenzhen-talks-2026-11-18", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/vladimir-putin", "to": "node/xi-jinping", "name": "talks in Shenzhen, 50th meeting (Nov 18)", "tieType": "Russia-China leaders' talks in Shenzhen the day before the Trump-Xi-Putin trilateral (Kremlin, Nov 18 2026)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-18", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-18 (v37)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-18", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-18-powermap-v37-V-putin-xi-shenzhen-talks-2026-11-18", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE (Kremlin, 'Russian-Chinese talks', Nov 18 2026, opened): Putin and Xi held talks in Shenzhen on 'the comprehensive partnership and strategic cooperation' and international issues, continued over a working breakfast with Lavrov and Ushakov. SAID Xi: their third face-to-face meeting this year and 50th since 2013; relations 'as steadfast as a mountain'. SAID Putin: bilateral trade above US$200 billion for several years; 'Russian-Chinese foreign policy tandem is working steadily'. Sequence only: the day before the scheduled trilateral with Trump (map edge, pending).", "citation": ["http://en.kremlin.ru/events/president/news/81287"]}, {"@id": "tie/witkoff-kushner-berlin-coalition-2026-11-19", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/steve-witkoff-jared-kushner", "to": "node/volodymyr-zelensky", "name": "due in Berlin w/ Coalition of the Willing (Nov 19, scheduled)", "tieType": "envoys due at the Coalition of the Willing leaders' meeting in Berlin with Merz, Zelensky, Macron, Burnham (Nov 19 2026) - SCHEDULED, same day as the Shenzhen trilateral", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-19 (scheduled)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "changed", "statusDate": "2026-11-19", "statusNote": "Held Nov 19: envoys attended (AFP, NATO, Chancellery); scheduled -> held; see v38 Merz tie.", "addedIn": "2026-11-18 (v37)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-19", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-18-powermap-v37-V-witkoff-kushner-berlin-coalition-2026-11-19", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "SAID (Axios, Barak Ravid, Nov 16 2026, opened; a US official): Witkoff and Kushner planned a Thursday Berlin meeting with Ukrainian and European officials on security guarantees and postwar recovery; the official called it and Trump's China visit 'a coordinated diplomatic effort'; Rubio, Bessent and Chief of Staff Miller, travelling with Trump, were briefed. SAID (Ukrinform, Nov 18 2026 22:06, opened, German government sources): they arrive Nov 19, meet Chancellor Merz, attend the plenary and a joint press conference with Merz, Zelensky, Macron and UK PM Andy Burnham. SAID (Zelensky on X, Nov 18, register rows): the envoys will debrief in Berlin on the talks in China. Scheduled, not held at build. Axios: Ushakov said no agreement had been reached that Europe would have a seat at the table.", "citation": ["https://www.axios.com/2026/11/17/witkoff-kushner-ukraine-europe-russia-berlin-meeting", "https://www.ukrinform.net/rubric-polytics/4186174-witkoff-kushner-to-attend-coalition-of-the-willing-summit-in-berlin.html", "https://x.com/ZelenskyyUa/status/2123133098627928241"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-xi-putin-heads-of-state-declaration-2026-11-19", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/xi-jinping", "name": "trilateral held w/ Putin; Declaration toward Peace adopted (Nov 19)", "tieType": "first US-Russia-China trilateral summit held in Shenzhen (APEC sidelines); 'U.S.-Russia-China Heads of State Declaration toward Peace' adopted (Nov 19 2026)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-19", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-19 (v38)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-19", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-19-powermap-v38-V-trump-xi-putin-heads-of-state-declaration-2026-11-19", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (White House, 'U.S.-Russia-China Heads of State Declaration toward Peace', Nov 19 2026, opened; Kremlin readout/transcript 81303 via register row): Trump, Putin and Xi ('State Chairman of the People's Republic of China') met in Shenzhen on Nov 19 2026; the US and Russian heads of state thanked China for hosting. The text commits the three, as permanent UN Security Council members, to UN reform; says they 'plan to increase the production and supply of refined petroleum products' and reaffirm 'stable energy flows'; says state consent and 'respect for immunities of State officials are of paramount importance' and that 'the International Criminal Court and other similar bodies must not abuse their jurisdiction'; and reaffirms that 'a nuclear war cannot be won and must never be fought', with a three-way dialogue on nuclear risk and non-proliferation. SAID (Trump opening remarks, Kremlin transcript 81303, register row): he would suggest ways to protect 'our nations' sovereignty from rogue globalist organisations such as the International Criminal Court'. Context (Meduza via register row): Putin has been under an ICC arrest warrant since 2023; none of the three is a Rome Statute party. The declaration names no Ukraine or Iran terms; Kyiv and European governments were not parties. A Chinese government readout was not opened this pass.", "citation": ["https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefings-statements/2026/11/u-s-russia-china-heads-of-state-declaration-toward-peace/", "http://en.kremlin.ru/events/president/news/81303", "http://www.en.special.kremlin.ru/events/president/transcripts/81303"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-putin-shenzhen-bilateral-2026-11-19", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/vladimir-putin", "name": "bilateral in Shenzhen; Rubio+Bessent / Lavrov, Siluanov, Ushakov, Dmitriev (Nov 19)", "tieType": "Trump-Putin bilateral meeting after the APEC plenary in Shenzhen (Nov 19 2026); Rubio + Bessent across from Lavrov, Siluanov, Ushakov, Dmitriev", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-19", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-19 (v38)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-19", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-19-powermap-v38-V-trump-putin-shenzhen-bilateral-2026-11-19", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (Kremlin, 'Meeting with US President Donald Trump', Nov 19 2026 07:15, opened): after the APEC plenary Putin met Trump; Russian side: Foreign Minister Sergei Lavrov, Finance Minister Anton Siluanov, Presidential Aide Yury Ushakov and RDIF CEO / special presidential representative Kirill Dmitriev; US side: Secretary of State and National Security Adviser Marco Rubio and Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent. SAID (White House X posts, register row): Trump: 'We've known each other for a long time, and I think a lot of wonderful things can come out of this - or at least start.' SAID (Putin, later Kremlin trilateral readout, register row): at Trump's initiative 'considerable attention' went to Ukraine in the bilateral. SAID (Putin, AFP, Nov 19, opened): 'The American side is urging us to agree to the involvement of the Europeans'; Russia invited Europeans to Moscow through diplomatic channels. The Kremlin readout (81302, opened) lists participants only; any agreement text: not checked this pass.", "citation": ["http://en.kremlin.ru/events/president/news/81302", "https://x.com/WhiteHouse/status/2123274614210166931", "https://www.afp.com/en/europe-expects-join-new-ukraine-peace-talks-soon-says-merz"]}, {"@id": "tie/witkoff-kushner-merz-berlin-coalition-held-2026-11-19", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/steve-witkoff-jared-kushner", "to": "node/friedrich-merz-german-chancellor", "name": "attend Merz's Coalition of the Willing summit, Berlin; Trump calls in (Nov 19)", "tieType": "US envoys attend the Coalition of the Willing summit hosted by Merz in Berlin (Nov 19 2026), hours after the Shenzhen trilateral; Trump calls in from Air Force One", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-19", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-11-19", "statusNote": "Held; four-party format SAID (Zelensky); no date or venue (Merz: UAE possible).", "addedIn": "2026-11-19 (v38)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-19", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-19-powermap-v38-V-witkoff-kushner-merz-berlin-coalition-held-2026-11-19", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "social", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 4, "description": "DONE (AFP, Nov 19 2026 21:03, opened; NATO news release Nov 19 and German Chancellery press-conference transcript, search pages seen; Ukrinform Nov 19 15:18, search page seen): Witkoff and Kushner attended the Berlin Coalition of the Willing summit hosted by Chancellor Friedrich Merz, co-chaired by Macron and UK PM Andy Burnham, with Zelensky, more than 25 leaders (Chancellery: almost 40 delegations) and the EU and NATO chiefs; Merz thanked both envoys by name at the joint press conference. SAID (Kushner, per AFP): Trump called into the talks from Air Force One; 'President Trump wants to make a deal with Europe by his side. He's not looking to impose anything unilaterally'; an 'Article Five-like security guarantee' is 'something that President Trump is open to, but obviously it has to be in America's interest'. SAID (Merz, AFP): new talks 'soon' with Europe at the table alongside the US, Russia and Ukraine; a neutral venue still sought, the UAE named as possible; 'a Yalta format cannot bring peace'; he called the China summit a 'photo op'. SAID (Zelensky on X, register row): a decision that Europeans join the negotiation formats; next meeting four-party (Ukraine, Europe, America, Russia). SAID (Witkoff, SEPeaceMissions, register row): talks 'frank and productive'. Held one day after it was scheduled; no date or venue set for a four-party round.", "citation": ["https://www.afp.com/en/europe-expects-join-new-ukraine-peace-talks-soon-says-merz", "https://www.nato.int/en/news-and-events/articles/news/2026/11/19/nato-secretary-general-attends-meeting-of-the-coalition-of-the-willing-in-berlin", "https://www.bundeskanzler.de/bk-de/aktuelles/-wir-haben-eine-klare-idee-vom-frieden--2461988", "https://x.com/SEPeaceMissions/status/2123557907107045790"]}, {"@id": "tie/bonta-nvidia-investigative-subpoena-2026-11-19", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/rob-bonta-california-ag", "to": "node/nvidia", "name": "CA AG serves investigative subpoena (chips to China? misled investors?) (Nov 19)", "tieType": "California Attorney General serves an investigative subpoena on Nvidia over whether chips or confidential information went to China and whether Nvidia misled investors (Nov 19 2026)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-19", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-24", "statusNote": "No Nvidia response or return date on record (Reuters explainer, Nov 24).", "addedIn": "2026-11-19 (v38)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-24", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-19-powermap-v38-V-bonta-nvidia-investigative-subpoena-2026-11-19", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (California Department of Justice press release, 'Attorney General Bonta Serves Investigative Subpoena on Nvidia', Thursday Nov 19 2026, opened): Attorney General Rob Bonta 'today served an investigative subpoena on Nvidia related to the news of former Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang's affair with an alleged Chinese spy'; the department asks whether Nvidia's advanced chips or confidential information 'may have gone to China and whether Nvidia misled investors and the public', to evaluate whether Nvidia's actions violated California law. SAID (Bonta, same release): the conduct of Nvidia and its former CEO 'raises bright red flags'; 'Companies cannot mislead their investors.' A subpoena is an inquiry, not a finding or a complaint. Page published 3:28:44 PM EST and updated 5:29:07 PM EST per its metadata (register correction row). Nvidia's response: not checked this pass (hole filed). Third government inquiry on the Huang file after the House chairs' interviews (Dec 1-2) and the WSJ-reported SEC probe (anon.).", "citation": ["https://oag.ca.gov/news/press-releases/attorney-general-bonta-serves-investigative-subpoena-nvidia", "https://www.politico.com/news/2026/11/19/rob-bonta-probes-nvidia-over-jensen-huang-scandal-01177017"]}, {"@id": "tie/teter-nvidia-form144-30k-shares-2026-11-19", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/timothy-teter-nvidia-general-counsel", "to": "node/nvidia", "name": "GC files Form 144: proposed sale of 30,000 sh (~$4.5M) (Nov 19)", "tieType": "Form 144 notice of proposed sale of 30,000 Nvidia shares (~$4.54M) by Nvidia's general counsel, accepted 4:45:59 PM EST Nov 19 2026", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-19", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "changed", "statusDate": "2026-11-23", "statusNote": "Form 4 filed Mon Nov 23 2026 (accession 0001696841-26-000016, EDGAR updated 4:54 PM EST): 12 open-market sales on Nov 19 totaling 30,000 shares under a May 22 2026 10b5-1 plan. Notice -> executed and reported.", "addedIn": "2026-11-19 (v38)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-23", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-19-powermap-v38-V-teter-nvidia-form144-30k-shares-2026-11-19", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE (SEC EDGAR Form 144, accession 0001921094-26-001223, filing index opened: filed and accepted 2026-11-19 16:45:59; subject NVIDIA CORP CIK 0001045810; reporting person Teter Timothy S., CIK 0001696841): notice of a proposed sale of 30,000 common shares through Charles Schwab, aggregate market value USD 4,542,782, approximate sale date 11/19/2026, shares acquired as PSU/RSU equity compensation (29,537 on 12/10/2025 and 463 on 06/17/2026) per the filing text (register row). Teter is the Nvidia general counsel named in the House chairs' Nov 12 request and agreed to a Dec 2 transcribed interview. A Form 144 is a notice, not proof of an executed sale; no Form 4 for the sale was found this pass (hole filed). Time order only: the filing was accepted 1 h 17 min after the California AG's Nvidia subpoena page was first published (3:28:44 PM EST); no link between the two is claimed or shown.", "citation": ["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1045810/000192109426001223/0001921094-26-001223-index.html", "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1045810/000192109426001223/0001921094-26-001223.txt"]}, {"@id": "tie/mast-hfac-release-nvidia-amd-china-chip-licenses-2026-11-19", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/house-chairs-mast-moolenaar-crawford", "to": "node/jeff-kessler-commerce-under-secretary-bis", "name": "Mast publishes BIS China chip-license data: >879k approved (Nov 19)", "tieType": "HFAC Chairman Mast uses Export Control Reform Act authority to publish Nvidia/AMD China AI-chip license data: 3.4 million chips requested, >879,000 approved by BIS (Nov 19 2026)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-19 ; 2025-12 to 2026-05 (approvals, per Reuters)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-19 (v38)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-19", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-19-powermap-v38-V-mast-hfac-release-nvidia-amd-china-chip-licenses-2026-11-19", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (House Foreign Affairs Committee press release, 'Chairman Brian Mast Exercises Legislative Authority to Publicly Release AI Chip License Information for China', Nov 19 2026, opened): Mast used his Export Control Reform Act authorities to release export-license application information on Nvidia's and AMD's AI-chip licenses for China. The release lists requested sales of 3.4 million AI chips and approval of more than 879,000 by BIS, 'including approvals for AI chip exports to Department of War-designated Chinese Military Companies like Alibaba and Tencent', and 'requests by NVIDIA to depend on possible chip-smuggling fronts'. SAID (Reuters via register row): the approvals ran December 2025 to May 2026. 'Possible chip-smuggling fronts' is the committee's characterization, not a finding by BIS or a court. BIS sits under Under Secretary Kessler, who reports to Secretary Lutnick. A Commerce response: not checked this pass. Republican chair, same week as Guthrie's and the Democrats' letters.", "citation": ["https://foreignaffairs.house.gov/news/press-releases/chairman-brian-mast-exercises-legislative-authority-to-publicly-release-ai-chip-license-information-for-china", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/19/nvidia-amd-china-chip-sales-congress.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/davies-replaces-cairncross-national-cyber-director-2026-11-19", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/kirsten-davies-national-cyber-director-nominee", "to": "node/sean-cairncross-outgoing-national-cyber-director", "name": "Pentagon CIO Davies replaces Cairncross as cyber director (acting) (Nov 19)", "tieType": "White House national cyber director Cairncross leaves; Pentagon CIO Kirsten Davies named to replace him, acting (Nov 19 2026)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-19", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "changed", "statusDate": "2026-11-24", "statusNote": "Acting role moved to DNI Clayton Nov 23 (WH official via CNBC 2:12 PM EST and CyberScoop): Davies cannot be acting and nominee at once; she is ONCD senior adviser and will be nominated. Not yet on the Senate record.", "addedIn": "2026-11-19 (v38)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-24", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-19-powermap-v38-V-davies-replaces-cairncross-national-cyber-director-2026-11-19", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (NBC News, Monica Alba and Kyla Guilfoil, Nov 19 2026 7:48 PM EST, updated 11:02 PM EST, opened; Axios, Nov 19, opened): a White House official confirmed Sean Cairncross is leaving the Office of the National Cyber Director (in post since August 2025); a source close to the White House said Kirsten A. Davies, the Defense Department chief information officer, replaces him in an acting capacity; the post requires Senate confirmation. SAID (Cairncross written statement, Axios): 'it has been the honor of a lifetime to serve President Donald J. Trump'. SAID (Davies on X, per NBC): 'Under President Trump's leadership we will have a more secure, resilient; and supercharged technological future'; per CBC she thanked Trump and Chief of Staff Stephen Miller. At the Pentagon she advised Secretary Hegseth on IT and cybersecurity (her bio, per Axios). NBC: the White House did not provide details on the staffing changes. The change follows a week of outages that officials say were not cyberattacks; time order only, no cause stated in any record.", "citation": ["https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/white-house/national-cyber-director-sean-cairncross-leaving-kirsten-davies-replaci-rcna610329", "https://www.axios.com/2026/11/19/trump-national-cyber-director-sean-cairncross-leaving", "https://www.cbc.ca/news/world/cairncross-out-cyber-white-house-9.7429359"]}, {"@id": "tie/miller-pushed-out-cairncross-2026-11-19", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/stephen-miller", "to": "node/sean-cairncross-outgoing-national-cyber-director", "name": "reported: Miller pushed Cairncross out (2 WH officials) (Nov 19)", "tieType": "reported: Chief of Staff Miller sought the change and pushed Cairncross out (two White House officials, Axios, Nov 19 2026)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-19", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-19 (v38)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-20", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-19-powermap-v38-I-miller-pushed-out-cairncross-2026-11-19", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID as reported (Axios, Nov 19 2026, opened): 'two White House officials said President Trump's new chief of staff, Stephen Miller, sought the change and pushed out Cairncross because, one said, he \"lacked the strong cyber credentials to perform the job.\"' Pushback in the same piece: two other sources described the departure as amicable. Unnamed sources only; Miller has not said this on record and no White House statement was found. Mediaite repeats Axios and adds nothing new. Grade I until a named source or document.", "citation": ["https://www.axios.com/2026/11/19/trump-national-cyber-director-sean-cairncross-leaving", "https://www.mediaite.com/politics/stephen-miller-reportedly-pushed-out-top-cybersecurity-official-for-lacking-expertise/"]}, {"@id": "tie/losapio-palantir-ciso-cisa-hearing-2026-11-19", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/michael-losapio-cisa-nominee", "to": "node/palantir", "name": "Palantir CISO = CISA nominee; Senate hearing (Nov 19)", "tieType": "Palantir's chief information security officer, Trump's CISA director nominee, gets his Senate Homeland Security confirmation hearing (Nov 19 2026)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11 (nominated) ; 2026-11-19 (hearing)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-19", "statusNote": "Hearing held Nov 19; committee vote likely after Thanksgiving (The Record); Tillis/Wyden holds reported (search summary, not opened).", "addedIn": "2026-11-19 (v38)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-19", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-19-powermap-v38-V-losapio-palantir-ciso-cisa-hearing-2026-11-19", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (The Record, Martin Matishak, Nov 19 2026, opened; HSGAC hearing transcript and Bloomberg Law, search pages seen): Mike LoSapio, Palantir's chief information security officer, nominated on the White House Nov 9 2026 nominations list (joined row) to lead the Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency, testified before Senate Homeland Security (Chairman Rand Paul). SAID (LoSapio): he would bring 'the community and the national labs' together and report a 'gap analysis'; 'I don't necessarily believe more money means more security'; asked who won the 2020 election, 'I'm not going to answer the question about an election six years ago'; asked if the Capitol was attacked on Jan 6 2021, 'No, I don't believe there was an attack.' SAID (Sen. Blumenthal): he is 'disqualified'. The Record: CISA has had no Senate-confirmed chief for almost two years (Nick Andersen acting since February) and lost one third of its staff; committee vote likely after Thanksgiving. A nominee from a Thiel-chaired DoD contractor to lead civilian cyber defense; conflict ruling or ethics agreement: not checked this pass.", "citation": ["https://therecord.media/cisa-losapio-nomination-trump", "https://www.politico.com/live-updates/2026/11/19/congress/cisa-michael-losapio-hearing-2020-election-01175841", "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/us-law-week/palantir-executive-tapped-for-cisa-to-testify-following-outages"]}, {"@id": "tie/heidrick-approaches-haas-nvidia-ceo-2026-11-18", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/rene-haas-arm-ceo", "to": "node/nvidia", "name": "reported: search firm approached Arm's Haas for CEO (Nov 18)", "tieType": "reported: Nvidia board's search firm Heidrick & Struggles approached Arm CEO Rene Haas about the CEO job (Bloomberg, person familiar, Nov 18 2026)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-18 ; 2026-11-19 (Guardian)", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "changed", "statusDate": "2026-11-23", "statusNote": "Approach overtaken by Huang's Nov 22 reinstatement; no later report that Haas was hired or that talks continued.", "addedIn": "2026-11-19 (v38)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-23", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-19-powermap-v38-I-heidrick-approaches-haas-nvidia-ceo-2026-11-18", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID as reported (The Guardian, Lauren Almeida, Nov 19 2026, opened, citing Bloomberg; Kalshi news page, search result seen: Bloomberg Nov 18 1:45 PM ET, 'a person familiar'): Heidrick & Struggles, retained by Nvidia's board, has started contacting candidates and approached Arm CEO Rene Haas, who worked at Nvidia 2006-2013 as general manager of computing products; other reported names: Ian Buck (Nvidia VP), Lisa Su (AMD CEO), Johny Srouji (Apple). SAID (Haas, Austin conference Nov 18, per Guardian): Huang is 'a legend'. Nvidia and Arm were approached for comment (Guardian); no reply on record. An approach is not an offer; anonymous source; Kalshi odds are a market price, not a fact.", "citation": ["https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/19/nvidia-new-ceo-search-jensen-huang-arm-rene-haas", "https://news.kalshi.com/p/nvidia-ceo-odds-rene-haas"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-said-fired-cairncross-2026-11-20", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/sean-cairncross-outgoing-national-cyber-director", "name": "Trump SAID he fired Cairncross: 'not good enough' (Nov 20)", "tieType": "SAID: the President says he fired National Cyber Director Cairncross because he 'didn't think that person was good enough' (Nov 20 2026 news conference)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-19 (exit) ; 2026-11-20 (SAID, 1:33 PM EST post)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-11-20", "statusNote": "SAID on camera; no written dismissal on record.", "addedIn": "2026-11-20 (v39)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-20", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-20-powermap-v39-V-trump-said-fired-cairncross-2026-11-20", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID (C-SPAN @cspan post 2123847096063197601, Fri Nov 20 2026 1:33 PM EST, 10-second clip from the Nov 20 White House news conference, opened via the X API this pass): Q: 'Why did you fire the cyber chief though yesterday?' President Trump: 'Because I didn't think that person was good enough.' Sequence: on Nov 19 a White House official told NBC Cairncross was 'leaving' and two sources told Axios the departure was 'amicable' (v38 ties); on Nov 20 the President describes it as a firing. This is the President's own account, on camera; it does not say who proposed the change, so the Axios report that Miller pushed it (v38, I) stays I. No written dismissal or resignation letter is on record.", "citation": ["https://x.com/cspan/status/2123847096063197601", "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/white-house/national-cyber-director-sean-cairncross-leaving-kirsten-davies-replaci-rcna610329"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-names-davies-national-cyber-director-wh-2026-11-20", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/kirsten-davies-national-cyber-director-nominee", "name": "WH: Trump named Davies to lead cyber office (Nov 19-20)", "tieType": "appointment: White House release says President Trump 'named Kirsten A. Davies to lead' the Office of the National Cyber Director (release Nov 20 2026, naming Nov 19)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-19 (named) ; 2026-11-20 (WH release)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-27", "statusNote": "WH Nominations page latest is still Nov 16 (opened Nov 27); Davies not yet sent.", "addedIn": "2026-11-20 (v39)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-27", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-20-powermap-v39-V-trump-names-davies-national-cyber-director-wh-2026-11-20", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (whitehouse.gov release 'President Trump Taps Pentagon Cyber Chief Kirsten Davies as National Cyber Director', dated Nov 20 2026, opened this pass): 'Yesterday, President Donald J. Trump named Kirsten A. Davies to lead the White House Office of the National Cyber Director.' SAID in the same release: praise from Secretary of State Rubio, Secretary of War Hegseth ('dedicated patriot and professional'), DNI Jay Clayton, OSTP Director Michael Kratsios and Under Secretary of War Anthony Tata. The release does not say 'acting' and names no Senate nomination; Axios (opened) says the post requires Senate confirmation and quotes an administration official that she 'has already been Senate-confirmed' (for her DoD CIO post, not this office). The upgrade from v38: the naming is now on an official White House page, not only a source to NBC. A nomination (PN number) is still not on record.", "citation": ["https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/11/president-trump-taps-pentagon-cyber-chief-kirsten-davies-as-national-cyber-director/", "https://www.axios.com/2026/11/19/trump-national-cyber-director-sean-cairncross-leaving"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-asks-miller-run-for-president-2026-11-20", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/stephen-miller", "name": "Trump to Miller: 'most powerful man'; 'run for president?' (Nov 20)", "tieType": "SAID: at the Nov 20 2026 news conference Trump calls Chief of Staff Miller 'the most powerful man in the world' and asks 'Do you want to run for president?'", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-20", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-20 (v39)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-20", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-20-powermap-v39-V-trump-asks-miller-run-for-president-2026-11-20", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID (Fox News, Peter D'Abrosca, Nov 20 2026 4:28 PM EST, opened; C-SPAN @cspan post 2123853373191360990, 1:57 PM EST, 175-second clip, opened via the X API; the register row transcribed the clip): Trump introduced Chief of Staff Stephen Miller as 'the most powerful man in the world'; Miller said what Trump 'has achieved over the last two years is more than any president has achieved by far in American history' and 'the next two years are going to be the greatest two years in American history'; Trump: 'He was better than these two guys' (Vance and Rubio, standing beside him) and 'Do you want to run for president?' Fox calls it a 'lighthearted moment' that drew laughter. No answer from Miller on the clip. A spoken remark only: no endorsement, filing or campaign; the '2028' in some captions is not in the opened clip (register row).", "citation": ["https://www.foxnews.com/politics/trump-floats-unexpected-name-successor-powerhouses-rubio-vance-stand", "https://x.com/cspan/status/2123853373191360990"]}, {"@id": "tie/kirkland-trump-deal-11-8m-free-work-agencies-2026-11-19", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/kirkland-ellis", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "Kirkland: $11.8M free work for Commerce, DoD, USPS, DFC under Trump deal", "tieType": "settlement performance: Kirkland & Ellis (2025 $125M free-services deal with the Trump administration) reports at least $11.8M of free work for federal agencies (letter to lawmakers, Nov 2026)", "category": "pardon/settlement", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-04-11 (deal, Truth Social) ; 2026-11-05 (letter, two days after the midterms) ; 2026-11-19 (Democrats' release)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-20", "statusNote": "Letters to nine other firms Nov 19; answers due none stated; Kirkland's letter not public; Democrats take both chambers Jan 3 2027.", "addedIn": "2026-11-20 (v39)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-20", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-20-powermap-v39-V-kirkland-trump-deal-11-8m-free-work-agencies-2026-11-19", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (Bloomberg Law, Ryan Tarinelli, Nov 19 2026, updated Nov 20, opened, describing a letter from Kirkland's outside counsel Beth Wilkinson to lawmakers; House Judiciary Democrats release Nov 19 2026, opened): Kirkland & Ellis, which agreed in 2025 to $125M in free legal services after an EEOC inquiry (Trump's Apr 11 2025 Truth Social post), has provided at least $11.8M: about $4M to the Commerce Department, $2.2M to the Defense Department, $1.6M to the US Postal Service, $2M to the US International Development Finance Corporation and $1.8M representing an investment entity created under the US-Japan memorandum of understanding; more than 6,400 hours. The letter says the firm declined work on the Kennedy Center naming and on challenges to USPS ballot transmittal. SAID (Raskin, Blumenthal, Schiff): 'this corrupt bargain went much further than originally understood'; they sent follow-up letters Nov 19 to nine firms (Latham, Simpson Thacher, Willkie, Sullivan & Cromwell, Cadwalader, A&O Shearman, Milbank, Paul Weiss, Skadden). Kirkland's letter says the deal had 'little impact' on its pro bono work (Reuters via Al Jazeera). 'Coercion' is the lawmakers' word, not a finding.", "citation": ["https://news.bloomberglaw.com/business-and-practice/kirkland-did-millions-in-work-for-trump-agencies-lawmakers-say", "https://democrats-judiciary.house.gov/media-center/press-releases/after-one-law-firm-reveals-being-coerced-into-providing-118-million-in-free-legal-work-to-trump-administration-ranking-members-raskin-and-blumenthal-and-sen-schiff-slam-nine-other-law-firms-for-stonewalling-congressional", "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/20/democrats-say-law-firm-gave-11-8m-worth-of-service-to-trump-administration"]}, {"@id": "tie/epshteyn-negotiated-kirkland-deal-2025", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/boris-epshteyn", "to": "node/kirkland-ellis", "name": "Kirkland letter: Epshteyn, Mailman negotiated its 2025 deal", "tieType": "negotiation: Kirkland's letter names Boris Epshteyn (the President's personal attorney) and May Mailman among those negotiating the 2025 deal for the administration", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2025 (negotiation) ; 2026-11 (letter, reported Nov 19 2026)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-20 (v39)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-20", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-20-powermap-v39-V-epshteyn-negotiated-kirkland-deal-2025", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID (Kirkland's letter to lawmakers signed by Beth Wilkinson, as reported by Bloomberg Law Nov 19 2026, opened): Kirkland partner Mark Filip and William Burck (Quinn Emanuel) negotiated for the firm; 'Wilkinson identified Boris Epshteyn, the president's personal attorney, and May Mailman as being involved in the negotiations on behalf of the Trump administration, among others.' The letter says Kirkland began talks after the Paul Weiss agreement set 'a precedent' and judged it 'prudent' to resolve the EEOC inquiry and avoid an executive order. House Judiciary Democrats' Nov 19 release (opened) says they had earlier 'sought records of Epshteyn's role in Kirkland's deal'. The letter itself was not opened (not public); Epshteyn has no on-record reply in these pieces.", "citation": ["https://news.bloomberglaw.com/business-and-practice/kirkland-did-millions-in-work-for-trump-agencies-lawmakers-say", "https://democrats-judiciary.house.gov/media-center/press-releases/after-one-law-firm-reveals-being-coerced-into-providing-118-million-in-free-legal-work-to-trump-administration-ranking-members-raskin-and-blumenthal-and-sen-schiff-slam-nine-other-law-firms-for-stonewalling-congressional"]}, {"@id": "tie/pet-russian-intelligence-ltf-assassination-plot-denmark-2026-11-20", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/russian-intelligence-services", "to": "node/loyal-to-familia-ltf-banned-danish-gang", "name": "PET: Russian intel used LTF gang in Copenhagen plot; attache expelled (Nov 20)", "tieType": "assessed tasking: Denmark's PET assesses Russian intelligence planned and initiated a thwarted Sept 25 2026 assassination attempt near Copenhagen, to be carried out by people linked to the banned gang LTF", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-09-25 (thwarted) ; 2026-11-20 (PET 16:39 Copenhagen = 10:39 AM EST)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-23", "statusNote": "Attache's seven-day window from Nov 20 runs to about Nov 27; no opened Moscow expulsion or trial date.", "addedIn": "2026-11-20 (v39)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-23", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-20-powermap-v39-V-pet-russian-intelligence-ltf-assassination-plot-denmark-2026-11-20", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (PET, Danish Security and Intelligence Service, release 20 Nov 2026 16:39, opened): an assassination attempt on a Ukrainian-American at a concert north of Copenhagen on 25 Sep 2026 was thwarted; three people stopped in a car with firearms and knives; two charged with attempted murder and with assisting a foreign intelligence service (Danish Criminal Code s.237/21 and s.108); the court extended their pre-trial detention to those counts on Nov 20. SAID (PET assessment; Director General Rasmus Kieffer-Kristensen): the operation was 'planned and initiated by Russian intelligence services', with people linked to LTF to carry it out. DONE (BBC, opened): Foreign Minister Lars Løkke Rasmussen said Russia's defence attaché must leave within seven days; Danish media name the target as rapper Kyivstoner (Albert Vasiliev). PM Mette Frederiksen's statement (stm.dk) attributes the attempt to Russia. Pushback: Russia's embassy called the allegations 'unsubstantiated' (BBC); the two accused pleaded not guilty (local media via BBC). An intelligence assessment, not a court finding.", "citation": ["https://pet.dk/en/about-pet/news-list/russia-uses-danish-criminal-networks-in-assassination-attempt-on-danish-soil/2026/11/20", "https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cmde1lj4yjxno", "https://stm.dk/presse/pressemeddelelser/2026/statement-by-the-prime-minister/"]}, {"@id": "tie/nvidia-board-reinstates-huang-ceo-2026-11-22", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/nvidia", "to": "node/jensen-huang", "name": "Nvidia board reinstates Huang as CEO (Nov 22; 8-K)", "tieType": "employment restored (board reinstated Huang as President, CEO and director Nov 22 2026, effective immediately; 8-K Item 5.02); board SAID it 'received input from senior levels of the United States government'", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-11 (resignation accepted) ; 2026-11-22 (board vote, unanimous) ; 2026-11-23 (8-K and release)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-11-23", "statusNote": "8-K filed; Huang is CEO again, not interim; independent-committee investigation continues.", "addedIn": "2026-11-23 (v40)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-23", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-23-powermap-v40-V-nvidia-board-reinstates-huang-ceo-2026-11-22", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (Nvidia 8-K, accession 0001045810-26-000090, Item 5.02, opened): 'On November 22, 2026, the Board of Directors of NVIDIA Corporation reinstated Jen-Hsun Huang as NVIDIA's President, Chief Executive Officer and member of the Board of Directors, effective immediately'; Colette Kress continues as EVP and CFO. SAID (Nvidia release Nov 23 2026, opened): the board 'voted unanimously' after meetings with Huang, 'received input from senior levels of the United States government, and based on that input, the Board is confident that Mr. Huang's reinstatement poses no national security risk'; Harvey C. Jones remains chair; the independent-committee investigation of the foreign-intelligence reporting 'will proceed to conclusion'; a new National Security and Export Control Committee of independent directors and a Chief Compliance Officer search. The release does not say what, if anything, Huang agreed to as a condition of return. Eleven days after the Nov 12 8-K that accepted his resignation with no reason given; six days after chair Jones told analysts the board did 'not intend to reinstate' him (CNBC, opened).", "citation": ["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1045810/000104581026000090/nvda-20261122.htm", "https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-board-reinstates-jensen-huang-as-president-ceo-and-board-director", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/23/trump-nvidia-jensen-huang.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-said-made-deal-huang-reinstatement-2026-11-23", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/nvidia", "name": "Trump: 'I made the deal' to reinstate Huang; gave board 'assurances' (Nov 23)", "tieType": "public statement (on the record, CNBC and NYT phone interviews + Truth Social): Trump SAID he spoke to Nvidia's board, 'convinced them', 'I made the deal' to reinstate Huang, and gave the board national-security 'assurances'", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-22 (Sunday board call, per Trump) ; 2026-11-23 (interviews; Truth Social 9:07 AM EST)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-23 (v40)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-23", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-23-powermap-v40-V-trump-said-made-deal-huang-reinstatement-2026-11-23", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "SAID (President Trump, CNBC phone interview with Eamon Javers, article published Mon Nov 23 2026 10:08 AM EST, opened): 'I convinced them'; 'I made the deal'; 'It was a lot easier to convince them yesterday than it was a week and a half ago'; the board asked for guarantees Huang was not a national-security threat, 'And we gave them assurances, at least with everything we know'; after the vote he called Huang: 'I ask you to do one thing, Jensen. Work hard.' SAID (NYT, Haberman and Swan, via the Philadelphia Inquirer Nov 23 2026 1:12 PM ET, opened): 'Did I do a good job last night?'; the board 'would have been much different yesterday, last night, when I spoke to them'. SAID (Truth Social 117666141823845971, created_at 2026-11-23T14:07:17Z = 9:07 AM EST, opened via the public API): the board 'made the correct and proper decision'; 'The Country needs Jensen's leadership at NVIDIA'. Anonymous context (CNBC, three people familiar with the board's thinking): the decision was 'sealed by a personal promise' from Trump on Sunday that Huang had not broken national-security laws; senior officials reached the board overnight Friday. Nvidia's own release says only 'input from senior levels of the United States government'. On Nov 12 Trump had posted that Tim Cook was the only man to take Huang's place.", "citation": ["https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/23/trump-nvidia-jensen-huang.html", "https://www.inquirer.com/news/nation-world/trump-influence-huang-nvidia-rehire-ceo-vance-rubio-china-spy-20261123.html", "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/117666141823845971"]}, {"@id": "tie/vance-worked-nvidia-board-huang-assurances-2026-11", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jd-vance", "to": "node/jensen-huang", "name": "Vance spoke to Huang, helped board get assurances (NYT, anon.) [I]", "tieType": "contact (NYT, two people: at Trump's request Vance spoke privately with Huang over the weekend and helped Nvidia's board get assurances) - anonymous", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-21/22 (weekend) ; 2026-11-23 (NYT, POLITICO)", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-23 (v40)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-23", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-23-powermap-v40-I-vance-worked-nvidia-board-huang-assurances-2026-11", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID, anonymous (NYT, Maggie Haberman and Jonathan Swan, via the Philadelphia Inquirer Nov 23 2026, opened; two people with knowledge): 'Over the weekend, Trump asked Vice President JD Vance to talk to Huang and work with Nvidia's board'; 'Vance spoke privately with Huang over the weekend and helped the Nvidia board get the assurances it needed'; only 'a tiny handful of officials' knew. The NYT notes Vance is close to Huang supporters such as David Sacks. Representatives for Huang and Vance declined to comment. CNBC (one person familiar, opened): Trump and Vance were briefed on the national-security elements and saw no evidence Huang did anything illegal. Vance has made no on-record statement; the White House referred POLITICO to Trump's CNBC remarks (POLITICO page did not load to the box).", "citation": ["https://www.inquirer.com/news/nation-world/trump-influence-huang-nvidia-rehire-ceo-vance-rubio-china-spy-20261123.html", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/23/trump-nvidia-jensen-huang.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-said-blanche-clayton-cleared-huang-2026-11-23", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/todd-blanche", "to": "node/jensen-huang", "name": "Trump: AG Blanche 'confirmed' no evidence vs Huang; no DOJ document", "tieType": "public statement relayed by the President (Trump SAID the Attorney General 'confirmed' the government has no evidence of unlawful conduct by Huang; named Blanche and DNI Clayton as consulted) - no DOJ document", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-23", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-25", "statusNote": "Vance SAID Nov 25 that DOJ and national-security officials (incl. Blanche) told him Huang is 'under no investigation'; Blanche on Nov 24 would not say. Still no DOJ document. SAID vs SAID.", "addedIn": "2026-11-23 (v40)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-25", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-23-powermap-v40-V-trump-said-blanche-clayton-cleared-huang-2026-11-23", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "SAID (President Trump, Truth Social 117666141823845971, Nov 23 2026 9:07 AM EST, opened via the public API): 'The Attorney General of the United States has confirmed that the U.S. Government does not possess evidence that he has engaged in any unlawful conduct.' SAID (NYT phone interview, via the Inquirer, opened): on whether Huang had a direct role in chip smuggling, 'All those guys knew about it' (naming Attorney General Todd Blanche and DNI Jay Clayton); 'I had to go to them before I recommended this. Look, I can't do this and then all of a sudden have somebody get indicted for, for whatever.' SAID (CNBC, opened): asked what Blanche told him, 'They did a pretty good investigation, and they felt that he, himself, was exonerated.' No Justice Department statement, letter or filing saying this was opened; DOJ and Commerce said Nov 17 they are investigating Megaspeed. The Attorney General's own words are not on record here: this is the President's account of them.", "citation": ["https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/117666141823845971", "https://www.inquirer.com/news/nation-world/trump-influence-huang-nvidia-rehire-ceo-vance-rubio-china-spy-20261123.html", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/23/trump-nvidia-jensen-huang.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/bis-megaspeed-entity-list-2026-11-23", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jeff-kessler-commerce-under-secretary-bis", "to": "node/megaspeed-singapore-entity-list-nov-2026", "name": "BIS puts Megaspeed + 6 affiliates on Entity List (Nov 23)", "tieType": "export blacklist (BIS final rule adds Megaspeed and six affiliates in Singapore, Malaysia and Thailand to the Entity List; license for all EAR items, presumption of denial)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-23 (filed for public inspection 4:15 pm) ; 2026-11-25 (Federal Register publication)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-11-25", "statusNote": "Printed in the Federal Register Nov 25 2026 as FR Doc. 2026-23999, 'Additions to the Entity List' (FR API, opened ~11:55 PM EST).", "addedIn": "2026-11-23 (v40)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-25", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-23-powermap-v40-V-bis-megaspeed-entity-list-2026-11-23", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (BIS final rule, Docket No. 261123-0006, RIN 0694-AK59, FR Doc. 2026-23999, 'Filed: 11/23/2026 4:15 pm; Publication Date: 11/25/2026', signed by Julia Khersonsky, Deputy Assistant Secretary for Strategic Trade; public-inspection text opened): the End-User Review Committee added 7 entities - MSFusion Sdn. Bhd., PT Megaspeed International and Speedmatrix Sdn Bhd (Malaysia); Apex Enterprise Solutions (Singapore) Private Limited, Megaspeed International Pte. Ltd. and Swiftdata Pte. Ltd. (Singapore); Megaspeed (Thailand) Co., Ltd. - 'because of the significant risk of these entities being or becoming involved in the diversion of advanced computing commodities to unauthorized end uses or end users', with a license requirement for all items subject to the EAR and a presumption of denial; a savings clause lets en-route shipments proceed. SAID (BIS spokesman Thomas Wackman to Semafor, opened): 'It is also now unlawful to export advanced SI chips to Megaspeed, even if the chips are produced outside the United States.' Semafor: the same day Nvidia's board reinstated Huang. Context: Bessent said Nov 13 that Treasury, Defense, State and USTR had backed listing 'for months' but 'Commerce holds the pen'.", "citation": ["https://www.federalregister.gov/public-inspection/raw_text/202/623/999.txt", "https://www.semafor.com/article/11/23/2026/commerce-to-add-megaspeed-to-trade-blacklist"]}, {"@id": "tie/lutnick-pure-lithium-51pct-stake-ask-2026-07", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/howard-lutnick", "to": "node/pure-lithium-ceo-emilie-bodoin", "name": "Lutnick asked Pure Lithium for 51% US stake; refused (Reuters docs) [I]", "tieType": "deal sought, refused (Reuters, documents + one person: Lutnick asked Pure Lithium for a 51% government stake in exchange for a Japan-pledge-funded plant it would not own; company refused; Commerce rejected a 9.9% counteroffer) - not public documents", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-07-29 (meeting) ; 2026-08-22 (Skadden memo) ; 2026-11-20 (Reuters)", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-23", "statusNote": "No Commerce confirmation or denial opened after the Nov 20 Reuters exclusive; no stake taken.", "addedIn": "2026-11-23 (v40)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-23", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-23-powermap-v40-I-lutnick-pure-lithium-51pct-stake-ask-2026-07", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID (Reuters exclusive, Ernest Scheyder, Nov 20 2026 6:02 PM, opened via Investing.com; documents reviewed by Reuters plus one person with direct knowledge): at a July 29 2026 meeting with CEO Emilie Bodoin, Commerce Secretary Howard Lutnick asked Pure Lithium to give Washington a 51% controlling stake; in exchange $1B from Japan's $550B investment pledge would build a plant owned by a Tokyo-Washington special-purpose vehicle that Pure Lithium would operate but not own. Skadden Arps memo (Aug 22): '51% is far outside precedent and invites scrutiny'; 'Commerce remains fixed on 51% equity'. Commerce rejected Pure Lithium's 9.9% counterproposal; Pure Lithium refused. Lutnick also asked for 100 batteries for Energy and Defense testing and said a takeover could help the company's Panasonic dispute. A Pure Lithium representative did not dispute the account; Commerce did not respond; a Commerce spokesperson said she did not think Lutnick is invested in Pure Lithium or I-Pulse. No stake was taken. The documents are not public, so I.", "citation": ["https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/exclusivelutnick-asked-battery-startup-pure-lithium-to-accept-us-takeover-documents-and-source-say-5042851", "https://www.cato.org/blog/battery-startup-turned-down-lutnicks-federal-takeover-attempt"]}, {"@id": "tie/commerce-ipulse-250m-chips-award-equity-2026-06-25", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/howard-lutnick", "to": "node/i-pulse-robert-friedland", "name": "Commerce: $250M CHIPS award + equity stake in Friedland's I-Pulse (Jun 25)", "tieType": "contract + equity (Commerce CHIPS R&D Office definitive agreement: $250M award to I-Pulse, co-founded by Robert Friedland; Commerce received a minority, non-controlling equity stake)", "category": "contract", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-06-25 (definitive agreement) ; 2026-07-29 (Friedland arranged the Lutnick-Pure Lithium meeting, per Reuters)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-23 (v40)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-23", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-23-powermap-v40-V-commerce-ipulse-250m-chips-award-equity-2026-06-25", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (NIST / Department of Commerce release, June 25 2026, opened): the CHIPS Research & Development Office signed a definitive agreement with I-Pulse for a $250 million award under the CHIPS and Science Act for silicon-carbide power semiconductors (pulsed-power drilling for geothermal and critical-minerals mining, manufacturing, medical, fusion); 'In connection with the award, the Department received a minority, non-controlling equity stake in I-Pulse'. SAID (Lutnick, same release): 'the Trump Administration is strengthening America's capabilities'. Reuters (Nov 20 2026, opened): I-Pulse was co-founded by Robert Friedland, one of Pure Lithium's largest shareholders, who arranged and attended the July 29 Lutnick-Pure Lithium meeting with Commerce senior adviser David Shapiro; Friedland declined to comment. Sequence only: the June award and the July meeting are two dated facts; no exchange is claimed.", "citation": ["https://www.nist.gov/news-events/news/2026/06/department-commerce-announces-definitive-agreement-i-pulse-250-million", "https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/exclusivelutnick-asked-battery-startup-pure-lithium-to-accept-us-takeover-documents-and-source-say-5042851"]}, {"@id": "tie/stephen-miller-katie-miller-marriage", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/stephen-miller", "to": "node/katie-miller", "name": "married", "tieType": "family (married; four children)", "category": "family", "kind": "register", "date": "ongoing (reported 2026-11)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-23 (v40)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-23", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-23-powermap-v40-V-stephen-miller-katie-miller-marriage", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE family tie: Katie Miller is the wife of White House Chief of Staff Stephen Miller; the couple have four children (Katie Miller on X, quoted by Mediaite and the Hindustan Times, opened: 'Nothing is more important than raising our four kids'). Family tie only.", "citation": ["https://www.mediaite.com/media/news/stephen-miller-reportedly-no-longer-recusing-himself-from-white-house-policy-matters-after-wife-cuts-business-ties/", "https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/stephen-miller-cleared-to-join-all-white-house-policy-discussions-after-wife-katie-cuts-spacex-paramount-business-ties-report-101794282425357.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/katie-miller-exits-spacex-miller-recusals-end-2026-11", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/katie-miller", "to": "node/spacex", "name": "Katie Miller leaves SpaceX, sells shares; Miller's AI/space recusals end", "tieType": "employment ended (adviser to SpaceX; left, sold SpaceX shares, forfeited unvested equity; cancelled a planned Paramount podcast deal) -> WH official SAID Stephen Miller is 'no longer subject to any recusals' (AI, space, Paramount)", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-06/09 (weekend after Miller's CoS announcement) ; 2026-11-09 (The Atlantic)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-23 (v40)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-23", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-23-powermap-v40-V-katie-miller-exits-spacex-miller-recusals-end-2026-11", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (The Atlantic, Michael Scherer, Nov 9 2026, as relayed by Mediaite Nov 9 9:28 pm and the Hindustan Times Nov 10, opened; the Atlantic page itself was not opened): Katie Miller left Elon Musk's SpaceX, where she was an adviser, sold her SpaceX shares, gave up unvested stock compensation and scrapped a planned podcast agreement with Paramount, days after Trump named Stephen Miller chief of staff (succeeding Susie Wiles). SAID (a White House official, to The Atlantic and the Daily Beast): 'Stephen Miller is no longer subject to any recusals and may fully participate in all meetings and policy matters.' White House ethics lawyers had required him to stay out of AI and space matters because of her SpaceX work, and out of Paramount matters after she pursued the podcast deal (The Atlantic, May 15 2026). Sale price, buyer and amount are not reported.", "citation": ["https://www.mediaite.com/media/news/stephen-miller-reportedly-no-longer-recusing-himself-from-white-house-policy-matters-after-wife-cuts-business-ties/", "https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/stephen-miller-cleared-to-join-all-white-house-policy-discussions-after-wife-katie-cuts-spacex-paramount-business-ties-report-101794282425357.html", "https://www.thedailybeast.com/katie-millers-secret-scramble-after-husbands-promotion-revealed"]}, {"@id": "tie/garcia-oversight-dems-vance-epstein-letter-2026-11-18", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/house-oversight-democrats-rep-robert-garcia", "to": "node/jd-vance", "name": "Oversight Dems to Vance: Epstein meetings, Maxwell transfer (due Dec 2)", "tieType": "oversight demand (letter to the Vice President: every administration meeting on Epstein, the files, the subpoena, and the Maxwell interview/transfer; due Dec 2 2026)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-18 (letter) ; 2026-12-02 (deadline)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-27", "statusNote": "Answer due Dec 2 2026; no reply surfaced in a Nov 27 search; WH counsel's Nov 18 line on minority requests stands.", "addedIn": "2026-11-23 (v40)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-27", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-23-powermap-v40-V-garcia-oversight-dems-vance-epstein-letter-2026-11-18", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID (letter, Rep. Robert Garcia for Oversight Democrats to Vice President JD Vance, Nov 18 2026, PDF opened): citing the NYT (Jun 10 2026), the letter says Vance met with senior officials in the Situation Room multiple times on the Epstein files, 'took a leading role', called the attention 'a huge problem', and was 'reportedly' the first to suggest that Ghislaine Maxwell be interviewed; it ties those talks to an 'apparent quid pro quo' in which Maxwell was moved to a minimum-security camp after her interview by then-Deputy AG Todd Blanche. It asks Vance by Dec 2 2026 to identify every meeting on Epstein, the files, the subpoena or the Transparency Act, every meeting on the Maxwell interview or transfer, and every official involved. These are the committee minority's and the NYT's characterizations, not findings. SAID (USA Today, Nov 23, opened): White House counsel William Scharf replied Nov 18 to Democratic document requests that they would be recognized only from full committees or chairmen. Democrats take the gavel Jan 3 2027.", "citation": ["https://oversightdemocrats.house.gov/imo/media/doc/2026-11-18garciatovanceresituationroommeeting.pdf", "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/2026/11/23/jeffrey-epstein-house-thomas-massie-democrats-investigate/92861249007/"]}, {"@id": "tie/netanyahu-said-nvidia-leadership-continuity-2026-11-23", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/benjamin-netanyahu", "to": "node/nvidia", "name": "Netanyahu: Huang's return 'good news' for Nvidia-Israel (Nov 23)", "tieType": "public statement (official Prime Minister's Office post praising Huang's return: 'Continuity in Nvidia's leadership is good news')", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-23 (12:08 PM EST)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-11-23 (v40)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-23", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-23-powermap-v40-V-netanyahu-said-nvidia-leadership-continuity-2026-11-23", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID (official @IsraeliPM post 2124913024800608427, Mon Nov 23 2026 12:08 PM EST, under the byline 'Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu:'; text confirmed by The Times of Israel, Lazar Berman, opened): 'Nvidia's partnership with Israel's tech sector has created enormous value for the company and for Israel's innovation economy. Continuity in Nvidia's leadership is good news for that partnership and for the global AI industry.' The Times of Israel calls him the caretaker premier and says Nvidia employs thousands of Israelis in R&D centers there; it also reports President Herzog celebrated the news. A statement, not a contract or investment.", "citation": ["https://x.com/IsraeliPM/status/2124913024800608427", "https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/netanyahu-huangs-return-to-nvidia-is-good-news/"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-said-huang-pardon-option-equity-stake-2026-11-24", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/jensen-huang", "name": "Trump: Huang pardon 'always an option'; Nvidia stake 'probably not too late' (Nov 24)", "tieType": "public statement (exclusive NY Post interview at the Resolute Desk): pardon for Huang 'always an option'; government equity stake in Nvidia 'probably not too late'; Huang should 'tell the truth' to Congress", "category": "pardon/settlement", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-24 (published 5:56 PM ET)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-11-25", "statusNote": "Vance Nov 25: Huang 'doesn't need a pardon at all'. No pardon and no equity request on record.", "addedIn": "2026-11-24 (v41)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-25", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-24-powermap-v41-V-trump-said-huang-pardon-option-equity-stake-2026-11-24", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID (President Trump, exclusive interview with The New York Post, Steven Nelson, Emily Goodin and Marisa Schultz, published Tue Nov 24 2026 5:56 PM ET, opened). Asked about a pardon for any potential crimes: 'It's always an option, I guess, but I don't think it'll be necessary.' On Huang's Dec 1 House transcribed interview and Dec 3 Senate Banking hearing: 'I don't think he needs to take the Fifth ... I want him to just tell the truth, and I mean, his lawyers are going to have to advise him, but I've always found him to be 100% aboveboard.' On a US government equity stake in Nvidia (the Post notes Intel's 10% stake last year): 'I thought about it. I said, \"You know, maybe I should do it,\" but I didn't bring it up at this point. It's probably not too late.' He said he intervened to restore Huang, including by giving assurances he faced no issues from the executive branch, because the 'wrong person' as CEO 'would be a terrible thing for our country'. He said he 'got into the business of chips, much more than the business of sex'. All SAID: no pardon issued and no equity request on record; an EDGAR full-text search of Nvidia 8-Ks Nov 22-24 (register row) shows only the reinstatement 8-K. CoinDesk (Jesse Hamilton, 10:35 PM EST, opened) notes a pardon cannot reach California's state probe.", "citation": ["https://nypost.com/2026/11/24/us-news/trump-leaves-door-open-to-jensen-huang-pardon-and-urges-him-not-to-plead-5th-to-congress-next-week/", "https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/11/24/trump-says-he-s-willing-to-give-nvidia-s-huang-a-pardon-doesn-t-think-he-needs-one"]}, {"@id": "tie/blanche-declines-confirm-huang-probe-2026-11-24", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/todd-blanche", "to": "node/jensen-huang", "name": "AG Blanche won't say Huang was probed: 'For what?' (Nov 24)", "tieType": "public statement (AG at a DOJ press conference): declines to say whether Huang was investigated; says he would have told the President of evidence of crimes; calls the President 'exactly right'", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-24 (reported 17:08 GMT / 12:08 PM EST)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-11-24", "statusNote": "SAID at a DOJ press conference; no DOJ document.", "addedIn": "2026-11-24 (v41)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-24", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-24-powermap-v41-V-blanche-declines-confirm-huang-probe-2026-11-24", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID vs SAID, dated document labels. Document 1 (Mon Nov 23 2026, CNBC interview; Truth Social 9:07 AM EST, both in v40): President Trump said 'They did a pretty good investigation, and they felt that he, himself, was exonerated' and that the AG 'has confirmed that the U.S. Government does not possess evidence that he has engaged in any unlawful conduct.' Document 2 (Tue Nov 24 2026, DOJ press conference, The Independent, Alex Woodward, 17:08 GMT, opened): AG Todd Blanche said the President 'talked to a lot of people going into the decision' and was 'exactly right'; 'To the extent that the Department of Justice had information he was committing crimes, or something like this, that's something I would've certainly told the president, if it were true'; 'What does that mean? Had Huang been investigated? For what? I don't understand the question'; DOJ has 'hundreds, if not more' export investigations; 'I don't know if there's going to be an investigation that starts tomorrow that will lead to different results'; reports that the President assured Nvidia DOJ would not prosecute rest on 'public reporting of leaks'; Nvidia is a 'good corporate citizen'. In the remarks The Independent quotes (article page opened Tue Nov 24 2026 before midnight EST), the AG does not confirm the investigation the President described, and the article cites no DOJ document. Two official statements: SAID vs SAID.", "citation": ["https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/americas/us-politics/todd-blanche-trump-jensen-huang-nvidia-investigations-b3090873.html", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/23/trump-nvidia-jensen-huang.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/tim-scott-huang-senate-banking-dec3-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/sen-tim-scott-senate-banking-chair", "to": "node/jensen-huang", "name": "Senate Banking: Huang sole public witness Dec 3 (scheduled)", "tieType": "committee hearing scheduled (public, sole witness): Senate Banking 'Protecting America's AI Advantage: Oversight of U.S. Export Controls', Thu Dec 3 2026", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-12 (Scott's request) ; 2026-11-23 (hearing notice) ; 2026-12-03 (hearing)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-27", "statusNote": "Senate Banking hearing page (opened Nov 27): Thu Dec 3 2026, 10:00 AM, Dirksen 106, open session, hybrid; sole witness Jensen Huang. Scheduled, not held.", "addedIn": "2026-11-24 (v41)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-27", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-24-powermap-v41-V-tim-scott-huang-senate-banking-dec3-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 4, "description": "SAID / scheduled (TechCrunch, Aisha Malik, Nov 23 2026 10:12 AM PST, opened: Huang 'is scheduled to testify before the Senate Banking Committee on December 3, according to a notice on the committee's website'; CNBC, Kif Leswing, Nov 24 10:44 AM EST, opened: hearing 'Protecting America's AI Advantage: Oversight of U.S. Export Controls'; Chairman Tim Scott (R-S.C.) said Huang will publicly testify as the sole witness; Reuters explainer (Kanishka Singh, Nov 23, opened via Investing.com): Huang 'has agreed to testify ... in a public hearing on December 3, the Senate Banking Committee said'). Same week: House Foreign Affairs, China Select and Intelligence transcribed interviews of Huang (Dec 1) and GC Teter (Dec 2), reaffirmed by the three chairs Nov 23 (HFAC release, opened); Huang was also the scheduled GTC DC keynote on Dec 1 (CNBC). Scheduled, not held. The committee notice itself was not opened (url_unchecked).", "citation": ["https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/23/jensen-huang-scheduled-to-testify-next-week-in-senate-following-reinstatement-as-nvidia-ceo/", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/24/jensen-huang-nvidia-congress-gtc.html", "https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/explainerwhat-are-the-various-us-federal-and-state-probes-faced-by-nvidia-and-jensen-huang-5046777", "https://foreignaffairs.house.gov/news/press-releases/chairmen-mast-moolenaar-and-crawford-release-statement-on-jensen-huang-s-reinstatement"]}, {"@id": "tie/meeks-calls-public-hfac-hearing-huang-2026-11-24", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/house-democrats-meeks-raskin-kamlager-dove", "to": "node/jensen-huang", "name": "Meeks: Huang must testify in public at HFAC (Nov 24)", "tieType": "public statement (HFAC ranking member release): calls on Chairman Mast to convene a public hearing with Huang after Trump's intervention; transcribed interview 'should not replace a public hearing'", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-24", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-24", "statusNote": "Request to Chairman Mast; no public HFAC hearing scheduled.", "addedIn": "2026-11-24 (v41)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-24", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-24-powermap-v41-V-meeks-calls-public-hfac-hearing-huang-2026-11-24", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "SAID (House Foreign Affairs Committee Democrats release, Nov 24 2026, opened): Ranking Member Gregory W. Meeks: 'President Trump's intervention to reinstate Jensen Huang as NVIDIA's CEO raises even more concerning questions about the administration's own role, questions the American people deserve to hear answered in public'; 'We have many questions surrounding the administration's role in approving exports that have put America's national security up for sale'; 'A transcribed interview is critical to our oversight efforts but it should not replace a public hearing. Chairman Mast should convene one.' The release says Huang is scheduled for a transcribed interview with the committee's ranking member and chairman next week and is already confirmed for Senate Banking. A request, not a hearing; Democrats take the House gavel Jan 3 2027.", "citation": ["https://democrats-foreignaffairs.house.gov/2026/11/meeks-calls-for-public-hfac-hearing-with-nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang/"]}, {"@id": "tie/clayton-acting-ncd-davies-nominee-2026-11-23", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jay-clayton", "to": "node/kirsten-davies-national-cyber-director-nominee", "name": "DNI Clayton made acting cyber director; Davies to be nominated (Nov 23)", "tieType": "office handoff (acting National Cyber Director moves from Davies to DNI Clayton pending her nomination; Davies becomes ONCD senior adviser)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-19 (Davies named acting) ; 2026-11-23 (Clayton acting; Davies to be nominated)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-24", "statusNote": "Clayton acting; Davies nomination not yet on the Senate record.", "addedIn": "2026-11-24 (v41)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-24", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-24-powermap-v41-V-clayton-acting-ncd-davies-nominee-2026-11-23", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID (announcement; no nomination or designation document opened). CNBC (Megan Cassella, Kevin Breuninger, Mon Nov 23 2026 2:12 PM EST, opened): a White House official, not named, said DNI Jay Clayton 'has been tapped to serve as acting national cyber director while the Trump administration's permanent nominee for the role awaits Senate confirmation'; Trump had added AI czar to Clayton's portfolio in October. CyberScoop (Tim Starks, Nov 23, opened): a White House official said 'President Trump has decided to nominate her [Kirsten Davies] to serve as national cyber director'; Davies 'will serve as senior adviser for the Office of the National Cyber Director' because 'the same person cannot serve in the acting role of a position while also being the nominee for it'. Clayton, on the record (statement to CyberScoop): 'I look forward to working with the ONCD team to ensure Kirsten has a seamless transition into the role upon her confirmation by the Senate.' Clayton now holds DNI, the White House Super Intelligence Force chair and acting National Cyber Director at once. CyberScoop also notes FHFA Director Bill Pulte was acting DNI Jun-Aug 2026. The nomination is not yet on the Senate record.", "citation": ["https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/23/jay-clayton-cyber-director-kirsten-davies-trump.html", "https://cyberscoop.com/kirsten-davies-jay-clayton-national-cyber-director/"]}, {"@id": "tie/pentagon-gm-drone-parts-talks-2026-11-24", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/us-dept-of-war-pentagon", "to": "node/general-motors-gm-defense", "name": "Pentagon-GM drone-parts talks (WSJ, people familiar; no deal)", "tieType": "reported contract talks (WSJ, people familiar): Pentagon in early talks with GM, Ford, Magna and others to supply drone components (motors, actuators, sensors, lidar) to drone makers; no deal", "category": "contract", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-24", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-24", "statusNote": "Talks reported; no contract, award or DPA order on record.", "addedIn": "2026-11-24 (v41)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-24", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-24-powermap-v41-I-pentagon-gm-drone-parts-talks-2026-11-24", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "SAID / reported (I). The Wall Street Journal (not opened; paywall), citing people familiar, reported Tue Nov 24 2026 that the Pentagon is in early talks with General Motors, Ford and other manufacturers to help mass-produce military drones by supplying parts (actuators, engines, sensors, lidar) to drone companies; GM is weighing drone motors and has shown the most appetite 'at the request of high-ranking defense officials', and is in talks with RTX and L3Harris on similar deals; no agreements finalized (Reuters via Investing.com, Nathan Gomes, opened; Quartz, opened). On the record: a Pentagon official told Reuters 'The Department of War is actively partnering with domestic manufacturers, suppliers, and emerging tech firms to build a resilient, high-capacity industrial base ... of next-generation unmanned and autonomous systems'; a Ford spokesperson said its Pentagon talks concern military vehicles and satellites with Revolution Space (Ford announced a minority investment in Revolution Space Nov 23); GM declined to comment on the report; Magna had nothing to add. No contract, Defense Production Act order or award on record. Semafor (opened) ties the push to munitions shortfalls in the nine-month Iran conflict; that is its framing.", "citation": ["https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/pentagon-in-talks-with-general-motors-and-ford-on-military-drones-wsj-reports-5047560", "https://qz.com/pentagon-gm-ford-drone-production-talks-112426", "https://www.semafor.com/article/11/24/2026/pentagon-eyes-gm-for-drone-production-wsj"]}, {"@id": "tie/rutte-trump-mar-a-lago-scheduled-2026-11-25", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/mark-rutte-nato-secretary-general", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "Rutte to meet Trump at Mar-a-Lago (Nov 25, scheduled)", "tieType": "scheduled meeting (NATO media advisory): Rutte meets Trump at Mar-a-Lago Wed Nov 25 2026, plus senior Administration officials; no media opportunity", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-24 (advisory) ; 2026-11-25 (meeting)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "changed", "statusDate": "2026-11-25", "statusNote": "Held Wed Nov 25 (about 7 PM EST, closed press, dinner after); WH joint statement sent post-lid (pool note 10:21 PM EST). See trump-rutte-mar-a-lago-joint-statement-2026-11-25.", "addedIn": "2026-11-24 (v41)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-25", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-24-powermap-v41-V-rutte-trump-mar-a-lago-scheduled-2026-11-25", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "social", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID / scheduled (NATO media advisory, 24 Nov 2026, opened): 'From 24 to 25 November 2026, the NATO Secretary General, Mr Mark Rutte, will travel to Florida. On Wednesday, 25 November 2026, the Secretary General will meet with the President of the United States, Mr Donald J. Trump, at Mar-a-Lago. He will also meet with senior Administration officials. There will be no media opportunity.' Reuters (via Investing.com, search excerpt) reports the White House confirmed the meeting. Announced, not recorded as held. The advisory names no agenda; the officials are not named.", "citation": ["https://www.nato.int/en/news-and-events/events/media-advisories/2026/11/24/nato-secretary-general-to-visit-the-united-states-of-america", "https://x.com/NATOpress/status/2125178725884920130"]}, {"@id": "tie/bis-lists-alibaba-apex-megaspeed-2026-11-23", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/alibaba-group-apex-enterprise-solutions-singapore", "to": "node/megaspeed-singapore-entity-list-nov-2026", "name": "BIS lists Alibaba's Apex with Megaspeed; Alibaba: 'erroneous' (Nov 23-24)", "tieType": "trade restriction (BIS Entity List, same rule as Megaspeed) + financing link (Megaspeed unit Speedmatrix pledged equipment and IP to Alibaba's Apex as security, Jun 18 2024); Alibaba disputes", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2024-06-18 (Speedmatrix-Apex security agreement) ; 2026-11-23 (rule filed) ; 2026-11-24 (Alibaba statement)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-11-25", "statusNote": "Same rule printed Nov 25 (FR Doc. 2026-23999); no removal or correction on record; Alibaba's challenge not filed on record.", "addedIn": "2026-11-24 (v41)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-25", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-24-powermap-v41-V-bis-lists-alibaba-apex-megaspeed-2026-11-23", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "DONE (BIS final rule, FR Doc. 2026-23999, public-inspection text opened): the seven entities added include 'Apex Enterprise Solutions (Singapore) Private Limited' with Megaspeed International Pte. Ltd. and Swiftdata Pte. Ltd. under Singapore; license required for all EAR items, presumption of denial. DONE (corporate records, The Straits Times, Annabelle Liang, Nov 24 2026 4:40 PM SGT, opened): Apex's ultimate holding company is Alibaba Group Holding (immediate holder Cloud Intelligence (Cayman) Holding); Megaspeed's Malaysian unit Speedmatrix pledged IT and network equipment, IP and related rights to Apex under an agreement dated June 18 2024 as security for contractual obligations; Apex is registered at Lazada One, leased by Alibaba and Lazada. SAID (Alibaba spokesperson to The Straits Times): 'Adding Apex Enterprise Solutions to the Entity List is erroneous because Apex has never diverted advanced computing chips subject to US export restrictions'; 'We will seek all legal avenues to protect our rights and reputation.' The rule states no reason specific to Apex; the financing link is the paper the Straits Times found, not BIS's stated basis.", "citation": ["https://www.federalregister.gov/public-inspection/raw_text/202/623/999.txt", "https://www.straitstimes.com/business/alibaba-disputes-us-blacklisting-of-singapore-subsidiary-over-chip-rerouting-risks", "https://traictory.com/news/2026-11-25-megaspeed-entity-list-rule"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-nominates-oneill-mdnc-judge-2026-11-24", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/jim-o-neill-m-d-n-c-judicial-nominee", "name": "Trump picks Forsyth DA O'Neill for federal bench (Nov 24)", "tieType": "appointment (judicial nomination announced on Truth Social; recommended jointly by Sens. Tillis and Budd); lame-duck Senate window before Jan 3 2027", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-24 (12:40 PM EST post)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-27", "statusNote": "WH Nominations page (opened Nov 27) still latest Nov 16; partial materials at Judiciary since Nov 25.", "addedIn": "2026-11-24 (v41)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-27", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-24-powermap-v41-V-trump-nominates-oneill-mdnc-judge-2026-11-24", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "SAID (Truth Social 117672641177788145, created 2026-11-24T17:40:10Z = 12:40 PM EST, opened via the public API): 'I am pleased to nominate Jim O'Neill to serve as Judge on the United States District Court for the Middle District of North Carolina. Jim has the strong support of both North Carolina Senators, Ted Budd and Thom Tillis ... Now, let's get him confirmed!' WUNC (Adam Wagner, Nov 24 6:08 PM EST, search excerpt) says O'Neill, Forsyth County DA since 2009, lost his re-election to Democrat Amara Hunter in November; Tillis and Budd jointly put his name forward; longtime Tillis consultant Paul Shumaker also worked on O'Neill's re-election campaign; the seat opens because Judge Thomas D. Schroeder sought senior status (Jul 31); the Republican Senate has weeks to confirm before Democrats take control in January. Announced; nomination not yet on the Senate record.", "citation": ["https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/117672641177788145", "https://www.wunc.org/politics/2026-11-24/trump-forsyth-county-jim-oneill-federal-judge", "https://www.wxii12.com/article/president-trump-nominates-forsyth-county-jim-oneill-federal-judge/74523150"]}, {"@id": "tie/vance-said-huang-no-pardon-no-investigation-2026-11-25", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jd-vance", "to": "node/jensen-huang", "name": "Vance: Huang 'doesn't need a pardon at all', 'under no investigation' (Nov 25)", "tieType": "public statement to reporters (Wright-Patterson AFB, Ohio): Huang 'doesn't need a pardon', DOJ and national-security officials told the VP Huang is 'under no investigation'; Vance names AG Blanche among those he spoke with", "category": "pardon/settlement", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-25 (remarks after the Thanksgiving Eve meal; CBS updated 3:46 PM EST, NY Post 2:45 PM EST, AP 5:26 PM EST)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-11-25", "statusNote": "SAID to reporters; no DOJ document.", "addedIn": "2026-11-25 (v42)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-25", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-25-powermap-v42-V-vance-said-huang-no-pardon-no-investigation-2026-11-25", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 4, "description": "SAID (Vice President JD Vance to reporters at Wright-Patterson AFB, Wed Nov 25 2026; CBS News, Kathryn Watson, updated 3:46 PM EST, opened; AP via WTOP 5:26 PM EST, opened; NY Post 2:45 PM EST, opened): 'I don't think he needs a pardon at all ... I haven't seen any evidence, again, that he committed a crime. And if there is evidence that he committed a crime, then that's up to relevant authorities to actually bring a prosecution against him. And again, I was told by the Department of Justice and multiple officials in our national security apparatus that he was under no investigation.' Asked who gave the assurances, Vance said 'multiple people in the United States government', including Attorney General Todd Blanche (CBS). He said 'ultimately, it was the board's decision to bring Jensen Huang back'. SAID vs SAID with dated labels: Trump (NY Post, Nov 24): a pardon is 'always an option, I guess, but I don't think it'll be necessary'; AG Blanche (DOJ press conference, Nov 24, The Independent): would not say whether Huang was investigated ('For what?'); Vance (Nov 25): DOJ told him Huang is 'under no investigation'. No DOJ document states either account. Context (AP, two people familiar, anonymous): CIA, FBI and ODNI officials gave congressional intelligence staff a classified briefing on the matter Tue Nov 24. CBS reports Trump owned millions of dollars in Nvidia stock as he pushed for the reinstatement (CBS's statement; not re-checked tonight).", "citation": ["https://www.cbsnews.com/news/vance-says-jensen-huang-doesnt-need-pardon/", "https://wtop.com/national/2026/11/vance-says-jensen-huang-wont-need-a-pardon-as-scrutiny-of-nvidia-scandal-builds-in-washington/", "https://nypost.com/2026/11/25/us-news/i-dont-think-jensen-huang-needs-a-pardon-jd-vance-says-i-talked-to-the-attorney-general/", "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2026/11/25/vance-trump-pardon-nvidia-huang-congress/ddc7b8f2-e918-11f1-8db0-6f1e3c389e7c_story.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/senate-dems-demand-accounting-huang-return-2026-11-24", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/senate-democratic-ranking-members-cantwell-coons-warren-wyden-reed", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "5 Senate Dem ranking members demand accounting of Trump's role in Huang return (Nov 24)", "tieType": "oversight demand (joint statement by five Senate committee ranking members: Commerce, Banking, Finance, Armed Services + Coons): the administration must give Congress 'a full accounting of its role in Huang's return' (five questions)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-24 (evening; 'tonight's joint statement')", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-25", "statusNote": "Minority statement; no answer on record; 'in January, if not before'.", "addedIn": "2026-11-25 (v42)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-25", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-25-powermap-v42-V-senate-dems-demand-accounting-huang-return-2026-11-24", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "SAID (Senate Commerce Committee Democratic release dated November 24, 2026, opened): Sens. Maria Cantwell (Commerce ranking), Chris Coons, Elizabeth Warren (Banking ranking), Ron Wyden (Finance ranking) and Jack Reed (Armed Services ranking): 'President Trump has acknowledged personally intervening on Huang's behalf, and Nvidia has acknowledged that it received ‘input from senior levels of the United States government’ ... This administration must immediately provide Congress with a full accounting of its role in Huang's return.' Five questions: which officials engaged Nvidia or its board and what assurances or commitments they gave; what intelligence assessments informed that advocacy and which agencies were consulted; when the President, the Vice President and senior officials first learned of Huang's relationship and the counterintelligence concerns; what the administration knew about Nvidia's export-control compliance; what safeguards exist. 'Congress and the American people are owed answers, and we intend to get them, in January, if not before.' Minority statement; no letter, deadline or subpoena; Democrats take the Senate majority Jan 3 2027.", "citation": ["https://www.commerce.senate.gov/press/dem/release/joint-statement-from-senators-cantwell-coons-warren-wyden-reed-on-nvidias-decision-to-reinstate-jensen-huang-as-ceo/", "https://www.commerce.senate.gov/press/dem/release/cantwell-statement-on-reinstatement-of-jensen-huang/"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-rutte-mar-a-lago-joint-statement-2026-11-25", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/mark-rutte-nato-secretary-general", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "Trump-Rutte meet at Mar-a-Lago; joint statement (Nov 25, held)", "tieType": "meeting held (Mar-a-Lago, closed press, ~7 PM EST, dinner after) + joint statement (Russia-Ukraine war, Iran conflict, defense spending and industrial base)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-25 (meeting evening; statement sent post-lid, pool note 10:21 PM EST)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-11-26", "statusNote": "NATO's own page (Nov 26) carries the joint statement text and photos of the Trump and Miller meetings.", "addedIn": "2026-11-25 (v42)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-26", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-25-powermap-v42-V-trump-rutte-mar-a-lago-joint-statement-2026-11-25", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 4, "description": "DONE (meeting held; White House pool note #6, AFP's Danny Kemp, sent 10:21 PM EST Nov 25, opened): the White House sent a joint statement 'post-lid following the meeting between POTUS and NATO's Rutte, which remained closed press'. SAID (joint statement text): 'President Trump and Secretary General Rutte had an outstanding meeting this evening at ... Mar-a-Lago. The meeting was very impactful, with the war between Russia and Ukraine and the conflict in Iran being the primary subjects ... We also discussed the importance of Russia avoiding any actions that intentionally, or unintentionally, expand the war, and the importance of obtaining a peaceful resolution to the war as rapidly as possible ... the importance of continuing to expand defense spending and investment in our industrial base, both in the United States and across NATO.' Anadolu (opened) carries the same statement. SAID (Rutte on Fox & Friends before the meeting, Scripps, search excerpt): 'What President Trump is doing, also in the meeting in Shenzhen, is testing Putin.' No document, commitment or figure was released; the statement is words only.", "citation": ["https://www.forth.news/lists/whpool/ChQpqrFNxQHXxRtMBrZ8p", "https://www.aa.com.tr/en/world/trump-nato-chief-discuss-ukraine-iran-defense-spending/4138144", "https://www.scrippsnews.com/politics/nato-chief-says-trump-is-testing-putin-ahead-of-mar-a-lago-meeting", "https://www.nato.int/en/news-and-events/events/media-advisories/2026/11/24/nato-secretary-general-to-visit-the-united-states-of-america"]}, {"@id": "tie/ustr-greer-301-excess-capacity-determinations-2026-11-25", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jamieson-greer-us-trade-representative", "to": "node/xi-jinping", "name": "USTR Greer: China 'unreasonable' under 301, tariffs up to 20% proposed (Nov 25)", "tieType": "trade action proposed (Section 301 determinations: China and 13 other economies 'unreasonable'; proposed tariffs up to 20% on goods of China net of the forced-labor 301 rate; comments to Jan 5 2027, hearings Jan 25 2027) - six days after the Nov 19 US-Russia-China declaration (time order only, cause not claimed)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-03-11 (investigations initiated) ; 2026-11-25 (determinations + proposed actions) ; 2027-01-05 (comments due)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-25", "statusNote": "Proposed for comment (due Jan 5 2027; hearings Jan 25 2027); no tariff in effect.", "addedIn": "2026-11-25 (v42)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-25", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-25-powermap-v42-V-ustr-greer-301-excess-capacity-determinations-2026-11-25", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "SAID (USTR press release, November 25 2026, opened): 'Today, United States Trade Representative Jamieson Greer determined under Section 301 ... that the acts, policies, and practices of 14 economies relating to structural excess capacity and production in manufacturing sectors are unreasonable and burden or restrict U.S. commerce'; for China USTR proposes 'to consider applying tariffs of up to 20 percent, net of the rate of duty applied to the good under the Section 301 investigation related to the prohibition on the importation of goods produced with forced labor, on goods of China not identified in the annexes'; written comments due January 5 2027, hearings January 25 2027. Greer: 'since 2016, leaders ranging from Donald Trump, to Joe Biden, to Xi Jinping, to Emmanuel Macron have recognized the threat ...'. The investigations were initiated March 11 2026 (91 FR 12886). SAID vs SAID with dated document labels: White House, Nov 19 2026, 'U.S.-Russia-China Heads of State Declaration toward Peace' (no trade or tariff language) vs USTR, Nov 25 2026, determinations and proposed tariffs. Proposed for comment; no tariff in effect. The six days between the two documents are time order only, not cause.", "citation": ["https://ustr.gov/about/policy-offices/press-office/press-releases/2026/november/ustr-makes-determinations-and-proposes-actions-14-section-301-investigations-relating-structural", "https://ustr.gov/sites/default/files/files/Press/Releases/2026/China%20FRN.pdf", "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/03/17/2026-05214/initiation-of-section-301-investigations-acts-policies-and-practices-of-certain-economies-relating", "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefings-statements/2026/11/u-s-russia-china-heads-of-state-declaration-toward-peace/"]}, {"@id": "tie/sp-nvidia-aa-creditwatch-negative-2026-11-25", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/s-p-global-ratings", "to": "node/nvidia", "name": "S&P puts Nvidia AA on CreditWatch negative over governance (Nov 25)", "tieType": "credit rating action: Nvidia 'AA' issuer and senior unsecured ratings placed on CreditWatch negative; management and governance modifier cut to neutral from positive (90-day review)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-25 (Research Update; Bloomberg Law 10:46 PM UTC = 5:46 PM EST)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-25", "statusNote": "90-day CreditWatch (to about Feb 23 2027); rating not lowered.", "addedIn": "2026-11-25 (v42)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-25", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-25-powermap-v42-V-sp-nvidia-aa-creditwatch-negative-2026-11-25", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (S&P Global Ratings Research Update dated Nov 25 2026, filed in the register from the S&P disclosure page): S&P placed the 'AA' issuer credit rating on NVIDIA Corp. and the 'AA' issue-level rating on its senior unsecured debt on CreditWatch with negative implications and revised its management and governance modifier to neutral from positive; the rating was not lowered; S&P 'could downgrade NVIDIA over the next 90 days if, after conducting further due diligence, we determine that deficiencies remain', expecting any cut to be one notch unless investigations or disclosures harm reputation or prospects. SAID (S&P reasoning): 'The departure, then reinstatement of the CEO, does not sufficiently answer our questions regarding board oversight of executive code of conduct'; 'S&P Global Ratings is unaware of any remedial action enacted by the board.' Bloomberg Law (Davide Barbuscia, opened) reports the same action. Review window ends about Feb 23 2027.", "citation": ["https://news.bloomberglaw.com/artificial-intelligence/nvidia-at-risk-of-rating-cut-by-s-p-over-governance-concerns-3", "https://www.spglobal.com/ratings/en/regulatory/article/-/view/sourceId/101720856"]}, {"@id": "tie/kushner-md-meets-putin-no-nuclear-assurance-2026-11-25", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jared-kushner", "to": "node/vladimir-putin", "name": "Kushner: Putin 'reassured us' on nukes; territory 'deadlock' (MD Meets, Nov 25)", "tieType": "public interview (Axel Springer CEO Mathias Doepfner's 'MD Meets' podcast): territory 'a little bit of a deadlock' after 'many, many hours with President Putin'; Putin 'reassured us' on not using nuclear weapons (no document); war 'a proxy war where Europe is funding and arming Ukraine'", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-25 (episode released; AFP 23:14 Arab News time)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-11-25", "statusNote": "SAID in an interview; no document records the assurance.", "addedIn": "2026-11-25 (v42)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-25", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-25-powermap-v42-V-kushner-md-meets-putin-no-nuclear-assurance-2026-11-25", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "other", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "SAID (US envoy Jared Kushner on the 'MD Meets' podcast hosted by Axel Springer CEO Mathias Doepfner, released Wed Nov 25 2026; AFP via Arab News, opened): 'What Steve and I have deciphered from having many, many hours with President Putin and from the Russian team, is that you know the territorial issue is right now a little bit of a deadlock'; the war is 'a proxy war where Europe is funding and arming Ukraine against Russia'; 'it won't take a lot of miscalculation for this thing to escalate massively'; 'Europe's bought over $250 billion ... from Russia during this conflict ... if the data that I'm seeing is correct'. Per the register row (DW live blog and Clash Report citing BILD excerpts; not re-opened tonight): 'So far, Putin has showed restraint. He's agreed not to use nuclear weapons ... and he's reassured us that that's not his intention', and Putin is 'a grandmaster of politics'. SAID only: no Kremlin, White House or State document records a no-nuclear-use commitment; six days after the Nov 19 Shenzhen declaration's 'a nuclear war cannot be won and must never be fought'.", "citation": ["https://www.arabnews.com/world/us-envoy-kushner-warns-against-ukraine-war-escalation-3014051", "https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-poland-to-set-up-no-fly-zone-near-ukraine-border/live-80047122", "https://clashreport.com/world/articles/kushner-putin-nuclear-weapons-restraint-nk573kns11"]}, {"@id": "tie/ushakov-calls-witkoff-kushner-post-shenzhen-2026-11-25", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/yuri-ushakov", "to": "node/steve-witkoff-jared-kushner", "name": "Ushakov: phoned Witkoff and Kushner after the Nov 19 summit (stated Nov 25)", "tieType": "contact (Kremlin aide Ushakov SAID he spoke by phone with both US envoys after the Nov 19 Putin-Trump meeting); no dates or content given", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-19..25 (calls, undated) ; 2026-11-25 (stated to Vesti; RIA 16:23 MSK = 8:23 AM EST)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-11-25", "statusNote": "SAID by the Kremlin side; no US readout.", "addedIn": "2026-11-25 (v42)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-25", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-25-powermap-v42-V-ushakov-calls-witkoff-kushner-post-shenzhen-2026-11-25", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID (Kremlin foreign-policy aide Yuri Ushakov to Vesti, reported by RIA Novosti 16:23 Moscow time = 8:23 AM EST Nov 25 2026, opened): Ushakov said he spoke by phone with US special envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner after the Putin-Trump meeting in Shenzhen on November 19: 'Yes, I spoke by phone with both the one and the other' (translated). No call dates or content stated; Ushakov said Europeans joining the talks is not being discussed (RIA headline). Same day Kushner told 'MD Meets' the territorial issue is 'a little bit of a deadlock'. Contact only, SAID by one side; a US readout was not checked tonight.", "citation": ["https://ria.ru/20261125/ushakov-2133881495.html", "https://tass.com/politics/2224797"]}, {"@id": "tie/cornyn-blocks-gaiser-wh-vets-fahey-2026-11-23", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/sen-john-cornyn-r-tx-outgoing", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "Cornyn blocks Trump's Gaiser; WH vets Cornyn pick Fahey (Nov 23-24)", "tieType": "pushback + appointment track: Cornyn withholds his blue slip on Trump's N.D. Tex. nominee T. Elliot Gaiser (DOJ OLC head); the White House starts an FBI background check on Cornyn's pick Steve Fahey (person familiar; Cornyn thanks Trump and Patel on X); Gaiser's nomination 'dead' (MS NOW source)", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-21..22 (FBI check began 'this weekend') ; 2026-11-23 (Reuters 1:49 PM EST; Cornyn X post) ; 2026-11-24 (MS NOW 8:31 PM EST)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "changed", "statusDate": "2026-11-27", "statusNote": "Reuters story re-run Nov 27 (The Independent): Trump 'taking steps to replace' Gaiser; WH silent; WH Nominations page latest Nov 16; Gaiser not withdrawn on record.", "addedIn": "2026-11-25 (v42)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-27", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-25-powermap-v42-V-cornyn-blocks-gaiser-wh-vets-fahey-2026-11-23", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "other", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "SAID (Reuters, Nate Raymond, Nov 23 2026 1:49 PM EST, opened via Yahoo): a person familiar says the White House initiated an FBI background check on Steve Fahey, Cornyn's preferred pick for the Northern District of Texas, signalling it may nominate him in place of T. Elliot Gaiser (head of DOJ's Office of Legal Counsel), whose nomination Cornyn blocked by not returning his blue slip; the FBI also began a check on a second potential nominee backed by Sen. Thom Tillis. On record: Cornyn on X thanked Trump and FBI Director Kash Patel for initiating Fahey's background investigation, 'I hope the President will nominate him swiftly'; a White House official said it expects all of Trump's judicial nominees to be confirmed by year end. Trump on Fox News called Cornyn's move a 'tremendous disservice'. MS NOW (Nov 24 8:31 PM EST, opened): Gaiser's nomination is 'dead' (anonymous source); Cornyn: 'It is not going anywhere'; neither Senate nor WH sites show a withdrawal; the Judiciary Committee has no questionnaire from Fahey or O'Neill. The FBI check is attributed to a person familiar and confirmed by Cornyn's thanks; Cornyn's X post was not opened directly.", "citation": ["https://www.yahoo.com/news/politics/articles/white-house-takes-step-potentially-155110849.html", "https://www.ms.now/news/trump-nomination-federal-judge-texas-cornyn-gaiser-doj", "https://abovethelaw.com/2026/11/white-house-looks-ready-to-give-up-on-its-controversial-federal-judge-pick/"]}, {"@id": "tie/grassley-judiciary-receives-fahey-oneill-materials-2026-11-25", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/sen-chuck-grassley-r-ia-judiciary-chair", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "Judiciary gets partial Fahey and O'Neill paperwork (Nov 25); Grassley to test a path", "tieType": "paperwork received (Senate Judiciary: partial materials for two potential nominees, Fahey N.D. Tex. and O'Neill M.D.N.C.) + Grassley statement on a confirmation path", "category": "appointment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-25 (evening; Grassley release; Reuters Nov 26 6:35 AM)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-11-27", "statusNote": "No hearing date; no WH transmittal as of Nov 27.", "addedIn": "2026-11-26 (v43)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-27", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-26-powermap-v43-V-grassley-judiciary-receives-fahey-oneill-materials-2026-11-25", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (Senate Judiciary Committee release dated 11.25.2026, opened): 'This evening, the U.S. Senate Judiciary Committee received partial materials for two potential new judicial nominees: Steve Fahey, to fill a vacancy in the Northern District of Texas that has been open since October 2025, and Jim O'Neill, to fill a vacancy in the Middle District of North Carolina that has been open since July 2026.' SAID (same release, Grassley): he 'will continue his track record of ensuring President Trump's judicial nominations succeed by speaking to his colleagues and determining if there is any agreement on whether a path to confirmation exists for these additional nominations before the end of the year'; the committee 'will vote to advance thirteen additional judicial nominees in early December'. Reuters (Nate Raymond, Nov 26 6:35 AM, opened via Investing.com): Trump 'is moving to replace' Gaiser, whose N.D. Tex. nomination Cornyn blocked by withholding a blue slip, with Cornyn's pick Fahey; Cornyn lost a primary to a Trump-backed challenger and Democrats take the Senate on Jan 3 with a 56-seat majority; 'The White House did not respond to a request for comment.' The paperwork is partial and the release calls both 'potential' nominees: no White House nomination message and no hearing is on record, and the replacement of Gaiser is Reuters' reading, not a White House statement. Follow-up to the v42 Cornyn tie: the vetting step the sources described became paperwork at the committee.", "citation": ["https://www.judiciary.senate.gov/press/rep/releases/senate-judiciary-committee-receives-partial-materials-for-two-judicial-nominees", "https://www.investing.com/news/economy-news/trump-moves-to-replace-texas-judicial-nominee-opposed-by-senator-cornyn-5052436"]}, {"@id": "tie/rutte-miller-mar-a-lago-meeting-2026-11-25", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/mark-rutte-nato-secretary-general", "to": "node/stephen-miller", "name": "Rutte meets chief of staff Miller at Mar-a-Lago (NATO captions)", "tieType": "meeting (Mar-a-Lago; NATO photo captions: 'Meeting with Stephen Miller, White House Chief of Staff')", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-25/26 (NATO page dated 26 November 2026; meeting date not stated in the captions)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-11-26", "statusNote": "Photo captions only; no readout.", "addedIn": "2026-11-26 (v43)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-26", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-26-powermap-v43-V-rutte-miller-mar-a-lago-meeting-2026-11-25", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "other", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE (NATO News page 'Joint statement', dated 26 November 2026, opened): two photos on the page carry the caption 'Mark Rutte, NATO Secretary General, visit to the US. Meeting with Stephen Miller, White House CHief of Staff, at Mar a Lago.' (NATO's spelling) and four more are captioned bilateral meetings with President Trump at Mar-a-Lago. The page text names the Trump meeting as the evening of 25 November 2026. The Miller captions state two names only; a date, a time and the content are not in them. A White House or Miller account was not checked tonight. The joint statement text itself (already on the map) names Russia-Ukraine, Iran, defense spending and the industrial base. Whether Miller sat in on the Trump meeting is left open.", "citation": ["https://www.nato.int/en/news-and-events/articles/news/2026/11/26/joint-statement-by-the-president-of-the-united-states-of-america-and-the-nato-secretary-general"]}, {"@id": "tie/trump-gaggle-huang-absolutely-fine-second-term-2026-11-26", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/donald-trump", "to": "node/jensen-huang", "name": "Trump at Mar-a-Lago: Huang 'absolutely fine'; no call since return (Nov 26)", "tieType": "SAID (Mar-a-Lago press gaggle, Thanksgiving evening): Huang 'absolutely fine' 'based on information and belief'; has not spoken to him since the return; Huang 'calls it his second term'", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-26 (evening, about 6:55 PM EST; Bloomberg Nov 27)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-11-26", "statusNote": "An utterance; no DOJ or intelligence document.", "addedIn": "2026-11-26 (v43)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-26", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-26-powermap-v43-V-trump-gaggle-huang-absolutely-fine-second-term-2026-11-26", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID (Bloomberg, Josh Wingrove, Nov 27 8:39 AM GMT+8, opened; the page returned only the headline and the first lines): Trump, speaking to reporters at Mar-a-Lago on Thursday, said Huang 'is looking forward to his \"second term\"' as Nvidia CEO, that he has not spoken to Huang since Nvidia announced his return but 'probably will'. The register row for the same gaggle (PBS NewsHour recording, not re-opened tonight) adds: asked how he can be sure Huang is not a security threat when 'the DOJ says there's been no proper investigation', Trump said 'Based on information and belief, I think he's absolutely fine ... The information I have, which is a lot of information.' That quote rests on the register row. DONE is nothing here: it is an utterance. 'Absolutely fine' is not a Justice Department or intelligence document. It sits beside Trump's Nov 24 'always an option' pardon line, Blanche's Nov 24 non-answer and Vance's Nov 25 'under no investigation' (SAID, SAID, SAID); CBS (Nov 25, opened) reports Huang and Trump's team traded assurances over the Nov 21-23 weekend. Huang's House interview (Dec 1) and Senate Banking hearing (Dec 3) are still ahead.", "citation": ["https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-11-27/trump-jensen-huang-ceo-second-term-at-nvidia", "https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-board-reinstates-jensen-huang-as-president-ceo-and-board-director"]}, {"@id": "tie/rubio-memo-briefed-trump-alice-huang-intel-may-2026", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/marco-rubio", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "Rubio briefed Trump on Alice Huang intel before China trip (CBS, anon.) [I]", "tieType": "briefing + classified memo (CBS, U.S. officials and others familiar: Rubio memo on Alice Huang intercepts; briefing aboard Air Force One in May) - anonymous", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026 (memo earlier in year); May 2026 (Air Force One briefing); reported 2026-11-25", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-26", "statusNote": "Anonymous sourcing (CBS); no on-record confirmation; Dec 1 and Dec 3 appearances may surface it.", "addedIn": "2026-11-26 (v43)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-26", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-26-powermap-v43-I-rubio-memo-briefed-trump-alice-huang-intel-may-2026", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "SAID, anonymous (CBS News, updated Nov 25 9:25 AM EST, opened; 'U.S. officials and others directly familiar with the negotiations'): 'Earlier this year, Rubio had prepared a classified memorandum, based on U.S. intelligence that included intercepts of Alice Huang's conversations, warning Jensen Huang had a close relationship with Alice Huang, who was known to be in contact with an officer of China's Ministry of State Security.' 'Rubio also briefed Mr. Trump on the intelligence aboard Air Force One in May, before Jensen Huang joined the presidential delegation en route to China during a stop in Alaska.' CBS adds that Rubio and CIA Director Ratcliffe 'were not involved in the effort to reinstate Huang', that Rubio 'was particularly angry' when the reinstatement broke, and that allies of Rubio and Bessent say both expressed private concern but have not weighed breaking publicly. No named source, no document, and no on-record White House or State Department confirmation was found. The contents of the memo are classified. Order of events only: briefing in May, Huang on the China delegation, reinstatement push in November. The map does not claim one caused another.", "citation": ["https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-jensen-huang-nvidia-ceo-reinstated/"]}, {"@id": "tie/musk-told-trump-officials-huang-backers-export-controls-2026-11", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/elon-musk", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "Musk tells Trump officials tech backs Huang (CBS, anon.) [I]", "tieType": "contact (CBS, officials familiar: Musk spoke with Trump about export controls and said his tech and business contacts were 'steadfastly behind' Huang) - anonymous", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-21/23 (weekend of the reinstatement); reported 2026-11-25", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-26", "statusNote": "Anonymous sourcing (CBS); no on-record confirmation.", "addedIn": "2026-11-26 (v43)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-26", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-26-powermap-v43-I-musk-told-trump-officials-huang-backers-export-controls-2026-11", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "SAID, anonymous (CBS News, updated Nov 25 9:25 AM EST, opened): 'Billionaire Elon Musk spoke with Mr. Trump about export controls and told Trump officials that the people he knew in the tech and business communities were steadfastly behind Huang.' The same piece says the president 'had been on the phone with various Wall Street and Silicon Valley titans' with the takeaway that 'the U.S. needs a strong Nvidia', and that Commerce Secretary Lutnick, whose department enforces chip export controls, discussed Huang's return with Trump earlier but 'was not involved in the weekend strategizing'. Musk's public side is the Nov 13 'Stand With Jensen' petition tie already on the map. No date for the Musk call, no named source, no on-record Musk or White House comment found. Contact, not influence: the map does not claim Musk's words moved the decision.", "citation": ["https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-jensen-huang-nvidia-ceo-reinstated/"]}, {"@id": "tie/clayton-intel-deep-dive-alice-huang-board-backchannel-2026-11", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jay-clayton", "to": "node/donald-trump", "name": "DNI Clayton: Alice Huang intel review; board backchannel (CBS, anon.) [I]", "tieType": "intelligence review + backchannel (CBS, officials familiar: DNI Clayton's deep dive on Alice Huang circulated to Trump; Clayton helped connect Nvidia board members to administration officials) - anonymous", "category": "employment", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11 (before and during reinstatement weekend); reported 2026-11-25", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-26", "statusNote": "Anonymous sourcing (CBS); no ODNI statement.", "addedIn": "2026-11-26 (v43)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-26", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-26-powermap-v43-I-clayton-intel-deep-dive-alice-huang-board-backchannel-2026-11", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "SAID, anonymous (CBS News, updated Nov 25 9:25 AM EST, opened): 'Director of National Intelligence Jay Clayton had conducted a deep dive into U.S. intelligence related to Alice Huang and her interactions with Jensen Huang. The information was circulated to Trump and senior officials.' 'Clayton, who previously led the Securities and Exchange Commission, helped connect Nvidia board members to administration officials for backdoor discussions ... though he was not involved in the discussions surrounding Huang's reinstatement this weekend.' He was also consulted 'for his expertise in corporate governance matters'. CBS quotes Trump telling CNBC Huang was 'exonerated' after a 'pretty good investigation'; the AG was 'comfortable' confirming Huang was not under investigation (sources). No ODNI statement, no document, no named source. Clayton's role as intelligence reviewer and as board contact are both the sources' account; the map keeps them as SAID. The v40-v42 Blanche/Vance 'no investigation' ties are separate and still lack a DOJ document.", "citation": ["https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-jensen-huang-nvidia-ceo-reinstated/"]}, {"@id": "tie/coreweave-banks-45b-meta-gpu-loan-sale-2026-11-25", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/coreweave", "to": "node/meta", "name": "CoreWeave bankers prep $4.5B Meta-tied loan sale (Bloomberg, anon.) [I]", "tieType": "financing in preparation (Bloomberg, people with knowledge: $4.5B loan sale secured by GPUs for Meta; Morgan Stanley and MUFG as bankers) - anonymous", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-25 (Bloomberg 12:25 PM EST); sale 'as soon as next week'", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-26", "statusNote": "'As soon as next week' per Bloomberg's sources; no company announcement; terms could change.", "addedIn": "2026-11-26 (v43)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-26", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-26-powermap-v43-I-coreweave-banks-45b-meta-gpu-loan-sale-2026-11-25", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "other", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "SAID, anonymous (Bloomberg, Aaron Weinman and Jeannine Amodeo, Nov 25 12:25 PM EST, opened via Yahoo Finance): CoreWeave's bankers at Morgan Stanley and Mitsubishi UFJ Financial Group are preparing a $4.5 billion loan sale 'for as soon as next week', secured by GPUs for Meta Platforms, with proceeds drawn from escrow to fund GPUs for a data center in Dalton, Georgia (Core Scientific partnership); early yield talks about 7% to 7.5%; investors have registered interest in line with the size; 'Details and timing of the deal are still being finalized and could change'. CoreWeave and Morgan Stanley declined to comment; MUFG and Meta had not responded. Same article, TRACE and swaps per Bloomberg (not opened on a vendor screen): CoreWeave's 9% 2031 bond traded at record lows to yield 18% and five-year default protection rose the most ever, pricing over 70% default odds within five years. On the Nov 10 earnings call executives said the next delayed-draw term loan was expected 'in the coming weeks' (per the article). Nothing here is a company announcement or a closed deal. Nvidia's AA CreditWatch (S&P, Nov 25) and the Huang saga are separate ties; the map claims only that these dates sit side by side.", "citation": ["https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/coreweave-banks-sell-4-5-172523161.html"]}, {"@id": "tie/apollo-introduced-thrive-to-adt-2026-07-23", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/apollo-global-management", "to": "node/josh-kushner-thrive-capital", "name": "Apollo introduced Thrive to ADT (Jul 23), backed the bid; Josh Kushner signed (PREM14A)", "tieType": "deal introduction + financing (ADT preliminary proxy: Apollo introduced Thrive Holdings to ADT's CEO and CFO on Jul 23 2026; Apollo 'highly confident' letter for up to $11B on Sep 22) + Josh Kushner signs the merger agreement as CEO of Abode Parent", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-07-23 (introduction); 2026-09-22 (Apollo letter); 2026-10-29 (merger agreement); 2026-11-20 (PREM14A filed)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "DONE", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-11-27", "statusNote": "Preliminary proxy; definitive proxy and vote date pending.", "addedIn": "2026-11-27 (v44)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-27", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-27-powermap-v44-V-apollo-introduced-thrive-to-adt-2026-07-23", "newInVersion": true, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (ADT Inc. preliminary proxy statement, Schedule 14A PREM14A, filed with the SEC Nov 20 2026, accession 0001628280-26-075319, opened): under 'Background of the Merger', on July 23, 2026 ADT chairman and CEO James D. DeVries and CFO Jeffrey A. Likosar 'were introduced to representatives of Thrive Holdings by a representative of Apollo', then met Thrive and Apollo representatives; the Aug 3 Apollo NDA was signed 'in light of Apollo's role as a potential source of debt financing'; Thrive's third proposal ($9.85 a share) came 'together with a revised \"highly confident\" letter from Apollo, dated September 22, 2026, stating that Apollo was highly confident of its ability to provide up to $11 billion of financing'. The same filing notes Apollo affiliates sold their remaining ADT equity in May 2026. The merger agreement annexed to the proxy is signed for Abode Parent, LLC and Abode Merger Sub, Inc. by 'Joshua Kushner, Chief Executive Officer'. ADT's Oct 29 release says financing commitments were 'solely provided by funds managed by affiliates of Apollo'. SEQUENCE ONLY, not cause: the register's v23 tie dates the President's managed-account ADT sale to Jul 29 2026 (OGE 278-T), six days after this introduction; nothing in the proxy or the 278-T links the two, and a sale before a premium bid is no sign of foreknowledge. Status of the bid: go-shop runs to 11:59 PM New York time Nov 28 2026 (Excluded Party talks to Dec 8); close expected Q1 2027 subject to a stockholder vote and antitrust clearance.", "citation": ["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1703056/000162828026075319/adt-prem14a.htm", "https://investor.adt.com/News--Events/news/news-details/2026/ADT-to-be-Acquired-by-Thrive-Holdings-in-15-3-Billion-Transaction/default.aspx"]}, {"@id": "tie/shaheen-meeks-letter-rubio-woolf-usaid-files-2026-11-25", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/sen-jeanne-shaheen-sfrc-ranking-member", "to": "node/marco-rubio", "name": "Shaheen + Meeks letter to Rubio, Woolf on USAID Files PII (Nov 25)", "tieType": "oversight letter (SFRC and HFAC ranking members to Secretary of State Rubio and Acting USAID Administrator Bill Woolf: remove PII from the 'USAID Files' site)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-25 (letter); 2026-11-26 (release)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-27", "statusNote": "Letter sent Nov 25; no State or USAID reply on record.", "addedIn": "2026-11-27 (v44)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-27", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-27-powermap-v44-V-shaheen-meeks-letter-rubio-woolf-usaid-files-2026-11-25", "newInVersion": true, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "DONE (Senate Foreign Relations Committee minority release, published November 26, 2026, opened): Sen. Jeanne Shaheen (D-NH), SFRC ranking member, and Rep. Gregory W. Meeks (D-NY), HFAC ranking member, 'sent a letter to Secretary of State Marco Rubio and Acting USAID Administrator Bill Woolf' the day before. SAID (letter text in the release): links posted on USAID.gov 'include Personally Identifiable Information (PII) and potentially other sensitive data in likely contravention of federal law and regulations'; they urge the officials to 'immediately remove' that information and ask 'what review was done of these files to ensure compliance with the Privacy Act'; they say the site omits FOIA and Inspector General links. A minority ask with no deadline stated; Democrats take both chambers in January. No reply from State or USAID is on record in the sources opened tonight.", "citation": ["https://www.foreign.senate.gov/press/dem/release/shaheen-meeksdemand-answers-on-administrations-selective-release-of-usaid-files"]}, {"@id": "tie/benz-coristine-usaid-files-release-2026-11-25", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/mike-benz-foundation-for-freedom-online", "to": "node/usaid-remnant-omb-jurisdiction", "name": "Benz (and Coristine) front the USAID Files release; State points to OMB", "tieType": "document release (248 'USAID Files' posted on usaid.gov Nov 24-25; announced on X by Mike Benz and by DOGE alumnus Edward Coristine; State 'welcomes' it, refers questions to OMB)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-25 (announcement); 2026-11-26 (OCCRP); 2026-11-27 (WaPo)", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-27", "statusNote": "Party's account (OCCRP) plus NY Post; no government statement on who authorized the release.", "addedIn": "2026-11-27 (v44)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-27", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-27-powermap-v44-I-benz-coristine-usaid-files-release-2026-11-25", "newInVersion": true, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 4, "description": "DONE (official site usaid.gov, opened via its search extract): the relaunched site is titled 'USAID Files' and says the agency 'was weaponized to advance a radical agenda'; it posts files, memos and internal communications. SAID (OCCRP, Nov 26 2026, opened): Mike Benz 'appears to have orchestrated' the release and announced the relaunch on X on Nov 25; he 'was reportedly hired as a special government employee last December' to dig through USAID archives, and the State Department would not say whether he is an employee; State told OCCRP it 'welcomes this release' and referred questions to OMB, which it says 'now exercises executive and policy jurisdiction over the remaining elements of USAID'; OMB director Russ Vought 'has also suggested on X there was more to come'. SAID (New York Post, Nov 25 5:42 PM ET, opened): DOGE alumnus Edward Coristine announced the files on X. Washington Post (Nov 27 3:58 PM EST, opened, lead only): the site returned on Tuesday and consists of unredacted documents. OCCRP is a former USAID grantee and a plaintiff against the administration, so its account is a party's account: grade I. Who decided the release inside government is not on record.", "citation": ["https://www.occrp.org/en/feature/right-wing-influencer-involved-in-reckless-release-of-usaid-files", "https://nypost.com/2026/11/25/us-news/damning-usaid-files-reveal-just-how-biden-officials-weaponized-now-shuttered-agency/", "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2026/11/27/trump-administration-reboots-usaid-website-with-unredacted-memos-emails/", "https://www.usaid.gov/"]}, {"@id": "tie/dmitriev-amplifies-benz-usaid-occrp-2026-11-27", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/kirill-dmitriev", "to": "node/mike-benz-foundation-for-freedom-online", "name": "Putin envoy Dmitriev amplifies Benz on USAID Files (Nov 27)", "tieType": "amplification (Russian presidential envoy quote-posts Benz's USAID-OCCRP '$32 million' line and praises the USAID Files)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-27 (3:10 PM and 3:32 PM EST)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-11-27", "statusNote": "Posts live at pull.", "addedIn": "2026-11-27 (v44)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-27", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-27-powermap-v44-V-dmitriev-amplifies-benz-usaid-occrp-2026-11-27", "newInVersion": true, "sourceTier": "social", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "SAID (X posts opened via the fxtwitter API; times from register/xtime.py): Kirill Dmitriev, Russian presidential special envoy for investment and economic cooperation and RDIF CEO, at Fri Nov 27 2026 3:10 PM EST (status 2126408258449822097) quote-posted Mike Benz's 'Your hit piece left out that USAID paid you $32 million' (2126153437909819599, aimed at OCCRP) and wrote that OCCRP was 'controlled and funded $32 million by a corrupt USAID' and called it a 'SYSTEM of globalist lies'; at 3:32 PM EST (2126413996555149629) he replied in the same thread 'WWG1WGA. And legacy media predictably completely ignores revelations from USAID files.' The $32 million figure is Benz's own graphic (attributed to docs.candid.org), not checked here; OCCRP says its USAID funding was always disclosed and its contracts kept editorial control with OCCRP. An envoy on the Witkoff-Kushner channel speaking to a US audience in the US administration's frame; words only, no document of coordination.", "citation": ["https://x.com/kadmitriev/status/2126408258449822097", "https://x.com/kadmitriev/status/2126413996555149629", "https://x.com/MikeBenzCyber/status/2126153437909819599", "https://www.occrp.org/en/feature/right-wing-influencer-involved-in-reckless-release-of-usaid-files"]}, {"@id": "tie/bessent-taunts-pezeshkian-wonderful-winter-2026-11-27", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/scott-bessent", "to": "node/masoud-pezeshkian-iran-president", "name": "Bessent to Pezeshkian: 'Have a wonderful winter' (Nov 27)", "tieType": "public taunt (Treasury Secretary quote-posts video of Iran's president in an unheated office: 'Have a wonderful winter')", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11-27 (2:01 PM EST)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "statusDate": "2026-11-27", "statusNote": "Post live at pull; an utterance.", "addedIn": "2026-11-27 (v44)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-27", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-27-powermap-v44-V-bessent-taunts-pezeshkian-wonderful-winter-2026-11-27", "newInVersion": true, "sourceTier": "social", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "SAID (official @SecScottBessent post 2126391065468936387, opened via the fxtwitter API; Fri Nov 27 2026 2:01 PM EST per register/xtime.py): 'Good job, guys. Have a wonderful winter.' It quotes a Washington Post post (Nov 22) with video of Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian 'working in a dimly lit, unheated office and encouraging his citizens to do the same', which the Post says drew attention to Iran's energy crisis. The register row for the post also logs a repost by the official White House @RapidResponse47 account (not re-opened tonight). The Treasury Secretary publicly welcomes the winter shortage as a result of the pressure campaign; the DONE layer behind it is OFAC's Iran designations already on the register, and Iran's central bank governor's Nov 27 letter (register row) blames sanctions and the US naval blockade for higher prices. Words only.", "citation": ["https://x.com/SecScottBessent/status/2126391065468936387"]}, {"@id": "tie/nvidia-gb300-rack-alice-huang-linked-shanghai-site-2026-11", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/alice-huang-megaspeed", "to": "node/nvidia", "name": "Bloomberg: Blackwell GB300 rack at Alice Huang-linked Shanghai site (Nov 27)", "tieType": "hardware trail (Bloomberg: Chinese loan-collateral filings list an Nvidia GB300 NVL72 rack, Gigabyte-built, at a Shanghai site linked to Alice Huang)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-11 (filings); 2026-11-27 (Bloomberg, 6:45 AM EST)", "grade": "I", "saidDone": "SAID", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-27", "statusNote": "Bloomberg's document reading; Nvidia silent; Dec 1 and Dec 3 appearances may surface it.", "addedIn": "2026-11-27 (v44)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-27", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-27-powermap-v44-I-nvidia-gb300-rack-alice-huang-linked-shanghai-site-2026-11", "newInVersion": true, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": true, "nSourceDomains": 1, "description": "SAID (Bloomberg News, Nov 27 2026, via the Investing.com write-up opened tonight; paywalled original read through relays): documents submitted to Chinese regulators show two firms installed Blackwell hardware at the Yangtze River Delta Project in Shanghai, a facility linked to Alice Huang; Shanghai Shuoyao pledged a GB300 NVL72 rack as collateral for a 96 million yuan loan from Shanghai Innovation Bank, and Bloomberg traced its serial number through a public warranty database to Taiwan's Gigabyte; Shanghai Kezhan described a GB200 server there for a 90 million yuan loan from a leasing firm owned by a Shanghai government agency. Shanghai Shuoyao said this month it is a service provider for Megaspeed, 'limited to ordinary commercial cooperation'; Shanghai Kezhan is 83.3% owned by NeXPower Japan, which Caixin reported is controlled by Alice Huang. Gigabyte said it complies with applicable laws; Nvidia did not respond; Bloomberg says it lacks proof that Megaspeed sent the equipment. Blackwell exports to China need a US license. Reporting from documents Bloomberg describes; the filings themselves were not opened, so grade I.", "citation": ["https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/nvidia-blackwell-chips-found-in-shanghai-data-center-tied-to-alice-huang-5053414"]}, {"@id": "tie/leidos-air-force-cloud-one-prime-breach-2026-11", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/leidos", "to": "node/us-air-force-dept-of-the-air-force", "name": "Leidos runs Air Force Cloud One ($455M); platform breached (Reuters, Nov 27)", "tieType": "contract ($454.95M ceiling Cloud One task order, Dec 2025) + reported breach of the platform (Reuters, anonymous sources)", "category": "contract", "kind": "register", "date": "2025-12-10 (award); 2026-11-27 (Reuters)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-27", "statusNote": "Contract on record; breach anonymous-sourced, no named-office confirmation.", "addedIn": "2026-11-27 (v44)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-27", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-27-powermap-v44-V-leidos-air-force-cloud-one-prime-breach-2026-11", "newInVersion": true, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (Department of War contracts for Dec. 10, 2025, opened): Leidos Inc. 'was awarded a $454,954,000 ceiling' task order 'for Cloud One Architecture and common shared services', through Oct. 10, 2031, 11 offers, Air Force Life Cycle Management Center (FA8726-26-F-B002). SAID (Reuters, Mike Stone and Raphael Satter, Nov 27 2026, via Military Times, opened): three people familiar said hackers breached Cloud One, found within the past month or so during upgrade work; Cyber Command was called in (one source); migrations were paused and updates blocked; 'SAIC was the prime contractor for Cloud One until 2025, when Leidos took over'; Leidos 'referred questions to the Air Force'; the Air Force said it 'does not comment on the security posture' of specific systems. The contract is on the record; the breach rests on anonymous sources and no named office has confirmed or denied it. No claim of fault by Leidos.", "citation": ["https://www.defense.gov/News/Contracts/Contract/Article/4356793/", "https://www.militarytimes.com/news/your-military/2026/11/27/hackers-breach-us-air-force-flagship-cloud-one-computing-platform/"]}, {"@id": "tie/massie-khanna-efta2-dp27-218-vote-after-recess-2026-11", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/thomas-massie", "to": "node/ro-khanna", "name": "EFTA II petition hits 218 (Nov 11); Massie: vote after recess (Nov 27)", "tieType": "legislation (Epstein Files Transparency Act II: Discharge Petition No. 27 reached 218 signatures Nov 11; Massie SAID a recorded House vote comes after the Thanksgiving recess)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2026-07-15 (introduced); 2026-11-11 (218th signature); 2026-11-27 (Massie post)", "grade": "V", "saidDone": "BOTH", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "pending", "statusDate": "2026-11-27", "statusNote": "218 on the Clerk roster since Nov 11; House back Nov 30; vote date not set.", "addedIn": "2026-11-27 (v44)", "lastChecked": "2026-11-27", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-11-27-powermap-v44-V-massie-khanna-efta2-dp27-218-vote-after-recess-2026-11", "newInVersion": true, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 2, "description": "DONE (House Clerk, Discharge Petition detail for H.Res. 1430, opened Nov 27): petition dated August 31st, 2026, sponsor Thomas Massie, motion to discharge the Rules Committee from H.Res. 1430 (the rule for the EFTA II text in the H.R. 185 shell, per the register's Nov 7 row); signature 217 Adam Smith (Nov 10) and signature 218 John Garamendi (Nov 11). The Clerk page shows the House next sits Nov 30 2026 at noon. SAID (Anadolu Agency, Nov 27 2026, opened): Massie wrote on X that EFTA II 'will receive a recorded House vote after the Thanksgiving recess' and urged people to press 'your Republican Congressmen who might not have gotten the midterm message'; he introduced the bill Jul 15 with Reps. Ro Khanna and Teresa Leger Fernandez; Sens. Merkley and Lujan lead the Senate companion; the bill would give state attorneys general, lawmakers and victims standing to sue DOJ over compliance with the 2025 Act. The vote date is not set.", "citation": ["https://clerk.house.gov/DischargePetition/2026083127", "https://www.aa.com.tr/en/americas/us-congressman-calls-public-to-urge-lawmakers-to-back-epstein-files-bill/4140850"]}, {"@id": "tie/epstein-brockman-thiel-intro-2009", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jeffrey-epstein", "to": "node/john-brockman", "name": "seeks Thiel intro 2009", "tieType": "contact (seeks Thiel intro)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2009-08-17", "grade": "I", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v2)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-08-I-hannibal9972485-2108375472400720178-epstein-thiel-summers-digital-currency", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "primary", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 4, "description": "Epstein to Brockman, Re: Thiel: 'now is the time for a new financial alternative, that is what pay pal started as' - 26 days after Epstein's jail release. Row graded I (the 'plot' framing is unproven; the email itself is in the DOJ release).", "citation": ["https://x.com/Hannibal9972485/status/2108375472400720178", "https://www.justice.gov/epstein/files/DataSet%2010/EFTA01914006.pdf", "https://www.justice.gov/epstein/files/DataSet%209/EFTA00830272.pdf", "https://epsteinexposed.com/documents/efta-02467027", "https://www.epsteinscan.org/document/697481"]}, {"@id": "tie/epstein-wallwork-treasury-2014", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jeffrey-epstein", "to": "node/anne-shere-wallwork", "name": "meets Treasury on Bitcoin 2014", "tieType": "meeting (Treasury on Bitcoin)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2014-08-21", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v2)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-epstein-treasury-bitcoin-2014-wallwork-tffc", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "reference", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "~Thu Aug 21 2014 Epstein met Treasury TFFC Senior Counselor Anne Shere Wallwork on virtual currency; she noted he offered written thoughts; Aug 27 Epstein told Thiel 'I met with Treasury on Bitcoin'. No Fed/IRS/OCC/FinCEN attendee shown.", "citation": ["https://www.epsteinscan.org/document/697701", "https://tommycarstensen.com/epstein/data/documents/set9/00631/EFTA00631425.html", "https://epsteinexposed.com/documents/efta-02099970", "https://www.epsteinscan.org/document/697481", "https://www.epsteinscan.org/document/441176", "https://www.epsteinscan.org/document/697510", "https://epsteinexposed.com/documents/efta-02593836", "https://epsteinexposed.com/documents/efta-efta01914006"]}, {"@id": "tie/ito-wallwork-2014", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/joi-ito-mit-dci", "to": "node/anne-shere-wallwork", "name": "intro email + call set 2014", "tieType": "contact (intro email, call set)", "category": "contact", "kind": "register", "date": "2014-08-22 ; 2014-10-15", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v2)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-epstein-treasury-bitcoin-2014-wallwork-tffc", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "reference", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "Aug 22 2014 Joi Ito to Wallwork, cc Epstein ('he and I talk frequently'); Ito + Wallwork call scheduled Oct 15 2014 on the MIT Bitcoin Project (whether it happened not shown).", "citation": ["https://www.epsteinscan.org/document/697701", "https://tommycarstensen.com/epstein/data/documents/set9/00631/EFTA00631425.html", "https://epsteinexposed.com/documents/efta-02099970", "https://www.epsteinscan.org/document/697481", "https://www.epsteinscan.org/document/441176", "https://www.epsteinscan.org/document/697510", "https://epsteinexposed.com/documents/efta-02593836", "https://epsteinexposed.com/documents/efta-efta01914006"]}, {"@id": "tie/epstein-ito-dci-gift", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jeffrey-epstein", "to": "node/joi-ito-mit-dci", "name": "gift funds DCI launch 2015", "tieType": "funding (gift funds)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2015", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v2)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-epstein-crypto-coinbase-blockstream-mit-dci", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "Ito wrote in 2015 that Epstein 'gift funds' were used to underwrite the launch of the MIT Media Lab Digital Currency Initiative; MIT took >$800K from Epstein over 20 years.", "citation": ["https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/feb/09/jeffrey-epstein-crypto", "https://decrypt.co/356620/jeffrey-epstein-early-investor-coinbase-emails-reveal", "https://fortune.com/2026/02/06/jeffrey-epstein-files-coinbase-blockstream-michael-saylor-brock-pierce/"]}, {"@id": "tie/epstein-ito-fund-blockstream", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jeffrey-epstein", "to": "node/blockstream", "name": "$500K via Ito fund 2014", "tieType": "funding ($500K via Ito fund)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2014", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v2)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-epstein-crypto-coinbase-blockstream-mit-dci", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "2014: $500K into Blockstream through an investment fund Epstein co-owned with Joi Ito; Blockstream says the fund later divested.", "citation": ["https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/feb/09/jeffrey-epstein-crypto", "https://decrypt.co/356620/jeffrey-epstein-early-investor-coinbase-emails-reveal", "https://fortune.com/2026/02/06/jeffrey-epstein-files-coinbase-blockstream-michael-saylor-brock-pierce/"]}, {"@id": "tie/epstein-coinbase-3m", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jeffrey-epstein", "to": "node/coinbase", "name": "$3M stake 2014", "tieType": "funding ($3M stake)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2014", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v2)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-epstein-crypto-coinbase-blockstream-mit-dci", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "Epstein invested $3M in Coinbase in 2014 (DOJ files as reported by Guardian/Fortune/Decrypt).", "citation": ["https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/feb/09/jeffrey-epstein-crypto", "https://decrypt.co/356620/jeffrey-epstein-early-investor-coinbase-emails-reveal", "https://fortune.com/2026/02/06/jeffrey-epstein-files-coinbase-blockstream-michael-saylor-brock-pierce/"]}, {"@id": "tie/pierce-brokered-coinbase", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/brock-pierce", "to": "node/coinbase", "name": "brokered Epstein stake 2014", "tieType": "broker (Epstein stake)", "category": "business", "kind": "register", "date": "2014", "grade": "V", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v2)", "lastChecked": "2026-10-09", "registerRow": "grokbot-2026-10-09-V-epstein-crypto-coinbase-blockstream-mit-dci", "newInVersion": false, "sourceTier": "press", "singleSource": false, "nSourceDomains": 3, "description": "Brock Pierce (Tether co-founder) brokered Epstein's 2014 Coinbase investment; Coinbase co-founder Fred Ehrsam liaised with Pierce.", "citation": ["https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/feb/09/jeffrey-epstein-crypto", "https://decrypt.co/356620/jeffrey-epstein-early-investor-coinbase-emails-reveal", "https://fortune.com/2026/02/06/jeffrey-epstein-files-coinbase-blockstream-michael-saylor-brock-pierce/"]}, {"@id": "tie/epstein-pierce-sale-2018", "@type": "pm:Tie", "from": "node/jeffrey-epstein", "to": "node/brock-pierce", "name": "half-stake sale $15M 2018", "tieType": "business (half-stake sale, $15M)", "category": "funding", "kind": "register", "date": "2018", "grade": "I", "sequenceOnly": false, "status": "active", "addedIn": "2026-10-09 (v2)", "lastChecked": 